        <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Where do these AI tips and tricks come from?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"From official announcements and release notes by OpenAI, Anthropic, Google and Meta, and from popular posts on X by people who use these tools every day. We rewrite each item in our own words and link the original post or page."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How often is this page updated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We add new items most days. Each item shows the date it was announced and the date we last checked it, and the RSS and JSON feeds update with every build."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is Meta Muse?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Muse is Meta's personal AI agent, launched in September 2026, with its own model family (Muse Wonder and Muse Spark). See the Muse page for what it can do."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are prompt packs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Prompts that people have shared and tested for a specific job, like Nano Banana image series or a Muse ads audit. We describe what each one does and link the original so you can copy it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if a trick doesn't work for me?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Features roll out by plan and region, so check the availability line on each item. Some tips come from users on X and we haven't confirmed them in the current version; those end with a short note saying so. If something is wrong, tell us."}}]}</script>
