    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/lightning-ai-free-studio-24-7-up-to-30-credits/" class="hover:text-brand-600">A free cloud machine that runs 24/7 for your AI projects: Lightning AI&#039;s Free plan, plus up to 30 GPU credits</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Lightning AI, from the PyTorch Lightning team, has a $0 Free plan built for students and hobbyists. You can keep one CPU Studio (a ready-to-code cloud machine with terminal, notebooks, SSH and VS Code connect) running around the clock, though free Studios need a restart every 4 hours. You get 5 free credits at signup and 25 more if you add a card, which Lightning says works out to roughly 50 GPU hours on interruptible machines. Credits expire after 12 months.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It gives you a free always-on box to host a small agent, a bot or a notebook, plus enough GPU time to try fine-tuning or a local model without paying upfront.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Students, hobbyists and developers who want a free cloud dev machine for AI experiments or a place for a coding agent to run.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Who qualifies: anyone who signs up (phone number required to prevent abuse). Amount: 1 free CPU Studio active at a time, 24/7 with a restart every 4 hours; 5 credits at signup, plus 25 more after adding a card (up to 30, about 50 GPU hours on interruptible machines); 10 GB free storage, up to 2 concurrent GPUs. Deadline: none stated; unused credits expire after 12 months. Afterwards: pay-as-you-go GPU rates (for example T4 about $0.55/hr) or paid plans. Checked on lightning.ai/pricing on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
