    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/browserbase-free-plan-3-cloud-browsers-for-agents/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Let your agent browse the web in its own cloud browser, free: Browserbase gives 3 browsers and 1,000 searches at $0</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Browserbase runs headless cloud browsers that AI agents can drive like a person, plus Search and Fetch APIs for pulling web pages into an agent&#039;s context. Its Free plan includes 3 concurrent browsers, 1 browser hour, 3 agent runs, 1,000 Search calls, 1,000 Fetch calls, sessions up to 15 minutes and $5 in model tokens through its Model Gateway. It works with Playwright, Puppeteer, Selenium and its own Stagehand SDK, so you can hook it to Claude Code, Codex or Cursor projects.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Your agent gets a real browser that isn&#039;t your own logged-in one, which is safer for experiments and lets you test web automations before paying for scale.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers building browser agents, scrapers for permitted data, or web automations with coding agents.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Who qualifies: anyone who signs up. Amount: Free plan at $0/month with 3 concurrent browsers, 1 browser hour, 3 agent runs, 1,000 Search calls, 1,000 Fetch calls, 15-minute sessions, $5 in model tokens and 7-day data retention; no captcha solving on Free. Deadline: none stated. Afterwards: Developer plan $20/month (100 browser hours, then $0.12/hr) or higher tiers. Checked on browserbase.com/pricing on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
