        <time datetime="2026-11-10" class="text-slate-400">Nov 10, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-memory-rules-contradiction-audit-prompt/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Your AI&#039;s notes about you probably contradict each other: one prompt makes Claude Code list every conflict</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A Claude Code user asked Fable 5.2 to read the 194 memory notes his assistant keeps about how he works and point out where he contradicts himself. It surfaced pairs like &quot;brainstorm with me before any big build&quot; next to &quot;run long tasks overnight, don&#039;t ask me&quot;, and showed that a chunk of the notes were him correcting it. His prompt tells Claude Code to read every memory and rules file, list rules that conflict, rules said twice and notes about work that has stopped, and change nothing.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Conflicting instructions in CLAUDE.md and memory files are a quiet reason agents behave inconsistently. A read-only audit lets you clean them up yourself instead of guessing why the agent ignored a rule.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code users with a growing CLAUDE.md, rules files or memory notes, and anyone running long-lived agents with saved instructions.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Works in Claude Code on any paid plan with any model; the poster used Fable 5.2, but a cheaper model can handle a read-only review. Shared on X on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/ZeeshhDecodes/status/2120046833628299293" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @ZeeshhDecodes on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-memory-rules-contradiction-audit-prompt/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Your%20AI%27s%20notes%20about%20you%20probably%20contradict%20each%20other%3A%20one%20prompt%20makes%20Claude%20Code%20list%20every%20conflict&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-memory-rules-contradiction-audit-prompt%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Read every memory, rules and instruction file you use for me (CLAUDE.md files, rules folders, saved memories). Make three lists: rules that conflict with each other (quote both and say where each lives), rules that say the same thing twice, and notes about projects or work that look finished or abandoned. Don&#039;t edit anything; just show me the lists." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="4-carbon-now-available-ultra-api-2-10-until-nov-30" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-10" class="text-slate-400">Nov 10, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/4-carbon-now-available-ultra-api-2-10-until-nov-30/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google&#039;s strongest model is finally out: Gemini 4 Carbon hits the API at $2/$10, but only until November 30</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Two weeks after giving it only to vetted cyber defenders, Google has opened Gemini 4 Carbon, which it calls its strongest model, to the public. Developers on the paid Gemini API tier can call it in Google AI Studio and Android Studio, businesses get it in Gemini for business, and Google AI Ultra subscribers can pick it in the Gemini app, AI Mode in Search and Google Antigravity. Google pitches Carbon for long, multi-step coding, debugging, research and security work, and says Gemini 4 Argon is still the better everyday pick for most tasks.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a frontier-level model at an introductory $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens, so November is the cheap month to test it on your hardest jobs before the price doubles.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers on the paid Gemini API, Google AI Ultra subscribers, and teams comparing top models for long agentic coding or research runs.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Gemini API paid tier (AI Studio, Android Studio), Gemini for business, and Google AI Ultra in the Gemini app, AI Mode and Antigravity. Not announced for free or AI Pro users. API price: $2/$10 per 1M input/output tokens until November 30, 2026, then $4/$20. Checked on blog.google on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/gemini-4-carbon-now-available/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on blog.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/4-carbon-now-available-ultra-api-2-10-until-nov-30/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
