        <a href="/trending/cursor/gemini-4-carbon-tops-cursorbench-60-4-percent/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One day after Fable 5.2 took #1, Gemini 4 Carbon edged past it on CursorBench at 60.4%</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Cursor added Google&#039;s Gemini 4 Carbon to its model list on November 10 and says that at high effort it is now the top model on CursorBench, Cursor&#039;s own coding benchmark, with 60.4%. That nudges past Claude Fable 5.2, which Cursor had put on top a day earlier with 60% at max effort (56.9% at default). Google&#039;s Antigravity team also cites the CursorBench 4.0 ranking for Carbon.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> The top of the coding leaderboard changed hands in about 24 hours, and the gap is 0.4 points. For real work, the better test is your own repo, and the price per finished task, not the headline score.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Cursor users who pick models per task, and teams deciding between Gemini and Claude for agent runs.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">In Cursor&#039;s model picker from November 10, 2026; usage follows your Cursor plan and model pricing. The 60.4% score is Cursor&#039;s own benchmark result at high effort.</dd></div>        </dl>
