                                <article id="antigravity-swarm-one-prompt-team-of-agents" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-10" class="text-slate-400">Nov 10, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-swarm-one-prompt-team-of-agents/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Type /swarm and one prompt becomes a whole agent team: Antigravity&#039;s new mode with builders, a coordinator and verifiers</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google Antigravity is previewing /swarm, which hands your prompt to a coordinator agent that spins up parallel workers, each in its own git worktree so their edits don&#039;t collide, plus verifier agents that run tests and challenge the diffs. The agents talk on a shared message board you can watch live in a Swarm side pane (or a terminal board in the CLI), and you can pin each agent to a different model, for example Gemini 4 Carbon as coordinator and Argon for the routine edits.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Big changes that span dozens of files are where single agents fall apart. A built-in team with its own reviewers is a new way to run large migrations or redesigns, and you can still watch and steer every member.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers doing large refactors or migrations in Antigravity, and anyone curious about multi-agent coding without building their own orchestration.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">/swarm is rolling out in preview in the Antigravity app and CLI from November 10, 2026. Gemini 4 Carbon in Antigravity is for Google AI Ultra subscribers and Gemini for business. Google warns that swarms use quota much faster than a normal chat.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://antigravity.google/blog/gemini-4-carbon-in-google-antigravity" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google Antigravity on antigravity.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-swarm-one-prompt-team-of-agents/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Type%20%2Fswarm%20and%20one%20prompt%20becomes%20a%20whole%20agent%20team%3A%20Antigravity%27s%20new%20mode%20with%20builders%2C%20a%20coordinator%20and%20verifiers&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fantigravity-swarm-one-prompt-team-of-agents%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
