                                <article id="alphaproof-code-proves-signal-security-6-5-million-lines" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="research">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Research</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-10" class="text-slate-400">Nov 10, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/alphaproof-code-proves-signal-security-6-5-million-lines/" class="hover:text-brand-600">AI agents wrote 6.5 million lines of math proof that Signal&#039;s encryption code does what it promises</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google DeepMind introduced AlphaProof Code, a system where human experts write the security goals as formal specifications and teams of AI agents, powered by Gemini Carbon, write the proofs. Applied to libsignal, the code behind Signal&#039;s encryption, the agents produced about 6.5 million lines of Lean proof, checked automatically, showing forward secrecy, authentication and post-compromise security for one-to-one chats right down to the compiled AArch64 machine code. When the team put two old, already-fixed bugs back in, the system proved those versions insecure.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Formal verification has been too slow and costly for most real software. This suggests AI agents can make &#039;mathematically proven secure&#039; practical for important code, with humans reviewing only about 1% of the work.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Security engineers, people who build cryptography or critical software, and anyone curious about AI that checks code rather than writes it.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to: research results. The Lean specs and proofs are published on GitHub. Scope limits: one-to-one sessions in libsignal v0.105.4; key generation, group chats, side channels and the Signal apps themselves aren&#039;t covered, and the crypto primitives are assumed correct.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://deepmind.google/blog/introducing-alphaproof-code/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google DeepMind on deepmind.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/alphaproof-code-proves-signal-security-6-5-million-lines/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=AI%20agents%20wrote%206.5%20million%20lines%20of%20math%20proof%20that%20Signal%27s%20encryption%20code%20does%20what%20it%20promises&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Falphaproof-code-proves-signal-security-6-5-million-lines%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
