    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/uber-courier-and-expedia-hotel-booking-in-chat/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Muse can now send a package with Uber and book you an Expedia hotel, all from one chat</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta&#039;s Muse agent picked up two new connectors this week. Uber says Muse can now arrange an Uber Courier delivery in chat: it shows you the price, you approve the booking, and Uber handles the pickup. Muse also announced Expedia as a connector; Expedia told Skift it covers searching and booking hotels in plain language in the U.S., while changes and cancellations still go through Expedia&#039;s support.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> These are real errands with real money, done by an agent that asks before it pays. It&#039;s a good test of whether you&#039;d trust a chat assistant with logistics and travel.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse users in supported countries who send packages or book hotels, and anyone tracking which agents can actually transact.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">In the Muse app where Muse is available (18+). Expedia hotel booking is U.S.-only per Expedia; per Skift&#039;s test it books pay-now rates and linking an Expedia account unlocks member prices. Uber Courier follows Uber&#039;s own coverage and pricing. Delivery and hotel costs are yours.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Uber/status/2120157875591122975" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Uber on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/uber-courier-and-expedia-hotel-booking-in-chat/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
