                                <article id="fable-5-2-fermat-30-hours-cheaper-faster" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/fable-5-2-fermat-30-hours-cheaper-faster/" class="hover:text-brand-600">1,000 Claude agents formalized Fermat&#039;s Last Theorem in 30 hours: Fable 5.2 is out, faster and cheaper</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic released Claude Fable 5.2 and Claude Mythos 5.2, the same underlying model with different safeguards. Fable 5.2 is open to everyone and is built for the hardest, longest technical work. Anthropic says it writes up to 30% faster than Fable 5.1 and now costs $8 per million input tokens and $40 per million output, down from $10 and $50. In pre-release tests a team of about 1,000 Fable 5.2 agents fully formalized the proof of Fermat&#039;s Last Theorem in Lean in 30 hours, and one engineer had it coordinate over 1,000 subagents for eight days to build a prototype operating system that boots on a laptop. Mythos 5.2, with fewer cyber and biology blocks, is only for vetted organizations.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Anthropic&#039;s top public model just got cheaper and faster, and its own guidance is clear about when it&#039;s worth reaching for: long, ambiguous, multi-hour jobs where Opus 5.5 at high effort still falls short.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and teams running long agent sessions, big migrations, deep research or hardware and science work in Claude Code or on the Claude Platform.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Available November 9, 2026 in Claude apps, Claude Code and the Claude Platform (model id claude-fable-5-2), plus AWS, Google Cloud and Microsoft Azure. API price $8/$40 per million input/output tokens; optional fast mode (up to 2.5x faster) costs $16/$80. Fable runs inside Max and Ultra limits; Pro and Team standard seats normally pay with usage credits (free for one launch week, see the launch offer). Mythos 5.2 is limited to Anthropic&#039;s Cyber and Life Sciences Verification Programs. Checked on anthropic.com on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/claude-fable-and-mythos-5-2" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
