                                <article id="fable-5-2-designed-three-working-electronic-devices" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="research">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Research</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/fable-5-2-designed-three-working-electronic-devices/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One paragraph in, a working gadget out: Claude Fable 5.2 designed 3 devices that worked with no circuit fixes</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic and circuit-board maker Diode Computers gave Claude Fable 5.2 short briefs for three gadgets: a USB-C speakerphone, a home voice-assistant hub and a handheld virtual pet. From each prompt, Claude wrote the spec, drew the schematics, picked parts from US distributors, routed a four-layer circuit board, modeled a 3D-printable case and wrote the firmware. Diode built the boards straight from Claude&#039;s files with no back-and-forth, and all three prototypes worked without electrical changes; Anthropic says the speakerphone is still working after weeks of use.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Hardware has been the slowest part of building a product. If an AI can go from a paragraph to a buildable board, case and firmware in under a day, makers and small teams can prototype gadgets far faster, with engineers checking the work.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Hardware engineers, makers, hardware startups and students who prototype electronics and want an AI to draft schematics, PCB layouts, enclosures and firmware.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">This was Anthropic&#039;s pre-release test with Diode, not a packaged product. Fable 5.2 itself is available in Claude apps, Claude Code and the API ($8/$40 per million tokens); you still need your own PCB, CAD and fabrication tools. Anthropic notes the devices are early prototypes that haven&#039;t had electrical validation, antenna tuning, thermal testing or certification, and Anthropic has a commercial relationship with Diode. Checked on anthropic.com on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/claude-electronics-design" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/fable-5-2-designed-three-working-electronic-devices/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=One%20paragraph%20in%2C%20a%20working%20gadget%20out%3A%20Claude%20Fable%205.2%20designed%203%20devices%20that%20worked%20with%20no%20circuit%20fixes&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Ffable-5-2-designed-three-working-electronic-devices%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want a one-paragraph hardware brief reviewed before any files are produced. Ask me what the device should do, how it connects, and which parts I already have. Then outline the spec, schematic, parts list and review checks a human engineer should do. Do not order parts, contact a fabricator, or claim the design will work on the first build." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
