                                <article id="which-model-guide-fable-opus-sonnet-haiku-effort" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/which-model-guide-fable-opus-sonnet-haiku-effort/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Stop defaulting to the biggest model: Anthropic&#039;s new guide says when to use Fable 5.2, Opus, Sonnet or Haiku</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Alongside Fable 5.2, Anthropic updated its &#039;choosing a model&#039; guide. The advice: start most work on Opus 5.5, move up to Fable 5.2 only when Opus at xhigh or max effort still falls short on long or ambiguous agent work, and drop to Sonnet 5.5 for everyday coding or Haiku 5.5 for high-volume, low-latency jobs and subagents. It also says tuning the effort setting is often a better lever than switching models, and shows how to pair a cheap worker model with a frontier advisor or orchestrator so most tokens are billed at the lower rate.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Model choice is the biggest cost lever most teams ignore. Following this guide can cut the bill on agent workflows without losing quality where it matters.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers building on the Claude API or Claude Code who want to balance quality, speed and cost across agents and subagents.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free documentation on the Claude Platform docs site, updated for Fable 5.2 on November 9, 2026 and shared by ClaudeDevs on X. Model prices vary; see Anthropic&#039;s model comparison table. Checked on platform.claude.com on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/choosing-a-model" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Claude Platform Docs on platform.claude.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/which-model-guide-fable-opus-sonnet-haiku-effort/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Stop%20defaulting%20to%20the%20biggest%20model%3A%20Anthropic%27s%20new%20guide%20says%20when%20to%20use%20Fable%205.2%2C%20Opus%2C%20Sonnet%20or%20Haiku&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fwhich-model-guide-fable-opus-sonnet-haiku-effort%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want a model-choice plan for my project based on Anthropic’s guide, not a default to the largest model. Start from Opus 5.5, say when to change effort before switching, when Haiku 5.5 fits subagents, and when to escalate to Fable 5.2. Do not change my default model or spend usage credits unless I approve it." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
