                                <article id="ember-haiku-level-third-of-cost-per-task" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/ember-haiku-level-third-of-cost-per-task/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Meta&#039;s Muse Ember matches Claude Haiku 5.5&#039;s score at about a third of the cost per task: $0.10 per million input tokens</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta released Muse Ember, its smallest and cheapest Muse model, built for the repetitive work agents do all day: tool calls, coding subtasks, routing, extraction and parsing long documents. It reads text, images, audio, video and PDFs, has a 1M-token context window and can write up to 512K tokens. On the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index it scores 36, tying Claude Haiku 5.5 at max effort, at about $0.14 per task versus roughly $0.41, Meta says. Meta suggests pairing it with a bigger model: Muse Wonder or Spark plans, Ember handles the volume.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Subagent calls are where agent bills pile up. A model this cheap that holds its own on agent and coding benchmarks can cut the cost of high-volume workflows a lot.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers running coding agents, document pipelines or customer workflows who want a cheap, fast subagent model.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Available November 9, 2026 on the Meta Model API (muse-ember-1.0, Standard mode only) and in Muse Code on pay-as-you-go and every plan; also on Google Cloud and Oracle Cloud, and in OpenRouter and OpenCode per their announcements. Price: $0.10 input, $0.004 cached input and $0.50 output per million tokens for requests up to 200K input tokens; $0.30/$0.012/$1.50 above that. Benchmark claims are Meta&#039;s and Artificial Analysis&#039;s; Meta&#039;s own chart shows it trailing Haiku 5.5 on FrontierCode 2.0. Checked on research.meta.ai and dev.meta.ai on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://research.meta.ai/blog/muse-ember" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Meta AI on research.meta.ai ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/ember-haiku-level-third-of-cost-per-task/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Meta%27s%20Muse%20Ember%20matches%20Claude%20Haiku%205.5%27s%20score%20at%20about%20a%20third%20of%20the%20cost%20per%20task%3A%20%240.10%20per%20million%20input%20tokens&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fember-haiku-level-third-of-cost-per-task%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want to prototype one high-volume, bounded subtask on Muse Ember, such as classification or field extraction, and compare quality and cost with my current small model. Use model muse-ember-1.0 only after I provide an API key in an environment variable. Do not buy credits, deploy, or send me production traffic." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
