                                <article id="spacefast-publish-from-chatgpt-claude-free-plan" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/spacefast-publish-from-chatgpt-claude-free-plan/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Ask Claude or ChatGPT to &#039;put it on Spacefast&#039; and a live link comes back in the chat, free to start with no card</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Spacefast, from WordPress.com maker Automattic, opened to everyone on November 9. It isn&#039;t an AI builder: you keep using Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor or another agent, then ask it to publish with Spacefast, and a live web address comes back in the chat. Each project gets a private-by-default &#039;Space&#039; with a database, file uploads, version history, page comments and visitor stats. You can also drag a folder onto drop.fast, push from Git or run npx spacefast publish.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most AI-built pages and apps die as chat artifacts or on localhost. This gives them a real, shareable home with a database in one sentence, and the free plan covers small projects.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Non-developers, founders, marketers and students who make decks, sites, tools or small apps with AI and want to share them with a real link.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Personal plan is $0 with no card: $1 of usage included each month, 20 Spaces and 20 custom domains, commercial use allowed, daily backups kept 7 days. When the $1 is used up, new builds pause but live Spaces keep serving. Go is $5/month and Pro $15/month. You can publish without an account, but unclaimed Spaces expire after about 33 hours unless you claim them. Supports static HTML, Next.js, TanStack Start, Astro and PHP; built-in app login and email were listed as coming soon at launch. Checked on spacefast.com on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://spacefast.com/pricing" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Spacefast (Automattic) on spacefast.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/spacefast-publish-from-chatgpt-claude-free-plan/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Ask%20Claude%20or%20ChatGPT%20to%20%27put%20it%20on%20Spacefast%27%20and%20a%20live%20link%20comes%20back%20in%20the%20chat%2C%20free%20to%20start%20with%20no%20card&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fspacefast-publish-from-chatgpt-claude-free-plan%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want to prepare a small page or prototype for Spacefast publishing, then show me the exact publish request to use in chat. Explain that unpublished or unclaimed Spaces may expire, and do not publish, buy a plan, or make anything public unless I approve it." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="dots-connect-multiple-computers-pick-one-per-task" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/dots-connect-multiple-computers-pick-one-per-task/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Your ChatGPT dot can now use more than one of your computers: build on a spare machine while you keep coding</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI&#039;s always-on dot agents used to work with one connected computer at a time. Now you can connect several of your own machines to the same dot and tell it which one to use. OpenAI&#039;s example: the dot builds and tests your app on a dedicated machine while you keep coding on your laptop. Each thread runs on one computer at a time, so for parallel work you ask the dot to start a separate thread on each machine. The dot&#039;s cloud computer stays connected too.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Long builds and test runs no longer have to tie up the laptop you&#039;re working on, and a spare desktop or Mac mini becomes a remote worker you can direct from your phone.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">ChatGPT Pro and Business Premium users with dots who own more than one computer, especially developers with a spare build machine.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Announced by OpenAI Developers on X on November 9, 2026 and described in ChatGPT&#039;s dots docs. Needs the ChatGPT desktop app open and online on each computer. Dots are offered to ChatGPT Pro users outside the EEA, Switzerland and the UK, to Business Premium, and to eligible Enterprise workspaces. Access is all-or-nothing per computer (no per-folder permissions documented), and you can revoke each machine separately. Checked on learn.chatgpt.com on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/computers-and-apps" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on learn.chatgpt.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/dots-connect-multiple-computers-pick-one-per-task/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Your%20ChatGPT%20dot%20can%20now%20use%20more%20than%20one%20of%20your%20computers%3A%20build%20on%20a%20spare%20machine%20while%20you%20keep%20coding&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fdots-connect-multiple-computers-pick-one-per-task%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want a safe plan to connect a second computer to my ChatGPT dot for one build-and-test thread, while I keep working on this machine. List the desktop-app permission steps, remind me that one thread uses one computer, and do not install software, grant access, or start a task on another machine unless I approve it." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="codex-modretro-chromatic-make-game-boy-color-games" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-modretro-chromatic-make-game-boy-color-games/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Make your own Game Boy Color game with Codex, and play it in your browser even without the $200 handheld</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI and ModRetro put the Codex edition of the Chromatic, a Game Boy Color-compatible handheld, on OpenAI&#039;s Supply Co. store. The more interesting part is the free ModRetro Chromatic plugin in Codex: you describe a game, and Codex builds it as a GB Studio project, designs levels, animates sprites, checks graphics against the old hardware limits and builds a ROM. You can play and tweak it in a browser emulator inside Codex, then, if you own the handheld, stream it to the device or write it to the included cartridge.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a fun, low-stakes way to learn agentic coding: you see each change straight away in a playable game, and you don&#039;t need to buy hardware to start.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Hobbyists, students, retro gaming fans and parents who want a weekend project with Codex.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The ModRetro Chromatic: Codex Edition costs $200 including one programmable cartridge (extra cartridges $50); both showed &#039;restock soon&#039;, expected November 19, on November 10, 2026, and ship only to the US, Canada, Australia, New Zealand, Japan, UK and EU. The plugin runs in the Codex desktop app, which needs a ChatGPT plan that includes Codex. It is for original, self-made games only, not commercial ROMs or bypassing protections. Checked on openai.com on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/supply/co-lab/chromatic/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: OpenAI Supply Co. on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-modretro-chromatic-make-game-boy-color-games/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Make%20your%20own%20Game%20Boy%20Color%20game%20with%20Codex%2C%20and%20play%20it%20in%20your%20browser%20even%20without%20the%20%24200%20handheld&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fcodex-modretro-chromatic-make-game-boy-color-games%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want to try the ModRetro Chromatic plugin in the Codex desktop app on a small original game idea I will describe. Set up the plugin only if I already have Codex installed, preview the game in the browser emulator, and do not buy the $200 handheld, write a cartridge, or publish the ROM unless I approve it." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="codex-revives-bricked-cheap-smartwatch-custom-firmware" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-revives-bricked-cheap-smartwatch-custom-firmware/" class="hover:text-brand-600">He bricked a cheap smartwatch with Codex, then had Codex bring it back with his own firmware and iPhone alerts</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Japanese developer Taketo Fujimaki had a cheap smartwatch he&#039;d been given sitting in a drawer. His first try at having Codex hack it to show bot messages turned it into a paperweight. On his second try, he says Codex analyzed its Bluetooth traffic and its firmware and SDK, adjusted the screen driver, flashed custom firmware, hooked it into iPhone notifications, linked it with AI assistants and added an animated character that reacts to alerts. His video of the working watch drew over 100,000 views.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It shows coding agents can now take on hardware hacking that used to need a specialist, and also that it can go wrong: his first attempt bricked the device.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Tinkerers and makers with old gadgets they own and can afford to break, who want a hands-on agent project.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">A personal project shared on X on November 9, 2026, not an official OpenAI feature. Codex needs a ChatGPT plan that includes Codex. Only modify devices you own; flashing firmware can permanently break them and void warranties. Checked on X on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/tf_makimaki/status/2119758126740377972" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @tf_makimaki on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-revives-bricked-cheap-smartwatch-custom-firmware/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=He%20bricked%20a%20cheap%20smartwatch%20with%20Codex%2C%20then%20had%20Codex%20bring%20it%20back%20with%20his%20own%20firmware%20and%20iPhone%20alerts&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fcodex-revives-bricked-cheap-smartwatch-custom-firmware%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
