                                <article id="openai-control-room-stops-model-jobs-35-seconds" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-control-room-stops-model-jobs-35-seconds/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI built a kill switch for its own research models: Control Room stops a job&#039;s output within 35 seconds</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI described Control Room, a central service that every research inference job has to register with. Each job gets an ID tied to an approved safety case, and the inference engines ask Control Room for permission before answering each request. When a person or a misalignment monitor decides to stop a job, further model output is cut off within 35 seconds. The system fails closed: if Control Room itself goes down, all research inference is denied until it is back.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a concrete look at how a frontier lab plans to stop long-running agent jobs that misbehave, and a useful pattern for anyone running fleets of agents: put the off switch in the layer every call has to pass through, not in the agent&#039;s own code.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People who run many AI agents or long agent jobs, platform and security engineers, and anyone following AI safety practice.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to: OpenAI&#039;s internal research infrastructure, not ChatGPT or the API (OpenAI says its public serving stack already has central takedown). Fail-closed mode is live for frontier research workloads and rolling out to the rest over the next few days. Checked on openai.com on November 9-10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/control-room/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-control-room-stops-model-jobs-35-seconds/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%20built%20a%20kill%20switch%20for%20its%20own%20research%20models%3A%20Control%20Room%20stops%20a%20job%27s%20output%20within%2035%20seconds&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fopenai-control-room-stops-model-jobs-35-seconds%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="fable-5-2-github-copilot-pro-plus-vs-code-xcode" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/fable-5-2-github-copilot-pro-plus-vs-code-xcode/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude Fable 5.2 is now in GitHub Copilot, from VS Code to Xcode, but Business admins have to switch it on</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">GitHub made Anthropic&#039;s Claude Fable 5.2 generally available in GitHub Copilot for complex, multistep coding work across large codebases. GitHub says that in early testing it solved more tasks than Fable 5.1 while using fewer steps and tool calls. You can choose it in the model picker in VS Code, Visual Studio, Copilot CLI, the Copilot coding agent, the Copilot app, github.com, GitHub Mobile, JetBrains IDEs, Xcode and Eclipse. Fable 5.2 needs data retention by default so Anthropic can run its safety classifiers; retained data isn&#039;t used for training.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If your team already lives in Copilot, you can hand the hardest refactors and migrations to Fable 5.2 without a separate Anthropic account, and keep cheaper models for everyday edits.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">GitHub Copilot Pro+, Max, Business and Enterprise users, and the admins who manage Copilot model policies.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Generally available from November 9, 2026 on Copilot Pro+, Max, Business and Enterprise, rolling out gradually. Billed at provider list pricing under usage-based billing. On Business and Enterprise the Claude Fable 5.2 policy is off by default and an admin must enable it; zero-data-retention access is available only to eligible enterprises through the end of 2026. Not listed for Copilot Free or Pro. Checked on github.blog on November 10, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-09-claude-fable-5-2-in-github-copilot/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GitHub on github.blog ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/fable-5-2-github-copilot-pro-plus-vs-code-xcode/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20Fable%205.2%20is%20now%20in%20GitHub%20Copilot%2C%20from%20VS%20Code%20to%20Xcode%2C%20but%20Business%20admins%20have%20to%20switch%20it%20on&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Ffable-5-2-github-copilot-pro-plus-vs-code-xcode%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Plan, then carry out, this migration across the repo: [describe it]. First list every file you expect to touch and the risks. Wait for my OK, then make the changes in small commits, run the tests after each one, and give me a summary of what changed and anything you weren&#039;t sure about." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
