                                <article id="antigravity-knowledge-work-layout-no-terminal" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-knowledge-work-layout-no-terminal/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Not a coder? Google Antigravity now has a Knowledge Work layout with no terminal or git in sight</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google Antigravity added a Knowledge Work interface layout tuned for research, writing and artifacts. It keeps the same agent harness, plugins and MCP tools as the developer layout, but removes the terminal panes and git clutter that put non-engineers off. You switch layouts from the General tab in Settings, so the same app can look like an IDE for one person and a research workspace for another.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> The agent that writes code in Antigravity can now be handed to a researcher, writer or analyst without a wall of developer tooling in the way, which makes it easier to share one setup across a whole team.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Researchers, writers, analysts, PMs and anyone who wants an AI agent workspace but doesn&#039;t write code.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Announced November 9, 2026 by the official Google Antigravity account; available in Antigravity under Settings &gt; General. Antigravity&#039;s usual plans and quotas apply; the post doesn&#039;t mention extra cost.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/antigravity/status/2119913586109579283" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @antigravity on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-knowledge-work-layout-no-terminal/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Not%20a%20coder%3F%20Google%20Antigravity%20now%20has%20a%20Knowledge%20Work%20layout%20with%20no%20terminal%20or%20git%20in%20sight&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fantigravity-knowledge-work-layout-no-terminal%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
