                                <article id="zapier-automationbench-fable-5-2-2-3x-fable-5-1" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/zapier-automationbench-fable-5-2-2-3x-fable-5-1/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Zapier ran Fable 5.2 on real business workflows: 2.3x better than 5.1, but nearly 4x the cost of Opus per task</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Zapier CEO Wade Foster shared how Claude Fable 5.2 did on Zapier&#039;s AutomationBench, a test of real business automations. At max effort it scored 51.4%, versus 44.6% for Sonnet 5.5, 40.0% for Opus 5.5 and 22.4% for Fable 5.1. Even at low effort it scored 39.7%, about the same as Opus 5.5 at max, for a similar cost per task. The biggest gains were in finance, sales and HR workflows, and it averaged about 97 tool calls per task because it checks its work more.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a rare outside number on cost per task, not just accuracy: Foster puts Fable 5.2 at max effort at about $4.64 per task against $1.28 for Opus 5.5 and $1.00 for Sonnet 5.5, so the smart move is to route only the hard workflows to Fable.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Ops, finance, sales and HR teams automating work with AI, and anyone deciding which Claude model to put behind their agents.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Zapier&#039;s own benchmark figures, posted by its CEO on November 9, 2026; Foster says Fable 5.2 is live on Zapier now. Fable 5.2 API pricing is $8/$40 per million input/output tokens per Anthropic.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/wadefoster/status/2119874501747814409" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @wadefoster on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/zapier-automationbench-fable-5-2-2-3x-fable-5-1/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
