                                <article id="apple-watch-wear-os-call-your-agent-from-wrist" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/apple-watch-wear-os-call-your-agent-from-wrist/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Call your AI agent from your wrist: Muse is now on Apple Watch and Wear OS</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta brought its Muse personal agent to Apple Watch and Wear OS. From the watch you can type a text to Muse, dictate a message, or start a voice call and talk to it, and a watch-face complication keeps it one tap away. It&#039;s a companion to the phone app, so the errands Muse already handles, like reservations, reminders and email, can start from your wrist while your phone stays in your bag.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Quick asks (&#039;remind me&#039;, &#039;book that&#039;, &#039;what&#039;s next today&#039;) are where a wrist agent beats pulling out a phone. Muse still asks before it sends or spends, so keep approvals on.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse users with an Apple Watch or Wear OS watch who want hands-free errands.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free companion app; needs Muse set up on your phone (iOS 18+ with watchOS 9+, or Android 10+ with the Wear OS app from Google Play), per The Gadgeteer. Muse is 18+ and only in some countries, including the US, Canada, Japan and Singapore.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Muse/status/2119919277692383330" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Muse on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/apple-watch-wear-os-call-your-agent-from-wrist/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Call%20your%20AI%20agent%20from%20your%20wrist%3A%20Muse%20is%20now%20on%20Apple%20Watch%20and%20Wear%20OS&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fapple-watch-wear-os-call-your-agent-from-wrist%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
