                                <article id="fable-5-2-this-codebase-is-yours-ownership-prompt" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="prompts">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Prompt packs</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-09" class="text-slate-400">Nov 9, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/fable-5-2-this-codebase-is-yours-ownership-prompt/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One sentence makes Claude Fable 5.2 clean up duplicate code in about half of tries, up from under 1 in 10</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic&#039;s new prompting guide for Claude Fable 5.2 says the model pays close attention to who owns the code. With no ownership line, or when the code is framed as someone else&#039;s, it tends to add on top of what&#039;s there and only report nearby problems. Adding one sentence saying the codebase is the model&#039;s own made it merge repeated code in about half of Anthropic&#039;s small test tasks, versus under a tenth without it. The catch: about 1.5x the output tokens, extra unrequested changes such as tests and docs, and summaries that skip small edits.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s an official, measured switch between &#039;touch as little as possible&#039; and &#039;leave it better than you found it&#039;, and it tells you when to use each.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers using Fable 5.2 in Claude Code, Cursor or the API, especially for refactors and cleanup.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Works wherever you can set a system prompt or project instructions for Claude Fable 5.2 (Claude Code, the Claude API and tools that use it). Anthropic says to add it in new conversations, not mid-session. Guide published November 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/prompting-claude-fable-5-2" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on platform.claude.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/fable-5-2-this-codebase-is-yours-ownership-prompt/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=One%20sentence%20makes%20Claude%20Fable%205.2%20clean%20up%20duplicate%20code%20in%20about%20half%20of%20tries%2C%20up%20from%20under%201%20in%2010&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Ffable-5-2-this-codebase-is-yours-ownership-prompt%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="This codebase is yours: what it&#039;s for and how it&#039;s built are your call, and you&#039;ll keep building on it." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="simular-box-free-cloud-linux-desktop-for-your-agent" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-08" class="text-slate-400">Nov 8, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/simular-box-free-cloud-linux-desktop-for-your-agent/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Give your AI its own free computer: Simular&#039;s box is a cloud Linux desktop that Claude Code, Codex and Cursor can drive</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">box, from Simular, is a cloud Ubuntu desktop with Chrome and a terminal that your AI uses through a remote MCP server. Add it to Claude, ChatGPT, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor or VS Code and the agent can open a browser, click, type, read the screen and run commands on its own machine instead of yours. Simular says the box itself is free: one per account, sleeping when idle and waking when your AI connects, with model calls inside it drawing on your account&#039;s daily credits. Users sharing the deal on X report 1,000 free credits a day and roughly 4 CPUs, 8 GB RAM and 40 GB of disk.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Letting an agent loose on your own laptop is how files get deleted. A separate, free cloud desktop keeps browser automation and risky commands off your machine, and you can watch it live and take over.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone using Claude Code, Codex, Cursor or ChatGPT who wants their agent to browse, test websites or run commands without touching their own computer.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free: one cloud Linux desktop per Simular account, no card mentioned on the official page. Model calls inside the box use daily credits; Simular&#039;s page doesn&#039;t list the exact allowance (users report 1,000 a day) or the cost per action, and says to add credits or pick a plan on its Billing page when they run out. Your agent&#039;s own usage (Claude, Codex, Cursor) is still billed by that service. Checked on box.simular.ai on November 9, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://box.simular.ai/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Simular on box.simular.ai ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/simular-box-free-cloud-linux-desktop-for-your-agent/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Give%20your%20AI%20its%20own%20free%20computer%3A%20Simular%27s%20box%20is%20a%20cloud%20Linux%20desktop%20that%20Claude%20Code%2C%20Codex%20and%20Cursor%20can%20drive&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fsimular-box-free-cloud-linux-desktop-for-your-agent%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
