                                <article id="claude-s-agents-now-dream-overnight-they-re-read-their-own-s" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/claude-s-agents-now-dream-overnight-they-re-read-their-own-s/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude&#039;s agents now &quot;dream&quot; overnight: they re-read their own sessions and fix bad memories</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic&#039;s November 6 engineering post explains dreaming: a background pass that reviews agent session transcripts and memory notes while the agent is idle, then reorganizes what future sessions will read. Dreaming can correct wrong notes against the original transcript, build wiki-style memory maps, promote high-signal rules into the context that loads at session start, and fill gaps a single session left behind. Anthropic also shipped dreaming as a research preview in Claude Managed Agents, where a dream reads a memory store plus past sessions and writes a separate cleaned store you can review before using. In one Pokémon run, fixing a single wrong landmark note with dreaming changed whether Claude escaped Mt. Moon.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Long-running agents fail when they trust stale or wrong notes. Dreaming is a concrete way to clean that memory offline instead of re-explaining the project every morning.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Teams building Claude Managed Agents, Claude Code power users who keep CLAUDE.md or auto-memory files, and anyone designing multi-session agent harnesses.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Engineering write-up published November 6, 2026 on anthropic.com. Dreaming for Managed Agents is a research preview on the Claude Platform; developers request access. Cookbook and docs cover building your own dream workflow. Checked on Anthropic&#039;s post and Managed Agents dreams docs on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/components-of-agent-memory" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/claude-s-agents-now-dream-overnight-they-re-read-their-own-s/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%27s%20agents%20now%20%22dream%22%20overnight%3A%20they%20re-read%20their%20own%20sessions%20and%20fix%20bad%20memories&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fclaude-s-agents-now-dream-overnight-they-re-read-their-own-s%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want to audit my agent’s memory before reusing it. Compare the notes and session transcripts I provide, flag unsupported claims, and propose a separate corrected memory draft. Preserve evidence links and show changes for my review; do not overwrite the original notes." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
