                                <article id="can-ai-read-a-messy-wet-lab-gel-openai-s-biobasicsbench-says" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="research">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Research</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/can-ai-read-a-messy-wet-lab-gel-openai-s-biobasicsbench-says/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Can AI read a messy wet-lab gel? OpenAI&#039;s BioBasicsBench says GPT-6 Astra gets 66.7%</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI and enzyme-design biotech Ligo published BioBasicsBench on November 6, 2026: 100 routine wet-lab tasks built from real experiment evidence such as gel images, colony plates, microscopy stacks, sequencing files, instrument exports and bench videos. Agents must interpret raw data, spot errors and say when the evidence cannot support a conclusion, graded against expert rubrics. At the shared xhigh reasoning setting, GPT-6 Astra earned a mean 66.7% of available credit versus 43.8% for GPT-5.6 Sol across seven models and 18,500 graded attempts. OpenAI also publishes failure modes where Astra still overcounts colonies, overrides controls with assumptions, or drops contradictory observations.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Biology agents are only useful if they can read the same messy lab outputs scientists see every day. This benchmark shows progress and where models still invent answers the data does not support.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Wet-lab scientists, biotech teams evaluating lab agents, and builders comparing GPT-6 Astra to older OpenAI models on multimodal science work.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Research announcement and scores published by OpenAI on November 6, 2026. Tasks come from Ligo experiments with internal, external PhD and final reviews. No public task dump is described in the post. Checked on openai.com on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/measuring-how-ai-agents-handle-wet-lab-science/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/can-ai-read-a-messy-wet-lab-gel-openai-s-biobasicsbench-says/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Can%20AI%20read%20a%20messy%20wet-lab%20gel%3F%20OpenAI%27s%20BioBasicsBench%20says%20GPT-6%20Astra%20gets%2066.7%25&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fcan-ai-read-a-messy-wet-lab-gel-openai-s-biobasicsbench-says%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want to understand the BioBasicsBench report, not treat a benchmark score as lab validation. Summarize its task types, scoring method and reported limitations from the official article. Separate observations from assumptions and explain where human expert review remains necessary." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="tell-muse-build-me-a-wedding-planner-and-it-becomes-a-live-s" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/tell-muse-build-me-a-wedding-planner-and-it-becomes-a-live-s/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Tell Muse &quot;build me a wedding planner&quot; and it becomes a live Space you can pin</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta launched Spaces inside the Muse app on November 6, 2026. You describe an idea in chat—a holiday gift tracker, school dashboard, trip planner, client hub, trivia game—and Muse builds a persistent, interactive mini-app you can pin to the sidebar or main tabs, hide, or schedule for weekdays versus weekends. Connected apps keep Spaces updated in the background with new dates, prices and messages, and you can check items off, add notes and refine the layout with follow-up prompts. Meta says Spaces are available everywhere Muse is available, with sharing still on the roadmap.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> One-off Muse chats die when you close the thread. A Space turns the same request into a reusable dashboard that stays current without rebuilding it every week.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse users who juggle planning, shopping, school calendars, freelancing or side projects and want a custom view instead of another spreadsheet.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Starting November 6, 2026, Spaces are available everywhere Muse is available per Meta&#039;s newsroom post. Sharing Spaces with others is listed as coming later. Checked on about.fb.com on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://about.fb.com/news/2026/11/introducing-spaces-customize-muse-app/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Meta on about.fb.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/tell-muse-build-me-a-wedding-planner-and-it-becomes-a-live-s/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Tell%20Muse%20%22build%20me%20a%20wedding%20planner%22%20and%20it%20becomes%20a%20live%20Space%20you%20can%20pin&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Ftell-muse-build-me-a-wedding-planner-and-it-becomes-a-live-s%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want a reusable trip-planning Space with an itinerary, a budget checklist and a notes area. Ask me for the missing dates and preferences before filling it in. Explain which connected apps would be needed for updates, and do not book, purchase or share anything." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="muse-forgets-2-4x-less-and-finishes-stuck-tasks-67-more-acti" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/muse-forgets-2-4x-less-and-finishes-stuck-tasks-67-more-acti/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Muse forgets 2.4x less and finishes stuck tasks 67% more: Active Memory and Active Focus land for everyone</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta is rolling specialized models trained with Muse Wonder into Muse and Meta AI. Active Memory teaches the models to separate temporary details from lasting ones, reason across time, and pull earlier context when it becomes relevant again—Meta reports a 2.4x reduction in forgetting critical goal information and Active Memory eval accuracy rising from 76% to 90%. Active Focus trains recovery from real-world bottlenecks so Muse keeps working toward a goal when something blocks it; Meta reports a 67% improvement completing everyday tasks with unexpected issues. Meta also says Personal Superintelligence Index scores moved from 38% to 47% on the new Muse models. These are Meta-reported evals, not an independent audit.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> The usual Muse complaint is repeating yourself and watching a task die when a booking page changes. Active Memory and Active Focus target those two failure modes without waiting for a full Muse Wonder rollout.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone already using Muse or Meta AI for multi-step personal or work tasks who keeps hitting forgotten context or abandoned goals.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rolling out starting November 6, 2026 to Muse and Meta AI users, per Meta AI Research and posts from AI at Meta, Mark Zuckerberg and Alexandr Wang. Numbers are Meta&#039;s own evals. Checked on research.meta.ai on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://research.meta.ai/blog/specialized-models-for-muse-and-metaai" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Meta AI Research on research.meta.ai ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/muse-forgets-2-4x-less-and-finishes-stuck-tasks-67-more-acti/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Muse%20forgets%202.4x%20less%20and%20finishes%20stuck%20tasks%2067%25%20more%3A%20Active%20Memory%20and%20Active%20Focus%20land%20for%20everyone&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fmuse-forgets-2-4x-less-and-finishes-stuck-tasks-67-more-acti%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want to check whether you retain my project’s constraints and recover when a task is blocked. First restate the goals and constraints I have actually supplied. If information is missing, ask rather than invent it. When blocked, explain the obstacle and propose a safe next step for my approval." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="talk-to-your-cursor-agent-out-loud-realtime-voice-chat-is-li" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="cursor" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-zinc-200 text-zinc-800 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-zinc-200">Cursor</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/talk-to-your-cursor-agent-out-loud-realtime-voice-chat-is-li/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Talk to your Cursor agent out loud: realtime voice chat is live on desktop, web and iOS</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Cursor&#039;s November 6, 2026 changelog adds Voice Chat with Agents: a two-way realtime call where you describe a change, ask what an agent is doing, and hear short progress notes while it works. It runs in the Agents Window, the IDE, on web and in Cursor for iOS. Start a call with the waveform button when the agent is idle and the chat input is empty; on iOS you can also say &quot;Hey Siri, call Cursor&quot; and mute or hang up from a Lock Screen Live Activity. Voice chat is powered by Grok Voice with selectable voices, and Privacy Mode keeps zero data retention. It is separate from dictation (the older Voice Mode that only turns speech into text).</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Hands-free steering matters when you are reviewing a diff on a walk or cannot type. You get spoken status instead of reading a wall of agent logs.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Cursor users on desktop, web or iOS who want to steer coding agents by voice instead of only typing.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Shipped in the Cursor changelog dated November 6, 2026. Update Cursor to get the waveform Start voice chat control. Privacy Mode supported with zero data retention for voice. Checked on cursor.com/changelog/voice-chat on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://cursor.com/changelog/voice-chat" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Cursor on cursor.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/cursor/talk-to-your-cursor-agent-out-loud-realtime-voice-chat-is-li/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Talk%20to%20your%20Cursor%20agent%20out%20loud%3A%20realtime%20voice%20chat%20is%20live%20on%20desktop%2C%20web%20and%20iOS&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fcursor%2Ftalk-to-your-cursor-agent-out-loud-realtime-voice-chat-is-li%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want to review this change by voice before editing anything. Explain the relevant diff, tell me which files would need changes, and give short progress updates. Ask for approval before modifying files or running commands that change project state." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="200-free-sandbox-compute-for-your-coding-agents-daytona-no-c" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/200-free-sandbox-compute-for-your-coding-agents-daytona-no-c/" class="hover:text-brand-600">$200 free sandbox compute for your coding agents: Daytona, no card</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Daytona runs instant sandboxes for AI coding agents and bills per second for reserved vCPU, memory and disk. Its pricing page advertises $200 in free compute included and a free trial with no credit card required. Docs confirm a free credit balance in the organization wallet that is consumed before paid credits, and state free credits are not available for GPU sandboxes. After free credits run out, standard pay-as-you-go rates apply (for example about $0.0504 per vCPU-hour and $0.0162 per GiB-hour of memory on the public pricing table). Startups can separately apply for up to $50k in credits.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Agent runs that need a clean Linux box eat local RAM and leave junk behind. Two hundred dollars of hosted sandbox time lets you try Claude Code, Codex or similar agents in isolation before you buy capacity.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and startups who want isolated sandboxes for coding agents without putting a card down for the first experiments.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Who qualifies: new Daytona sign-ups on the free trial; no credit card required per the pricing page. Amount: $200 free compute credits in the wallet; not usable for GPU sandboxes. Deadline: none stated on the public pricing or billing docs. Afterwards: pay-as-you-go per second. Checked on daytona.io/pricing and daytona.io/docs/en/billing on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.daytona.io/pricing" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Daytona on www.daytona.io ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/200-free-sandbox-compute-for-your-coding-agents-daytona-no-c/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=%24200%20free%20sandbox%20compute%20for%20your%20coding%20agents%3A%20Daytona%2C%20no%20card&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2F200-free-sandbox-compute-for-your-coding-agents-daytona-no-c%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want to evaluate an isolated sandbox for a small coding task. Help me estimate the resources I need from Daytona’s current pricing and identify which resources keep accruing charges. Explain the free-credit restrictions and a cleanup checklist; do not create resources or enable paid usage." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="deepmind-s-ai-agents-found-two-new-cracks-in-obsolete-1024-b" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/deepmind-s-ai-agents-found-two-new-cracks-in-obsolete-1024-b/" class="hover:text-brand-600">DeepMind&#039;s AI agents found two new cracks in obsolete 1024-bit RSA — 2048-bit stays safe</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">On November 6, 2026 Google DeepMind said human-guided AI agents uncovered two major weaknesses in legacy 1024-bit RSA cryptosystems while stress-testing encryption. Per VP Science Pushmeet Kohli&#039;s write-up, one result shows when an attacker controls roughly half or more of a padded signature block, padding adds no forgery protection, with a sandboxed reproduction on an already-solved 1024-bit benchmark key using about 3.5× less CPU time than prior work; a related algorithm improves short-fingerprint forgery estimates by roughly 1,600× for 1024-bit keys. The second result is a batch-factoring algorithm that cuts the average cost of factoring each additional 1024-bit key by about 30× versus previous batch methods. DeepMind stresses modern 2048-bit and larger RSA remain secure and that the work used retired 1024-bit systems as a safe proving ground.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Cryptographic hardness assumptions used to move slowly. AI-assisted cryptanalysis can probe them faster, so defenders need to keep migrating off obsolete key sizes and keep stress-testing standards.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Security engineers, cryptography teams and anyone still running or depending on 1024-bit RSA anywhere in a stack.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies as research disclosure from Google DeepMind on November 6, 2026. Affects obsolete 1024-bit RSA only; DeepMind states modern 2048-bit+ deployments remain secure. Technical papers linked from the announcement. Checked against DeepMind&#039;s X post and Kohli&#039;s article text on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/GoogleDeepMind/status/2118755418675765656" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google DeepMind on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/deepmind-s-ai-agents-found-two-new-cracks-in-obsolete-1024-b/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=DeepMind%27s%20AI%20agents%20found%20two%20new%20cracks%20in%20obsolete%201024-bit%20RSA%20%E2%80%94%202048-bit%20stays%20safe&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fdeepmind-s-ai-agents-found-two-new-cracks-in-obsolete-1024-b%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want a defensive reading of these RSA research papers. Summarize the assumptions, affected legacy key sizes and limitations, and distinguish signature-forgery work from batch factoring. Give me an inventory checklist for obsolete keys without producing exploit instructions or claiming modern RSA is broken." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="free-openfoam-cfd-agent-describe-a-flow-in-plain-english-rey" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/free-openfoam-cfd-agent-describe-a-flow-in-plain-english-rey/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Free OpenFOAM CFD agent: describe a flow in plain English, Reynolds returns the case and plots</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Standard Physics&#039; Reynolds is an agentic CFD tool that takes a plain-language flow description, writes and meshes an OpenFOAM case, solves it, and returns figures, numbers and a rerunnable case. The open-source OpenReynolds package is MIT-licensed on GitHub and installable with pip install openreynolds, so experts can inspect and re-run the ordinary OpenFOAM case locally or on their own servers. Hosted workspaces are free for individual engineers with a verified work email and no card, per the Reynolds product page. Companion product Archimedes uses the same simulation stack to search thousands of physical designs; Reynolds is the piece you can run yourself.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Classical CFD toolchains take weeks to learn. A free agent that emits real OpenFOAM cases lets engineers test ideas in hours without trusting a black-box surrogate.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Mechanical, aero and thermal engineers who need a first OpenFOAM run, plus researchers who want an open agentic CFD harness.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Who qualifies: individual engineers with a verified work email for the free hosted tier; no card. OpenReynolds is MIT open source for local or self-hosted use. Deadline: none stated. Afterwards: contact Standard Physics for pilots or paid capacity. Checked on standardphysics.com/reynolds on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://standardphysics.com/reynolds" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Standard Physics on standardphysics.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/free-openfoam-cfd-agent-describe-a-flow-in-plain-english-rey/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Free%20OpenFOAM%20CFD%20agent%3A%20describe%20a%20flow%20in%20plain%20English%2C%20Reynolds%20returns%20the%20case%20and%20plots&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Ffree-openfoam-cfd-agent-describe-a-flow-in-plain-english-rey%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want to scope a CFD study before running it. Ask me about the geometry, fluid, boundary conditions and quantities of interest. Propose a Reynolds/OpenFOAM workflow with assumptions, convergence checks and a rerunnable-case review. Do not treat a simulated result as validated physical performance." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="1-000-free-web-search-credits-a-month-for-your-agents-tavily" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
