                                <article id="1-251-physical-designs-in-12-hours-archimedes-agents-rewrite" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/1-251-physical-designs-in-12-hours-archimedes-agents-rewrite/" class="hover:text-brand-600">1,251 physical designs in 12 hours: Archimedes agents rewrite hardware and re-check what fails</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Archimedes from Standard Physics runs swarms of AI agents that write physical designs as code, test each one in a real physics simulator (via Reynolds / OpenFOAM), and keep improving the best designs. One published run explored 1,251 propeller designs in 12 hours across six agent teams on 12 cloud machines and kept a dual-medium propeller that reached about 90% of specialist performance in both air and water. Other case studies on the site include a data-hall cooling redesign claiming about $227k yearly savings, a turbine blade with 25.5% less loss versus a benchmark in 2D, and a low-spill mug. Archimedes re-tests leading designs on finer simulations and labels results that only hold when cold or that failed buildability checks.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most &quot;AI for hardware&quot; demos stop at a pretty CAD render. Archimedes publishes the loop that rejects designs when the finer simulation or real constraint check fails.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Hardware, thermal and fluids teams who want agentic design search with verifiable simulation, not prompt-only concepts.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Product from Standard Physics; contact kabir@inviscidai.com for pilots. Case studies and method described on standardphysics.com/archimedes. Open Reynolds solver stack is separately free for individuals with work email. Checked on the Archimedes page on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://standardphysics.com/archimedes" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Standard Physics on standardphysics.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/1-251-physical-designs-in-12-hours-archimedes-agents-rewrite/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=1%2C251%20physical%20designs%20in%2012%20hours%3A%20Archimedes%20agents%20rewrite%20hardware%20and%20re-check%20what%20fails&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2F1-251-physical-designs-in-12-hours-archimedes-agents-rewrite%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
