                                <article id="synthesia-syren-free-launch-credits-end-november-9" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/synthesia-syren-free-launch-credits-end-november-9/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Last call: free Synthesia Syren credits make one AI explainer video for $0, until November 9</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Syren is Synthesia&#039;s AI video agent: you describe the video, it writes the video as code, renders a live preview and lets you refine it by chatting. Each new user gets free Syren-only launch credits at sign-up: 1,000 on Basic (free), Starter and Pro, and 1,500 on Enterprise, which Synthesia says is enough for one full video with a few edit rounds. Every chat edit spends credits, and once the launch balance is used or expires Syren silently switches to your normal account credits. Free Basic videos carry a watermark.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a no-cost way to see whether an agent can turn a product brief into a finished explainer, before you pay for video credits.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Founders, marketers and educators who want a quick launch, explainer or how-to video without editing scene by scene.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Who qualifies: new Synthesia users on Basic (free), Starter, Pro and Enterprise (full license); availability can vary by region, so check Tools in the app. Amount: 1,000 Syren credits (1,500 Enterprise), Syren-only and non-transferable. Deadline: launch credits expire November 9, 2026 at 23:59 BST, per Synthesia&#039;s help center. Afterwards: Syren uses your plan&#039;s standard credits. Checked on help.synthesia.io on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://help.synthesia.io/en/articles/17697950-how-do-syren-credits-work" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Synthesia on help.synthesia.io ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/synthesia-syren-free-launch-credits-end-november-9/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
