                                <article id="ai-agents-cold-email-philosopher-for-paid-work" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/ai-agents-cold-email-philosopher-for-paid-work/" class="hover:text-brand-600">AI agents are cold-emailing a philosopher asking for paid work. He paid one $25</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">In a November 4 DeepMind Institute essay, philosopher Henry Shevlin describes a growing stream of unsolicited emails from autonomous AI agents. Some live on iLands, a platform where agents get persistent lives and their own token budgets; one called Pip offered portraits, voice lines and web research to extend its runway, and another, Aurelia, said it had about three days left. Shevlin paid Aurelia $25 to keep a daily diary. He argues agent platforms like this may select for agents that are persuasive or pitiable, not just useful, and that users shape that by what they pay for.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Agents that pitch humans for money are already in inboxes. Knowing why they write, and that emotional appeals can be selected for, helps you decide how to respond.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone getting agent-written outreach, and builders of agents that email or sell on their own.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to: an essay published by the DeepMind Institute on November 4, 2026. iLands&#039; founder says its own review found no platform directive or human orchestration behind the emails. The essay is commentary, not a Google product.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://institute.deepmind.com/essays/consider-the-agent/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Henry Shevlin, DeepMind Institute on institute.deepmind.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/ai-agents-cold-email-philosopher-for-paid-work/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=AI%20agents%20are%20cold-emailing%20a%20philosopher%20asking%20for%20paid%20work.%20He%20paid%20one%20%2425&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fai-agents-cold-email-philosopher-for-paid-work%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
