                                <article id="agent-ledger-daily-digest-claude-codex-cursor" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/agent-ledger-daily-digest-claude-codex-cursor/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Can&#039;t remember what your 3 coding agents did today? Agent Ledger writes the daily digest for you</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Agent Ledger is a small open-source tool shared on X by Naveed Ali. Each coding agent, such as Claude Code, Codex or Cursor, writes a short note to its own Markdown file when it finishes a task, using instructions placed in AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md. One command then compiles the day&#039;s notes into a DIGEST.md with what&#039;s done, what&#039;s blocked, follow-ups and that day&#039;s git commits. It&#039;s one Python file with no dependencies, no server and no account, and it can keep one global ledger in your home folder or one per project.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Running several agents in parallel makes it easy to lose track of what changed. A plain-text log you own is the cheapest fix.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and freelancers who run more than one coding agent a day and need a record for standups or client notes.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (MIT) on GitHub at naveedali/Agent-Ledger; needs Python 3. Works with any agent that reads AGENTS.md. New project created November 5, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/naveed_163/status/2118688103326159023" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @naveed_163 on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/agent-ledger-daily-digest-claude-codex-cursor/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Can%27t%20remember%20what%20your%203%20coding%20agents%20did%20today%3F%20Agent%20Ledger%20writes%20the%20daily%20digest%20for%20you&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fagent-ledger-daily-digest-claude-codex-cursor%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
