    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-trustmrr-522-ai-agent-startups-54-percent-zero/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude Code read all 12,244 startups on TrustMRR in 8 minutes: 54% of AI agent startups made $0 last month</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">An X user gave Claude Code one job: read every page of TrustMRR, a directory that shows startup revenue pulled from Stripe rather than screenshots. He says it got through all 123 pages in 8 minutes and found 522 of 12,244 startups sell an AI agent, 284 of them (54%) made $0 in the last 30 days, and just 15 made over $10,000, taking 84% of the money. Nine of the 15 sell more customers: sales outreach, ads, SEO or social posts. Four are solo founders who started this year, including one with 189 X followers reporting about $70,000 last month.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a quick reality check before you build yet another agent: revenue clusters around jobs businesses already pay for. It also shows a reusable trick, having an agent read a whole public directory and summarize it.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Indie hackers and founders deciding what agent product to build, and anyone who wants to try large-scale web research with Claude Code.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">A community analysis using Claude Code (included with Claude Pro, Max and Ultra plans) on TrustMRR&#039;s public listings. The figures are the author&#039;s own and were not checked against TrustMRR. Posted on X on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
