                                <article id="bot-alex-finn-6-always-on-jobs" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-07" class="text-slate-400">Nov 7, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-alex-finn-6-always-on-jobs/" class="hover:text-brand-600">6 jobs one creator handed to Grok Bot, from a 15-minute AI news watch to a side business he says runs itself</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Creator Alex Finn shared six things his Grok Bot does around the clock and invited people to copy them. It checks AI companies&#039; X accounts every 15 minutes and alerts him to big news, built and maintains a site he says earns revenue with no effort from him, clicks through the two apps he&#039;s building to find bugs and open pull requests for his review, repurposes his social posts into newsletter material, answers questions in his community, and reads PostHog retention data to flag at-risk subscribers and draft outreach that waits for his OK. He also says other agents can do the same jobs; he just finds Grok Bot easier.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a concrete list of always-on jobs you can copy, and most keep a human approval step before anything ships or gets sent.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Solo founders, creators and small teams who want a 24/7 agent watching news, apps or customers for them.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot is included in existing SuperGrok and Cursor Pro, Pro+, Ultra and Teams plans; new customers get it through The X Subscription from the $30/month Premium tier. The jobs use the X plugin, a browser and connectors you set up yourself. The revenue claim is the author&#039;s own. Posted on X on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/AlexFinn/status/2118882927610360204" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @AlexFinn on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-alex-finn-6-always-on-jobs/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
