        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-06" class="text-slate-400">Nov 6, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/living-brain-one-memory-across-chatgpt-cursor/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Stop re-explaining the project: Living Brain keeps one memory across ChatGPT, Claude and Cursor</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Living Brain stores project knowledge as pages outside any single model, then plugs into ChatGPT, Claude, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and terminal agents through MCP or a CLI. Capture a decision in Cursor, then ask about it later in ChatGPT or Claude without pasting the thread again. The product&#039;s own benchmarks claim 92.2% judged accuracy on LoCoMo across 1,540 questions and about 22.6x fewer tokens per question versus a 116K full-context baseline; treat those as vendor figures. Tools can list brains, search pages, read sources, show a graph and save new notes.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Every tool switch usually burns tokens re-teaching the same project. One brain that each client can search cuts that tax.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People who hop between ChatGPT, Claude and coding agents on the same long-running project.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Living Brain connects to Claude and ChatGPT with MCP sign-in, to Claude Code, Codex and Cursor with an API key, and to terminal agents via its CLI. Availability and pricing are as stated on livingbrain.com and docs.livingbrain.com; checked November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://livingbrain.com/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Living Brain on livingbrain.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/living-brain-one-memory-across-chatgpt-cursor/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
