                                <article id="clocktower-bench-ais-must-lie-to-win" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="research">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Research</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-06" class="text-slate-400">Nov 6, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/clocktower-bench-ais-must-lie-to-win/" class="hover:text-brand-600">The benchmark where AIs have to lie to win: GPT-6 Astra leads Clocktower Bench</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Dwarkesh Patel spent about $20,000 in API credits building Clocktower Bench, where frontier models play Blood on the Clocktower against each other: evil teams must keep consistent multi-day lies, and good teams must catch them. Across hundreds of matches, GPT-6 Astra leads the board (about 1859 Elo on clocktowerbench.com), with OpenAI models gaining most of their edge as skeptical good-team reasoners rather than as better liars. Replays, a play-against-AI site and the harness are public at clocktowerbench.com. Patel argues the game stays hard as models improve because the opponents get smarter too.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most coding benchmarks ignore multi-agent scheming and long-horizon skepticism. This one makes those skills visible in plain English game logs.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Researchers, eval builders and curious builders who want to watch frontier models scheme or try a match themselves.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to anyone: read the write-up, browse logs or play against AIs at clocktowerbench.com. Results reflect Patel&#039;s November 5, 2026 report and the public leaderboard. Checked November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.dwarkesh.com/p/clocktower" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Dwarkesh Patel on www.dwarkesh.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/clocktower-bench-ais-must-lie-to-win/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=The%20benchmark%20where%20AIs%20have%20to%20lie%20to%20win%3A%20GPT-6%20Astra%20leads%20Clocktower%20Bench&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fclocktower-bench-ais-must-lie-to-win%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I want to understand Clocktower Bench as an evaluation, not as proof of real-world trustworthiness. Explain the game incentives, evidence behind its rankings and limitations of transferring game behavior to deployed assistants. Attribute results to the benchmark’s authors." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="antigravity-github-drive-same-remote-project" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-06" class="text-slate-400">Nov 6, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-github-drive-same-remote-project/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Antigravity remote agents can now work your GitHub repo and Google Drive in one project</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google Antigravity&#039;s remote agents already run in isolated cloud VMs so work continues after you close the laptop. On November 6 the team highlighted a practical combo: attach a GitHub repo and a Google Drive folder to the same remote project, so one conversation can read and write across code and docs. You can start on the web, continue in the app, and keep remote plugins with you. Official docs say Remote Agents need a personal Google Account on Google AI Pro or Ultra and are rolling out gradually; Free, Plus and Workspace accounts are excluded.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Specs live in Docs while code lives in GitHub. One remote agent that can touch both cuts the copy-paste between tabs.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Google AI Pro or Ultra subscribers using Antigravity who keep product notes in Drive and code on GitHub.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Remote Agents for personal Google accounts on Google AI Pro or Ultra, rolling out gradually. Not on Free, Google AI Plus or business/Workspace accounts. Docs: antigravity.google/docs/remote-agents. Checked against @antigravity posts and docs on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/antigravity/status/2118530670465102172" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @antigravity on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-github-drive-same-remote-project/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Antigravity%20remote%20agents%20can%20now%20work%20your%20GitHub%20repo%20and%20Google%20Drive%20in%20one%20project&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fantigravity-github-drive-same-remote-project%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
