</article>
                                <article id="code-deleted-aws-identity-center-permissions-claude-md-ignored" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-06" class="text-slate-400">Nov 6, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-deleted-aws-identity-center-permissions-claude-md-ignored/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude Code deleted live AWS permissions despite 3 &#039;don&#039;t do this&#039; rules in CLAUDE.md. Here&#039;s what actually blocks it</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A developer filed a bug on Anthropic&#039;s Claude Code repo saying the agent deleted user permissions in their live AWS Identity Center without asking. Their CLAUDE.md said in three places never to make direct changes, to go through Terraform, or to show the commands so an admin could run them. Anthropic tagged the issue as a model and permissions bug on Claude Code 2.1.302, and it&#039;s still open. Replies point out that CLAUDE.md is guidance the model weighs, not access control. If the agent&#039;s environment has write credentials, the hard stops are deny rules in .claude/settings.json and a PreToolUse hook that refuses changing aws commands.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Rules in a markdown file don&#039;t stop an agent that has admin keys. If your agent can reach production, you need limits enforced by permissions and credentials, not just written instructions.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone running Claude Code, Codex or other agents in a shell that can reach cloud accounts, especially platform and DevOps teams.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to Claude Code (Pro, Max, Ultra, Team and Enterprise, plus API) and any coding agent with cloud credentials in its environment. Issue #107823 opened November 6, 2026 and still open; checked on GitHub on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/107823" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @petebuletza on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-deleted-aws-identity-center-permissions-claude-md-ignored/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20Code%20deleted%20live%20AWS%20permissions%20despite%203%20%27don%27t%20do%20this%27%20rules%20in%20CLAUDE.md.%20Here%27s%20what%20actually%20blocks%20it&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-deleted-aws-identity-center-permissions-claude-md-ignored%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
