                                <article id="images-2-6-gifs-and-saved-reference-images" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="images">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Images &amp; media</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/images-2-6-gifs-and-saved-reference-images/" class="hover:text-brand-600">ChatGPT can make GIFs now, and you can save a face or product once and call it back with @Name</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI released ChatGPT Images 2.6 on November 4, 2026. ChatGPT can now generate short animated GIFs, not just still images, and you can save a reference photo, such as yourself, a pet, a mascot or a product, give it a name, and pull it into later prompts by typing @ and that name. OpenAI says it&#039;s available in ChatGPT and in Codex across all tiers on web, desktop and mobile, with GIFs still rolling out. You can&#039;t edit a GIF you upload. For developers, two new API models, gpt-image-2.6-flare and gpt-image-2.6-sunburst, are coming with about 50% faster generation, and the image API can return a GIF with 2 to 64 frames.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Keeping the same character or product looking the same across many images used to mean re-uploading and re-explaining it every time. A saved @reference plus GIF output covers stickers, reaction GIFs, product loops and simple social animations in one chat.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Social media managers, small brands, creators making stickers or mascots, and developers adding image or GIF generation to apps.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">OpenAI says Images 2.6 is in ChatGPT and Codex across all tiers on web, desktop and mobile; GIF creation is rolling out gradually, so it may not show up for everyone yet. Uploaded GIFs can&#039;t be edited. The API models gpt-image-2.6-flare and gpt-image-2.6-sunburst are announced as coming to the API. Checked on OpenAI&#039;s X posts, the ChatGPT release notes and the image generation docs on November 5, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2118124944928432327" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on X ↗</a>
