    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-agent-found-948-linux-kernel-root-bugs/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI&#039;s agent pipeline built working exploits and candidate patches for 948 Linux root bugs in one run, for about $1,279 each</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI&#039;s security researchers described an autonomous pipeline that finds, exploits and patches vulnerabilities. In a single run in mid-October 2026 using an upcoming cyber model, it reproduced 1,724 vulnerabilities and produced 948 working local privilege escalation exploits for the Linux kernel, each with a candidate patch, plus 291 proof-of-concepts for information leaks. The whole run cost $1,213,430 in API credits, roughly $1,279 per privilege escalation. OpenAI says the patches are candidates, not merged fixes, and that within 10 days more than 100 of the bugs had been patched or staged by others.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Finding and proving a single kernel root bug has traditionally taken an expert days or weeks. At around $1,279 each, AI-driven bug hunting at scale is now realistic, which raises the stakes for everyone who ships or runs Linux to patch quickly.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Security teams, Linux maintainers, sysadmins and anyone tracking how fast AI is changing vulnerability research.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">This is a research write-up, not a product you can use. The cyber model it used isn&#039;t released yet. The exploits aren&#039;t public, and OpenAI describes coordinating with maintainers on fixes. Checked on OpenAI&#039;s post and its X announcement on November 5, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/a-thousand-fewer-paths-to-root" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-agent-found-948-linux-kernel-root-bugs/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
