                                <article id="alibaba-qz-browser-agent-in-your-own-chrome" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/alibaba-qz-browser-agent-in-your-own-chrome/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Alibaba open-sourced qz, a browser agent that works inside the Chrome you&#039;re already logged into, and Claude Code can hand it tasks</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">qz is an open-source browser agent from Alibaba, released under Apache-2.0. It runs in a side panel of your normal Chrome, using the sites you&#039;re already signed in to, so it doesn&#039;t stop at login walls. You describe a task in one sentence and it clicks through pages, and it can run several tasks at once, each with its own subtasks. Saying &#039;Save this as a Skill&#039; turns a finished workflow into something you can rerun. You can connect DeepSeek, OpenAI, Claude or a local model, or sign in with a ChatGPT account. Claude Code, Codex and Grok Bot can send it web tasks through its CLI or MCP server.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Many browser agents run in a separate cloud browser and fail as soon as a site asks you to log in. Working inside your own browser fixes that, but it also means the agent acts with your real accounts, so it&#039;s worth watching closely.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and power users who want their coding agent to pull data from sites they&#039;re logged into, like dashboards, admin panels or research tools.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (Apache-2.0) on GitHub; you pay your chosen model provider. It&#039;s a young project (version 0.1.6 at the time of checking). Because it uses your live sessions, test it on low-stakes accounts first. Repository checked on November 5, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/thisdudelikesAI/status/2118282483204788570" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @thisdudelikesAI on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/alibaba-qz-browser-agent-in-your-own-chrome/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
