                                <article id="bot-iphone-alarm-webhook-morning-briefing" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-iphone-alarm-webhook-morning-briefing/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Stop your iPhone alarm and Grok Bot starts your morning briefing: an 8-step Shortcuts trick with no schedule and no prompt</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A Grok Bot user shared how he made his Bot react to real life instead of a clock: when he stops his morning alarm, his iPhone sends a webhook to Grok Bot, and a routine starts preparing his daily briefing. He asked his Bot to create a briefing routine with a webhook trigger, then built an iPhone Shortcuts automation on &#039;Alarm is stopped&#039; that POSTs to the routine&#039;s URL with the Bot&#039;s Authorization key. xAI&#039;s docs confirm routines can be triggered by a webhook call, with the key sent as a Bearer token. He suggests the same idea for leaving work, connecting to CarPlay, arriving home or tapping an NFC tag.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Routines that start when something happens fit your day better than fixed schedules: the briefing is ready when you&#039;re actually up, even on a lie-in.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users on iPhone who want hands-free triggers for briefings, commutes or evening routines.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot comes with The X Subscription from the $30/month Premium tier up; legacy SuperGrok and Cursor paid plans also include it. Webhook-triggered routines are in xAI&#039;s Grok Bot docs; the alarm trigger uses Apple&#039;s Shortcuts app (Personal Automation) on iPhone. Checked on the creator&#039;s X post and xAI&#039;s &#039;Skills and routines&#039; docs on November 5, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Michael_Fenech_/status/2118383590446624846" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Michael_Fenech_ on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-iphone-alarm-webhook-morning-briefing/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Stop%20your%20iPhone%20alarm%20and%20Grok%20Bot%20starts%20your%20morning%20briefing%3A%20an%208-step%20Shortcuts%20trick%20with%20no%20schedule%20and%20no%20prompt&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-iphone-alarm-webhook-morning-briefing%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Create a routine called Morning Briefing that runs when its webhook is called. When it runs, send me today&#039;s calendar, my top 3 unread emails that need a reply, and the weather. Then give me the webhook POST URL and key so I can call it from an iPhone Shortcut." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-3d-campus-watch-your-bot-teams-work" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-3d-campus-watch-your-bot-teams-work/" class="hover:text-brand-600">His Grok Bot built him a 3D campus where he walks into each bot team&#039;s room, watches them work and approves it on the spot</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A Grok Bot user says his main Bot, Mika, built him a 3D &#039;campus&#039; for his bot teams after he kept sending it back for changes: a flat page became 3D rooms, then got fitted to his phone. He walks into any team&#039;s room to see what each bot is working on and approves work right there, without opening a chat. A usage battery at the top shows how much of the week&#039;s allowance is gone, and one tap shows which team and which bots burn the most tokens. He says it&#039;s not a built-in feature, and he open-sourced the repo: you give your main Bot the link, approve its connections, and it builds and deploys the page itself. His post drew over 20,000 views.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Once you run several bots, the hard part is seeing who is doing what and what it costs. A per-team view of work and token use is a pattern worth copying, 3D or not.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users running several teams of bots who want one place to supervise them and track weekly usage.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot comes with The X Subscription from the $30/month Premium tier up; legacy SuperGrok and Cursor paid plans also include it. The campus is a community project, not an xAI feature; the creator says it only works with Grok Bot and is built around a main Bot, team leads, groups and routines. Read any repo before letting your Bot deploy it.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Sar_Barshem/status/2118343933218508970" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Sar_Barshem on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-3d-campus-watch-your-bot-teams-work/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=His%20Grok%20Bot%20built%20him%20a%203D%20campus%20where%20he%20walks%20into%20each%20bot%20team%27s%20room%2C%20watches%20them%20work%20and%20approves%20it%20on%20the%20spot&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-3d-campus-watch-your-bot-teams-work%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-paper-trading-agents-10k-each-day-10" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-paper-trading-agents-10k-each-day-10/" class="hover:text-brand-600">He&#039;s paper-testing Grok Bot trading agents with $10K of play money each. By day 10, 3 were retired and the best was up 67% on paper</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A trader on X is posting a daily log of a paper-trading experiment: several Grok Bot trading agents, each given $10,000 of simulated money. On day 10 he reported that his best agent, a SPY/TSLA strategy, had six green days in a row and a paper balance of $16,719.60, up 67.2% since it started on October 26, while agents #6, #7 and #8 had been retired and six were still running. He labels every update &#039;paper trading, NFA&#039; (not financial advice). This is a look at what people are testing, not investment advice: ten days of paper results, after the losers were removed, say very little about how a strategy would do with real money.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Running several agents side by side and retiring the weak ones is a sensible way to test ideas safely. Just remember the survivors will always look good on a short chart.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People curious about agent-run trading strategies who want to experiment without risking money.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot comes with The X Subscription from the $30/month Premium tier up; legacy SuperGrok and Cursor paid plans also include it. Results are self-reported, paper trading only, with no real money involved. Not investment advice.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/adamtrades20/status/2118360144249757856" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @adamtrades20 on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-paper-trading-agents-10k-each-day-10/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=He%27s%20paper-testing%20Grok%20Bot%20trading%20agents%20with%20%2410K%20of%20play%20money%20each.%20By%20day%2010%2C%203%20were%20retired%20and%20the%20best%20was%20up%2067%25%20on%20paper&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-paper-trading-agents-10k-each-day-10%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
