                                <article id="personal-finance-beta-us" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/personal-finance-beta-us/" class="hover:text-brand-600">&quot;Where did my money go this month?&quot; Claude can now answer from your real bank accounts, read-only</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic launched Personal Finance in Claude on November 5, 2026. You sign in to your own bank or card accounts through Plaid, and Claude can then answer plain-English questions from your balances and up to two years of transactions: where the money went, what is left before payday, whether a bill has crept up, or what an APR has cost you this year. It can also build spending charts, a calendar of what&#039;s due or a dashboard you keep adjusting. Access is read-only, so Claude can&#039;t move, manage or invest money, and chats inside the Personal Finance hub aren&#039;t used for training.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It turns an evening of opening banking apps and doing the math into one question, and it can spot double charges or creeping bills you&#039;d otherwise miss.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">US Claude Pro, Max and Ultra subscribers who want a quick read on their spending without a budgeting app.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Beta rolling out this week on the Pro, Max and Ultra plans in the US. Bank connections go through Plaid; read-only. Checked on Anthropic&#039;s announcement on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://claude.com/resources/articles/introducing-personal-finance-in-claude" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on claude.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/personal-finance-beta-us/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=%22Where%20did%20my%20money%20go%20this%20month%3F%22%20Claude%20can%20now%20answer%20from%20your%20real%20bank%20accounts%2C%20read-only&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fpersonal-finance-beta-us%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Open Personal Finance in Claude&#039;s sidebar, connect one bank or card through Plaid, then ask: &quot;Where did my money go this month, and is that more than usual?&quot; Ask which transactions sit behind any number, and unlink the account when you are done." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="omni-1-2-flash-15-second-video" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="video">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Video</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/omni-1-2-flash-15-second-video/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google&#039;s video model now makes 15-second clips you can edit by chatting, and it&#039;s 30% cheaper</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Gemini Omni 1.2 Flash, released November 5, 2026, generates video natively up to 15 seconds long (up from 10), with the length set in one-second steps from 3 to 15. You can now fix a clip turn by turn in conversation, swapping a background, product or lighting instead of starting over, and it holds faces, outfits, packaging text and brand colors more steadily across camera moves. Speech and lip-sync are more natural. On the Gemini API the price drops 30% to $0.07 per second of 720p video, and Google says Google Vids can generate 15-second clips at no additional cost.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> A full 15-second ad or explainer in one generation, plus edits that don&#039;t throw away the take, cuts both cost and wasted attempts.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Marketers, creators and developers making product clips, social ads or short explainers.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Generally available in the Gemini API, Google AI Studio and Google Cloud; in Flow and Google Vids; multi-turn editing rolling out to all Google AI subscribers in the Gemini app, with 15-second clips in the app for Google AI Ultra. Checked on Google&#039;s blog on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/introducing-gemini-omni-1-2-flash/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on blog.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/omni-1-2-flash-15-second-video/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Google%27s%20video%20model%20now%20makes%2015-second%20clips%20you%20can%20edit%20by%20chatting%2C%20and%20it%27s%2030%25%20cheaper&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fomni-1-2-flash-15-second-video%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="In Google AI Studio, pick Gemini Omni 1.2 Flash, set length to 12 seconds at 720p, generate a product clip, then refine with: &quot;swap the background to a forest, keep the characters&quot;. Upscale only the best take to 1080p." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="voice-realtime-avatars-us" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/voice-realtime-avatars-us/" class="hover:text-brand-600">You can now phone your Muse: real-time voice with an avatar that reacts as you talk, out for everyone in the US</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta rolled out Voice in the Muse app on November 5, 2026: tap the phone icon in the top-right corner and talk to your Muse in real time, interrupting it like a person. An expressive avatar, built on Meta&#039;s Muse Realtime Avatar research, reacts with facial expressions and gestures while it listens and speaks, and you can run it voice-only, side by side or full screen. There are hundreds of voices to choose from, and Muse keeps working on tasks in the background while you talk, so you can hand off errands on a walk or with your hands full.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Talking through a half-formed plan or rehearsing an interview out loud is faster than typing prompts, and the agent keeps doing the work while you speak.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse users in the US, especially anyone who wants to plan, brainstorm or delegate tasks hands-free.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rolling out now in the Muse app in the US on mobile, web and Mac; coming later to Meta&#039;s AI glasses and Muse Charm. Checked on Meta&#039;s newsroom post on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://about.fb.com/news/2026/11/introducing-muse-ai-voice-expressive-avatars/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Meta on about.fb.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/voice-realtime-avatars-us/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=You%20can%20now%20phone%20your%20Muse%3A%20real-time%20voice%20with%20an%20avatar%20that%20reacts%20as%20you%20talk%2C%20out%20for%20everyone%20in%20the%20US&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fvoice-realtime-avatars-us%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Update the Muse app, tap the phone icon, pick a voice and the side-by-side avatar, then say: &quot;Play the interviewer for a product manager role and push back on my answers.&quot; Hand off a follow-up task mid-call and check it in chat." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="launches-in-mexico" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/launches-in-mexico/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Meta&#039;s Muse lands in Mexico, its first Latin American country, with Rappi, Liverpool and Cinépolis on the way</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Muse, Meta&#039;s personal AI agent, became available in Mexico on November 5, 2026, announced by the official Muse account and Meta&#039;s Alexandr Wang. According to Infobae&#039;s report, it works in Spanish for adults 18 and over on iOS, Android, muse.ai and WhatsApp, is free to use with optional paid plans, and comes with connectors to local brands such as Cinépolis, Coppel, Despegar, Kavak, Kueski, Liverpool and Rappi, some of which switch on after launch. Like elsewhere, Muse runs tasks inside its own isolated cloud computer and browser.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s the first Latin American launch for a mainstream personal agent, and local connectors mean it can act on everyday services rather than just chat.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People in Mexico who want an agent for errands, shopping and planning, and brands watching where agent connectors launch next.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Mexico, Spanish, ages 18+, on iOS, Android, muse.ai and WhatsApp; free to start with optional subscriptions. Local connectors roll out gradually. Checked on the Muse and Alexandr Wang posts and Infobae&#039;s report on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Muse/status/2118438974385541359" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Muse on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/launches-in-mexico/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Meta%27s%20Muse%20lands%20in%20Mexico%2C%20its%20first%20Latin%20American%20country%2C%20with%20Rappi%2C%20Liverpool%20and%20Cin%C3%A9polis%20on%20the%20way&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Flaunches-in-mexico%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="If you are in Mexico, open muse.ai or the Muse app, create an account, connect Gmail or Google Calendar first, then ask Muse to draft a weekend plan. Confirm which local connectors (Rappi, Liverpool, Cinépolis) are live before relying on them." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="build-live-apps-share-link" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="cursor" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-zinc-200 text-zinc-800 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-zinc-200">Cursor</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/build-live-apps-share-link/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Cursor will now build your app, add a database and login, and hand you a live link, no localhost</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Cursor&#039;s November 5, 2026 release lets a cloud agent take an app from description to a live URL. Tell the agent you want to build an app and it scaffolds the web app, spins up a Postgres database if needed, adds sign-in behind Cursor SSO and provisions hosting. Before anything goes live it runs deterministic and agentic security checks for problems such as secrets in app files, and nothing is published until checks pass and you click publish. You pick a domain, then share with specific people, groups or your whole team; on individual plans you can also share publicly.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most internal tools built with agents never leave a laptop. This puts hosting, auth and a security check in the same flow, so a quick tool can actually get used.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Teams building internal dashboards, ops tools or demos, and solo builders who want a shareable prototype.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">All paid Cursor plans with cloud agents enabled; repos on Cursor Origin or GitHub (GitLab coming). Admins can see and unpublish every app. Checked on Cursor&#039;s changelog on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://cursor.com/changelog" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Cursor on cursor.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/cursor/build-live-apps-share-link/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Cursor%20will%20now%20build%20your%20app%2C%20add%20a%20database%20and%20login%2C%20and%20hand%20you%20a%20live%20link%2C%20no%20localhost&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fcursor%2Fbuild-live-apps-share-link%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="In Cursor, start a cloud agent and say: &quot;Build an app where my team can book desks for next week.&quot; Provide any secrets it asks for, review the security check, pick a domain, publish, and share the live link with your team." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="openai-gpt-6-cyber-81-firefox-bugs" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-gpt-6-cyber-81-firefox-bugs/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI&#039;s new GPT-6 Cyber found 81 high-severity Firefox bugs that years of testing missed</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI introduced GPT-6 Cyber on November 5, 2026, the model behind its Linux kernel work announced a day earlier. OpenAI says it produced evidence for 81 previously unknown high-severity Firefox vulnerabilities, with Mozilla already shipping fixes, and scored 48.5% on the ExploitGym benchmark versus 32.1% for GPT-5.6 Cyber. It was trained to stay inside the scope a researcher sets and avoided out-of-scope targets in 99.93% of tests without its deployment prompt. OpenAI rates it Critical for cybersecurity under its Preparedness Framework, so access is limited to approved Daybreak Red customers for now.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> AI is now finding serious bugs in heavily tested software faster than maintainers can patch them, so keeping dependencies updated matters more than ever.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Security teams, open-source maintainers and anyone who ships software that depends on browsers, kernels or common libraries.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to: approved Daybreak Red customers through the API and Codex, expanding over time; GPT-5.6 Cyber goes to all Daybreak Red customers. Checked on OpenAI&#039;s announcement on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-6-cyber/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-gpt-6-cyber-81-firefox-bugs/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%27s%20new%20GPT-6%20Cyber%20found%2081%20high-severity%20Firefox%20bugs%20that%20years%20of%20testing%20missed&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fopenai-gpt-6-cyber-81-firefox-bugs%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Update Firefox today, then open Mozilla&#039;s security advisories and check for the new high-severity fixes. If you maintain software, publish a security contact and a clear disclosure process before the next AI-found report lands." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="glasp-free-for-university-students" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/glasp-free-for-university-students/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Students: Glasp&#039;s AI summaries and chat with every model are free for 12 months with a university email</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Glasp, the web and PDF highlighter with built-in AI, now has a free Student plan. Sign in with a university email (addresses ending in .edu, academic endings like .ac.uk or .edu.au, and some universities by name) and you get, every 30 days: 100 AI summaries of videos, articles and PDFs, 100 AI chat credits on all models, 50 PDF chat messages and 120 minutes of audio transcription. No credit card is needed. The plan lasts 12 months from activation and can be renewed in its last 30 days if you&#039;re still studying.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s roughly 30x the Free plan&#039;s summaries at $0, which covers a semester of lecture videos and reading for most students.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">University students who summarize lecture videos, papers and articles.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Who qualifies: university students with a recognised academic email. Amount: 100 summaries, 100 chat credits, 50 PDF chats and 120 min transcription per 30 days. Deadline: no end date announced; each plan runs 12 months and is renewable while you study. Afterwards: back to the Free plan (3 summaries every 7 days), or Pro at $12.50 a month billed yearly ($150/year). Glasp says limits may change. Checked on glasp.co/students and glasp.co/pricing on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://glasp.co/students" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Glasp on glasp.co ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/glasp-free-for-university-students/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Students%3A%20Glasp%27s%20AI%20summaries%20and%20chat%20with%20every%20model%20are%20free%20for%2012%20months%20with%20a%20university%20email&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fglasp-free-for-university-students%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Open glasp.co/pricing, start the Student plan with your university email, then summarize one long PDF and ask a follow-up chat question on the same document to confirm the credits applied." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="viktor-ai-employee-email-100-free-credits" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
