                                <article id="api-free-tier-phone-qr-verification" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/api-free-tier-phone-qr-verification/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Getting a 403 on Gemini&#039;s free tier? Some projects now need a 10-second phone QR check</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google&#039;s Gemini API docs now say Google AI Studio and the Gemini API require mobile device verification on some free tier projects and accounts, to stop automated abuse. Extra projects, or projects created outside AI Studio, can show &quot;Verification needed&quot; and return a 403 FREE_TIER_VERIFICATION_REQUIRED error until verified. You scan a QR code with an Android phone or iPhone; no phone number is shared and no app is installed. Making a new API key in the same project doesn&#039;t skip the check, and paid tier projects don&#039;t need it.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If your free-tier script or agent suddenly fails with a 403, this is likely why, and the fix takes a minute.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and hobbyists using the free Gemini API, especially across several Google Cloud projects.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to: some free tier projects and accounts in Google AI Studio and the Gemini API; paid tier projects are exempt. Checked on Google&#039;s verification doc on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/verification" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google AI for Developers on ai.google.dev ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/api-free-tier-phone-qr-verification/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Getting%20a%20403%20on%20Gemini%27s%20free%20tier%3F%20Some%20projects%20now%20need%20a%2010-second%20phone%20QR%20check&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fapi-free-tier-phone-qr-verification%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="If Gemini returns 403 FREE_TIER_VERIFICATION_REQUIRED, open the link in the error (or Projects in AI Studio), click Verify device, scan the QR with your phone as Owner or Editor, wait for Project verified, then retry the request." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="openai-private-safety-processing-zdr" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-private-safety-processing-zdr/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI&#039;s Private Safety Processing: safety review without OpenAI keeping your prompts</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Zero Data Retention with Private Safety Processing (ZDR with PSP) lets OpenAI run offline, automated safety review on API traffic without retaining customer prompts or responses in OpenAI&#039;s own systems. Eligible interactions are encrypted and written to storage you control (AWS S3, Azure Blob, GCS or OCI), then reviewed inside a hardware-attested runtime that disables human access. Only bounded safety signals leave that runtime in plaintext. You can add customer-managed encryption with Enterprise Key Management, and OpenAI Dev published the guide alongside an official explainer on X.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Enterprise buyers who need ZDR no longer have to choose between zero retention and meaningful abuse review. Records stay in your bucket under your keys.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">API teams and security leads at organizations already approved for Zero Data Retention, or applying for it.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to organizations approved for Zero Data Retention (or Modified Abuse Monitoring with PSP). Enabled per OpenAI project after you connect and validate external storage. Org admins set it up in API console Data controls or via the Management API. Checked on OpenAI developer docs and @OpenAIDevs on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/private-safety-processing" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on developers.openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-private-safety-processing-zdr/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%27s%20Private%20Safety%20Processing%3A%20safety%20review%20without%20OpenAI%20keeping%20your%20prompts&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fopenai-private-safety-processing-zdr%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="If your org has ZDR, open the OpenAI API console Data retention page, read the Private Safety Processing setup for your cloud, and list the exact bucket policy and 30-day lifecycle steps your admin still needs to finish." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="huggingface-moe-training-handbook-free" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/huggingface-moe-training-handbook-free/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Hugging Face just open-sourced an MoE training handbook built from 800k GPU-hours</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Hugging Face released The Ultimate MoE Training Handbook as a free, open guide to training Mixture-of-Experts models with Megatron-LM. The team says the lessons come from about 800,000 GH200 GPU-hours of MoE runs on CSCS&#039;s Alps cluster. The write-up is long (on the order of 70k words) with 55 interactive figures, runnable scripts and recommended flags covering expert counts, all-to-all communication, router choices, load balancing, upcycling, serving and RL. Hugging Face co-founder Thomas Wolf announced it on X with a direct link to the Space.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most top open models are MoEs, but the training know-how stayed inside a few labs. This is a concrete, free runbook you can actually follow.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">ML engineers and researchers who have trained a dense model and want to train or serve an MoE next.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Who qualifies: anyone. Amount: free handbook, figures and scripts. Deadline: none. Afterwards: still free. Read it at the Hugging Face moe-blogpost Space; figure gallery and gist scripts are linked from the announcement. Checked on the Space and @Thom_Wolf&#039;s post on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://huggingface.co/spaces/huggingface/moe-blogpost" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Hugging Face on huggingface.co ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/huggingface-moe-training-handbook-free/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Hugging%20Face%20just%20open-sourced%20an%20MoE%20training%20handbook%20built%20from%20800k%20GPU-hours&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fhuggingface-moe-training-handbook-free%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Open the Hugging Face MoE handbook Space, pick the recommended Megatron-LM flag block for a first single-node MoE, and ask your coding agent to turn it into a config file plus a one-page experiment checklist." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
