                                <article id="metr-anthropic-ai-progress-doubled-12x-uplift" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/metr-anthropic-ai-progress-doubled-12x-uplift/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Two years of progress in one: METR spent 11 weeks inside Anthropic and found Claude is improving about 2x faster</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Independent evaluator METR reviewed internal Anthropic data from August 12 to October 29, 2026 to see how much AI is speeding up AI research. Its estimate: Anthropic&#039;s benchmark scores have grown about 1.9x faster since October 2025 than before (95% interval 1.5x to 2.8x), roughly two years of past progress in one year, and the speedup was not caused by faster growth in training compute. METR thinks most of today&#039;s acceleration, perhaps around 80%, comes from staff using Claude for R&amp;D, and says loose Slack polls put self-reported uplift at about 12x in October. Anthropic redacted much of the supporting evidence, which METR flags clearly.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If labs are using their own models to build the next ones faster, release cadence and capability jumps could speed up too. It is one of the first outside looks at that loop, with big caveats about redactions.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone tracking where AI models are heading, from engineering leaders planning tool budgets to people following AI safety policy.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies as a public research report from METR, published November 5, 2026 (updated November 6). METR says Anthropic redacted a majority of the evidence it found most informative and that the true acceleration could be closer to 1.3x or 3x. Checked on metr.org on November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://metr.org/blog/2026-11-05-anthropic-ai-rd-acceleration-assessment/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @METR on metr.org ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/metr-anthropic-ai-progress-doubled-12x-uplift/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Two%20years%20of%20progress%20in%20one%3A%20METR%20spent%2011%20weeks%20inside%20Anthropic%20and%20found%20Claude%20is%20improving%20about%202x%20faster&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fmetr-anthropic-ai-progress-doubled-12x-uplift%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
