                                <article id="ling-3-2-flash-free-api-two-weeks-claude-code" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/ling-3-2-flash-free-api-two-weeks-claude-code/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Free until about November 19: Ling-3.2-flash, the 1M-context model Ant says beats Opus 5 on three vision tests, works in Claude Code</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Ant Group&#039;s Ling team released Ling-3.2-flash on November 5: a mixture-of-experts model with 560B total and 25B active parameters, a 1M-token context window, and native image, text and video input. Ant&#039;s changelog says the API is free for the first two weeks after launch, and it speaks both the OpenAI and Anthropic protocols, so you can point Claude Code or any OpenAI-style client at it. Ant reports it beating Claude Opus 5 (max) on three vision benchmarks, including OmniDocBench 1.5 (92.21 vs 90.56); those are the vendor&#039;s own numbers.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> A free window on a big multimodal model is a cheap way to test PDF-to-code, screenshot-to-frontend or long-document agent jobs before you pay for them. Run your own comparison instead of trusting the vendor&#039;s benchmark table.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and tinkerers who want to try a long-context, vision-capable model in Claude Code or their own scripts at zero cost for a short window.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free for the first two weeks after the November 5, 2026 launch, per Ant Ling&#039;s official changelog. Ant hasn&#039;t posted an exact end time, so treat November 18 as the last safe day; the post-promo price isn&#039;t on Ant&#039;s official price page yet. Needs an Ant Ling platform account and API token; check the console for sign-up and billing requirements in your region. Open weights for 3.2-flash haven&#039;t been released. Checked on developer.ant-ling.com on November 9, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://developer.ant-ling.com/en/docs/getting-started/changelog" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Ant Ling on developer.ant-ling.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/ling-3-2-flash-free-api-two-weeks-claude-code/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Free%20until%20about%20November%2019%3A%20Ling-3.2-flash%2C%20the%201M-context%20model%20Ant%20says%20beats%20Opus%205%20on%20three%20vision%20tests%2C%20works%20in%20Claude%20Code&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fling-3-2-flash-free-api-two-weeks-claude-code%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
