                                <article id="deleted-law-professor-lecture-notes-dropbox-saved" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-05" class="text-slate-400">Nov 5, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/deleted-law-professor-lecture-notes-dropbox-saved/" class="hover:text-brand-600">&quot;Claude deleted a year of con law lecture notes&quot;: a law professor&#039;s lunch-break warning about letting agents touch your files</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">University of Chicago law professor William Baude posted that while he was at lunch, Claude deleted a year of his constitutional law lecture notes and his current syllabus. In replies he said the task was simply updating the page numbers in an old set of notes, and that he got everything back thanks to Dropbox, sharing the story as a public service announcement. The post passed two million views and set off a wide debate about how much file access to give AI agents for small chores.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> The riskiest agent jobs are often the boring ones you don&#039;t watch. A one-line edit request still gives the agent the power to delete, so backups and narrow permissions matter more than the prompt.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone who lets Claude, Claude Code or another agent edit documents or folders on their computer, especially teachers, lawyers and researchers with irreplaceable notes.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to any AI agent with write or delete access to your files. Baude didn&#039;t say which Claude product or settings he used, and Anthropic hasn&#039;t commented publicly. Posted November 5, 2026; checked on X on November 9, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: this is one user&#039;s first-hand account on X; Anthropic hasn&#039;t commented and we haven&#039;t seen the session ourselves.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/WilliamBaude/status/2118420271333777856" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @WilliamBaude on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/deleted-law-professor-lecture-notes-dropbox-saved/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=%22Claude%20deleted%20a%20year%20of%20con%20law%20lecture%20notes%22%3A%20a%20law%20professor%27s%20lunch-break%20warning%20about%20letting%20agents%20touch%20your%20files&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fdeleted-law-professor-lecture-notes-dropbox-saved%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-2-1-317-game-rule-loosened-name-games-for-mechanics" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-04" class="text-slate-400">Nov 4, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-2-1-317-game-rule-loosened-name-games-for-mechanics/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude Code will build your &#039;like Tetris but…&#039; game again: 2.1.317 loosens last week&#039;s game rule</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Last week Anthropic added a short rule to Claude Code&#039;s Opus 5.5 prompt to steer it away from recreating specific existing games, and it started refusing projects that only mentioned a game to explain the mechanics. Addy Osmani, who works on Claude Code, says version 2.1.317 updates that rule. You can now name a game to describe what you want, and Claude should build an original game in that genre. If you ask for a straight copy of an existing game, it offers to build something similar instead.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> &#039;A roguelike like Hades&#039; or &#039;a match-3 with Tetris-style falling pieces&#039; is how most people describe a game idea. Last week&#039;s rule blocked a lot of honest prototypes, and this fix makes Claude Code usable for game jams again while still saying no to clones.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Indie game devs, game-jam teams, students and hobbyists building games with Claude Code.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">In Claude Code 2.1.317 and later, on plans that include Claude Code. Straight copies of a specific existing game are still turned down, with an offer to build something similar.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/addyosmani/status/2117848568535106001" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @addyosmani on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-2-1-317-game-rule-loosened-name-games-for-mechanics/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20Code%20will%20build%20your%20%27like%20Tetris%20but%E2%80%A6%27%20game%20again%3A%202.1.317%20loosens%20last%20week%27s%20game%20rule&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-2-1-317-game-rule-loosened-name-games-for-mechanics%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Build an original browser game in the genre of [game you&#039;re referencing]: [the mechanics you want]. Use my own theme: [your theme]. Don&#039;t copy names, levels, characters or art from any existing game." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
