                                <article id="openai-to-acquire-pierre-code-storage" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-04" class="text-slate-400">Nov 4, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-to-acquire-pierre-code-storage/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI is buying Pierre, the Git-for-agents startup behind Lovable&#039;s and Bolt&#039;s code storage</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI says it will acquire the Pierre Computer Company. Pierre makes Code Storage, a Git hosting service designed for AI agents that companies such as Lovable, Bolt and Amp use to store the code their agents write, plus the open-source Trees, Diffs and Highlights libraries for showing file trees and code changes. Trees and Diffs already power parts of the Codex app. OpenAI says Pierre&#039;s open-source projects stay open, current Code Storage customers can keep using it, and its features will move into Codex. The price wasn&#039;t shared and the deal still needs regulatory approval.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Agents write far more code, branches and commits than people do, and ordinary Git hosting wasn&#039;t built for that. Paired with OpenAI&#039;s own Git work, this looks like OpenAI building its own code-hosting layer for Codex, which some reporters see as a challenge to GitHub.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Codex users, teams building app builders on Code Storage, and anyone watching the fight over where agent-written code lives.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to: Pierre Code Storage customers (service continues for now) and users of the open-source Trees, Diffs and Highlights libraries (they stay open source). The deal is pending regulatory approval; terms weren&#039;t disclosed.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/openai-to-acquire-pierre" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-to-acquire-pierre-code-storage/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%20is%20buying%20Pierre%2C%20the%20Git-for-agents%20startup%20behind%20Lovable%27s%20and%20Bolt%27s%20code%20storage&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fopenai-to-acquire-pierre-code-storage%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="heygen-voice-turbo-free-api-until-november-30" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-04" class="text-slate-400">Nov 4, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/heygen-voice-turbo-free-api-until-november-30/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Free text-to-speech for your agents: HeyGen Voice Turbo API costs $0 until November 30</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">HeyGen is offering a free version of its fast Voice Turbo text-to-speech model through its API. If you set the model to heygen-voice-1-turbo-free, requests cost $0 until November 30, 2026, with no credit card and no credit balance needed. It works with HeyGen&#039;s public and instant voices but not professional voice clones, and it&#039;s limited to 30 requests a minute per member on shared, best-effort capacity, so it can return 429 busy errors. A free request is never quietly switched to paid. Any coding agent, including Claude Code, can call it with a single POST to api.heygen.com/v3/models/audio/tts.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Voice is often the last piece missing from agent demos, narrated videos and voice prototypes. A month of free, fast TTS through an API is enough to build and test one without a bill.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers prototyping voice agents, narrated explainers or read-aloud features with Claude Code or any other agent.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free for anyone with a HeyGen API key until November 30, 2026, with no card needed. Public and instant voices only, 30 requests a minute, shared capacity and no uptime guarantee. Afterwards, paid Voice Turbo (heygen-voice-1-turbo) is $4 per 1M characters and standard HeyGen Voice is $15 per 1M characters; HeyGen hasn&#039;t said what happens to the free model after November 30. Checked on HeyGen&#039;s blog and docs November 4, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.heygen.com/blog/heygen-voice-turbo" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @HeyGen on www.heygen.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/heygen-voice-turbo-free-api-until-november-30/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Free%20text-to-speech%20for%20your%20agents%3A%20HeyGen%20Voice%20Turbo%20API%20costs%20%240%20until%20November%2030&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fheygen-voice-turbo-free-api-until-november-30%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Add text-to-speech to [your project] by calling POST https://api.heygen.com/v3/models/audio/tts with model heygen-voice-1-turbo-free, a public voice_id and my text. Read the API key from an environment variable, retry 429 errors with a short backoff, and add a TODO to switch models before November 30, 2026." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-background-subagents-status-updates-99-percent-cheaper" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-04" class="text-slate-400">Nov 4, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-background-subagents-status-updates-99-percent-cheaper/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude Code&#039;s background subagents just got cheaper to run: each status update now costs about 99% less</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">When a Claude Code subagent runs in the background, it refreshes its one-line status every 30 seconds. Until now, each refresh re-read the subagent&#039;s whole conversation, which quietly ate into your usage limit. Anthropic&#039;s Claude Code team says Haiku 5.5 now writes that status from short notes instead, so each update costs about 99% less. The subagent itself still runs on its own model. Across whole sessions with background subagents, Anthropic measured about 5% less of the limit used, which works out to roughly 6% more prompts on the same plan.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you lean on background subagents for long refactors, test runs or research, you were paying for status lines you barely read. This is a free saving you get just by updating. It won&#039;t double your limit, but it&#039;s around 6% more prompts on the same plan.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code users who run background subagents on Pro, Max, Ultra, Team or Enterprise plans.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Live for most Pro, Max and Ultra users and for everyone on Team and Enterprise, in Claude Code v2.1.316 and later. No extra cost and no setting to change.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/ClaudeDevs/status/2118063143167693011" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @ClaudeDevs on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-background-subagents-status-updates-99-percent-cheaper/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20Code%27s%20background%20subagents%20just%20got%20cheaper%20to%20run%3A%20each%20status%20update%20now%20costs%20about%2099%25%20less&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-background-subagents-status-updates-99-percent-cheaper%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Run this as a background subagent: [the task, e.g. run the full test suite and list failures with likely causes]. Keep working in the background and report back with a short summary when you&#039;re done, while I keep working in the main session." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="voice-remixing-3-8-flash-tts" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-04" class="text-slate-400">Nov 4, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/voice-remixing-3-8-flash-tts/" class="hover:text-brand-600">&quot;Make it sound older, with a British accent&quot;: Gemini can now remix any of its voices with a plain-English prompt</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Voice Remixing lets you take an existing Gemini voice, either a prebuilt one from the 2,000+ voice library or a voice you designed yourself, and change it by describing what you want: older, calmer, higher pitch, more energy, a different accent. Gemini saves the result as a new voice with its own voice_ ID and gives you a short WAV preview. The original voice isn&#039;t changed, and you can keep remixing the new one step by step. You can use the saved voice for speech with Gemini 3.8 Flash TTS or Gemini 3.8 Flash-Lite TTS.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Getting a character voice right usually means trying dozens of presets. Now you can start from one that&#039;s close and say what to change. That&#039;s useful for narrators, game characters and voice agents that need a consistent, recognisable voice.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and creators building narration, audiobooks, games or voice agents on the Gemini API.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Live now in Google AI Studio and the Gemini API. Creating remixed voices through the API needs a paid-tier (Tier 1 or higher) Gemini API project. You can store up to 200 custom voices per project, and each is kept for a year after its last use. Speech is billed at normal Gemini 3.8 TTS rates.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/voice-remixing" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on ai.google.dev ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/voice-remixing-3-8-flash-tts/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=%22Make%20it%20sound%20older%2C%20with%20a%20British%20accent%22%3A%20Gemini%20can%20now%20remix%20any%20of%20its%20voices%20with%20a%20plain-English%20prompt&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fvoice-remixing-3-8-flash-tts%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Starting from the voice [base voice], make it [one or two changes: age, pitch, pace, energy, accent]. Keep everything else the same." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="vault-particle-first-3d-structure" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="research">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Research</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-04" class="text-slate-400">Nov 4, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/vault-particle-first-3d-structure/" class="hover:text-brand-600">A 40-year biology mystery: Claude helped Anthropic&#039;s lab map the first 3D structure of a vault particle from bacterial life</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Vaults are huge, hollow, barrel-shaped protein particles first found in 1986, and nobody knows what they do. Anthropic&#039;s biology lab used Claude to search sequence data for vault-like proteins in bacteria and the viruses that infect them, to improve how the particles were isolated, and to run the cryo-EM processing software that turns thousands of images into a 3D model. The result is the first experimental 3D structure of a vault from a bacteriophage: 96 copies of one protein, wider and rounder than the mammalian version. Claude had a first full model ready in 34 hours, a job Anthropic says would normally take weeks to months by hand. Anthropic also says Claude made some simple mistakes along the way that its researchers had to catch.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> This is a concrete, checkable example of an AI model speeding up real lab science, from searching the literature to running the structure software. It&#039;s also candid about the limits: humans directed the work and corrected mistakes.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Researchers, biotech teams and anyone curious about how AI agents are being used in real science.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">A research write-up and preprint from Anthropic. The vaults have so far only been made in E. coli in the lab, and what they do is still unknown. The workflow used Claude in an internal multi-agent setup, not a public product.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/investigating-vault-particles-with-claude" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @AnthropicAI on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/vault-particle-first-3d-structure/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=A%2040-year%20biology%20mystery%3A%20Claude%20helped%20Anthropic%27s%20lab%20map%20the%20first%203D%20structure%20of%20a%20vault%20particle%20from%20bacterial%20life&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fvault-particle-first-3d-structure%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="postman-auto-installed-plugins-claude-code-codex" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-04" class="text-slate-400">Nov 4, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/postman-auto-installed-plugins-claude-code-codex/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Check your agent configs: Postman&#039;s desktop app reportedly installed its plugins into Claude Code and Codex without asking</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A GitHub issue that reached Hacker News&#039; front page says opening the Postman desktop app on a Mac installed Postman plugins into Claude Code and Codex on its own. It also added a Codex startup hook telling the agent to use Postman&#039;s API skill for almost any API task, plus a remote MCP connection and a Postman CLI. The reporter shows a line from Postman&#039;s own log marking the install as an automatic upgrade. Postman&#039;s plugin README says its installer approves its own Codex hook, which skips the review Codex normally asks you to do. The reporter says there&#039;s no evidence of data being taken.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Hooks and plugins can steer what your coding agent does in every project. An app adding them without asking is a trust problem, and a good reminder to check what&#039;s loaded into your agents.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers who have Postman&#039;s desktop app and use Claude Code or Codex, especially on macOS.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Reported on macOS with Postman 12.33.4, with a similar report on 12.35.1. Postman&#039;s plugin includes a remove command to uninstall it.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/SeanScott/status/2117969927600558192" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @SeanScott on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/postman-auto-installed-plugins-claude-code-codex/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Check%20your%20agent%20configs%3A%20Postman%27s%20desktop%20app%20reportedly%20installed%20its%20plugins%20into%20Claude%20Code%20and%20Codex%20without%20asking&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fpostman-auto-installed-plugins-claude-code-codex%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="List every plugin, hook, skill and MCP server loaded into my coding agents. Check ~/.claude/settings.json, ~/.codex/config.toml, ~/.codex/ hooks and ~/.local/bin, and flag anything mentioning postman. Don&#039;t change or delete anything; just show me the list so I can decide." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-airpods-case-mouse-swift-driver" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-04" class="text-slate-400">Nov 4, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-airpods-case-mouse-swift-driver/" class="hover:text-brand-600">He turned his AirPods case into a mouse in one evening with Claude Code, without writing a line of Swift</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">X user @_Aquarelle says he and Claude Code built a small Swift menu-bar app for his MacBook that turns his AirPods case into a pointer. Pointing the case moves the cursor, tapping the lid clicks, a double tap double-clicks, tapping the side right-clicks, and tilting and holding scrolls. His first version was too jumpy because his hand shakes slightly, so he asked Claude to add smoothing and a dead zone, and now he closes tabs from the couch three meters away. He says he described what he wanted, broke it, complained, and let Claude fix it until it worked.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a fun example of how far &#039;describe it, test it, complain&#039; can go with a coding agent, even for low-level input handling in a language you don&#039;t know. Smoothing and dead zones are the kind of fixes that used to need an expert.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Mac tinkerers and hobbyists who want to build small hardware-input hacks without knowing Swift.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">A personal project, not a released app. Needs Claude Code on a plan that includes it and a Mac with AirPods. He hasn&#039;t said exactly how the app reads the case&#039;s movement, so your results may vary.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/_Aquarelle/status/2118025451989880983" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @_Aquarelle on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-airpods-case-mouse-swift-driver/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
