    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/cognition-swe-2-flash-free-in-devin-until-november-30/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Cognition&#039;s new SWE-2 Flash coding model runs 3x faster at a fifth of SWE-2&#039;s price, and it&#039;s free in Devin until November 30</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Cognition released SWE-2 Flash on November 4, 2026, a smaller coding model built on Thinking Machines&#039; Inkling-Small (276B total, 12B active parameters) with an extra mid-training stage before reinforcement learning. Cognition says it runs at about 200 tokens a second, 3x the speed of its bigger SWE-2, at one-fifth of SWE-2&#039;s price, and scores 20.0 on Terminal-Bench 4.0 and 24.0 on FrontierCode 2.0. It&#039;s available now in Devin Desktop and the Devin CLI, and the launch page says it&#039;s free through November 30. The weights are not public; Cognition says it is building a program to share them with trusted partners.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Cheap, fast models are what you want for code review, docs updates and small fixes. A free month is a no-risk way to see how much of your daily agent work a small model can handle.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers using Devin, and anyone comparing small coding models for routine agent work like reviews and automations.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">In Devin Desktop and Devin CLI, free through November 30, 2026 per Cognition&#039;s launch page; trackers report the free use applies on paid Devin plans (Pro $20/month, Max $200/month and Teams), and Devin&#039;s Free plan has limited model access. After November 30 it&#039;s billed at what Cognition calls one-fifth of SWE-2&#039;s price; a list price wasn&#039;t published yet. Checked on cognition.com and devin.ai/pricing on November 5, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://cognition.com/blog/swe-2-flash" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Cognition on cognition.com ↗</a>
