    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/kimi-k3-1-pro-open-weights-terminal-bench-claude-code/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Moonshot just released Kimi K3.1 Pro&#039;s weights: a 2.8-trillion-parameter model that scored 65.7 on Terminal-Bench, 0.7 behind Opus 5.5</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Moonshot AI published the weights of Kimi K3.1 Pro on Hugging Face on November 4, 2026. It&#039;s a mixture-of-experts model with 2.8 trillion total and 104 billion active parameters, a 1-million-token context window and a built-in vision encoder, post-trained from Kimi K3 for coding and agent work. On Moonshot&#039;s own model card it scores 65.7 on Terminal-Bench 4.0, run in the Claude Code harness, against 66.4 for Claude Opus 5.5 and 58.2 for GPT-6 Astra, and it leads that table on SWE Marathon (51.7). It trails the closed models on other tests such as Program Bench. The weights use a custom Kimi K3.1 Pro license.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> An open-weight model this close to the top closed models on agentic coding gives teams another option they can host themselves or buy from several providers, instead of depending on one vendor.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Teams that self-host models or shop around inference providers, and developers comparing models for coding agents.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Weights on Hugging Face under the custom kimi-k3.1-pro license (read it before commercial use); also served by Moonshot&#039;s API. The weights are huge, so running it yourself needs a multi-GPU server; most people will use a hosted API. Benchmarks are Moonshot&#039;s own. Checked on the Hugging Face model card and Moonshot&#039;s X post on November 5, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://huggingface.co/moonshotai/Kimi-K3.1-Pro" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Moonshot AI on huggingface.co ↗</a>
