    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-copilot-in-xcode-coding-assistant/" class="hover:text-brand-600">GitHub Copilot now lives inside Xcode&#039;s own coding assistant, on every Copilot plan</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">GitHub announced on November 4, 2026 that Copilot now works directly inside Xcode&#039;s built-in coding assistant, as a public preview starting with Xcode 27.3 beta. You set it up under Xcode &gt; Settings &gt; Intelligence, and it uses your existing Copilot subscription on any plan. The separate GitHub Copilot for Xcode extension keeps working, so iOS and Mac developers can choose between the native assistant panel and the extension. You need a Mac on macOS Tahoe 26.6 or later.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Apple developers get Copilot in Xcode&#039;s native assistant without a third-party extension, using the subscription they already pay for.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">iOS, iPadOS and macOS developers who already pay for GitHub Copilot.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Public preview; Xcode 27.3 beta on macOS Tahoe 26.6 or later; all Copilot plans. Checked on GitHub&#039;s changelog on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-04-github-copilot-is-now-available-in-xcodes-coding-assistant" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GitHub on github.blog ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-copilot-in-xcode-coding-assistant/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
