    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Researcher Tibor Blaho reported that ChatGPT&#039;s web checkout pricing config now includes a &quot;Family Basic&quot; subscription lineup. Community follow-ups say the price tags lined up with existing individual plans often listed as Go $8, Plus $20, ProLite $100, Pro $200 and ProMax $500 per month (tax exclusive in the screenshots people shared). OpenAI has not announced a family plan, seat counts, shared limits or a launch date. Treat this as a code-config spotting, not a shipping product.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Households that juggle several ChatGPT seats have asked for a family plan for years. This is the first concrete checkout string, even if nothing is live yet.</p>
