                                <article id="oumi-faie-frontier-ai-engineer-agents" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-04" class="text-slate-400">Nov 4, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/oumi-faie-frontier-ai-engineer-agents/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Oumi&#039;s FAiE is an AI engineer that builds agents and retrains the models behind them</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Oumi&#039;s Fall 2026 launch extends FAiE (Frontier AI Engineer) across the full agent loop. You describe what an agent should do in plain language; FAiE helps define tools, generate multi-turn data, design evaluators, train or refine the underlying model, deploy and fold production failures back into the next round. Bring Your Own Harness lets teams keep their existing orchestration, tools and memory while plugging Oumi in for evaluation and training. The release adds Direct Preference Optimization on top of supervised fine-tuning, with group relative policy optimization in private preview.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most teams can demo an agent. Few can turn production failures into better weights. FAiE targets that missing training loop.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Product and ML teams that already ship agents and need evaluation plus model improvement without rebuilding their harness.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Announced November 4, 2026 on oumi.ai and @oumi_ai. Agent development, Bring Your Own Harness and DPO are part of the Fall Launch; GRPO is private preview. Check oumi.ai for current plan access. Checked on the launch page and docs on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://oumi.ai/product-launch/fall26" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Oumi on oumi.ai ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/oumi-faie-frontier-ai-engineer-agents/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Oumi%27s%20FAiE%20is%20an%20AI%20engineer%20that%20builds%20agents%20and%20retrains%20the%20models%20behind%20them&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Foumi-faie-frontier-ai-engineer-agents%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
