                                <article id="truffle-secrets-revocation-program-free" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-04" class="text-slate-400">Nov 4, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/truffle-secrets-revocation-program-free/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Truffle Security will help revoke 1.4M live leaked API keys for free</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Truffle Security launched a free Secrets Revocation Program for any company that issues API keys, tokens or similar credentials. Its research team scans public GitHub, GitLab, Docker Hub, npm, PyPI, Hugging Face, Android apps and Firefox add-ons, verifies every finding with TruffleHog, then either posts live secrets to your webhook for you to revoke within 14 days or calls a revocation endpoint you provide. The launch post says 1.4 million verified live credentials are already in scope, 81% of keys reported last year still worked six months later, and early partners include Hugging Face, Notion, Vercel, Resend, RubyGems and Twilio.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Notifying developers rarely kills keys. Automatic issuer-side revocation is how Google drove live Cloud key rates down, and AI agents are leaking more keys into new places.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Security and platform teams at any company that issues customer API keys or tokens.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Who qualifies: organizations that issue credentials. Amount: free to join (early access agreement). Deadline: none stated for joining; webhook participants must revoke or explain within 14 days of each disclosure. Afterwards: still free per Truffle. Checked on Truffle&#039;s blog and program page on November 6, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://trufflesecurity.com/blog/launching-the-secrets-revocation-program" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Truffle Security on trufflesecurity.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/truffle-secrets-revocation-program-free/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Truffle%20Security%20will%20help%20revoke%201.4M%20live%20leaked%20API%20keys%20for%20free&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Ftruffle-secrets-revocation-program-free%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
