                                <article id="revolut-2000-engineers-glm-5-3-self-hosted-90-percent-cheaper" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-04" class="text-slate-400">Nov 4, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/revolut-2000-engineers-glm-5-3-self-hosted-90-percent-cheaper/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Revolut moved 2,000 engineers off Claude Code and Codex to a self-hosted model and cut AI coding costs about 90%</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Revolut has made a self-hosted copy of Z.ai&#039;s open-weight GLM 5.3 the default coding model for about 2,000 engineers, replacing Claude Code and Codex as the default, according to its head of AI operations and infrastructure, David Abitbol, speaking at the AI Engineer conference in New York. He said Revolut now spends about a tenth of what it paid US labs, serving everyone from 56 Nvidia B200 GPUs at a blended cost near $0.30 per million tokens. Revolut says engineers stopped rationing tokens, and the switch coincided with about 60% better coding time and 70% better lead time.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> When tokens are effectively unlimited, people hand more work to AI. It&#039;s a big data point for teams weighing open-weight models on their own hardware against per-seat or per-token bills.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Engineering leaders and finance owners watching AI coding spend, and teams considering self-hosted open-weight models.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to Revolut&#039;s internal engineering setup as described by Revolut&#039;s David Abitbol and reported by Cybernews on November 4, 2026 (updated November 5). The figures are Revolut&#039;s own. Revolut says it runs public model weights on US infrastructure with a human in the loop. Checked November 7, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://cybernews.com/ai-news/revolut-chinese-models/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Cybernews on cybernews.com ↗</a>
