    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-free-mystery-models-crouton-pulse-alpha-1m-context/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Two mystery AI models just went free with 1M-token context: Crouton Alpha and Pulse Alpha, and nobody will say who built them</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Two anonymous preview models appeared this week at $0. Crouton Alpha, listed on OpenRouter on November 3, has a 1,048,576-token context window, takes text, images, video, PDFs and audio, and supports tool calling and structured outputs. OpenRouter pitches it for agent sub-tasks, tool use and document analysis, and its page shows Claude Code as the top app sending it traffic. OpenCode lists both Crouton Alpha Free and Pulse Alpha Free as free models; model trackers list Pulse Alpha with a 1M context too. Neither developer has been named, and guesses online about which lab is behind them are unconfirmed.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> A free model with a million-token context is a cheap way to run big-context agent jobs, like reading a whole repo or a long PDF, without burning paid tokens. Anonymous previews like these don&#039;t last, so it&#039;s worth testing now.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers running coding agents or batch document jobs who want to try a long-context model at no cost, for non-sensitive work.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free for a limited time; neither OpenRouter nor OpenCode gives an end date. OpenRouter says the anonymous provider may keep Crouton prompts but doesn&#039;t use them for training, and it isn&#039;t available through EU in-region routing. On OpenCode, both are free while the team collects feedback; Crouton isn&#039;t offered in the EU, Pakistan, China and several other countries, and Pulse isn&#039;t offered in the EU/EEA, Russia, Ukraine and a few others. OpenCode&#039;s free models only work from OpenCode itself. Checked on OpenRouter and OpenCode&#039;s model docs November 4, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openrouter.ai/stealth/crouton-alpha" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenRouter on openrouter.ai ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-free-mystery-models-crouton-pulse-alpha-1m-context/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
