                                <article id="auto-connect-plugins-team-enterprise-managed-auth" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-03" class="text-slate-400">Nov 3, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/auto-connect-plugins-team-enterprise-managed-auth/" class="hover:text-brand-600">No more signing in to every work app: Claude Team and Enterprise can now auto-connect Slack, Notion, Figma and 18 more for the whole company</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic added Enterprise-managed auth for Claude connectors. An admin authorizes a connector once for the organization, and teammates are connected automatically the first time they use it, with no sign-in page or consent screen. It works two ways: through your identity provider (Okta for now, with SSO), which is generally available, or with Claude-issued auth (beta), which needs no identity provider and matches people to their accounts by email. Admins choose which roles get each connector and which permissions Claude can request. Anthropic&#039;s help page lists 21 supported connectors, including Slack, Notion, Figma, Linear, Atlassian, HubSpot, Asana and Supabase.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Rolling Claude out to a team usually stalls on everyone connecting their own tools. This makes the connectors work on day one and lets admins pilot a connector with one team before turning it on for everyone.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Admins and IT leads rolling out Claude Team or Enterprise, and builders of Claude plugins and MCP servers.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Team and Enterprise plans. IdP-managed auth is generally available and needs SSO with a supported identity provider (Okta for now). Claude-issued auth is in beta and works with 14 connectors whose providers support it, such as Figma, Notion, Linear, Datadog and Supabase. Plugin builders can add support so their MCP server accepts Claude as a trusted issuer.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/15537633-auto-connect-your-organization-s-apps-to-claude" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on support.claude.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/auto-connect-plugins-team-enterprise-managed-auth/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=No%20more%20signing%20in%20to%20every%20work%20app%3A%20Claude%20Team%20and%20Enterprise%20can%20now%20auto-connect%20Slack%2C%20Notion%2C%20Figma%20and%2018%20more%20for%20the%20whole%20company&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fauto-connect-plugins-team-enterprise-managed-auth%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I&#039;m a Claude Team or Enterprise admin rolling out managed authorization for the [connector] connector. Write a one-page pilot plan: which custom role gets it first, which permissions Claude should be allowed to request, how to run the connection test, and a short message asking 2-3 teammates to confirm it works." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
