                                <article id="finances-voice-talk-about-your-money" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-03" class="text-slate-400">Nov 3, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/finances-voice-talk-about-your-money/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Ask ChatGPT out loud where your money went: Finances now works in voice, and it&#039;s on the free plan in the US</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI added voice support to Finances in ChatGPT, so you can talk through questions about your spending, subscriptions, savings, investments and credit instead of typing them. Finances connects your bank and card accounts through Plaid and your credit report through Experian, then answers using that data and shows a dashboard of spending, bills, subscriptions, net worth and credit score. The connections are read-only: OpenAI says ChatGPT can&#039;t move money, pay bills, make trades or act as your financial adviser.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Hunting for forgotten subscriptions or a spending spike is the kind of chore people put off. Asking out loud while you do something else makes it a two-minute job.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People in the US who want a quick read on their spending and subscriptions without opening a budgeting app.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">US only, on Free, Go, Plus and Pro, on web, iOS and Android. Bank data connects through Plaid and credit data through Experian; you can use either or both. Read-only: it can&#039;t move money or trade, and it&#039;s not financial advice.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/personal-finance-chatgpt/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/finances-voice-talk-about-your-money/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
