        <time datetime="2026-11-03" class="text-slate-400">Nov 3, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/make-your-muse-dance-share-instagram/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Forget TikTok dances: Meta&#039;s Muse can now dance on command, and you can post the clip straight to Instagram, Facebook or WhatsApp</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta&#039;s chief AI officer Alexandr Wang announced a new Muse feature: you can now make your Muse avatar dance and share the clip. In a Muse chat you tap your Muse, hit the share button at the top right, and send the dancing clip to Instagram, Facebook or WhatsApp, or save it to your phone. His post came with a demo video and passed 75,000 views within a day. It&#039;s a quick, playful way to try the Muse app or make something for your Stories.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It turns your Muse from a helper you chat with into something you can show off. Expect a wave of dancing Muse clips in your feed, and it&#039;s an easy, low-stakes way to try the app.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse users, creators who post Stories, and anyone looking for a fun first thing to do with Muse.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">In the Muse app chat, per Alexandr Wang&#039;s post. The post doesn&#039;t list plan or region limits; if your app has it, you&#039;ll see it under the share button.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/2117722403996569768" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Alexandr Wang (@alexandr_wang) on X ↗</a>
