                                <article id="antigravity-fortran-to-rust-174k-lines-59-minutes" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-03" class="text-slate-400">Nov 3, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-fortran-to-rust-174k-lines-59-minutes/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google&#039;s agents turned a 174,000-line Fortran ocean model into safe Rust in 59 minutes, and it ran faster</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">The Antigravity team used Gemini 4 Argon agents to port FVCOM, a coastal ocean model with 174,774 lines of Fortran across 264 files, to safe Rust in 59 minutes. Their write-up says the Rust version matched the original on 100 random seeds to 12 decimal places, uses 54% less memory, runs 1.88 times faster (883 ms down to 469 ms), shipped with 42 tests at 96.8% branch coverage, and caught 6 long-standing bugs on the way. The whole workflow is released as an open-source skill in Google&#039;s Skills repo on GitHub, which you run with /migrate-to-rust and a repo URL.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Old Fortran and C still run weather, climate and engineering code, and the people who wrote it are retiring. A repeatable, test-checked migration skill turns &#039;rewrite it someday&#039; into an afternoon experiment you can actually check.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Research software engineers, scientific computing teams and anyone maintaining legacy Fortran.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The skill is free and open source in Google&#039;s Skills repo on GitHub. Running it needs Antigravity with access to Gemini 4 Argon; model limits depend on your Google AI plan. Google&#039;s numbers are for FVCOM, so your own results will vary.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://antigravity.google/blog/modernizing-40-year-old-scientific-code-with-gemini-4-argon" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @antigravity on antigravity.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-fortran-to-rust-174k-lines-59-minutes/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Google%27s%20agents%20turned%20a%20174%2C000-line%20Fortran%20ocean%20model%20into%20safe%20Rust%20in%2059%20minutes%2C%20and%20it%20ran%20faster&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fantigravity-fortran-to-rust-174k-lines-59-minutes%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
