                                <article id="gpt-6-astra-designed-codex-device-under-a-week" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="research">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Research</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-03" class="text-slate-400">Nov 3, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/gpt-6-astra-designed-codex-device-under-a-week/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Two OpenAI staff and GPT-6 Astra designed a real gadget for talking to Codex in under a week, from case to circuit board</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI tested whether GPT-6 Astra could design a physical device without anyone editing its work directly. Astra wrote the requirements, designed the look and the enclosure, picked the electronic parts, laid out the circuit board, and wrote the firmware and software that connect the device to Codex. Two team members did it as a side project in under a week, and a contract manufacturer built a small batch of prototypes in under a month. OpenAI is upfront that it still took several rounds of review, because Astra didn&#039;t always account for the factory&#039;s tolerances and assembly details. The same post covers work with Chip Ganassi Racing on turning 3D scans into editable CAD and drawings, and with Mazda on vehicle design simulations.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> AI-written code is old news. An AI-designed circuit board and enclosure that a factory actually built shows these models moving into hardware, while the manufacturing gaps show why engineers still need to check the work.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Hardware engineers, makers and product teams curious about using ChatGPT or Codex for CAD, PCB and firmware work.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">An OpenAI research and engineering update, not a product launch. GPT-6 Astra is available in ChatGPT and Codex on supported plans. OpenAI is inviting engineering firms and software vendors to work with it on these workflows.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/accelerating-engineering-for-the-physical-world" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/gpt-6-astra-designed-codex-device-under-a-week/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Two%20OpenAI%20staff%20and%20GPT-6%20Astra%20designed%20a%20real%20gadget%20for%20talking%20to%20Codex%20in%20under%20a%20week%2C%20from%20case%20to%20circuit%20board&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fgpt-6-astra-designed-codex-device-under-a-week%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
