                                <article id="bot-negotiated-comcast-internet-bill" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-03" class="text-slate-400">Nov 3, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-negotiated-comcast-internet-bill/" class="hover:text-brand-600">His Grok Bot called Comcast, turned down 3 upsells and talked his internet bill down by almost $500 a year</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Creator Peter Yang asked his Grok Bot to phone Comcast about his internet bill. He told it he was paying $84 a month and that rival Sonic was offering fiber for $49, and to use that as leverage. In his recording, the Bot navigates the phone menu, answers small talk (&#039;I don&#039;t actually have eyes on the sky&#039; when the rep asked about the weather), turns down three upsells, and leans on the rival offer. He says it got him a lower price and faster speed, worth almost $500 a year. He also shares more prompts to try: cancelling a gym, waiting on hold with an airline, booking tables and getting contractor quotes.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Bill negotiation is the phone call everyone puts off. This shows the new calling feature handling a real, pushy retention call. It works best when you give the Bot the facts and your limits up front.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone in the US who hates waiting on hold or haggling over bills, cancellations and refunds.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Uses Grok Bot&#039;s built-in phone calls, which @bot announced on November 4. Calls currently work only with US numbers, and each call identifies itself as a virtual assistant. Results will vary by company and rep.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/petergyang/status/2117638801296380159" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @petergyang on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-negotiated-comcast-internet-bill/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
