                                <article id="opus-5-5-tops-semianalysis-gdpx-12-percent" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/opus-5-5-tops-semianalysis-gdpx-12-percent/" class="hover:text-brand-600">SemiAnalysis&#039; new GDPx benchmark: the best AI model scores just 12% on high-value expert work, and it&#039;s Claude Opus 5.5</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Research firm SemiAnalysis released GDPx, a benchmark of 206 agentic tasks across 11 high-value domains such as chip design, cyber, biology, finance and law, built with 14 data partners. The top score on its leaderboard is Claude Opus 5.5 at 12.0%, followed by Gemini 4 Carbon at 10.9%, GPT-6 Astra at 9.6% and Muse Wonder Full at 9.0%; Grok 4.7 sits at 3.9%. SemiAnalysis also says safety classifiers held back Opus 5.5 and GPT-6 Astra in cyber, biology and alignment tasks, so it publishes a second ranking with those domains removed, plus a cost-versus-score chart.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most benchmarks are close to maxed out. One where the leader scores 12% shows how much real expert work agents still can&#039;t finish, and the cost chart shows which model gives the most per dollar.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Teams choosing a model for agent work in technical or regulated fields, and anyone tired of saturated leaderboards.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">The leaderboard and per-domain comparison are free to browse at gdpx.semianalysis.com; the methodology write-up is on the SemiAnalysis Substack. Scores are SemiAnalysis&#039; own and will change as models are added.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://gdpx.semianalysis.com/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @SemiAnalysis on gdpx.semianalysis.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/opus-5-5-tops-semianalysis-gdpx-12-percent/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=SemiAnalysis%27%20new%20GDPx%20benchmark%3A%20the%20best%20AI%20model%20scores%20just%2012%25%20on%20high-value%20expert%20work%2C%20and%20it%27s%20Claude%20Opus%205.5&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fopus-5-5-tops-semianalysis-gdpx-12-percent%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
