                                <article id="google-flow-50-free-credits-every-day" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/google-flow-50-free-credits-every-day/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google Flow gives 50 free AI video credits every day, even without a subscription, but there&#039;s a catch at peak hours</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google&#039;s Flow help page says every account gets 50 Google Flow credits a day to generate images and video, with or without a subscription. The daily refresh is triggered by your first generation, and unused credits don&#039;t roll over. Non-subscribers can still make images and use the Flow Agent at any time, but may not be able to generate video during peak hours, roughly 2 PM to 5 PM UTC. Paid Google AI plans add a monthly pool on top: 200 extra credits on AI Plus and 1,000 on AI Pro.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most AI video tools give a one-off trial or nothing. A daily refill means you can keep testing ideas every day without paying.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Creators, marketers and hobbyists who want to try AI video and image generation before paying for a plan.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free; you must be 18 or older with a verified age and in a supported region. Google&#039;s getting-started page still lists a Google AI plan as a requirement, and qualifying Google Workspace business and education plans include Flow with 50 daily credits at no extra charge, so whether your free account opens Flow can vary. Free video can be unavailable roughly 2 PM to 5 PM UTC (6 PM to 9 PM Dubai time). Paid plans add 200 (AI Plus) to 25,000 (AI Ultra) monthly credits. Checked November 2, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://support.google.com/flow/answer/16526234?hl=en" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google Flow Help on support.google.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/google-flow-50-free-credits-every-day/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Google%20Flow%20gives%2050%20free%20AI%20video%20credits%20every%20day%2C%20even%20without%20a%20subscription%2C%20but%20there%27s%20a%20catch%20at%20peak%20hours&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fgoogle-flow-50-free-credits-every-day%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Write me five short video prompts for Google Flow for a product teaser, each under 8 seconds, with the camera move, setting and lighting spelled out." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-goldman-sachs-limits-to-engineers" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-goldman-sachs-limits-to-engineers/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Goldman Sachs just took Claude Code away from its traders and bankers, and some of them are not happy</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Bloomberg reports that Goldman Sachs has stopped most of its staff from using advanced AI coding tools after a review of productivity and risk. For months the bank let bankers use Anthropic&#039;s Claude Code and Microsoft&#039;s GitHub tools at work. Internal guidance updated in October now limits them to engineers only. Some traders who had used the tools to speed up jobs like watching client trading flows and building market models are frustrated by the change.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a clear sign that big companies are drawing a line between who may run coding agents and who may not. When non-engineers start writing and running code with an agent, risk and review teams get nervous fast.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone pushing coding agents beyond the engineering team at a bank, insurer or other regulated company, and the IT and risk people who have to sign off.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">This is a policy at one company, not a product change. Claude Code and GitHub Copilot are still sold normally to everyone else. Details come from Goldman&#039;s internal guidance as reported by Bloomberg on November 2, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://news.bloomberglaw.com/capital-markets/goldman-restricts-traders-and-bankers-from-using-some-ai-tools" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Bloomberg News (Todd Gillespie) on news.bloomberglaw.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-goldman-sachs-limits-to-engineers/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Goldman%20Sachs%20just%20took%20Claude%20Code%20away%20from%20its%20traders%20and%20bankers%2C%20and%20some%20of%20them%20are%20not%20happy&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-goldman-sachs-limits-to-engineers%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="anthropic-17-billion-quarter-amended-s1" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-17-billion-quarter-amended-s1/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Anthropic made $17.0 billion in one quarter, up 1,127% in a year, its new IPO filing shows</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic filed an amended S-1 with the SEC on November 2, 2026, adding numbers for the three months to September 30. Revenue was $17.0 billion, up 1,127% year over year, while compute and infrastructure costs grew 382% over the same period. The company swung to a $567 million operating loss, from $974 million of operating income in the June quarter. It now has more than 1,900 customers paying $1 million or more a year and more than 11,900 paying $100,000 or more. Its purchase and lease commitments, almost all for compute, total about $895.4 billion.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Claude&#039;s maker is growing faster than almost any software company on record, and it&#039;s spending close to a trillion dollars on future compute to keep up. Those numbers shape Claude prices, usage limits and how long the current plans last.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude users, developers betting on Anthropic&#039;s platform, and anyone following the AI IPO race.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">The filing is free to read on SEC EDGAR. No share price range has been set yet. This is a filing summary, not investment advice.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2130357/000162828026068676/0001628280-26-068676-index.htm" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Anthropic, PBC (SEC filing) on www.sec.gov ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-17-billion-quarter-amended-s1/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Anthropic%20made%20%2417.0%20billion%20in%20one%20quarter%2C%20up%201%2C127%25%20in%20a%20year%2C%20its%20new%20IPO%20filing%20shows&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fanthropic-17-billion-quarter-amended-s1%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-calacanis-40k-tools-2m-value-seven-jobs" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-calacanis-40k-tools-2m-value-seven-jobs/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Jason Calacanis says under $40K a year of AI tools now does $2M+ of work and has automated seven full-time jobs</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Investor and podcaster Jason Calacanis posted that he spends under $40,000 a year on tokens and subscriptions from Anthropic, Lovable, Grok Bot, ElevenLabs and a long tail of other tools, and gets more than $2 million in value across his companies LAUNCH and This Week in Startups. He says they&#039;ve automated at least seven full-time jobs and are about twice as fast at the average task. His advice: if you haven&#039;t spent around 30 hours a week with the products released in the last 90 days, you don&#039;t know how much has changed. The post passed 300,000 views within hours.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a rare public cost-versus-value number from someone running real companies. Even if the figures are rough, the ratio is why so many small teams are rebuilding their workflows around agents right now.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Founders, small-business owners and team leads deciding whether paid AI tools pay for themselves.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">His numbers are his own estimate and weren&#039;t broken down by tool. Every product he names has its own paid plans, and some have free tiers.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Jason/status/2117126320962351277" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Jason Calacanis (@Jason) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-calacanis-40k-tools-2m-value-seven-jobs/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
