                                <article id="open-duet-self-hosted-agent-team" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/open-duet-self-hosted-agent-team/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude Duet still has a waitlist, but Open Duet lets you run your own team of AI coworkers free on your computer</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Open Duet is an open-source workspace for building a team of named AI agents, each with a role, an engine, a workspace and memory you can review and edit. A lead agent can hand work to specialists, routines can run on a schedule, a webhook or by hand, and agents ask before acting, with modes like Ask first, Accept edits or Plan only. A routine never approves its own actions. You can connect GitHub, Gmail and Google Calendar through your own Composio key, and pair a phone app with your server to approve or deny tool calls. It&#039;s Apache-2.0 licensed and passed 6,500 GitHub stars.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Proactive agent teams are the hot new product category, and most official versions are waitlisted or need top-tier plans. This lets you try the idea today with accounts you already pay for.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and tinkerers who want an always-on agent team on their own machine or server.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (Apache-2.0), with a desktop app, self-hosting or a separate hosted service. It doesn&#039;t include a model: you bring your own engine and provider account, such as Claude or Codex. The project says it&#039;s in active development, so expect rough edges.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/Anil-matcha/open-duet" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Anil-matcha (GitHub) on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/open-duet-self-hosted-agent-team/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20Duet%20still%20has%20a%20waitlist%2C%20but%20Open%20Duet%20lets%20you%20run%20your%20own%20team%20of%20AI%20coworkers%20free%20on%20your%20computer&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fopen-duet-self-hosted-agent-team%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
