</article>
                                <article id="dots-getting-gpt-6-1-terra-more-people" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/dots-getting-gpt-6-1-terra-more-people/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI says dots are getting GPT-6.1 Terra, which is faster, has more personality and should bring dots to more people</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI&#039;s Tibo Sottiaux posted that the company is expanding the set of frontier models that power dots, its always-on ChatGPT agents, to include GPT-6 Astra and GPT-6.1 Terra, with more to come. He says Terra brings speed and a nicer personality, and will help OpenAI offer dots to more people. Today dots need ChatGPT Pro or Business Premium. Terra is OpenAI&#039;s cheaper, faster model for computer use, so running dots on it could make the agents affordable on lower plans. The post got about 5,000 likes and 1,000 replies within hours.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Dots have been locked to OpenAI&#039;s most expensive plans. A cheaper model underneath is usually how a premium feature reaches Plus and other plans.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">ChatGPT users waiting for dots on their plan, and current Pro users who want faster replies from their dot.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">No date, plan list or region was given. Dots are currently for eligible Pro and Business Premium users (not in the EEA, Switzerland or UK at launch). GPT-6.1 Terra is already in ChatGPT and the API.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: this is a plan shared on X by OpenAI&#039;s Tibo Sottiaux; it hasn&#039;t shipped yet and no timing has been announced.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/thsottiaux/status/2117283124833055196" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Tibo Sottiaux (@thsottiaux), OpenAI on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/dots-getting-gpt-6-1-terra-more-people/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%20says%20dots%20are%20getting%20GPT-6.1%20Terra%2C%20which%20is%20faster%2C%20has%20more%20personality%20and%20should%20bring%20dots%20to%20more%20people&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fdots-getting-gpt-6-1-terra-more-people%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="exa-free-10-dollars-search-credits-every-month" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/exa-free-10-dollars-search-credits-every-month/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Give your agent web search for free: Exa refills $10 of API credit every month, no card needed</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Exa, a search API built for AI agents, gives every new account $10 in free credits on sign-up, up to about 2,500 Lite searches, and resets the free balance to $10 on the first of every month. No payment method is needed. Teams that finish onboarding in the dashboard also get a one-time $10 bonus. Exa has a hosted MCP server and an agent skill, so Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and other MCP clients can use it as their web search tool. After the free credit, you pay per request, starting at $4 per 1,000 searches.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Good web search is one of the most useful tools you can give a coding or research agent, and a monthly free refill is enough for side projects and testing.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and hobbyists building agents in Claude Code, Codex, Cursor or their own code who need live web results.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free tier for everyone: $10 of credit at sign-up, reset to $10 on the first of each month, plus a one-time $10 onboarding bonus. No deadline is listed. Paid usage after that: Search from $4 per 1,000 requests, Contents $1 per 1,000 pages, Answer $5 per 1,000 requests. Checked on Exa&#039;s pricing page November 2, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://exa.ai/pricing" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Exa on exa.ai ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/exa-free-10-dollars-search-credits-every-month/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Give%20your%20agent%20web%20search%20for%20free%3A%20Exa%20refills%20%2410%20of%20API%20credit%20every%20month%2C%20no%20card%20needed&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fexa-free-10-dollars-search-credits-every-month%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
