                                <article id="messages-api-threads-send-only-new-messages" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/messages-api-threads-send-only-new-messages/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Stop resending the whole chat: Claude&#039;s new message threads let agents send only the new turn and start replying about a third faster</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Message threads are now in public beta on the Claude Messages API. Your first request sends the full conversation, system prompt and tools with a thread parameter set to create. After that, each request carries only the new messages plus the ID of Claude&#039;s previous response, and the API rebuilds the rest on the server. Anthropic says this cuts the wait before Claude starts answering by roughly a third on very long sessions. Threads are held encrypted in memory, expire five minutes after the last request, and fall back to a full replay if they&#039;ve gone (the SDK helper does that for you).</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Long-running coding and support agents can resend hundreds of thousands of tokens on every turn. Threads shrink each request and cut latency without changing how you&#039;re billed.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers building long-running agents on the Claude API, Claude Platform on AWS, Microsoft Foundry or Google Cloud.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Public beta on all models, using the anthropic-beta header message-threads-2026-08-12. Standard token prices and rate limits apply, since Claude still reads the full conversation each turn. Not available with zero data retention, HIPAA setups, Message Batches or token counting. Checked on Anthropic&#039;s docs November 3, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://claude.com/resources/articles/message-threads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Anthropic (@ClaudeDevs) on claude.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/messages-api-threads-send-only-new-messages/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Stop%20resending%20the%20whole%20chat%3A%20Claude%27s%20new%20message%20threads%20let%20agents%20send%20only%20the%20new%20turn%20and%20start%20replying%20about%20a%20third%20faster&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fmessages-api-threads-send-only-new-messages%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="anthropic-residency-paid-350k-no-ml-background" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-residency-paid-350k-no-ml-background/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Anthropic will pay senior engineers and professors $350K to $500K a year to switch into AI safety, no ML background needed</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic opened applications for the Anthropic Residency, a paid, fixed-term research program for established technical leaders who want to move into AI safety work. Placements last six weeks, three months or six months, with an Anthropic mentor, a dedicated compute budget and time to learn modern ML. Pay is $350,000 to $500,000 a year equivalent. Anthropic is looking for professors in quantitative fields, technical founders and staff-level engineers, and says you don&#039;t need a PhD, ML experience or papers. San Francisco is preferred, but remote is possible, especially for shorter stints.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a rare paid on-ramp into frontier AI research for experienced people from other fields, with mentors who lead Anthropic&#039;s alignment and interpretability teams.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Staff-level engineers, technical founders and professors in quantitative disciplines who want to work on AI safety full-time.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applications close November 22, 2026, through separate US and UK postings. Compensation is $350,000 to $500,000 per year equivalent, for the length of the placement. Checked on Anthropic&#039;s alignment blog November 3, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://alignment.anthropic.com/2026/anthropic-residency/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Anthropic (@AnthropicAI) on alignment.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-residency-paid-350k-no-ml-background/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
