                                <article id="openai-lifeval-everyday-tasks-benchmark" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-lifeval-everyday-tasks-benchmark/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI&#039;s new LifeVal test grades ChatGPT on real life, from kindergarten enrollment to diabetes meal plans, and its models score over 90%</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI published LifeVal, an evaluation built around the everyday jobs people most want help with: caregiving, health, school, household admin, personal finances, shopping and government services. It started from two large time-use studies and a new survey of 3,995 people. The sample tasks are things an assistant has to actually do, like shortlisting kindergartens after a move, planning meals for a parent with a new diabetes diagnosis or finding a home that fits a budget and commute. OpenAI shows its current models scoring between about 90% and 100% on the examples, and says it has used LifeVal for a year to push browser use, computer use and connectors.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most AI benchmarks test exam-style knowledge. LifeVal shows where OpenAI is steering ChatGPT: toward an agent that finishes errands, not just one that gives advice.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">ChatGPT users curious about what the agent can handle day to day, and anyone tracking how AI labs measure progress.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">LifeVal is a research evaluation, not a product feature. The browser, computer-use and connector features it measures are in ChatGPT, and some need paid plans. Checked on OpenAI&#039;s site November 3, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/lifeval/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: OpenAI (@OpenAI) on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-lifeval-everyday-tasks-benchmark/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
