    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/firecrawl-headless-clay-1000-free-credits/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Build lead lists inside ChatGPT or Claude for free: Firecrawl&#039;s &#039;headless Clay&#039; searches 250M people with 1,000 free credits a month</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Firecrawl launched what it calls headless Clay: lead and company enrichment you run by chatting with ChatGPT or Claude. Through the Firecrawl plugin, your agent can search more than 250 million people and 26 million companies, pull work emails, job history and company data, and assemble a prospect list in the same conversation where you plan outreach. Every account gets 1,000 free Firecrawl credits a month. Apollo&#039;s people search costs 0 credits, so you can find names for free and only spend credits on contact details (a FullEnrich work email costs 30 credits per email found).</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Enrichment tools usually mean another subscription and a separate dashboard. This puts prospect research in the chat you already use, with enough free credit to test it on a real list.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Founders, sales and recruiting folks who build prospect or candidate lists, and anyone who wants their agent to look up companies.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free for every Firecrawl account: 1,000 credits a month, no deadline listed. You need a signed-in account (it isn&#039;t part of the keyless tier). Paid plans add more credits; Firecrawl says it costs up to 88% less than Clay at scale. Checked on Firecrawl&#039;s changelog and blog November 3, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.firecrawl.dev/changelog/headless-clay" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Firecrawl on www.firecrawl.dev ↗</a>
