                                <article id="altman-next-gpt-10000-agents-four-days" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/altman-next-gpt-10000-agents-four-days/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Sam Altman says the model that ran as 10,000 agents for four straight days on Navier-Stokes is the next GPT, and it&#039;s coming soon</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Speaking at the ADIPEC energy conference in Abu Dhabi on November 2, Sam Altman said OpenAI&#039;s Navier-Stokes result came from about 10,000 agents of an upcoming GPT model working for roughly four days, and that this model is the next GPT to be released. He also said AI has gone from trailing the best scientists at the start of the year to mostly being smarter than them, while stressing people must stay in control. OpenAI&#039;s own September write-up describes on the order of 10,000 concurrent agents reaching the result in about 88 hours. The Clay Mathematics Institute hasn&#039;t recognised any solution.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s the clearest hint yet about OpenAI&#039;s next model: one built to run as huge teams of cooperating agents on long research problems.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone following OpenAI&#039;s roadmap, and teams planning work around multi-agent research tools.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">No release date, name or pricing has been announced. The math result is still disputed and hasn&#039;t been accepted by the Clay Mathematics Institute. Checked against OpenAI&#039;s Navier-Stokes post and conference coverage November 3, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://thursdaytimes.com/2026/11/02/science/technology/sam-altman-adipec-ai-smarter-scientists-adnoc-openai/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: The Thursday Times on thursdaytimes.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/altman-next-gpt-10000-agents-four-days/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Sam%20Altman%20says%20the%20model%20that%20ran%20as%2010%2C000%20agents%20for%20four%20straight%20days%20on%20Navier-Stokes%20is%20the%20next%20GPT%2C%20and%20it%27s%20coming%20soon&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Faltman-next-gpt-10000-agents-four-days%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
