    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-claude-code-agent-bus-talk-to-each-other/" class="hover:text-brand-600">This dev wired his Grok Bot and Claude Code into one &#039;agent bus&#039; so they message each other all day</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Developer Koshik showed a small local service he calls an agent bus that lets his Grok Bot and an active Claude Code session talk to each other. Every agent connects to the one service, which passes messages using MCP, the Agent Client Protocol, Claude channels and Grok Bot webhooks. He was replying to a popular post wishing a Grok Bot could spin up Claude sessions. In his demo video the bots hand work back and forth without him copying anything between windows.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most people still copy and paste between agents. A shared message bus lets a planning bot hand tasks to a coding agent and get results back on its own.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers who run both Grok Bot and Claude Code and want them to coordinate.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">A personal project shown on X, not a released product. You need Grok Bot (paid) and Claude Code (paid Claude plan or API).</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/rajkoshik/status/2117267913900220441" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Koshik (@rajkoshik) on X ↗</a>
