    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-data-bot-team-data-scientist-70-hours/" class="hover:text-brand-600">SpaceXSI gave every employee a Grok Bot data scientist, and it did about 70 hours of the data team&#039;s work in one week</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">SpaceXSI&#039;s data science team built Data Bot, a shared Team Bot in Grok Bot that anyone at the company can message or add to a Slack channel. The team taught it through skills: how core metrics like active users and revenue are defined and queried, how to investigate a spike or drop (checking holidays or logging changes first), how to run and read A/B tests, chart style rules, and dbt conventions. It queries the warehouse, writes reports and builds Databricks or Hex dashboards, and it has shared memory that the team approves before it&#039;s shared. PMs use it for usage questions, marketers to see what campaign recipients did next. SpaceXSI estimates it handled about 70 hours of data-team work last week.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a template for any small expert team that has become a bottleneck: teach one shared bot how you work, and everyone else gets answers in minutes while the experts keep the hard questions.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Data, analytics and ops teams fielding the same questions every day, and PMs and marketers waiting on them.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Team Bots are a Grok Bot feature; check what your Grok Bot plan includes. Data Bot itself is SpaceXSI&#039;s internal bot, so you&#039;d build your own with your warehouse and skills. SpaceXSI&#039;s team also used Databricks, Hex, dbt, Braze and Slack.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.ai/news/data-bot" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: SpaceXSI (Sally Xu) on x.ai ↗</a>
