                                <article id="anthropic-flashprove-prove-which-model-answered" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-flashprove-prove-which-model-answered/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Was that answer really from the model you paid for? Anthropic&#039;s open-source FlashProve can now prove it, at 110 tokens a second on one GPU</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic released FlashProve, an open-source research prototype for &#039;provable inference&#039;: a model provider commits to a set of weights, then attaches a cryptographic proof (a zkSNARK) showing a response came from exactly that model, without revealing the weights. Anyone can check a proof on a CPU, no GPU needed, in about 17 to 21 seconds. On Meta&#039;s 400B-parameter Llama 4 Maverick, one H100 generated proofs at about 110 tokens per second, with roughly 19 MB of proof per 1,024-token request, about 70-95 times the GPU time of normal inference. Anthropic says Claude helped build the system, and the key security properties are machine-checked in Lean. Code and proofs are under Apache 2.0.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Today you can&#039;t check whether a router or provider quietly swapped in a cheaper model, or whether someone tampered with the responses. Proofs like this could let customers, auditors and regulators verify it.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">AI security researchers, auditors and evaluators, and developers who buy model access through third-party routers.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">A research prototype on GitHub (anthropics/FlashProve) under Apache 2.0. Limits Anthropic lists: proofs cover contexts up to 1,024 tokens, greedy decoding on an integer version of the model, and Mixture-of-Experts models. Running the full example needs a large GPU machine; verifying a proof needs only a CPU.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/provable-inference" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-flashprove-prove-which-model-answered/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Was%20that%20answer%20really%20from%20the%20model%20you%20paid%20for%3F%20Anthropic%27s%20open-source%20FlashProve%20can%20now%20prove%20it%2C%20at%20110%20tokens%20a%20second%20on%20one%20GPU&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fanthropic-flashprove-prove-which-model-answered%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="openai-pando-git-backend-built-with-codex" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-pando-git-backend-built-with-codex/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI rebuilt its Git servers in 10 weeks with Codex agents, and pushes got about 5x faster</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI&#039;s engineering blog describes Pando, a new Git backend written in Rust that serves its internal code. One engineer designed the core, and teams of Codex agents wrote most of the implementation in about 10 weeks. Pando has been in production since April, keeps the standard Git protocol so normal clients still work, delivers close to a petabyte of Git data a day, and cut median push latency by nearly 80%, roughly five times faster. Pando itself is internal, but the client-side fixes live in OpenAI&#039;s Git fork and some have gone upstream.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> This is a big real-world example of agents building core infrastructure, not just app features, with one human owning the design. It&#039;s a useful pattern to copy: a person writes the architecture and the tests, and agents fill in the rest.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Platform and infrastructure engineers, and teams deciding how much of a big system to hand to coding agents.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">A write-up only: Pando is OpenAI-internal and can&#039;t be installed. The Git client changes are in OpenAI&#039;s public git fork, and some are already upstream in Git.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/scaling-git-at-openai/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-pando-git-backend-built-with-codex/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%20rebuilt%20its%20Git%20servers%20in%2010%20weeks%20with%20Codex%20agents%2C%20and%20pushes%20got%20about%205x%20faster&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fopenai-pando-git-backend-built-with-codex%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
