                                <article id="2-5-pro-flash-auto-route-december-1" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-02" class="text-slate-400">Nov 2, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/2-5-pro-flash-auto-route-december-1/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Still calling gemini-2.5-pro? From December 1, Google will quietly answer with 3.8 Flash instead</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google has deprecated gemini-2.5-pro and gemini-2.5-flash, and you can no longer pick them in Google AI Studio. From December 1, 2026, every API request that still names gemini-2.5-pro will be served by gemini-3.8-flash and billed at 3.8 Flash rates. Requests to gemini-2.5-flash will go to gemini-3.5-flash-lite at Flash-Lite rates. Your code won&#039;t get an error, but the newer models have breaking API changes: stricter function calling and thought_signature checks, thinking_level instead of thinking_budget, and some sampling parameters and prefilled model turns removed.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> A silent model swap can break agents and pipelines that rely on thinking_budget, prefilled turns or older function-calling behaviour, and the bill changes too. Migrating on your own schedule beats finding out from a failed job on December 1.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and teams with apps, agents or scripts still pinned to gemini-2.5-pro or gemini-2.5-flash.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to all Gemini API users. Both models are already gone from AI Studio&#039;s picker, and API auto-routing starts December 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/deprecations" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on ai.google.dev ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/2-5-pro-flash-auto-route-december-1/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Still%20calling%20gemini-2.5-pro%3F%20From%20December%201%2C%20Google%20will%20quietly%20answer%20with%203.8%20Flash%20instead&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2F2-5-pro-flash-auto-route-december-1%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Find every place this repo calls gemini-2.5-pro or gemini-2.5-flash. Migrate them to gemini-3.8-flash / gemini-3.5-flash-lite, replace thinking_budget with thinking_level, remove prefilled model turns and unsupported sampling params, and list anything I should test by hand." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
