                                <article id="nvidia-skillspector-scan-agent-skills-before-install" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/nvidia-skillspector-scan-agent-skills-before-install/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Installing a viral agent skill? NVIDIA&#039;s free scanner checks it first for prompt injection and data leaks</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">SkillSpector is NVIDIA&#039;s open-source security scanner for AI agent skills used by Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI and MCP servers. Point it at a Git repo, URL, zip, folder or single file and it checks for 71 risky patterns in 17 categories, including prompt injection, data exfiltration, privilege escalation, supply-chain risks and MCP tool poisoning. It runs fast static checks and an optional LLM review, then gives a 0 to 100 risk score with severity labels and a recommendation, in terminal, JSON, Markdown or SARIF. NVIDIA&#039;s research found vulnerabilities in 26.1% of 31,132 skills analyzed. The repo has more than 23,000 GitHub stars and is circulating again as new skills go viral on X.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Skills run with your agent&#039;s permissions, so one bad skill can read files or send data out. A one-minute scan before installing is cheap insurance.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone installing skills or MCP servers into Claude Code, Codex, Cursor or Gemini CLI, and teams that want a gate in CI.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (Apache 2.0); needs Python 3.12+ or Docker. The optional LLM review uses your own provider key. A risk score is a guide, not a guarantee. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/NVIDIA/SkillSpector" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @NVIDIA on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/nvidia-skillspector-scan-agent-skills-before-install/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Installing%20a%20viral%20agent%20skill%3F%20NVIDIA%27s%20free%20scanner%20checks%20it%20first%20for%20prompt%20injection%20and%20data%20leaks&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fnvidia-skillspector-scan-agent-skills-before-install%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Before I install this skill, run skillspector scan --no-llm on its folder, then walk me through the risk score and every high-severity finding and tell me whether it is safe to add." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="magpie-codex-on-deepseek-claude-code-on-kimi" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/magpie-codex-on-deepseek-claude-code-on-kimi/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Run Codex on DeepSeek and Claude Code on Kimi: magpie lets every coding agent use any model</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">magpie is a free, open-source app with a local gateway (127.0.0.1:3425) that sits between your coding agents and model providers. It translates between the OpenAI Chat, OpenAI Responses, Anthropic Messages and Gemini formats, so you can pick a model per agent: Codex on DeepSeek, Claude Code on Kimi, Gemini CLI on GLM, or a local model. It supports dozens of agents, can fail over between providers, and can mask keys, emails and card numbers before requests leave your computer. The repo has passed 27,000 GitHub stars and shipped a new release on November 1.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Each agent normally locks you into its own vendor&#039;s models and config files. One local switchboard makes it easy to try cheaper or faster models in the agent you already like.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers who use Codex, Claude Code or Gemini CLI and want to try DeepSeek, Kimi, GLM, OpenRouter or local Ollama models without rewiring each tool.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (MIT) for macOS and Linux, plus a Go install and Docker image. You pay your chosen providers as usual. magpie can also route through plans you&#039;re signed in to (Claude, ChatGPT and others); check each provider&#039;s terms before using a subscription outside its own apps, and you can turn subscription discovery off in Settings. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/yetone/magpie" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @yetone on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/magpie-codex-on-deepseek-claude-code-on-kimi/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Run%20Codex%20on%20DeepSeek%20and%20Claude%20Code%20on%20Kimi%3A%20magpie%20lets%20every%20coding%20agent%20use%20any%20model&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fmagpie-codex-on-deepseek-claude-code-on-kimi%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Help me set up magpie with a DeepSeek provider, then start Codex on it with the magpie command and confirm requests go through 127.0.0.1:3425 with my API key masked." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="hypergrok-trading-desk-paper-trading-team" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/hypergrok-trading-desk-paper-trading-team/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Build a seven-bot trading desk in Grok Bot, where no trade happens without your OK (paper trading only)</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">HyperGrok Trading Desk is an open-source template that sets up a team of seven Grok Bot roles: Desk Lead, Market Analyst, Research Analyst, Strategist, Risk Manager, Execution Trader and Trade Reviewer. Only the Execution Trader can ever hold exchange keys, the desk starts in research mode, and every trade needs your approval. It&#039;s a hands-on way to learn how multi-bot teams split work, check each other and keep a human in charge. Version 1.7.1 shipped on November 1, and a keyless demo shows the morning briefing without connecting any wallet.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a clear, working example of role separation in a bot team: analysts can&#039;t trade, the trader can&#039;t decide alone and a reviewer checks the result. That pattern carries over to any high-stakes workflow.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users who want to learn multi-bot team design on a realistic but low-risk example. Paper trading only, not investment advice.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (MIT). Needs Grok Bot, which is a paid plan; it also runs in Claude Code, Cursor, Codex and Gemini CLI. Paper trading only, not investment advice: stay in research mode or use a testnet wallet with play money, and never connect real funds to an experimental agent. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/galleonlabs/hypergrok-trading-desk" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Galleon Labs on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/hypergrok-trading-desk-paper-trading-team/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Build%20a%20seven-bot%20trading%20desk%20in%20Grok%20Bot%2C%20where%20no%20trade%20happens%20without%20your%20OK%20%28paper%20trading%20only%29&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fhypergrok-trading-desk-paper-trading-team%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Run the keyless HyperGrok opening_bell.py demo for ETH and explain what each of the seven desk roles would do with this briefing, without connecting any wallet or exchange keys." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="for-open-source-6-months-claude-ultra-free" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/for-open-source-6-months-claude-ultra-free/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Maintain a package people depend on? Anthropic gives you 6 months of Claude Ultra free</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic&#039;s Claude for Open Source program now gives accepted open-source maintainers and contributors 6 months of Claude Ultra for free. Ultra is the new name for the $200-a-month top consumer plan (it used to be Max 20x), so the page was updated after the October 30 rename. You qualify through any one route: packages with 500+ dependent repos, 100+ dependent packages or 200,000+ monthly downloads; a listed committer role on a big foundation or language project; 100+ merged pull requests into repos you don&#039;t own in the last 12 months; a repo with 20+ outside contributors in a year; or a repo with an OpenSSF criticality score of 0.4 or higher.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Ultra is Claude&#039;s $200-a-month plan, so 6 months is worth about $1,200 of Claude Code and chat usage for people who keep open-source software running. The bar is wider than most people think: 100 merged PRs to other people&#039;s repos in a year is enough.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Open-source maintainers, core contributors to foundation or language projects, prolific outside contributors and anyone keeping a widely used package alive.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free for 6 months for accepted applicants; apply on claude.com/contact-sales/claude-for-oss. No closing date is listed. When the 6 months end, Anthropic emails you; a previous paid plan resumes at its old rate unless you cancel, otherwise you drop to the free plan. Claude Ultra normally costs $200 a month. Checked November 2, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://claude.com/contact-sales/claude-for-oss" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on claude.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/for-open-source-6-months-claude-ultra-free/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Maintain%20a%20package%20people%20depend%20on%3F%20Anthropic%20gives%20you%206%20months%20of%20Claude%20Ultra%20free&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Ffor-open-source-6-months-claude-ultra-free%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Check my GitHub profile and packages against the Claude for Open Source routes (dependents, downloads, merged outside PRs, outside contributors, OpenSSF score) and tell me which route I fit and what links to include." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-picked-and-bought-surprise-gift-x-money" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-picked-and-bought-surprise-gift-x-money/" class="hover:text-brand-600">She gave Grok Bot $100 and said &quot;surprise me.&quot; A gift showed up at her door</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Investor Justine Moore (a16z) told her Grok Bot to surprise her with a present, let it spend up to $100 from her X Money account, and asked it to use her tweets and their past chats to choose. The package later arrived, with a small Halloween extra. Elon Musk quoted the post on November 1 saying Grok Bot will research gifts your friends and family would love and buy them, and the pair of posts passed 800,000 views. It&#039;s an early public example of an agent that picks, pays and ships on its own inside a hard budget.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Gift shopping is research plus taste plus checkout, and this shows an agent doing all three with a spending cap. The holiday season is a natural test for it, and the $100 limit is the pattern to copy.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users in the US with X Money, and anyone curious how far to trust an agent with a card.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot needs an eligible X or Grok plan. X Money is only offered where X supports it (currently US states), and Grok Bot connects it when you connect X. Musk&#039;s post describes the gift use case; xAI hasn&#039;t published a separate gift-shopping feature page.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
