    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/meta-humanoid-robot-max-fourier-body-for-muse/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Meta reportedly built &quot;Max&quot;, a 106-pound humanoid robot meant to give Muse a body, in three months</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">According to The Information, Meta built a humanoid prototype called Max with Shanghai robotics company Fourier in about three months. Max is reportedly about 1.5 m tall and 48 kg, runs on Nvidia&#039;s Jetson Thor chip, and has a face display, speakers and five-fingered hands for small objects. Work on Max 2, with a new torso, better hands, a projector and stair sensors, began in September. The report says Meta&#039;s leadership sees humanoids as a physical form for its Muse agent doing household chores. Meta told the outlet the work is internal research and it has no plans to sell the units.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Muse already shops and plans for people on screens. A robot body is the next step in the race to put assistants into homes, and Meta is now reportedly building real hardware for it.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People following Meta&#039;s Muse, home robotics and where AI agents go after the phone.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Not a product: Meta calls it internal research with no plans to sell these units and no launch date. Muse itself is available now in Meta&#039;s apps.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/lukas_m_ziegler/status/2116827905963524539" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @lukas_m_ziegler on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/meta-humanoid-robot-max-fourier-body-for-muse/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Meta%20reportedly%20built%20%22Max%22%2C%20a%20106-pound%20humanoid%20robot%20meant%20to%20give%20Muse%20a%20body%2C%20in%20three%20months&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fmeta-humanoid-robot-max-fourier-body-for-muse%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
