                                <article id="anthropic-engineer-fighting-game-claude-generated-sprites" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-engineer-fighting-game-claude-generated-sprites/" class="hover:text-brand-600">An Anthropic engineer is building a fighting game with Claude, and just added a fire-kicking taekwondo master</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Thariq, who works on Claude Code at Anthropic, keeps sharing his side project: an elemental fighting game built with AI. On November 1 he added a taekwondo master who fights with fire and switched the art from 3D models to generated sprites. Earlier posts show Claude building him a custom animation editor to tune a jump, and a &quot;vibe UI&quot; pass made with Claude plus GPT for images. His rule from the first post: don&#039;t outsource the creative part to AI, use it to bring your own vision to life.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a practical template for solo game making: let the agent build tools (an animation editor, a UI pass) while you keep the design decisions. Getting AI to build the editor, not just the game, is the trick worth copying for any creative project.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Indie game developers, hobbyists and anyone using Claude Code for creative side projects.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code is included with Claude Pro, Max and Ultra plans. Image generation for sprites needs a separate image model.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/trq212/status/2116976789046350040" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @trq212 on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-engineer-fighting-game-claude-generated-sprites/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=An%20Anthropic%20engineer%20is%20building%20a%20fighting%20game%20with%20Claude%2C%20and%20just%20added%20a%20fire-kicking%20taekwondo%20master&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fanthropic-engineer-fighting-game-claude-generated-sprites%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
