                                <article id="code-levelsio-vlog-edit-58-minutes-to-10" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="video">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Video</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-levelsio-vlog-edit-58-minutes-to-10/" class="hover:text-brand-600">levelsio dumped 58 minutes of DJI clips into a folder and Claude Code cut them into a 10-minute vlog on its own</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Indie maker Pieter Levels (levelsio) copied 14 clips, about 58 minutes of footage from his DJI camera, into a folder, opened Claude Code with Opus 5.5 there and asked it to edit them into a 10-minute vlog for X and YouTube. Claude transcribed his speech locally with mlx-whisper, pulled frames into contact-sheet grids so it could see each clip, used a voice-matching model to tell his voice from other people&#039;s, picked the cuts as a JSON list of clip, start and end times, made thumbnails with OpenCV face detection and burned captions in with Pillow. He says he only made a few adjustments and didn&#039;t ask for any of that tooling.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Editing is the part that stops most people from vlogging. A coding agent that can read transcripts, look at frames and write a cut list turns a long afternoon of trimming into a short review.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Creators, founders and anyone with a camera roll of raw clips who wants a rough cut without learning an editor.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code on a paid Claude plan; he said it used a tiny slice of his $100 a month plan. He ran it on a MacBook Pro, where mlx-whisper uses Apple&#039;s MLX; other machines need a different Whisper build. Your own results will vary with footage and prompts.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/levelsio/status/2116959423117857026" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @levelsio on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-levelsio-vlog-edit-58-minutes-to-10/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=levelsio%20dumped%2058%20minutes%20of%20DJI%20clips%20into%20a%20folder%20and%20Claude%20Code%20cut%20them%20into%20a%2010-minute%20vlog%20on%20its%20own&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-levelsio-vlog-edit-58-minutes-to-10%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Can you edit these clips into a 10 minute vlog for X and YouTube? Transcribe what I say, look at frames from each clip, pick the best parts, and show me the cut list before you render." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-poteto-tibo-game-1150-prs-4-days" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-poteto-tibo-game-1150-prs-4-days/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One developer, 4 days, about 1,150 PRs: a full arcade game you can play inside an X post, built with Grok Bot running Cursor</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Developer Lauren (poteto) shipped tibo&#039;s game at tibo.dog, a browser arcade game made with Grok Bot orchestrating a Cursor project. She says it took 4 days as a side project and landed around 1,150 pull requests. Her rules are the interesting part: every bug she found became a lint rule, TLA+ formal specs checked the story, cutscene and game state machines, per-frame code lives in .hot.ts files where allocations are banned, and code comments are banned in favour of better names and tests. The music and pixel art are generated by code, the simulation is deterministic so high scores are replayed server-side, and the first download stays around 124 KB gzipped.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It shows how a solo builder can keep an agent fast and safe at once: turn every mistake into an automatic check, so the agent can&#039;t repeat it on the next PR.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers running coding agents on real projects, and game makers curious how far a weekend side project can go.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The game is free to play at tibo.dog. Grok Bot and Cursor need their own accounts and plans. Her workflow is her own; she says about 80% of her time went into playtesting and feeding notes back to the bot.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/poteto/status/2117004709198475365" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: poteto (Lauren) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-poteto-tibo-game-1150-prs-4-days/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=One%20developer%2C%204%20days%2C%20about%201%2C150%20PRs%3A%20a%20full%20arcade%20game%20you%20can%20play%20inside%20an%20X%20post%2C%20built%20with%20Grok%20Bot%20running%20Cursor&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-poteto-tibo-game-1150-prs-4-days%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="This bug just slipped through. Write a lint rule or test that would have caught it, add it to CI, and fix any existing code that breaks the new rule." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
