</article>
                                <article id="bot-elon-serving-cost-unsustainably-high" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-elon-serving-cost-unsustainably-high/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Asked for a Grok Bot usage reset, Elon Musk said the cost of serving it was &quot;unsustainably high relative to revenue&quot;</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">After a user asked Elon Musk on X for a Grok Bot reset because lots of people said their usage ran out fast this week, Musk replied that the cost of serving Grok Bot was unsustainably high relative to revenue. The reply drew millions of views and thousands of replies, many from users saying they had hit their weekly cap early and were waiting for it to refresh. No reset was announced in the reply, and no new limit numbers were published with it.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a rare direct statement that tighter Grok Bot usage reflects cost, not a glitch, so heavy users shouldn&#039;t count on a quick reset.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot subscribers who rely on it daily and keep hitting their weekly usage cap.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to Grok Bot plans; check your own usage page for your current allowance and refresh date, since limits differ by plan.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2116992258520064397" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @elonmusk on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-elon-serving-cost-unsustainably-high/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Asked%20for%20a%20Grok%20Bot%20usage%20reset%2C%20Elon%20Musk%20said%20the%20cost%20of%20serving%20it%20was%20%22unsustainably%20high%20relative%20to%20revenue%22&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-elon-serving-cost-unsustainably-high%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
