                                <article id="github-game-off-2026-shift-free-jam" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-game-off-2026-shift-free-jam/" class="hover:text-brand-600">GitHub Game Off 2026 is open: a free month-long game jam with the theme SHIFT, and your AI coding agent can help you ship</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">GitHub&#039;s annual Game Off jam is running through November with the theme SHIFT: shift gears, shift perspectives, shift reality, or a game played with the Shift keys. Anyone can enter for free, solo or as a team, using any language, engine or tools, as long as the game&#039;s source is in a public GitHub repository and the game is submitted on itch.io. Entrants then rate each other&#039;s games in categories including Overall, Gameplay, Graphics, Audio, Innovation and Theme Interpretation.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> A month, a theme and a deadline are exactly what a side project needs, and with coding agents a solo builder can now ship a lot more game in that time.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers, artists and first-time game makers who want a deadline and an audience for a small game.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free to enter with free GitHub and itch.io accounts. Submissions run from November 1 until December 1, 2026 at 13:37 PST (1:37 AM Dubai time on December 2), and voting runs until January 1, 2027 at 13:37 PST. The jam page doesn&#039;t state a specific AI policy, so check it and the community tab before relying on generated art or audio. Checked November 2, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://itch.io/jam/game-off-2026" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: GitHub on itch.io on itch.io ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-game-off-2026-shift-free-jam/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=GitHub%20Game%20Off%202026%20is%20open%3A%20a%20free%20month-long%20game%20jam%20with%20the%20theme%20SHIFT%2C%20and%20your%20AI%20coding%20agent%20can%20help%20you%20ship&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fgithub-game-off-2026-shift-free-jam%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Give me three small game ideas for a game jam with the theme SHIFT that one person can finish in a month, with the core mechanic, controls and a simple art style for each." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="hyperframes-html-to-video-agent-skills" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="video">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Video</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/hyperframes-html-to-video-agent-skills/" class="hover:text-brand-600">HyperFrames by HeyGen is free and open source: install its skills and ask Claude Code to make you a video</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">HyperFrames is HeyGen&#039;s open-source framework that turns HTML, CSS, media and seekable animations into MP4 videos, with skills that teach coding agents the whole production loop: plan the video, write the HTML, wire the animations, add media, lint, preview and render. It&#039;s Apache 2.0 licensed, has a Claude Code plugin and works with Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI and other agents that support skills. It came top of a widely shared list of GitHub repos that turn Claude into a motion designer.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Because the video is code, your agent can edit it like any other file, and every render comes out the same, which makes revisions fast.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers, founders and marketers who want product intros, explainers or social clips without After Effects.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (Apache 2.0); needs Node.js 22 or newer. You still pay for whatever coding agent you use. Checked November 2, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: HeyGen on GitHub on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/hyperframes-html-to-video-agent-skills/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=HyperFrames%20by%20HeyGen%20is%20free%20and%20open%20source%3A%20install%20its%20skills%20and%20ask%20Claude%20Code%20to%20make%20you%20a%20video&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fhyperframes-html-to-video-agent-skills%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Using /hyperframes, create a 10-second product intro with a fade-in title, a background video and subtle background music." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="jelly-rubiks-cube-four-ai-same-prompt" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/jelly-rubiks-cube-four-ai-same-prompt/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Same prompt, four AIs, one jelly Rubik&#039;s cube: Gemini 4 Argon finished for $0.55 while Opus 5.5 cost $11.10</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">An X user gave four models the same prompt, a Rubik&#039;s cube made of jelly, and posted the results side by side with what each run cost and how long it took: DeepSeek V4.1 Flash at $6.36 and 1 hour, Claude Opus 5.5 at $11.10 and 1 hour 23 minutes, GPT-6 Astra at $4.27 and 1 hour 13 minutes, and Gemini 4 Argon at $0.55 and 32 minutes. In his view DeepSeek&#039;s cube looked the most like jelly this time, after an earlier round where Astra made plastic and Gemini treated jelly as a colour.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Single-prompt head-to-heads show how much price and time vary for the same creative task, and that the most expensive model isn&#039;t automatically the best result.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone choosing a model for 3D, animation or creative coding work who cares about cost as much as looks.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Each model needs its own account or API access. The costs and times are from one person&#039;s runs and will vary with your setup and prompt.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/0xRhinoX/status/2116950986661171337" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @0xRhinoX on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/jelly-rubiks-cube-four-ai-same-prompt/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Same%20prompt%2C%20four%20AIs%2C%20one%20jelly%20Rubik%27s%20cube%3A%20Gemini%204%20Argon%20finished%20for%20%240.55%20while%20Opus%205.5%20cost%20%2411.10&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fjelly-rubiks-cube-four-ai-same-prompt%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Build an interactive 3D Rubik&#039;s cube made of jelly in a single HTML file with three.js: soft wobbly physics when it turns, translucent glossy material, and drag-to-rotate controls." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-statementbridge-saas-built-by-agent-stack" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-statementbridge-saas-built-by-agent-stack/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One founder&#039;s paid SaaS is built by a chain of agents: Grok Bot manages, Claude Code writes the code, Codex reviews it</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Erwin Fennema says he built StatementBridge, a niche financial software product, almost entirely with AI. It started as an internal tool and is now a live SaaS with paying customers. His setup splits the work between agents: Grok Bot manages development and gives instructions, Claude Code writes the code inside Cursor, Codex reviews the code separately, and automated tests run before GitHub deploys it to Render. His post passed 600,000 views.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Using one agent to write and a different one to review copies how real teams catch mistakes. Adding tests before every deploy is what makes a setup like this safe enough to charge customers for.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Solo founders and small teams who want to ship a real product with agents and still keep quality checks in place.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Each tool needs its own plan: Grok Bot, Cursor with Claude Code, Codex, GitHub and Render. He hasn&#039;t shared his prompts or costs. Results depend on your product and how good your tests are.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/erwin_fennema/status/2116981289613971587" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Erwin Fennema (@erwin_fennema) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-statementbridge-saas-built-by-agent-stack/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=One%20founder%27s%20paid%20SaaS%20is%20built%20by%20a%20chain%20of%20agents%3A%20Grok%20Bot%20manages%2C%20Claude%20Code%20writes%20the%20code%2C%20Codex%20reviews%20it&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-statementbridge-saas-built-by-agent-stack%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Review this pull request as a strict senior engineer. List bugs, security issues and missing tests, ranked by severity. Don&#039;t rewrite the code; just tell me what must change before merge." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
