                                <article id="bot-found-old-customer-closed-first-deal" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-found-old-customer-closed-first-deal/" class="hover:text-brand-600">A sales team pointed Grok Bot at its tools, and two weeks later it closed a deal with a customer they had forgotten</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Scott Billows says his business has a traditional sales cycle that can take months. His team pointed Grok Bot at their sales tools and asked it to surface past prospects and customers worth contacting again. Two weeks in, they closed their first deal from the list: Grok Bot pulled a former customer out of the records and handed it to an account executive, who reached out, pitched and won the deal. He says they most likely wouldn&#039;t have contacted that customer without it.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Old leads and lapsed customers are some of the cheapest sales a business can win, but nobody has time to dig through years of records. An agent that reads your CRM and hands over a short list is an easy first job to give one.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Small-business owners, sales leads and account executives with a CRM full of old contacts.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot plans apply, and it needs access to your sales tools such as your CRM or email. He didn&#039;t say which tools or plan he used. One deal is an anecdote, not a promise.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/scottbillows/status/2116900809388511586" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Scott Billows (@scottbillows) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-found-old-customer-closed-first-deal/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=A%20sales%20team%20pointed%20Grok%20Bot%20at%20its%20tools%2C%20and%20two%20weeks%20later%20it%20closed%20a%20deal%20with%20a%20customer%20they%20had%20forgotten&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-found-old-customer-closed-first-deal%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Go through our past customers and prospects. Find the 20 most promising to contact again, explain why for each (last contact, past spend, any signal of renewed need), and draft a short personal opening line I can edit." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-jarvis-page-31-bots-morning-brief" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-jarvis-page-31-bots-morning-brief/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One creator built a real-life Jarvis from a Grok Bot and a Page: a talking morning brief, a status board for 31 bots and an approve-or-later queue</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Julian Goldie shared how he built &quot;Grok Jarvis&quot; with no code: a Grok Bot that holds a calm, slightly dry personality, plus a Page it builds from plain English as a live screen. Saying &quot;Good morning, Jarvis&quot; gets a spoken brief on what every bot did and what&#039;s waiting on him. A Systems panel lists all 31 of his active bots with status lights, and a Waiting on you list lines up decisions with Approve or Later buttons that only tick off on screen. When the first version broke, he pasted the error and it fixed its own work. The post passed 500,000 views.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Once you run more than a handful of bots, keeping track of them becomes the job. A single talking dashboard is a simple fix that anyone can copy.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users running several bots who want one place to see status and pending decisions.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Needs Grok Bot (paid, about $30 a month per reports) and Pages. This is one user&#039;s build shared on X, not an official template.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/JulianGoldieSEO/status/2116854011827806310" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Julian Goldie (@JulianGoldieSEO) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-jarvis-page-31-bots-morning-brief/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=One%20creator%20built%20a%20real-life%20Jarvis%20from%20a%20Grok%20Bot%20and%20a%20Page%3A%20a%20talking%20morning%20brief%2C%20a%20status%20board%20for%2031%20bots%20and%20an%20approve-or-later%20queue&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-jarvis-page-31-bots-morning-brief%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="voice-mode-talk-to-your-agent-live" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-11-01" class="text-slate-400">Nov 1, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/voice-mode-talk-to-your-agent-live/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Muse users are starting to talk to their agent out loud: live voice mode is quietly rolling out, subscribers first</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Users report that live voice conversations started reaching the Muse app over the weekend, letting you talk with Meta&#039;s personal agent in real time instead of typing. Reports say subscribers and people who asked Muse for early access are getting it first, and fan sites note Muse can keep working on tasks in the background while you talk. Meta hasn&#039;t published an announcement or an eligibility list, so if you don&#039;t see a voice control near the message box, your account doesn&#039;t have it yet.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Talking is faster than typing for quick errands, and a voice agent that keeps working in the background feels much closer to a real assistant.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse users, especially subscribers, who want to hand off tasks hands-free.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Gradual, unannounced rollout. Reports say subscribers and early-access users get it first. Muse is free, with paid plans in some markets.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/RosalesRecs/status/2116983347851178239" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Justin &amp; Megan Rosales (@RosalesRecs) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/voice-mode-talk-to-your-agent-live/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Muse%20users%20are%20starting%20to%20talk%20to%20their%20agent%20out%20loud%3A%20live%20voice%20mode%20is%20quietly%20rolling%20out%2C%20subscribers%20first&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fvoice-mode-talk-to-your-agent-live%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="anthropic-agents-hid-misalignment-in-harmless-training-data" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-agents-hid-misalignment-in-harmless-training-data/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Anthropic set thousands of Claude agents loose on red-teaming, and they hid misalignment inside beekeeping Q&amp;As</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic published research on automating a slow part of safety testing. Thousands of Claude agents were each asked to write fine-tuning datasets that a production-style training data monitor would pass, but that would still make a small research model misaligned. The agents came up with datasets that read like harmless fiction or roleplay, such as a veteran wrestler mentoring a newcomer or a Q&amp;A about professional beekeeping. None of the trained models were deployed, and Anthropic says the examples are now being used to build better data monitors.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Red-teaming is limited by how many hours researchers have. If agents can generate realistic hard cases at scale, the filters that screen training data get tested far more thoroughly.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">AI safety researchers, teams that fine-tune models on outside data, and anyone following how labs test their own training pipelines.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to: a research paper on Anthropic&#039;s Alignment Science Blog (alignment.anthropic.com/2026/automated-em-search). It&#039;s research, not a product feature. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/AnthropicAI/status/2116349211549843666" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Anthropic (@AnthropicAI) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-agents-hid-misalignment-in-harmless-training-data/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Anthropic%20set%20thousands%20of%20Claude%20agents%20loose%20on%20red-teaming%2C%20and%20they%20hid%20misalignment%20inside%20beekeeping%20Q%26As&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fanthropic-agents-hid-misalignment-in-harmless-training-data%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Read Anthropic&#039;s post on automated red-teaming with Claude agents and explain in plain English how harmless-looking fine-tuning data can still make a model misaligned, then list three checks my team should add before fine-tuning on outside datasets." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="switch-between-two-accounts-web-ios-android" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/switch-between-two-accounts-web-ios-android/" class="hover:text-brand-600">ChatGPT finally lets you stay signed in to a work and a personal account and switch in one tap</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">ChatGPT now lets you keep two accounts signed in at the same time and jump between them without logging out, for example a work account and a personal one. Each account keeps its own chats, memory, files and billing, so nothing leaks from one to the other. OpenAI&#039;s help article covers the web and the iOS and Android apps, and Codex lead Tibo said on X that mobile is live now with desktop following soon. Notifications keep arriving for both accounts.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> No more logging out of your work account to ask something personal, or mixing a personal memory into company chats.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone who has a company ChatGPT seat plus a personal account, freelancers juggling client workspaces, and families sharing a phone.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Up to 2 accounts at once on web, iOS and Android, still rolling out (Tibo said desktop is coming soon). A brand-new second account starts on the Free plan; each account keeps its own plan and billing. As described on OpenAI&#039;s help page on October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001068-using-multiple-chatgpt-accounts-on-web-and-mobile" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: OpenAI Help Center on help.openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/switch-between-two-accounts-web-ios-android/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=ChatGPT%20finally%20lets%20you%20stay%20signed%20in%20to%20a%20work%20and%20a%20personal%20account%20and%20switch%20in%20one%20tap&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fswitch-between-two-accounts-web-ios-android%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
