                                <article id="agent-desktop-vercel-computer-use-any-coding-agent" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/agent-desktop-vercel-computer-use-any-coding-agent/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Vercel&#039;s free agent-desktop lets Claude Code drive your Mac, Windows or Linux apps in the background, each agent with its own cursor</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Vercel Labs open-sourced agent-desktop, described as &quot;agent-browser, for your whole computer&quot;. It&#039;s a command-line tool and C library that lets any coding agent, such as Claude Code, Codex or Cursor, use desktop apps by reading the operating system&#039;s accessibility tree instead of guessing from screenshots. A snapshot gives every button and field a short reference, the agent clicks or types on that reference, then snapshots again to check the result. It runs in the background while you keep working, and several agents can share one machine, each with its own cursor.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Your agent can now test the desktop app it just built, or handle a task in an app with no API, while reading structured text that costs far fewer tokens than screenshots.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers building desktop apps, and anyone who wants a coding agent to operate native apps on their own computer.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source from Vercel Labs (github.com/vercel-labs/agent-desktop). Supports macOS 13+, Windows 10 1809+ and Linux with AT-SPI (Ubuntu 24.04+). macOS needs Accessibility permission. It&#039;s an experiment, so try it on a test machine or throwaway app first. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/ctatedev/status/2116323148706771302" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Chris Tate (@ctatedev), Vercel Labs on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/agent-desktop-vercel-computer-use-any-coding-agent/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Vercel%27s%20free%20agent-desktop%20lets%20Claude%20Code%20drive%20your%20Mac%2C%20Windows%20or%20Linux%20apps%20in%20the%20background%2C%20each%20agent%20with%20its%20own%20cursor&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fagent-desktop-vercel-computer-use-any-coding-agent%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Use agent-desktop to open the Notes app, create a note titled &quot;Test&quot; with today&#039;s date, then snapshot again and confirm the note exists. Don&#039;t touch any other app." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="opus-4-8-fast-mode-ends-nov-30-switch-opus-5-5" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/opus-4-8-fast-mode-ends-nov-30-switch-opus-5-5/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Opus 4.8 fast mode stops working November 30: switch to Opus 5.5 before your requests start failing</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Claude Code 2.1.316 says fast mode on Opus 4.8 has been deprecated since October 30 and will be removed on November 30, 2026, after which those requests return an error. Anthropic points users to Opus 5.5, which has its own fast mode. The same release adds CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_EFFORT so subagents can get their own effort level instead of copying your session&#039;s, and CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_ULTRATHINK to switch the ultrathink keyword off entirely.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Scripts, CI jobs or settings files that still pin Opus 4.8 with fast mode will break on November 30 unless you change them.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code users and teams who set Opus 4.8 fast mode in settings, scripts or automation.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to: Claude Code users on Opus 4.8 fast mode. Deprecated October 30, removed November 30, 2026, as listed in the Claude Code changelog for 2.1.316, checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Claude Code changelog (Anthropic) on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/opus-4-8-fast-mode-ends-nov-30-switch-opus-5-5/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Opus%204.8%20fast%20mode%20stops%20working%20November%2030%3A%20switch%20to%20Opus%205.5%20before%20your%20requests%20start%20failing&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fopus-4-8-fast-mode-ends-nov-30-switch-opus-5-5%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Search this repo and my config files for any use of Opus 4.8 with fast mode, list every place it appears, and propose the change to Opus 5.5 so nothing breaks after November 30, 2026." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="watermark-older-models" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/watermark-older-models/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude&#039;s invisible text watermark is coming to older models too, including Opus 4.7 and Sonnet 4.6</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic says Claude now weaves an invisible watermark into the text it writes, to meet the EU AI Act&#039;s transparency code. Models launched since August 2, 2026 carry it from day one, and Anthropic is now adding it to earlier models such as Opus 4.7, Opus 4.6 and Sonnet 4.6. It applies across the API, the Claude apps, Claude Code and Cowork, and on AWS, Google Cloud and Microsoft Foundry. Generated image files also get C2PA Content Credentials. Detection is in private preview for regulators, media, researchers and similar groups.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you publish or ship Claude-written text, it may now carry a hidden mark that eligible groups can detect. Anthropic notes very short or heavily edited text is harder to detect, and a mark doesn&#039;t prove who wrote the ideas.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Teams shipping Claude output to customers, writers and publishers, and anyone handling EU AI Act compliance.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to: supported Claude models on the API, Claude apps, Claude Code, Cowork and cloud partners, worldwide. Older models are being added in stages; Anthropic&#039;s email to API customers reportedly gave November 3 as the date. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/16266773-how-claude-marks-ai-generated-content" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on support.claude.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/watermark-older-models/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%27s%20invisible%20text%20watermark%20is%20coming%20to%20older%20models%20too%2C%20including%20Opus%204.7%20and%20Sonnet%204.6&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fwatermark-older-models%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Read Anthropic&#039;s announcement about Claude&#039;s text watermark and summarize which models and products carry it, what the watermark is for under the EU AI Act, and what it means for text my team publishes." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="planassist-council-planning-58-percent" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/planassist-council-planning-58-percent/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google DeepMind&#039;s PlanAssist cut planning officers&#039; assessment time by up to 58% in three UK councils</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google DeepMind built PlanAssist with the UK government to help council planning officers work through household planning applications. In pilots at Barnet, Camden and Dorset, it cut the time officers spent assessing cases by up to 58%, and over 70% of its draft reports were approved with no edits. It&#039;s now expanding to 12 more councils for a 12-month beta, with a goal of reaching every English council in 2027 if testing goes well. Officers still make every decision.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Planning backlogs hold up home extensions and building work for weeks. A tool that drafts the paperwork while humans keep the final say is a practical template for AI in government.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">UK homeowners waiting on planning decisions, council staff, and anyone following AI in public services.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to: pilot and beta councils in England only (Barnet, Camden, Dorset, plus 12 more in a 12-month beta). Not a public product. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/GoogleDeepMind/status/2116524000977285321" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google DeepMind (@GoogleDeepMind) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/planassist-council-planning-58-percent/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Google%20DeepMind%27s%20PlanAssist%20cut%20planning%20officers%27%20assessment%20time%20by%20up%20to%2058%25%20in%20three%20UK%20councils&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fplanassist-council-planning-58-percent%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Read Google DeepMind&#039;s PlanAssist announcement and summarize the pilot results in Barnet, Camden and Dorset, what the tool does for planning officers, and what still needs a human decision." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="agents-built-dancing-pumpkin-robot" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/agents-built-dancing-pumpkin-robot/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One plain-English prompt, one dancing robot: Google&#039;s agents designed a 12-joint jack-o&#039;-lantern bot with no manual CAD</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">For Halloween, Google showed a real, physical jack-o&#039;-lantern robot that dances, with 12 degrees of freedom. A Google DeepMind team says it started from a single plain-English description, and AI agents running on Gemini 4 Argon in Antigravity designed the parts and simulated the movement, with nobody drawing it in CAD by hand. People then built the robot from that design. It&#039;s a playful demo, but it shows agents handling mechanical design and simulation, not just code.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Hardware design usually needs CAD skills and many rounds of trial and error. Agents that design and simulate first could make robotics prototyping open to far more builders.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Makers, robotics hobbyists, hardware engineers and anyone curious what coding agents can do beyond software.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">A demo from Google, not a product. Gemini 4 Argon and Antigravity are available to try, but results for physical design will vary. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Google/status/2116522684154585227" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google (@Google) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/agents-built-dancing-pumpkin-robot/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
