                                <article id="bot-family-cyber-shield" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-family-cyber-shield/" class="hover:text-brand-600">A dad built &#039;Family Cyber Shield&#039;, a Grok Bot that walks his family through locking down their phones and Macs</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A Grok Bot user shared a bot he calls Family Cyber Shield, built to keep his family safer online without constant scary alerts. He says it helps set up DNS filtering on a phone and Mac to block known scam and harmful sites, walks you through turning on the Mac firewall, helps set up passkeys and two-factor sign-in, and flags suspicious emails, double-checking before it raises an alarm. You make each change yourself, and he says the bot never asks for passwords or codes. He shared it as a template others can copy.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most families never finish basic security setup because it&#039;s tedious. A patient bot that explains each step can get it done without handing over any passwords.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Parents and anyone who ends up as the family&#039;s tech support.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Needs a Grok Bot plan (The X Subscription from the $30/month Premium tier up, or existing SuperGrok and Cursor subscribers). The template link is in the creator&#039;s post. Never share passwords or one-time codes with any bot. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: shared by a user on X; we haven&#039;t tested this template ourselves.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Texas_Twins_Dad/status/2116335904692330881" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Texas_Twins_Dad on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-family-cyber-shield/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=A%20dad%20built%20%27Family%20Cyber%20Shield%27%2C%20a%20Grok%20Bot%20that%20walks%20his%20family%20through%20locking%20down%20their%20phones%20and%20Macs&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-family-cyber-shield%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Walk me step by step through securing my family&#039;s Mac: turn on the firewall, then help me set up passkeys for our main email. Don&#039;t ask for any passwords or codes; I&#039;ll do every change myself." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-on-pebble-watch" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-on-pebble-watch/" class="hover:text-brand-600">No Grok Bot wearable yet? One builder put his on a Pebble watch: talk to your wrist, get the answer there</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Builder Alex Lunder made a rough Grok Bot wearable on a Pebble Time 2 smartwatch. You speak to the watch, it sends the request to his own Grok Bot, and the answer shows up on his wrist; he can also reply by voice from a notification. He built it with the Pebble SDK and shared a short video of it working. It&#039;s a home-made project, not an official xAI product, but it shows how a personal agent can reach a cheap wearable you might already own.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> People keep asking for AI glasses and pins. A watch you already wear can do much of the same job for quick questions and reminders.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users who tinker with gadgets, and Pebble owners who want voice access to their agent.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">A personal project, not a product. Needs a Grok Bot plan and a Pebble watch plus the Pebble SDK to build something similar. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: shared by its builder on X; we haven&#039;t tried it ourselves.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/AlexLunder/status/2116489333607678119" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Alex Lunder (@AlexLunder) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-on-pebble-watch/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=No%20Grok%20Bot%20wearable%20yet%3F%20One%20builder%20put%20his%20on%20a%20Pebble%20watch%3A%20talk%20to%20your%20wrist%2C%20get%20the%20answer%20there&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-on-pebble-watch%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I have a Pebble Time 2. Outline how a home-made app could send a spoken request from the watch to my own Grok Bot and show the reply on my wrist, and list what I would need from the Pebble SDK." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
