                                <article id="hex-local-voice-dictation-for-any-agent" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/hex-local-voice-dictation-for-any-agent/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Talk to any coding agent instead of typing: OpenCode&#039;s team ships Hex, local voice dictation for Mac, Windows and Linux</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">The team behind OpenCode released a stable version of Hex, a voice dictation app that runs on your own machine. Hold a shortcut (Option on a Mac), say what you want, let go, and Hex pastes the text wherever your cursor is, so it works with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, OpenCode or any chat box. It runs locally rather than sending audio to a cloud service, and installs on Mac (Apple silicon, macOS 15 or later), Windows and Linux. The launch post passed 640 likes.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Long prompts are easier to say than to type, and talking often gives an agent more context. Local dictation keeps your voice on your own computer.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers who write long prompts to coding agents, and anyone who&#039;d rather speak than type.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Download from anoma.ly/hex. Mac needs Apple silicon and macOS 15 or later; Windows and Linux installers are also offered. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/opencode/status/2116555630236577819" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: OpenCode (@opencode) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/hex-local-voice-dictation-for-any-agent/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Talk%20to%20any%20coding%20agent%20instead%20of%20typing%3A%20OpenCode%27s%20team%20ships%20Hex%2C%20local%20voice%20dictation%20for%20Mac%2C%20Windows%20and%20Linux&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fhex-local-voice-dictation-for-any-agent%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I just installed Hex for local voice dictation. Help me set a push-to-talk shortcut and write three short spoken prompt templates I can use with my coding agent for bug fixes, reviews and refactors." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
