                                <article id="3-8-flash-free-tier-price-doubles-january" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/3-8-flash-free-tier-price-doubles-january/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Gemini 3.8 Flash is free on the Gemini API free tier, and the paid price doubles on January 1</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google&#039;s pricing page (updated October 30, 2026) lists Gemini 3.8 Flash, its most capable Flash model for long software engineering tasks and agents, as free of charge on the Gemini API free tier for input, output and context caching. On the paid tier it costs $0.75 per million input tokens and $3.75 per million output tokens through December 31, 2026, then $1.50 and $7.50 from January 1, 2027. Batch and Flex modes aren&#039;t on the free tier, and free-tier data is used to improve Google&#039;s products.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> You can prototype agents and coding tools on a strong model for free, and if you plan to pay, the next two months are the cheapest it will be.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and hobbyists building with the Gemini API, especially anyone testing agents before committing to a paid plan.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free tier: free input, output and caching, with rate limits shown per project in Google AI Studio. Paid tier: $0.75 in and $3.75 out per 1M tokens through December 31, 2026, then $1.50 and $7.50 from January 1, 2027. Free-tier prompts may be used to improve Google&#039;s products. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing#gemini-3.8-flash" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google AI for Developers on ai.google.dev ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/3-8-flash-free-tier-price-doubles-january/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
