                                <article id="api-computer-use-ga-browser-android-desktop" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/api-computer-use-ga-browser-android-desktop/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Gemini&#039;s Computer Use tool is now generally available, and it can drive a browser, an Android phone or a desktop</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google moved Computer Use to general availability in the Gemini API on October 30, 2026, in both the Interactions and GenerateContent APIs. The model looks at screenshots and returns clicks, typing and other UI actions, which your own code carries out, for example with Playwright. It now works across browser, mobile (Android) and desktop environments, each action comes with an intent explaining what it&#039;s trying to do, and you can set safety policies so steps like payments, sending messages or creating accounts need your confirmation. There&#039;s also optional prompt injection detection and a Docker reference sandbox.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Agents that can operate apps without an API are moving from preview to something Google supports for production, with built-in brakes for risky actions.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers automating web forms, QA testing, back-office tools or Android flows that have no API.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Paid tier only, not available on the Gemini API free tier, billed at the model&#039;s normal token rates. Supported models include gemini-3.8-flash (recommended), gemini-4-argon and gemini-3.5-flash-lite. Needs the google-genai SDK 2.7.0 or later. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/computer-use" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google AI for Developers on ai.google.dev ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/api-computer-use-ga-browser-android-desktop/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Gemini%27s%20Computer%20Use%20tool%20is%20now%20generally%20available%2C%20and%20it%20can%20drive%20a%20browser%2C%20an%20Android%20phone%20or%20a%20desktop&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fapi-computer-use-ga-browser-android-desktop%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
