                                <article id="codex-shared-usage-limits-december" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-shared-usage-limits-december/" class="hover:text-brand-600">From December, ChatGPT and Codex will share one usage allowance on Plus, Pro and Business, measured in tokens</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI says that starting in December, the usage allowance on Plus, Pro and Business plans will be shared across ChatGPT and Codex, as it brings the agentic features of Work into the main ChatGPT experience. Usage will be counted in tokens, so bigger models and longer tasks use more of it, while Instant chat won&#039;t count at all. OpenAI expects most people won&#039;t hit resets more often than they do now. You&#039;ll see your combined remaining usage and reset times in Settings, under Usage, and if you run out you can wait, upgrade or buy credits.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you lean on Codex for long coding runs, those tasks will now draw from the same pool as your ChatGPT work, so heavy days in one can limit the other.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">ChatGPT Plus, Pro and Business subscribers who also use Codex, especially heavy coding-agent users.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Starts in December 2026 for Plus, Pro and Business plans. Instant chat doesn&#039;t draw from the allowance; extra usage can be bought as credits. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001625-understanding-chatgpt-and-codex-usage-limits" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: OpenAI Help Center on help.openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-shared-usage-limits-december/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=From%20December%2C%20ChatGPT%20and%20Codex%20will%20share%20one%20usage%20allowance%20on%20Plus%2C%20Pro%20and%20Business%2C%20measured%20in%20tokens&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fcodex-shared-usage-limits-december%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Explain how the shared ChatGPT and Codex usage allowance starting in December works on my plan, what counts toward it, and give me three habits to use fewer tokens on long Codex tasks." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-android-cli-plugin-official" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-android-cli-plugin-official/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google&#039;s official Android CLI plugin lets Claude Code create Android apps, run emulators and read live device screens</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">The Android team published an official plugin that adds an android-cli skill to Claude Code, Codex and Antigravity. The skill teaches your agent to use Android CLI, so it can create Android projects, run apps, manage the SDK and virtual devices, inspect live device screens and UI hierarchies, connect to Android Studio, test with Journeys and search the Android docs. The repo holds only the plugin; you install Android CLI itself separately from developer.android.com. It&#039;s Apache 2.0 licensed.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Your coding agent can now check its own Android work on an emulator, reading the screen and UI tree instead of guessing, using Google&#039;s own tooling.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Android developers who use Claude Code, Codex or Antigravity, and web developers who want an agent to help them ship a first Android app.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (Apache 2.0). Requires Android CLI, installed separately from developer.android.com/tools/agents/android-cli, plus Claude Code, Codex or Antigravity. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/android/android-cli-plugin" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Android (Google) on GitHub on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-android-cli-plugin-official/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Google%27s%20official%20Android%20CLI%20plugin%20lets%20Claude%20Code%20create%20Android%20apps%2C%20run%20emulators%20and%20read%20live%20device%20screens&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-android-cli-plugin-official%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
