</article>
                                <article id="anthropic-messages-api-rewritten-in-rust" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-messages-api-rewritten-in-rust/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Anthropic rewrote its Messages API in Rust with Claude writing the code, and says CPU use dropped 40-50%</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">On the Latent Space podcast, Anthropic&#039;s Katelyn Lesse described how the team moved the Messages API, the backend behind Claude&#039;s API, to Rust even though nobody on the team was a Rust developer. According to the widely shared summary, Claude wrote the code while engineers wrote the plan and checked that the old and new versions gave matching results on real traffic, and CPU use fell by 40-50%. Latent Space host swyx&#039;s post about it passed 2,400 likes, and the clip has been read as a sign that the risky &#039;big rewrite&#039; is now doable with agents.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a real production example of using an agent for a full language migration, with humans owning the plan and the testing rather than the typing.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Engineering leads weighing a rewrite or language migration, and anyone curious how Anthropic uses Claude on its own systems.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">The account comes from the Latent Space podcast; Anthropic hasn&#039;t published a written write-up we could find. The same approach works with Claude Code on any paid Claude plan.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported on X from a podcast interview; we haven&#039;t seen Anthropic confirm the figures in writing.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/somi_ai/status/2116050219989373170" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Somi AI (@somi_ai), citing Katelyn Lesse on Latent Space on X ↗</a>
