                                <article id="karpathy-hackertube-built-in-two-hours" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/karpathy-hackertube-built-in-two-hours/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Karpathy built a YouTube for hackers in about 2 hours with Claude Code: 6,454 videos picked from Hacker News comments</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Andrej Karpathy launched HackerTube, a video site built from the YouTube links people recommend on Hacker News. He wrote that he built it in about two hours with Opus 5.5 at medium effort in the Claude Code desktop app. Opus downloaded HN comments and ran Sonnet over them with Claude Code Workflows to narrow them to roughly 40,000 relevant comments and 6,454 videos from 2007 to 2026, sorted into about 150 topics. The site shows a frame from the middle of each video instead of the clickbait thumbnail, has keyboard shortcuts and data export, and makes For You picks without any account. His manual steps were a Google Cloud API key, a server and a domain.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a clear, real example of a one-evening project where the agent did the data mining, classification and the web app, and the human only handled keys, hosting and taste.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code users looking for a weekend-project pattern, and anyone who wants a calmer, comment-curated video feed.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">HackerTube is free to browse at hackertube.org. Recreating the build needs Claude Code (included in paid Claude plans) plus your own API key, server and domain. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://karpathy.bearblog.dev/hacker-tube/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Andrej Karpathy on karpathy.bearblog.dev ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/karpathy-hackertube-built-in-two-hours/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Karpathy%20built%20a%20YouTube%20for%20hackers%20in%20about%202%20hours%20with%20Claude%20Code%3A%206%2C454%20videos%20picked%20from%20Hacker%20News%20comments&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fkarpathy-hackertube-built-in-two-hours%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Download the last 12 months of comments from &lt;community&gt; that link to YouTube videos. Use a cheaper model to keep only comments that genuinely recommend the video, group the videos into about 30 topics, and build a static site with one page per topic. Use a frame from the middle of each video as its thumbnail. Ask me before using any API key." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="stageshow-skill-faux-ui-product-shots" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/stageshow-skill-faux-ui-product-shots/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One install gives your coding agent a designer&#039;s eye: Stageshow makes polished product shots, bento grids and cursor demos</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Stageshow is a free agent skill from designer Benji Taylor that teaches coding agents to make faux product UI for marketing: clean stills, feature cards, cursor-driven demo animations and bento grids, built as React components. It ships with a component kit, reference notes and dozens of examples. Small scripts film and measure the result so the agent can check its own work before showing you. It works with Claude Code, Codex, Grok Build and Gemini, and has a local playground. His launch post passed 8,300 likes and 13,000 bookmarks.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Launch pages and social posts need tidy product visuals, and this lets the agent that built your app also make the marketing shots, instead of you staging screenshots by hand.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Indie developers, founders and designers shipping landing pages, changelogs and launch posts.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source; install it with the skills CLI. Benji notes it may take a few rounds of feedback to get a shot right. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://benji.org/stageshow" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Benji Taylor (@benjitaylor) on benji.org ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/stageshow-skill-faux-ui-product-shots/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=One%20install%20gives%20your%20coding%20agent%20a%20designer%27s%20eye%3A%20Stageshow%20makes%20polished%20product%20shots%2C%20bento%20grids%20and%20cursor%20demos&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fstageshow-skill-faux-ui-product-shots%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Use the stageshow skill to make a 1200x630 still of our dashboard for a launch post: hide real customer data, show the new export feature in focus, and add a cursor hovering over the Export button. Film it and check spacing before showing me." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="api-invisible-watermark-nov-7" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/api-invisible-watermark-nov-7/" class="hover:text-brand-600">From November 7, Grok&#039;s API quietly watermarks the text it writes. Here&#039;s what changes and how admins can turn it off</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">xAI&#039;s developer docs say that from November 7, 2026, text from grok-4.7, grok-4.6, grok-4.5, grok-4.3 and the grok-4.20 reasoning, non-reasoning and multi-agent models will carry an invisible statistical watermark by default. It covers the Responses and Chat Completions APIs, including structured outputs and tool-call arguments. xAI says it&#039;s for EU AI Act transparency rules, needs no code changes and doesn&#039;t affect quality or speed. Watermarked responses carry an x-watermark: true header, team admins can opt out per model in the Console, and access to the detection API is by application.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you ship Grok-written text to customers or must meet EU AI Act rules, you&#039;ll want to know it&#039;s marked, and decide per model whether to keep it on.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and team admins using the xAI API in products, especially those serving users in the EU.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">On by default for the listed models from November 7, 2026, at no extra cost. Opt-out is per model in Console &gt; Team settings &gt; Model output watermarking and takes effect within about 5 minutes. Detection is statistical and the detection API is by application only. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://docs.x.ai/developers/advanced-api-usage/watermarking" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: xAI docs on docs.x.ai ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/api-invisible-watermark-nov-7/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=From%20November%207%2C%20Grok%27s%20API%20quietly%20watermarks%20the%20text%20it%20writes.%20Here%27s%20what%20changes%20and%20how%20admins%20can%20turn%20it%20off&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fapi-invisible-watermark-nov-7%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="List every Grok model my app calls, check which ones get xAI&#039;s text watermark from November 7, 2026, and add logging of the x-watermark response header so I can confirm it after the change." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="patrick-collison-improvements-box-liquid-software" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/patrick-collison-improvements-box-liquid-software/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Stripe&#039;s Patrick Collison adds an &#039;improvements&#039; box to his own apps: type a wish, an agent builds it</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Stripe CEO Patrick Collison wrote that he&#039;s adding an &quot;improvements&quot; feature to all his personal vibe-coded apps: a free-text box wired to a coding agent that implements whatever is submitted. He said one other person using one of his apps has already shipped 150 improvements in a few days, and called the idea &quot;liquid software&quot;. He also raised open questions about whether it stays maintainable, how it works for shared apps, and whether it can be secure. His post passed 3,000 likes. He didn&#039;t name a specific agent; you can build the same pattern with Claude Code or any coding agent you use.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It shrinks fixing a rough edge from opening an editor to typing one sentence, which changes how people treat the small tools they build for themselves.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People with personal or family apps they built with AI and want to keep improving without sitting down to code.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">A pattern, not a product. Building it needs a coding agent (for example Claude Code, included in paid Claude plans) and a project in Git. Collison himself suggests it&#039;s best for personal apps; keep it away from shared or sensitive apps until you&#039;ve added review. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/patrickc/status/2116636967517798672" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Patrick Collison (@patrickc) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/patrick-collison-improvements-box-liquid-software/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Stripe%27s%20Patrick%20Collison%20adds%20an%20%27improvements%27%20box%20to%20his%20own%20apps%3A%20type%20a%20wish%2C%20an%20agent%20builds%20it&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fpatrick-collison-improvements-box-liquid-software%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Add an &quot;Improvements&quot; box to this app: a small text field in the footer that appends each request with a timestamp to improvements.md. Then write a script I can run that asks you to implement the oldest open request on a new git branch, run the tests, and stop for my review. Never touch auth, payments or secrets from this flow." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="deepseek-super-agent-proactive-coding-agent" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/deepseek-super-agent-proactive-coding-agent/" class="hover:text-brand-600">DeepSeek open-sourced a coding agent that doesn&#039;t wait for a prompt: it watches your repo and answers with a pull request</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">DeepSeek&#039;s Harness team published dsh-superagent, a research prototype of a proactive coding agent for one GitHub repository. It listens to GitHub (and optionally Feishu chats). When an allowed person asks for work, or a rule your team wrote allows it, it opens a work item, does the job in its own isolated agent session and folder, and replies in the original thread, often with a pull request. A web panel shows only what needs a person. Its design rule is to take as little human attention as possible: it speaks only when someone must act or can use the result. The repo passed 6,000 GitHub stars within a day.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most coding agents sit idle until you type. This is a public look at how a frontier lab runs an agent that picks up work by itself, with guardrails on who can ask it and when it may speak.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and small teams who already use Claude Code or another coding agent and want to experiment with an always-on repo assistant on a test repository.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (MIT). DeepSeek says it&#039;s a research prototype, not an official product: it may have bugs and differs from their internal version. Needs Node 22.19+ or 24+, pnpm, git, tmux and the GitHub CLI 2.48+, plus a separate GitHub account for the agent. Model costs depend on the agent you connect. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/deepseek-ai/dsh-superagent-prototype" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: DeepSeek Harness team on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/deepseek-super-agent-proactive-coding-agent/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=DeepSeek%20open-sourced%20a%20coding%20agent%20that%20doesn%27t%20wait%20for%20a%20prompt%3A%20it%20watches%20your%20repo%20and%20answers%20with%20a%20pull%20request&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fdeepseek-super-agent-proactive-coding-agent%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Read SETUP.md in this repository and set up dsh-superagent with me one question at a time, pointed at my test repo and a separate GitHub account, and show me the full plan before installing anything." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="herdr-desktop-app-agents-keep-running" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/herdr-desktop-app-agents-keep-running/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Close the app and your agents keep working: Herdr is a free desktop home for Claude Code, Codex and their helpers</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Herdr is a free, open-source native app for running Claude Code, Codex and any other terminal agent side by side. The agents live in a background service (herdr-core), so they keep running after you close the window. Agents can start helpers themselves, for example Claude Code launching a Codex reviewer with hc run --bg codex and getting a message back when it&#039;s done, and you can add remote machines over SSH. A widely shared setup on X uses it to have one lead agent coordinate up to ten workers, with Claude Code writing and Codex reviewing.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Juggling several agents in terminal tabs gets messy fast and dies when a window closes. Herdr gives multi-agent work a stable home and lets agents hand tasks to each other.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers who run more than one coding agent at a time, or want a writer-and-reviewer setup between Claude Code and Codex.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (Apache 2.0). macOS on Apple silicon, Linux and Windows. You still need your own Claude Code, Codex or other agent plans, and every helper an agent starts uses your limits. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://herdr.dev" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Herdr (herdr.dev) on herdr.dev ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/herdr-desktop-app-agents-keep-running/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Close%20the%20app%20and%20your%20agents%20keep%20working%3A%20Herdr%20is%20a%20free%20desktop%20home%20for%20Claude%20Code%2C%20Codex%20and%20their%20helpers&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fherdr-desktop-app-agents-keep-running%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Here is the output of hc --skill. Use it to start a Codex reviewer in the background with hc run --bg codex on my current branch, and tell me when its review comes back." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-50-dollar-muse-charm-verge-waveshare" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-31" class="text-slate-400">Oct 31, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-50-dollar-muse-charm-verge-waveshare/" class="hover:text-brand-600">No coding experience, $50 of hardware, a few Claude Code sessions: The Verge&#039;s Sean Hollister built his own Muse Charm before Meta ships one</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">The Verge&#039;s Sean Hollister bought a $50 Waveshare ESP32-S3 1.75C touchscreen pendant, one of the devkits Meta itself suggests for building a &#039;Muse Gadget&#039; that talks to Muse. Out of the box it did little, so he plugged it into his PC and asked Claude Code to add what was missing. In a few sessions it built a swipeable conversation history, spoken replies with an ElevenLabs voice, a remote shutter and live preview for his phone camera, a batch of avatars with a Tamagotchi-style care game, and a working pocket-watch face, which he says took about 15 minutes. He says he has no coding experience and can&#039;t vouch for the code&#039;s quality.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It shows a non-programmer can now reprogram real hardware just by describing what they want. A cheap devkit plus a coding agent can do things an off-the-shelf gadget can&#039;t.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Tinkerers, makers and Muse fans who want a pocket AI gadget, and anyone curious about vibe-coding hardware.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The Waveshare ESP32-S3 1.75C costs about $50. Claude Code needs a paid Claude plan or API credits, and the device talks to Muse through Meta&#039;s open-source Muse Gadget code and the Muse phone app. Hollister used an ElevenLabs free-tier voice.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/1013375/muse-charm-gadgets-preview-waveshare-esp32-claude-vibe-code" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Sean Hollister, The Verge on www.theverge.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-50-dollar-muse-charm-verge-waveshare/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=No%20coding%20experience%2C%20%2450%20of%20hardware%2C%20a%20few%20Claude%20Code%20sessions%3A%20The%20Verge%27s%20Sean%20Hollister%20built%20his%20own%20Muse%20Charm%20before%20Meta%20ships%20one&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-50-dollar-muse-charm-verge-waveshare%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-voice-call-from-tesla-browser" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-voice-call-from-tesla-browser/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Talk to your own Grok Bot from a Tesla: no app needed, just the car&#039;s browser</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A Cybertruck owner found a way to talk straight to his own Grok Bot from the truck, instead of only reaching the regular Grok assistant built into the car. He opens the Tesla&#039;s web browser, goes to x.com or grok.com, picks the specific Grok Bot he wants, taps voice call and allows the car&#039;s microphone. He says it needs no app and no special setup. That means the bot that already knows your calendar, inbox and tasks can take requests on the drive, like adding a reminder or prepping a meeting brief.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Your car&#039;s built-in assistant doesn&#039;t know your work. A voice call to your own bot brings its memory, connected apps and routines into the drive.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Tesla owners who already use Grok Bot and want hands-free access while parked or on the road.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Needs a Grok Bot plan (The X Subscription from the $30/month Premium tier up, or existing SuperGrok and Cursor subscribers) and a Tesla with the web browser. The browser and microphone behavior may vary by car model, software version and region. Only start or manage calls when it&#039;s safe, following local laws. Checked October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Texas_Twins_Dad/status/2115957277567893839" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Texas_Twins_Dad on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-voice-call-from-tesla-browser/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Talk%20to%20your%20own%20Grok%20Bot%20from%20a%20Tesla%3A%20no%20app%20needed%2C%20just%20the%20car%27s%20browser&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-voice-call-from-tesla-browser%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I&#039;m driving to my 3 pm meeting. Add a reminder to call the dentist tomorrow morning, and send me a short brief for the meeting in chat so I can read it when I park." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
