                                <article id="openai-private-intelligence-business-data" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-private-intelligence-business-data/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI Private Intelligence: zero data retention, private inference and approval rules for business agents</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI announced Private Intelligence, a set of protections for businesses that want to use its most capable models on sensitive work. The page describes strict limits on OpenAI&#039;s own access to business content, Zero Data Retention and Private Inference for eligible workflows, with Private Inference listed as an API preview built on confidential computing. Businesses own their inputs and outputs, and they decide what agents can access, which tools and actions are allowed, and when an agent needs a human approval. OpenAI says it built the controls with some of its largest customers.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Data handling is the main reason many companies still keep AI agents away from their most sensitive work. This puts retention, inference privacy and agent permissions in one place that security teams can review.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">IT, security and compliance leads at companies using ChatGPT business plans or the OpenAI API, and teams planning agents that touch sensitive data.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to OpenAI business products. Zero Data Retention and Private Inference are for eligible workflows, and Private Inference is in API preview, as stated on OpenAI&#039;s page on October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/business/private-intelligence/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-private-intelligence-business-data/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%20Private%20Intelligence%3A%20zero%20data%20retention%2C%20private%20inference%20and%20approval%20rules%20for%20business%20agents&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fopenai-private-intelligence-business-data%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Read openai.com/business/private-intelligence and summarize what Zero Data Retention, Private Inference and the agent approval controls cover, then list the questions my security team should ask our OpenAI account contact." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-rule-no-recreating-existing-games" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-rule-no-recreating-existing-games/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude Code reportedly got a new rule: original games yes, clones of existing games no</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A widely shared post on X, viewed close to 900,000 times, says Claude Code picked up a new server-side instruction around October 27 under a flag named tengu_heron_brook, with no setting to switch it off. The quoted rule tells Claude to build original games, games in a genre and games made from the user&#039;s own designs and assets, but not a recreation of a specific existing game, even if it is renamed or called original. Anthropic hasn&#039;t publicly confirmed the rule, and developers are debating what it means for remakes, fan projects and modding.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If it holds, prompts like &#039;make me Flappy Bird&#039; may get pushback, while &#039;make me an endless flyer with my own art&#039; should still work. Game makers will want to frame requests around their own designs.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Indie game developers, hobbyists and students who use Claude Code to build or prototype games.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Reported for Claude Code around October 27, 2026. Not confirmed by Anthropic when we checked on October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/chasmmmmmmmmmmm/status/2116062991686721968" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @chasmmmmmmmmmmm on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-rule-no-recreating-existing-games/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20Code%20reportedly%20got%20a%20new%20rule%3A%20original%20games%20yes%2C%20clones%20of%20existing%20games%20no&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-rule-no-recreating-existing-games%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Build an original 2D platformer from my own design doc and assets in /design: a fox who swaps between day and night to open new paths. Start with a playable first level." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-70-punk-bands-youtube-playlist-30-seconds" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-70-punk-bands-youtube-playlist-30-seconds/" class="hover:text-brand-600">70 punk bands, one YouTube playlist, 30 seconds: a dad&#039;s Grok Bot concert prep (Elon called it &#039;great&#039;)</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Economist Peter St Onge posted that in his first week with Grok Bot he bought concert tickets for a festival with 70 punk bands and asked his Bot to build a YouTube playlist of each band&#039;s top songs to send to his kids. He says it took him 30 seconds, and that doing it by hand would have taken so long he wouldn&#039;t have bothered. The post passed 750,000 views, and Elon Musk quoted it with &#039;It&#039;s great @Bot&#039;.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Turning a long line-up into something you can actually listen to is tedious, clicky work, exactly the kind of chore an agent with a browser can take off your hands before a show.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Festival-goers, parents prepping kids for a concert, and anyone who wants to discover a line-up before buying tickets.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot comes with The X Subscription from the $30/month Premium tier up; existing SuperGrok and Cursor subscribers keep it. You&#039;ll need to be signed in to YouTube for the Bot to save a playlist. This is one user&#039;s experience. Checked October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/profstonge/status/2115971209141670228" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @profstonge on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-70-punk-bands-youtube-playlist-30-seconds/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=70%20punk%20bands%2C%20one%20YouTube%20playlist%2C%2030%20seconds%3A%20a%20dad%27s%20Grok%20Bot%20concert%20prep%20%28Elon%20called%20it%20%27great%27%29&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-70-punk-bands-youtube-playlist-30-seconds%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Here&#039;s the festival line-up. Build a YouTube playlist with the top 1-2 songs from each of these bands and send me the link." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-simlock-one-simulator-per-agent" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-simlock-one-simulator-per-agent/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Running Claude Code and Codex side by side on a mobile app? Simlock gives each agent its own simulator</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Szymon Chmal introduced Simlock, a free, open-source tool from Callstack Incubator that turns your machine into a self-managing simulator cloud, so each coding agent gets its own iOS or Android device, whether a simulator or a real phone, instead of fighting over the same one. Agents request a lease when they need to test mobile work, several machines can sit behind one API, and it can already be used in T3 Code. Replying to the launch, app developer David Barnard said Codex and Claude Code had created almost 70 simulators (about 300GB, by his recollection) while working on just two apps, so he set up a daily Codex check-in to watch disk space and suggest what to delete.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Parallel agents testing mobile apps can collide on one simulator or quietly fill your disk with dozens of new ones. A lease system and a regular cleanup check keep both under control.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">iOS and Android developers running several coding agents, such as Claude Code, Codex or Cursor, at once.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Simlock is free and open source on GitHub (callstackincubator/simlock). The project is new, so expect rough edges.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/ChmalSzymon/status/2116118360270495865" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @ChmalSzymon on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-simlock-one-simulator-per-agent/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Running%20Claude%20Code%20and%20Codex%20side%20by%20side%20on%20a%20mobile%20app%3F%20Simlock%20gives%20each%20agent%20its%20own%20simulator&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-simlock-one-simulator-per-agent%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="List every iOS simulator on this Mac with its size and when it was last used (xcrun simctl list devices and ~/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator). Suggest which ones to delete, but ask me before deleting any." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="ultra-no-5-hour-limit-max-renamed" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/ultra-no-5-hour-limit-max-renamed/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude&#039;s $200 plan is now Ultra, and it drops the 5-hour limit for verified accounts</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic renamed its Max plans. Max 5x is now simply Max at $100 a month, with five times Pro usage in every 5-hour window and every week. Max 20x is now Ultra at $200 a month, and for verified accounts it no longer has a 5-hour session limit at all, only a weekly limit set at ten times Pro. Existing subscribers don&#039;t need to do anything. Newer accounts keep a temporary 5-hour limit until they are verified and get an email when it is lifted. Claude&#039;s pricing page also lists monthly API credits on both plans.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> The 5-hour reset is the limit heavy Claude Code users hit most often in the middle of a long task. On Ultra, a long session now only counts against the weekly budget.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and power users already on Max 20x, and anyone deciding between the $100 and $200 Claude plans.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Max is $100 a month and Ultra is $200 a month, as listed on claude.com/pricing on October 31, 2026. No 5-hour limit applies to verified Ultra accounts; weekly limits still apply.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/claudeai/status/2116220869479428500" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Claude (Anthropic) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/ultra-no-5-hour-limit-max-renamed/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%27s%20%24200%20plan%20is%20now%20Ultra%2C%20and%20it%20drops%20the%205-hour%20limit%20for%20verified%20accounts&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fultra-no-5-hour-limit-max-renamed%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
