                                <article id="android-studio-bring-your-own-agent-antigravity" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/android-studio-bring-your-own-agent-antigravity/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Android Studio now runs Antigravity, Claude Agent, Codex and 40+ other agents right inside the IDE</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Android Studio&#039;s stable release adds Bring Your Own Agent: you can plug in more than 40 agents that speak the Agent Client Protocol, including Google&#039;s Antigravity, Claude Agent, Codex and JetBrains Junie, and use them in the IDE&#039;s agent window. Google says these agents can use Android Studio&#039;s own tools, such as builds, the Emulator and Logcat, along with 30-plus Android skills, so they can build, run and debug an app instead of only editing files. Antigravity announced on October 30 that its agent is now available there.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Android developers no longer have to switch between a terminal agent and the IDE. The agent can see the emulator and logs that a human would use to debug.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Android developers who already use Antigravity, Claude Code, Codex or another coding agent, and teams standardising on one agent across IDEs.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Android Studio is free. Each agent needs its own account: Antigravity works with a Google AI Pro or Ultra plan or a Gemini API key, while Claude Agent and Codex use your Anthropic or OpenAI plan.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://developer.android.com/blog/posts/ai-agents-android-studio-integration" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Android Developers on developer.android.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/android-studio-bring-your-own-agent-antigravity/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Android%20Studio%20now%20runs%20Antigravity%2C%20Claude%20Agent%2C%20Codex%20and%2040%2B%20other%20agents%20right%20inside%20the%20IDE&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fandroid-studio-bring-your-own-agent-antigravity%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="In Android Studio&#039;s agent window, using Antigravity: build my app, run it on the Emulator, read Logcat for any crash, then propose a fix and show me the diff before changing anything." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="sued-company-small-claims-settled" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/sued-company-small-claims-settled/" class="hover:text-brand-600">He let Muse take a company to small claims court. He says it settled within 20 minutes of being served</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Phillip Jackson, who said earlier this month that Muse could file small claims cases, posted an update that&#039;s been viewed close to 300,000 times. He says the company he sued through Muse agreed to settle within 20 minutes of being served, paid within 10 days including extra recovery costs, and that Muse then filed the motion to dismiss, which the court accepted. It&#039;s one person&#039;s account of a single case, but it&#039;s a vivid example of an agent handling paperwork most people avoid.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Small claims is designed for people without lawyers, yet the forms and deadlines put many off. If an agent can draft and track the filings, more people may follow through on disputes they&#039;d otherwise drop.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse users with a clear, small consumer dispute, such as an unpaid refund or deposit, who want help with the paperwork. This is not legal advice.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse is a paid personal agent. Court filing fees and rules depend on your location. Status unverified: this is the poster&#039;s own account and wasn&#039;t confirmed by Muse or court records when we checked on October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/philwinkle/status/2116180121447014434" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Phillip Jackson (@philwinkle) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/sued-company-small-claims-settled/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=He%20let%20Muse%20take%20a%20company%20to%20small%20claims%20court.%20He%20says%20it%20settled%20within%2020%20minutes%20of%20being%20served&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fsued-company-small-claims-settled%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Check my county&#039;s small claims rules, filing limit and fees for a case against [company] over [what happened]. List the evidence I should gather and draft the claim, but don&#039;t file anything until I&#039;ve reviewed it." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="aura-autopilot-open-source-game-playtesting-agent" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/aura-autopilot-open-source-game-playtesting-agent/" class="hover:text-brand-600">An open-source agent that playtests your game for you: Aura&#039;s Autopilot plugs into Claude Code or Codex</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Aura open-sourced Autopilot under the Apache 2.0 licence. It is an agent that plays your game inside the editor, moving, clicking and checking what happens, so it can find bugs and broken flows the way a human tester would. It supports Unreal Engine 5.4 to 5.8, Unity 6 and Godot 4.7 or newer on Windows and macOS. You can run it on your existing Claude Code or Codex subscription or bring your own API key. Aura says it is more accurate and almost twice as fast as Claude Code at playtesting; that is Aura&#039;s own benchmark.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Coding agents can write game code, but they rarely check that the game actually plays. A free playtesting agent closes that loop for small studios without a QA team.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Indie and small-studio game developers on Unreal, Unity or Godot who already use Claude Code or Codex.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (Apache 2.0). Uses your own Claude Code or Codex subscription or an API key. Runs in the editor, not on shipped builds.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/ramenvr/autopilot" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Aura on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/aura-autopilot-open-source-game-playtesting-agent/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=An%20open-source%20agent%20that%20playtests%20your%20game%20for%20you%3A%20Aura%27s%20Autopilot%20plugs%20into%20Claude%20Code%20or%20Codex&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Faura-autopilot-open-source-game-playtesting-agent%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Start play mode and playtest the first level of my game: move through it, click every menu and door, and report each bug or broken flow you find with the steps to reproduce it." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="gemma-4-in-orbit-suncatcher-haiku" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/gemma-4-in-orbit-suncatcher-haiku/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google ran Gemma 4 on a TPU in orbit, and the satellite&#039;s first answer was a haiku</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google&#039;s Project Suncatcher, which explores solar-powered AI compute in space, launched a test satellite with Planet on October 1. Google says it has now run its open Gemma 4 model on a TPU aboard that satellite and shared the reply it sent back to Earth: &#039;Blue marble below / Data streams in silent grace / Starlight feeds my core.&#039; Google calls it an early test of running AI hardware in orbit, with a pair of linked satellites planned as the next step in 2027.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a real first step toward data centres powered directly by sunlight in space, an idea Google is studying because AI&#039;s energy use keeps growing. It&#039;s also a fun way to see that the same open model you can download is now running in orbit.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone following AI infrastructure and energy, and developers curious to try the same Gemma 4 model on their own machine.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Research project, not a product. Gemma 4 itself is an open model you can try free in Google AI Studio or run locally.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/google-research/project-suncatcher-satellite-response/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google Research on blog.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/gemma-4-in-orbit-suncatcher-haiku/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Google%20ran%20Gemma%204%20on%20a%20TPU%20in%20orbit%2C%20and%20the%20satellite%27s%20first%20answer%20was%20a%20haiku&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fgemma-4-in-orbit-suncatcher-haiku%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Write a haiku about my project, [describe your project], in the style of the one Gemma 4 sent back from orbit: &#039;Blue marble below / Data streams in silent grace / Starlight feeds my core.&#039;" class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="slides-edit-entire-deck-one-prompt" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/slides-edit-entire-deck-one-prompt/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One prompt, whole deck: Gemini in Google Slides can now restyle or rewrite every slide at once</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Gemini in Google Slides can now edit many slides or a whole presentation from a single prompt in the side panel. It can restyle fonts, backgrounds and colours across a deck, match the look of another presentation, rewrite content using files from your Google Drive, merge several slides into one or add new ones. Changes land as normal editable slides, a summary appears in the panel, and you can undo or use version history to roll back.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Fixing fonts, colours and outdated numbers slide by slide is one of the dullest parts of deck work. This turns it into a single request you can still review and undo.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone who builds or updates presentations in Google Slides, especially teams refreshing old decks to a new brand or template.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rolling out from October 29, 2026, English only, for Google AI Pro and Ultra, Workspace Business Standard and Plus, Enterprise Standard and Plus, and AI Pro for Education. Workspace customers get higher promotional limits through at least December 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/10/edit-entire-presentations-with-gemini-in-Google-Slides.html" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google Workspace Updates on workspaceupdates.googleblog.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/slides-edit-entire-deck-one-prompt/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=One%20prompt%2C%20whole%20deck%3A%20Gemini%20in%20Google%20Slides%20can%20now%20restyle%20or%20rewrite%20every%20slide%20at%20once&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fslides-edit-entire-deck-one-prompt%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Update this whole deck to match the style of [reference file], keep my content, and merge any slides that repeat the same point." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="agents-api-auto-review-async-compaction-time-awareness" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/agents-api-auto-review-async-compaction-time-awareness/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI&#039;s Agents API now reviews risky commands before they run, and can be told to timebox a task to 10 minutes</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI&#039;s Agents API team shipped a batch of updates this week. Auto Review checks the commands an agent wants to run for bad behavior before executing them, the way Codex already does. Compaction can now happen in the background so long sessions don&#039;t stall, and an experimental time-awareness mode gives the model a sense of time passing, so instructions like &quot;timebox CI fixes to 10 minutes&quot; actually work. You can also change a session&#039;s tools at any point, and system prompts are now cached across sessions automatically.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> These are the pieces long-running agents keep tripping on: unsafe commands, sessions that freeze to compact, and no sense of a deadline. Automatic prompt caching also trims the bill.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers building agents on the OpenAI Agents API, especially CI, ops and coding agents that run for a long time.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Agents API (public beta) on the OpenAI platform, billed at normal API rates. The openai-python 3.42.0 release (October 31) adds the compaction, review, tool and time-awareness settings. Time awareness is experimental. Announced by OpenAI&#039;s Agents API team and the OpenAI Developers account on October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/stevendcoffey/status/2116303789649236048" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Steve Coffey (@stevendcoffey), OpenAI on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/agents-api-auto-review-async-compaction-time-awareness/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%27s%20Agents%20API%20now%20reviews%20risky%20commands%20before%20they%20run%2C%20and%20can%20be%20told%20to%20timebox%20a%20task%20to%2010%20minutes&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fagents-api-auto-review-async-compaction-time-awareness%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Read OpenAI&#039;s Agents API update notes and show how to turn on Auto Review and background compaction in my agent, plus an example instruction that uses time awareness to timebox a CI fix to 10 minutes." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="use-claude-subscription-in-opencode-claude-agent-provider" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/use-claude-subscription-in-opencode-claude-agent-provider/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenCode 2.2.3 can run on your Claude subscription: install Claude Code, log in and pick Claude Agent</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenCode 2.2.3 added a built-in Claude Agent provider. Instead of an API key, it runs the Claude Code you already have installed, so OpenCode can use your Claude Code login and models while keeping its own interface, tools and session controls. The OpenCode account announced it on X as &quot;you can now use your claude subscription in OpenCode&quot;. The same release also speeds up long sessions in the desktop app and fixes several side-panel bugs.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you like OpenCode&#039;s interface but already pay for Claude, you no longer need a separate API key and a second bill to use Claude models in it.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">OpenCode users who also have a Claude subscription or Claude Code login, and developers comparing coding-agent front ends.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">OpenCode is free and open source; the provider needs Claude Code installed and signed in, and usage counts against your own Claude plan. OpenCode says it uses the local Claude Code through Anthropic&#039;s Agent SDK. Anthropic&#039;s Agent SDK terms limit third-party products from offering claude.ai login unless approved, and Anthropic hasn&#039;t commented on this release, so check your plan&#039;s terms. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/releases/tag/v2.2.3" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: OpenCode (@opencode) on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/use-claude-subscription-in-opencode-claude-agent-provider/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenCode%202.2.3%20can%20run%20on%20your%20Claude%20subscription%3A%20install%20Claude%20Code%2C%20log%20in%20and%20pick%20Claude%20Agent&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fuse-claude-subscription-in-opencode-claude-agent-provider%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Help me update OpenCode to 2.2.3 or later, confirm Claude Code is installed and logged in, then select the Claude Agent provider and check which models it offers." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-block-writes-outside-working-directories" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-block-writes-outside-working-directories/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One Claude Code setting now keeps it from writing anywhere outside your project, even when you skip permission prompts</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Claude Code 2.1.314 added a permissions setting called blockWritesOutsideWorkingDirectories. When it&#039;s on, the Write, Edit and NotebookEdit tools refuse any path outside your working directories in every permission mode, including the mode that skips approval prompts. Daniel San tested it with Write and Edit and both were blocked. The same release adds idle compaction in the VS Code extension and the desktop app.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Running Claude with fewer prompts is faster, but a stray edit to a dotfile or another repo is painful. This draws a hard line around the project folder.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code users who run long sessions with few approval prompts, and teams setting safe defaults for everyone.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code 2.1.314 or later, on any plan that includes Claude Code. Listed in Anthropic&#039;s Claude Code changelog, checked October 31, 2026. It covers the file-writing tools; shell commands follow your normal permission rules.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/dani_avila7/status/2116311689683427511" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Daniel San (@dani_avila7) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-block-writes-outside-working-directories/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=One%20Claude%20Code%20setting%20now%20keeps%20it%20from%20writing%20anywhere%20outside%20your%20project%2C%20even%20when%20you%20skip%20permission%20prompts&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-block-writes-outside-working-directories%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Add blockWritesOutsideWorkingDirectories to my Claude Code settings.json permissions, then try to write a test file outside this project and confirm the write is refused." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="skills-replace-gems-save-prompts-run-with-slash" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/skills-replace-gems-save-prompts-run-with-slash/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Gemini Skills: save your best instructions once, run them with a slash, and get ready for Gems moving on Nov 17</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Skills in the Gemini app let you save instructions you use all the time and run them again by typing &quot;/&quot;, so you skip the repetitive prompting. You can build a skill straight from a chat and stack several together for bigger jobs. Google is replacing Gems with skills: Gems move into Settings on November 17, 2026, and a new Customize area holds your skills alongside more than 40 connected apps. Google&#039;s Gemini account highlighted skills again in its October Drops on X.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you retype the same instructions for weekly reports, emails or study notes, a skill turns that into one command. Gem users should move their setups before November 17.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Gemini users with go-to prompts, and anyone who built Gems they still rely on.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Available to personal Google accounts, rolling out since October 13 and expected to finish by mid-November. For Workspace business and enterprise customers, Gems keep working until at least March 1, 2027, and leftover Gems are turned into draft skills. As stated by Google, checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/09/skills-gemini-app-workspace.html" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google Workspace Updates on workspaceupdates.googleblog.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/skills-replace-gems-save-prompts-run-with-slash/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Gemini%20Skills%3A%20save%20your%20best%20instructions%20once%2C%20run%20them%20with%20a%20slash%2C%20and%20get%20ready%20for%20Gems%20moving%20on%20Nov%2017&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fskills-replace-gems-save-prompts-run-with-slash%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="/weekly-report Turn these notes into my weekly update: three wins, two blockers, next week&#039;s priorities, under 150 words." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="ios-share-sheet-send-photos-links-files-to-chat" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/ios-share-sheet-send-photos-links-files-to-chat/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Send anything to Muse from your iPhone&#039;s Share button: photos, links and files land straight in your chat</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta&#039;s Muse app now shows up in the iOS Share sheet. From Photos, Safari, Files or most other apps, you tap Share, choose Muse, and the photo, link or file goes straight into your Muse chat. That saves you from saving a screenshot, switching apps and attaching it by hand, which makes it quicker to ask Muse to summarize an article, read a document or work with a picture you just took.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> The fewer steps between finding something and asking about it, the more often you&#039;ll actually hand it to your assistant.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">iPhone users who use Muse to summarize articles, check documents or ask about photos.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse app on iOS, announced by the Muse account on October 30, 2026. Update the app if Muse doesn&#039;t appear in your Share sheet yet.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Muse/status/2116259784491974948" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Muse (@Muse) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/ios-share-sheet-send-photos-links-files-to-chat/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Send%20anything%20to%20Muse%20from%20your%20iPhone%27s%20Share%20button%3A%20photos%2C%20links%20and%20files%20land%20straight%20in%20your%20chat&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fios-share-sheet-send-photos-links-files-to-chat%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I&#039;m sharing an article to you from Safari. Summarize it in five bullets, pull out any dates or numbers, and tell me which claims I should verify." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="one-robots-txt-line-ai-training-opt-out" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/one-robots-txt-line-ai-training-opt-out/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One robots.txt line will soon tell OpenAI, Google, Microsoft and Anthropic not to train on your site</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI, Google, Microsoft and Anthropic are backing one shared robots.txt rule for AI training. You add a group for the user agent __usage_ai-training with Disallow: / (or allow only some folders), and each company says it will treat that as your training preference. It&#039;s based on an IETF draft written by Anthropic&#039;s Kevin Kelley. Timing differs: Microsoft from February 1, 2027, Google in early 2027, OpenAI in the coming months, and Anthropic says it has started. Your existing GPTBot, ClaudeBot and Google-Extended rules keep working.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Today you have to block a different crawler name for every AI lab. One shared line is far easier to set and harder to forget, though it states a preference about training, not a block on crawling or search.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Website owners, publishers, bloggers and SEO teams who want control over whether their pages train AI models.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to: any website with a robots.txt file. Support rolls out by company: Microsoft from Feb 1, 2027, Google in early 2027, OpenAI in the coming months, Anthropic already starting. A wildcard (*) group does not count as this signal. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/helping-websites-express-ai-training-preferences" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/one-robots-txt-line-ai-training-opt-out/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=One%20robots.txt%20line%20will%20soon%20tell%20OpenAI%2C%20Google%2C%20Microsoft%20and%20Anthropic%20not%20to%20train%20on%20your%20site&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fone-robots-txt-line-ai-training-opt-out%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Look at my site&#039;s robots.txt and add a __usage_ai-training group that disallows AI training on everything except /blog/, without changing how search crawlers are handled. Explain each line you add." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-reanimate-skill-rebuild-animations" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-reanimate-skill-rebuild-animations/" class="hover:text-brand-600">/reanimate: point Claude Code at an animation you love and it rebuilds it in your code, then films both to compare</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">reanimate is a free skill for Claude Code from developer Niaz Morshed. You give it a link, a video or a GIF of an animation, and it records the original in a real browser, writes down every moving part, rebuilds it with what your project already uses (CSS, Framer Motion, GSAP or three.js), then records the copy and compares timing and pixels. It repeats, usually two to five rounds, until they match, and reports anything still off. The launch post passed 3,900 bookmarks.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Asking an agent to copy motion from a screenshot usually misses, because it can&#039;t see the movement. A record-compare-fix loop gives it a real target to hit.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Front-end developers and designers using Claude Code who want a head start on polished UI animations.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free skill; runs on Bun on macOS or Linux. The first run downloads Chromium and ffmpeg (about 250 MB). Tested with Claude Code. It copies what you point it at, so fonts, images and code still belong to their owners. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: shared by its creator on X; we haven&#039;t run it ourselves.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/niazmorshed_/status/2116006291852423247" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Niaz Morshed (@niazmorshed_) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-reanimate-skill-rebuild-animations/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=%2Freanimate%3A%20point%20Claude%20Code%20at%20an%20animation%20you%20love%20and%20it%20rebuilds%20it%20in%20your%20code%2C%20then%20films%20both%20to%20compare&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-reanimate-skill-rebuild-animations%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="/reanimate this hero animation from the link I paste, rebuilding it with the animation library this project already uses, and show me the timing comparison when it matches." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="health-dashboard-whoop-apple-health" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/health-dashboard-whoop-apple-health/" class="hover:text-brand-600">In about an hour, Muse built one health dashboard from his Whoop, Apple Health and Cronometer data</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A Muse user says he spent about an hour with Meta&#039;s Muse agent turning his scattered health data into one dashboard. He pulled in exports from Whoop (recovery and sleep), Apple Health and Cronometer (food and nutrition), and Muse used its own cloud computer to build the dashboard, which he shared as screenshots. It&#039;s a good example of a weekend project an agent can do for you: combine data from apps that don&#039;t talk to each other into one view you actually check.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Fitness and food apps rarely share data with each other. An agent that merges your own exports gives you one picture of sleep, training and diet without a developer.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People who track fitness, sleep or nutrition across several apps and want one simple view.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Needs access to Meta&#039;s Muse agent and data exports from your own apps. Health data is sensitive: only upload what you&#039;re comfortable sharing, and treat the dashboard as a personal tracker, not medical advice. Checked October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: shared by a user on X; we haven&#039;t recreated it ourselves.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/ProShopGuyMF1/status/2116308259930075434" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Mike McMahon (@ProShopGuyMF1) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/health-dashboard-whoop-apple-health/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=In%20about%20an%20hour%2C%20Muse%20built%20one%20health%20dashboard%20from%20his%20Whoop%2C%20Apple%20Health%20and%20Cronometer%20data&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fhealth-dashboard-whoop-apple-health%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Here are my exports from Whoop, Apple Health and Cronometer. Build one dashboard showing sleep, recovery, daily steps and protein over the last 30 days, and point out any week that looks unusual. This is for personal tracking, not medical advice." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="jio-ai-pro-no-argon-in-antigravity" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/jio-ai-pro-no-argon-in-antigravity/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Got free Google AI Pro through Jio? Google confirms it won&#039;t unlock Gemini 4 Argon in Antigravity</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Reliance Jio customers in India on an eligible 5G plan get 18 months of Google AI Pro bundled free, but many found Gemini 4 Argon missing in Google&#039;s Antigravity coding IDE. Varun Mohan, who leads Antigravity at Google, replied on X that Google doesn&#039;t have capacity to give tens of millions of Jio users access to Argon, and that upgrading to a paid plan gives access today. His earlier confirmation drew more than 15,000 views, and Indian developers are now sharing how the bundle differs from directly paid Pro in Antigravity.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Millions of developers in India got this bundle, and knowing the limit saves hours of reinstalling and troubleshooting an IDE that will never show the model.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Jio Google AI Pro users in India, and anyone on a bundled or promotional Google AI Pro plan who codes in Antigravity.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Per Google&#039;s Antigravity lead, Jio-bundled Google AI Pro doesn&#039;t include Gemini 4 Argon in Antigravity; a directly paid Google AI Pro plan does. Google hasn&#039;t said whether other promotional plans are treated the same way. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/_mohansolo/status/2116071352201548184" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Varun Mohan (@_mohansolo), Google Antigravity on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/jio-ai-pro-no-argon-in-antigravity/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Got%20free%20Google%20AI%20Pro%20through%20Jio%3F%20Google%20confirms%20it%20won%27t%20unlock%20Gemini%204%20Argon%20in%20Antigravity&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fjio-ai-pro-no-argon-in-antigravity%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Tell me which Gemini models my Antigravity plan includes, and for this task pick the best model I actually have access to, explaining what I&#039;d gain from Argon if I upgraded." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="scenario-3d-os-skills-blender-unreal-unity" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-30" class="text-slate-400">Oct 30, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/scenario-3d-os-skills-blender-unreal-unity/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude Code can now drive Blender, Maya, Unreal and Unity: Scenario&#039;s free pack adds about 80 game-art skills</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Scenario open-sourced a skills pack it calls a 3D OS for coding agents. It holds about 80 skills in six departments (animation, art, modeling, look dev and lighting, worlds, and pipeline) plus expert skills for Blender, Maya, ZBrush, Unreal, Unity, Godot and Roblox. Install it once and Claude Code, Codex or Cursor can plan an asset, generate concepts and models through Scenario, then script the cleanup, rigging or scene setup in the 3D tool you already use. The founder&#039;s launch post passed 3,000 likes and 5,000 bookmarks.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> 3D work is full of repetitive scripting and fiddly tool menus. Packaging that know-how as agent skills lets a solo developer ask for an asset or a scene in plain English and get working pipeline steps.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Indie game developers, 3D artists and technical artists who use Blender, Unreal, Unity or Godot and already run a coding agent.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The skills are free and open source (MIT, scenario-labs/skills on GitHub). Skills that generate images, 3D models or animation call Scenario&#039;s service and need a Scenario account, so usage costs follow your Scenario plan. The expert skills for Blender, Unreal and the rest only drive software you have installed. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/emmanuel_2m/status/2116188727579918358" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Emmanuel de Maistre, Scenario (@emmanuel_2m) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/scenario-3d-os-skills-blender-unreal-unity/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20Code%20can%20now%20drive%20Blender%2C%20Maya%2C%20Unreal%20and%20Unity%3A%20Scenario%27s%20free%20pack%20adds%20about%2080%20game-art%20skills&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fscenario-3d-os-skills-blender-unreal-unity%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
