                                <article id="edit-files-in-chat-free" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/edit-files-in-chat-free/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Gemini now edits your PDFs, decks and spreadsheets right in the chat, even on the free plan</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">The Gemini app can now generate, preview and edit files without you leaving the chat. That covers documents, PDFs, presentations, spreadsheets, Markdown, plain text and code. Expand a file to full screen and type your own edits, or highlight a passage and ask Gemini to rewrite or explain just that part. When you&#039;re done, open it in Google Slides or Sheets, download it as PPTX or PDF, or save it to Drive.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> The usual loop is copy the draft, paste it into another app, fix it, paste it back. Now the draft, your edits and Gemini&#039;s edits live in one place.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone who drafts reports, slides or spreadsheets with Gemini, students and small teams in particular.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rolling out to all Gemini users in every supported language, including free personal accounts and Google Workspace. PDF editing works on web and mobile; the other file types are on the web for now.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/edit-files-directly/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on blog.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/edit-files-in-chat-free/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Gemini%20now%20edits%20your%20PDFs%2C%20decks%20and%20spreadsheets%20right%20in%20the%20chat%2C%20even%20on%20the%20free%20plan&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fedit-files-in-chat-free%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
