                                <article id="shareable-avatars-friends" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="images">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Images &amp; media</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/shareable-avatars-friends/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Your friends can now put you in their Gemini images and videos, but only if you say yes</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Gemini now lets you record your face and voice once to make a personal avatar, then use it in Nano Banana images and Gemini Omni videos by tagging yourself in a prompt with @ and your username. The new part is sharing: you can share your avatar with a friend&#039;s Gmail address, they accept it, and they can then tag you in their own prompts, like a video of the two of you doing a silly dance. Google says the character and voice stay consistent between creations. You can see who can use your avatar, set expiry dates, and remove anyone; removing someone stops new creations but doesn&#039;t delete what they&#039;ve already made.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Group photos and videos with friends no longer need everyone to upload selfies each time. The consent step and the revoke button matter, because this is your face and voice.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Friends, families and creators who make fun images or short videos together in Gemini.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Personal Google Accounts, 18+, English only for now, and not available in the EEA, Switzerland or the UK. Avatar images work in Gemini; avatar videos need a Google AI plan.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/GeminiApp/status/2115885244805251519" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GeminiApp on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/shareable-avatars-friends/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Your%20friends%20can%20now%20put%20you%20in%20their%20Gemini%20images%20and%20videos%2C%20but%20only%20if%20you%20say%20yes&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fshareable-avatars-friends%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Make a short video of @me and @friend doing a silly victory dance in a sunny park, keeping both our faces and voices consistent" class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="jules-shutting-down-export" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/jules-shutting-down-export/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google is shutting down Jules: save your sessions before November 11</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google is winding down Jules, its asynchronous coding agent, on December 31, 2026, and says what it learned is going into Google Antigravity. You can keep finishing sessions until November 11, 2026; after that Jules is read-only until the end of the year. Your code and pull requests stay in GitHub, but Jules-only data does not, so Google published an export path: install the Jules CLI, log in, and run Google&#039;s export prompt in a CLI coding agent from your home folder. It writes a ~/jules-export folder with your connected sources, per-repo setup scripts and memories, settings, environment variables, scheduled tasks, and a summary, logs and diffs for each session.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Setup scripts, repo memories and scheduled tasks took time to tune and don&#039;t live in GitHub. If you don&#039;t export them, they&#039;re gone at the end of the year.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and teams who used Jules, especially with scheduled tasks or custom setup scripts.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Sessions can be finished until November 11, 2026; read-only until December 31, 2026, when Jules shuts down. The export uses the free @google/jules CLI and any CLI coding agent.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://jules.google/docs/changelog/2026-10-29/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google Jules on jules.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/jules-shutting-down-export/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Google%20is%20shutting%20down%20Jules%3A%20save%20your%20sessions%20before%20November%2011&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fjules-shutting-down-export%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Read ~/jules-export and turn the setup scripts and memories for this repo into an AGENTS.md file: setup commands, test commands and the conventions Jules learned. Leave out anything from env-variables.json." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="antigravity-plugin-marketplace" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-plugin-marketplace/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Antigravity now has a plugin store: one click adds skills, MCP servers and subagents</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google Antigravity&#039;s Marketplace lets you browse, inspect and install curated plugins from Google and other developers. A plugin can bundle skills, MCP servers, rules, subagents and hooks, so one install replaces several setup steps. In the Antigravity App it sits under Customizations &gt; Marketplace, and anything you install there also shows up in the Antigravity CLI&#039;s Installed tab. Google&#039;s own shelf includes plugins for Firebase, Android, Flutter, Chrome DevTools and BigQuery. Plugin pages show the developer, version and links to the website and repository, and third-party plugins carry a notice that they come from other developers.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Wiring up MCP servers and skills by hand is where most agent setups stall. A store with one-click installs makes good setups shareable, but it also means you should check what a plugin can do before adding it.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers using Antigravity who want Firebase, Android, BigQuery or other integrations without manual config, and plugin authors.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">In the Antigravity App and CLI; Google doesn&#039;t list a separate charge for the Marketplace, and your usual Antigravity plan limits apply. Plugin authors can validate with agy plugin validate --strict and submit through Google&#039;s interest form.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://antigravity.google/docs/marketplace/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google Antigravity on antigravity.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-plugin-marketplace/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Antigravity%20now%20has%20a%20plugin%20store%3A%20one%20click%20adds%20skills%2C%20MCP%20servers%20and%20subagents&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fantigravity-plugin-marketplace%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Before I install this Marketplace plugin, list every skill, MCP server, rule, subagent and hook it bundles, what each one can access, and anything I should disable afterwards." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="ai-studio-xr-blocks" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/ai-studio-xr-blocks/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One prompt, an XR app with hand tracking: Google AI Studio adds XR Blocks</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google AI Studio now supports XR Blocks, Google&#039;s open-source library for extended reality apps built on three.js. You describe a 3D or mixed-reality app in plain words and AI Studio vibe codes it, with support for hand tracking and pinch gestures, physics that treats real tables and walls as surfaces, and 360-degree 3D holograms made from text or photos. You don&#039;t need a headset to start: XR Blocks has a desktop simulator in Chrome, and the same app can run on Android XR devices such as Samsung Galaxy XR with Chrome 136 or later.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> XR prototypes used to need a game engine and a lot of setup. Now a single prompt gets you something you can try in a browser, and then on a headset.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Designers, students and developers curious about AR/VR, and teams prototyping Android XR ideas.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">In Google AI Studio with a Google account (AI Studio&#039;s usual limits apply). Runs in the desktop simulator in Chrome; for real XR you need an Android XR device with Chrome 136+.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/GoogleAIStudio/status/2115902765780328883" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GoogleAIStudio on X ↗</a>
