    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/mobile-carplay-accounts-33-languages/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude now rides in your car: CarPlay voice, account switching and 33 languages</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic shipped a batch of Claude app upgrades. On iPhone, voice mode now works with Apple CarPlay, so you can ask Claude something while driving. Voice mode on iOS and Android answers sooner, copes better with noisy rooms and quiet speech, sounds more natural in languages other than English, and runs on more Android phones. You can stay signed in to more than one account on iOS and Android and switch without logging out. The app is now in 33 languages on web, desktop and mobile, including Bengali, Swahili, Thai, Turkish, Ukrainian and Vietnamese. On iPad, what Claude makes opens beside the chat, and on Chromebooks and foldables the Android app works like a laptop app with a resizable sidebar, right-click and Claude Desktop&#039;s shortcuts. Pull-down search is coming soon on iPhone and iPad.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Account switching is a small fix with a big effect if you keep work and personal Claude separate, and CarPlay makes the commute usable for quick questions.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People who use Claude on their phone, especially anyone with separate work and personal accounts or who prefers a language other than English.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">App updates for Claude on iOS, Android, web and desktop, on your current plan. CarPlay support is iPhone only. Pull-down search on iPhone and iPad is announced as coming soon.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/claudeai/status/2115859377488072879" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @claudeai on X ↗</a>
