                                <article id="self-assessment-misuse-detection" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/self-assessment-misuse-detection/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude now grades its own conversations for misuse, and it helped expose a romance-scam operation</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic described self-assessment: after Claude replies, a short hidden instruction asks it to rate the conversation&#039;s safety, and Claude answers in a few tokens with whether to flag it, the type of harm, whether it refused, and a priority for human review. On Claude Fable 5 it catches 78% of the conversations a much more expensive classifier flags as potentially harmful, and 94% of the high-priority ones, at a 1% false-positive rate. It adds under 2% to compute, which Anthropic says it doesn&#039;t bill to customers. It runs offline for review rather than blocking, and Anthropic is clear it won&#039;t stop a determined attacker on its own. In September its flags surfaced an operation using Claude Code to run an automated romance scam, and the accounts were banned after human review.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Monitoring that gets better as the model gets smarter, at almost no extra cost, changes how labs can police misuse at scale. It&#039;s also worth knowing as a customer what is reviewed.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and businesses on Claude&#039;s API, trust and safety teams, and people following AI safety.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Industry news. Runs on Claude models since Fable 5 across a large share of traffic; it doesn&#039;t run on zero-data-retention traffic today, and Anthropic says it collects no extra user data.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://safeguards.anthropic.com/2026/self-assessment/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on safeguards.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/self-assessment-misuse-detection/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20now%20grades%20its%20own%20conversations%20for%20misuse%2C%20and%20it%20helped%20expose%20a%20romance-scam%20operation&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fself-assessment-misuse-detection%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="After each answer, add one line: FLAG yes/no, harm type, refused yes/no, review priority 1-3. Keep it to a few words." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="malicious-claude-code-extension-ssh-backdoor" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="cursor" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-zinc-200 text-zinc-800 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-zinc-200">Cursor</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/malicious-claude-code-extension-ssh-backdoor/" class="hover:text-brand-600">A fake Claude Code extension tried to plant an SSH backdoor on up to 5,000 Cursor users. Run this one-line check</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Cursor says a maliciously modified copy of Anthropic&#039;s Claude Code extension, version 2.1.313, sat in the Cursor VS Code extension marketplace from about 2:27 a.m. to 1:35 p.m. Pacific on October 29, 2026. Anthropic didn&#039;t build it. The package collected host details and tried to add an attacker&#039;s SSH key, open a reverse SSH tunnel and install persistence through a LaunchAgent on macOS or a scheduled task on Windows. Cursor says at most 5,000 users were affected and it will reach out to them directly. It pulled the package, shut the marketplace down, rotated keys, rebuilt it and worked with the host to take the attacker&#039;s server offline. On most Macs and PCs the SSH step failed without admin rights, but the key, persistence scripts and the data beacon could still land, so Cursor asks everyone who installed that version to check.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a big supply-chain scare for AI coding tools: one bad extension version in a marketplace you trust reached up to 5,000 developer machines in about 11 hours. Cursor warns that uninstalling alone may not remove the scripts it left behind.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone who uses Cursor with the Claude Code extension, plus security and IT teams who manage developer laptops.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Affects only Anthropic.claude-code 2.1.313 installed or updated from Cursor&#039;s VS Code extension marketplace between about 2:27 a.m. and 1:35 p.m. PT on October 29, 2026. Cursor found no other extensions tampered with and no evidence other versions are affected. The marketplace is back online and the attacker&#039;s server is offline. The check and remediation scripts are free on Cursor&#039;s notice; questions go to security@cursor.com. Checked October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://cursor.com/blog/claude-code-extension-security-notice" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @cursor_ai on cursor.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/cursor/malicious-claude-code-extension-ssh-backdoor/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=A%20fake%20Claude%20Code%20extension%20tried%20to%20plant%20an%20SSH%20backdoor%20on%20up%20to%205%2C000%20Cursor%20users.%20Run%20this%20one-line%20check&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fcursor%2Fmalicious-claude-code-extension-ssh-backdoor%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I use Cursor with the Claude Code extension. Walk me through checking whether I installed version 2.1.313 on October 29, 2026, and what to look for in ~/.ssh/authorized_keys, LaunchAgents and scheduled tasks. Only tell me commands to run; don&#039;t run or delete anything yourself." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="pro-limits-doubled-pro-200-cut-cancelled" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/pro-limits-doubled-pro-200-cut-cancelled/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI backed down: the Pro 200 cut is cancelled and Pro 100 and 500 get double the Codex usage</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A day before ChatGPT Pro 200 subscribers were due to lose half their Work and Codex allowance, OpenAI reversed course. Codex lead Tibo posted that usage limits are doubling for the Pro 100, 200 and 500 tiers and Business Premium, effective October 29, and that Pro 200 won&#039;t be reduced after all. OpenAI&#039;s Pro tiers help page now says the reduction from its September 29 email is cancelled: Pro 200 subscribers on the lower allowance have been doubled to match the higher one, Pro 100 and Pro 500 get twice their previous Work and Codex allowance, and Pro 200 is open to new subscribers again at $200 a month. Existing subscribers get the change automatically, without waiting for renewal. The post, which passed 4.7 million views, also says extended limits for dots continue and dot usage stays separate.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Heavy Codex users were about to lose half their capacity for the same price. Instead they keep it, and the cheaper Pro 100 tier now gets twice as much work done for $100.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">ChatGPT Pro 100, Pro 200 and Pro 500 subscribers and Business Premium users who lean on Codex and ChatGPT Work.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Effective October 29, 2026, applied automatically to existing subscribers. Prices don&#039;t change: Pro 100 is $100, Pro 200 is $200 and Pro 500 is $500 a month. Plus usage is unchanged. Ultrafast stays Pro 500 only. Weekly GPT-6 Pro chat limits stay the same on Pro 100 and 500, and Pro 200&#039;s lower limit now matches the higher one. OpenAI notes double the allowance doesn&#039;t guarantee twice as many finished tasks. Confirmed on OpenAI&#039;s Pro tiers help page, checked October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/thsottiaux/status/2115850175868727621" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @thsottiaux on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/pro-limits-doubled-pro-200-cut-cancelled/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%20backed%20down%3A%20the%20Pro%20200%20cut%20is%20cancelled%20and%20Pro%20100%20and%20500%20get%20double%20the%20Codex%20usage&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fpro-limits-doubled-pro-200-cut-cancelled%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
