                                <article id="api-128mb-requests-bigger-pdfs-computer-use" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/api-128mb-requests-bigger-pdfs-computer-use/" class="hover:text-brand-600">The Claude API now takes 128 MB requests, 4x more room for giant PDFs and long computer-use sessions</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic raised the maximum request size for the Messages and Token Counting endpoints on the first-party Claude API from 32 MB to 128 MB. The team says image-heavy jobs, like long computer-use sessions full of screenshots and big PDFs, were hitting the 32 MB cap with plenty of context window still left, so this gives about 4x more room. Claude&#039;s API docs now list 128 MB for Messages and Token Counting, 256 MB for the Batch API and 500 MB for the Files API. Go over the limit and you get a 413 request_too_large error.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Fewer workarounds. You can send far more screenshots or a much bigger PDF in one call instead of splitting the job or shrinking every image.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers building computer-use agents, document pipelines and anything that sends lots of images or PDFs to Claude.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Live now on the first-party Claude API for Messages and Token Counting, at normal token prices. Cloud platforms keep their own lower limits: Bedrock is 20 MB, Google-managed Claude on Google Cloud is 30 MB, and Claude Platform on AWS, Anthropic-managed Google Cloud and Microsoft Foundry are 32 MB. Confirmed in Claude&#039;s API docs, checked October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/ClaudeDevs/status/2115923971279614171" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @ClaudeDevs on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/api-128mb-requests-bigger-pdfs-computer-use/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=The%20Claude%20API%20now%20takes%20128%20MB%20requests%2C%204x%20more%20room%20for%20giant%20PDFs%20and%20long%20computer-use%20sessions&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fapi-128mb-requests-bigger-pdfs-computer-use%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Upload report.pdf with the Claude Files API, then send a Messages request that references its file_id and asks Claude to summarize the document. Catch any 413 request_too_large error and split the job if you hit one." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="notebook-hundreds-free-textbooks" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/notebook-hundreds-free-textbooks/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Free for students: Gemini Notebook now opens hundreds of textbooks and turns them into quizzes and flashcards</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google added a Textbooks catalog to Gemini Notebook. Students can now add hundreds of textbooks from providers in the U.S. and India, including OpenStax, Open Textbook Library and S Chand Publishing, to a notebook at no charge. Once a textbook is added, every answer is grounded in that book with inline citations and direct links back to the source, and Gemini Notebook can turn the material into study guides, practice quizzes, flashcards and more. You don&#039;t have to hunt down and upload PDFs yourself. It builds on Google&#039;s Expert Intelligence push, which already let you add ebooks bought on Google Play Books.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> A free, citation-backed study buddy for your actual course book. Answers point to the page they came from, so you can check them instead of trusting a chatbot&#039;s memory.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">High school and college students, especially in the U.S. and India, plus teachers building study material.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free to add, from the Textbooks catalog inside Gemini Notebook. Google says the books come from providers in the U.S. and India (OpenStax, Open Textbook Library and S Chand Publishing) and gives &quot;hundreds&quot; of titles without an exact count. What&#039;s in the catalog may depend on your region. Confirmed on Google&#039;s blog, checked October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-notebook/new-access-textbooks/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on blog.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/notebook-hundreds-free-textbooks/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Free%20for%20students%3A%20Gemini%20Notebook%20now%20opens%20hundreds%20of%20textbooks%20and%20turns%20them%20into%20quizzes%20and%20flashcards&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fnotebook-hundreds-free-textbooks%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Using only the textbook in this notebook, make a 15-question practice quiz on chapters 3 and 4, mixing multiple choice and short answer. Put the answers with page citations at the end." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="model-spec-five-core-values" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/model-spec-five-core-values/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI rewrote ChatGPT&#039;s rulebook around 5 values and stopped calling it &quot;the assistant&quot;</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI updated its Model Spec, the public document describing how its models should behave. The new version is organized around five values: faithfulness to human intent, harm minimization, honesty and transparency, human agency, and care. It adds guidance on reading context such as conversations and memories to understand what people actually want, on supporting people&#039;s ability to decide for themselves, on following social norms and on controlling side effects when models take actions. It also retires most of the detailed style rules, since OpenAI says style should adapt to each person, while keeping defaults like answering objectively. The Spec now calls the model &quot;GPT&quot; instead of &quot;the assistant&quot;, and OpenAI admits its models don&#039;t fully follow it yet.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> As agents take more real actions, the rules about intent, side effects and not quietly steering you matter more than tone. This tells you what ChatGPT and Codex are being trained to do when your instructions run out.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">ChatGPT and Codex power users, developers building on OpenAI models, and anyone tracking AI safety and behavior.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">The updated Model Spec is free to read on OpenAI&#039;s site, and OpenAI is asking for public feedback. It describes target behavior, so changes reach models over time rather than all at once. Checked October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/updated-model-spec/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/model-spec-five-core-values/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%20rewrote%20ChatGPT%27s%20rulebook%20around%205%20values%20and%20stopped%20calling%20it%20%22the%20assistant%22&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fmodel-spec-five-core-values%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Explain the five core values in OpenAI&#039;s updated Model Spec in plain English, with one example of how each one changes what ChatGPT says to me." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-100-150-bots-running-one-business" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-100-150-bots-running-one-business/" class="hover:text-brand-600">&quot;Grok Bot gets shit done&quot;: one founder says 100 to 150 bots already work across his company</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Founder Quincy Lee posted that his company already has around 100 to 150 Grok Bots helping across the business, quoting one employee who said &quot;Grok Bot gets shit done&quot;. Elon Musk reposted it, and hours later posted &quot;Hire Grok Bot to be an employee&quot;, which passed 900,000 views. Musk also pointed out that Grok Bot has no free tier. Lee didn&#039;t list which jobs the bots do, but xAI&#039;s free Grok Bot for Work guide shows the pattern: an inbox manager, a calendar assistant, a research scout and one boss bot that the others report into, each read-only by default so nothing goes out until you say so.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a concrete picture of agents as headcount, not chat windows: many narrow bots, each with one job, reporting up to a person.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Founders, managers and small teams thinking about handing recurring work to agents.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot comes with The X Subscription from the $30/month Premium tier up; existing SuperGrok and Cursor subscribers keep it, and there&#039;s no free tier. The Grok Bot for Work guide is free on x.ai. Checked October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/QuincyEdmundLee/status/2115827875500949887" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @QuincyEdmundLee on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-100-150-bots-running-one-business/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=%22Grok%20Bot%20gets%20shit%20done%22%3A%20one%20founder%20says%20100%20to%20150%20bots%20already%20work%20across%20his%20company&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-100-150-bots-running-one-business%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Act as my first employee. Ask me 10 questions about my work week, then propose three narrow bots I should set up (name, one job each, schedule and what they must never do without my OK). Don&#039;t create anything yet." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-600k-daily-users-16-day-streak" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-600k-daily-users-16-day-streak/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Grok Bot went from about 70K to 600K daily users in 7 weeks, per Similarweb</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Traffic analytics firm Similarweb posted that Grok Bot&#039;s daily active users grew for 16 days in a row as of October 26, 2026, its longest growth streak so far. Its chart, which covers the iPhone and Android apps worldwide, starts at roughly 70,000 daily users on September 6 and ends at about 600,000 on October 26, roughly an 8x jump in seven weeks, with the steepest climb in mid to late October. These are Similarweb&#039;s own estimates for the mobile apps, not official figures from xAI, and they don&#039;t count desktop use.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Personal agents are moving from early adopters to a mainstream app category, which usually means faster feature releases and more templates and community bots to borrow from.</p>
