                                <article id="code-coding-agent-mania-warning" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-coding-agent-mania-warning/" class="hover:text-brand-600">&#039;It feels like a lot is getting done, but nothing is really happening&#039;: a former Claude Code engineer on coding agent mania</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Thariq, whose X profile says he formerly worked on Claude Code at Anthropic, posted that there&#039;s &#039;100% a kind of mania you can get into with coding agents&#039;, where you feel busy and productive running agents all day but little real progress is made, and that it is often a form of avoidance. The post passed a million views and 14,000 likes, with many developers replying that they recognise the pattern of spinning up more agents instead of finishing or shipping.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Running several agents at once can feel like progress even when nothing ships. It&#039;s a useful check for anyone whose day is now mostly prompting and watching agents.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and founders who run Claude Code, Codex or other agents in parallel for most of the day.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">An opinion post, free to read on X. Status unverified: it reflects the author&#039;s personal view and isn&#039;t an Anthropic statement, as of October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/trq212/status/2115937378674372783" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Thariq (@trq212) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-coding-agent-mania-warning/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=%27It%20feels%20like%20a%20lot%20is%20getting%20done%2C%20but%20nothing%20is%20really%20happening%27%3A%20a%20former%20Claude%20Code%20engineer%20on%20coding%20agent%20mania&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-coding-agent-mania-warning%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Before we start: the one outcome I want shipped today is [outcome]. Plan only the steps needed for that, flag anything off-plan, and at the end list what actually shipped." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="ponytail-skill-less-code-fewer-tokens" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/ponytail-skill-less-code-fewer-tokens/" class="hover:text-brand-600">The Claude Code skill with 180,000 GitHub stars: Ponytail makes your agent write about half the code</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Ponytail is an open-source skill that teaches coding agents to build the smallest thing that works: reuse native features, skip speculative abstractions and add a test where the logic is risky. Its own agentic benchmark (39 tasks, Opus 5.5 in headless Claude Code, five runs each) reports Ponytail 5 writing 53% fewer lines with 45% fewer output tokens, 26% lower cost and 41% less time than the same agent with no skill, while passing slightly more hidden checks. The repo has passed 180,000 stars, and v5.3.3 shipped on October 29.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Agents tend to over-build, and every extra line costs tokens now and review time later. A skill that pushes them toward minimal, tested code can cut both without changing your model or plan.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone using Claude Code, Codex, Cursor or Copilot who finds the agent&#039;s changes bloated or burns through usage limits quickly.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source (MIT). Works in Claude Code as a plugin and in Codex, Cursor, Copilot and other agents that read skills. The savings figures are from the project&#039;s own benchmark, so your results will vary by codebase. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Dietrich Gebert on github.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/ponytail-skill-less-code-fewer-tokens/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=The%20Claude%20Code%20skill%20with%20180%2C000%20GitHub%20stars%3A%20Ponytail%20makes%20your%20agent%20write%20about%20half%20the%20code&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fponytail-skill-less-code-fewer-tokens%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="With Ponytail on, add input validation to this form using the smallest change that works, reuse what the framework already provides, and show me the diff size compared with your usual approach." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-bill-tokens-rereading-chat-fix" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-bill-tokens-rereading-chat-fix/" class="hover:text-brand-600">75% of one user&#039;s Grok Bot tokens went to re-reading old chat: the 15-minute audit that shrinks your bill</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A widely read X article (over 500,000 views and 1,400 bookmarks) argues that most Grok Bot cost comes from setup, not work. Every reply and routine run re-reads the bot&#039;s whole conversation, so a bot that wakes every 15 minutes to find nothing still pays for its full history each time. The author says 75% of their exported tokens went to re-reading. The fix is a structure: one bot per domain with its own memory, rules written into each bot&#039;s description, a machine-checkable proof before work counts as done, and one front-door bot that routes requests to the rest.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you run several bots on schedules, the cost of long chats and empty routine runs adds up every night. A short audit can show where the usage actually goes before you add more bots.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users with several bots or frequent routines who hit their limits early or want a smaller bill.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Advice for any Grok Bot plan; no extra cost. The 75% figure is the author&#039;s own export, not an official number, and your split will depend on your bots and routines. Checked November 1, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">The usage figures come from the author&#039;s own account export. We haven&#039;t independently confirmed them, and your results may differ.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/m4lkxx/status/2115775972536434946" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @m4lkxx on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-bill-tokens-rereading-chat-fix/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=75%25%20of%20one%20user%27s%20Grok%20Bot%20tokens%20went%20to%20re-reading%20old%20chat%3A%20the%2015-minute%20audit%20that%20shrinks%20your%20bill&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-bill-tokens-rereading-chat-fix%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Review my bots and routines, list the ones that run often but rarely do anything, and suggest which to slow down, stop or restart with a fresh chat so I stop paying to re-read old history." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="neuralink-think-hey-neuralink-grok-agent-computer" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-29" class="text-slate-400">Oct 29, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/neuralink-think-hey-neuralink-grok-agent-computer/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Think &quot;Hey Neuralink&quot; and a Grok agent starts using the computer for you</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Neuralink&#039;s engineers spent 72 hours at the home of a participant in its VOICE speech-implant study and prototyped features with him. One of them triggers a Grok computer-use agent by thought: the participant imagines saying &quot;Hey Neuralink&quot; followed by a task, the decoder turns that into a command, and the agent carries the task out on the computer by itself. The same sprint added automatic detection of when he&#039;s trying to speak, live brain-signal visualizations, an iOS keyboard for BCI dictation, a lock-screen shortcut and BCI speech piped straight into iPhone calls.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> For people who can&#039;t speak or type, handing a whole task to an agent is far faster than steering a cursor letter by letter. It&#039;s a clear glimpse of agents as assistive tech, not just productivity tools.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People following brain-computer interfaces, accessibility and assistive tech, and anyone tracking where Grok agents are headed.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">A research prototype only, built with one clinical-trial participant. Neuralink devices are investigational and not approved by the FDA, and there&#039;s no product or release date for the Grok integration.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://neuralink.com/updates/72-hour-voice-hackathon/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Neuralink on neuralink.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/neuralink-think-hey-neuralink-grok-agent-computer/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Think%20%22Hey%20Neuralink%22%20and%20a%20Grok%20agent%20starts%20using%20the%20computer%20for%20you&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fneuralink-think-hey-neuralink-grok-agent-computer%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Summarize Neuralink&#039;s 72-hour sprint write-up: how the imagined &quot;Hey Neuralink&quot; phrase triggers a Grok computer-use agent, and the other features the team built for the participant." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="pro-200-allowance-halves-oct-30" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/pro-200-allowance-halves-oct-30/" class="hover:text-brand-600">ChatGPT Pro 200 usage gets cut on Oct 30. Check Settings for the 62,500 credits OpenAI is handing out</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI&#039;s Pro tiers help page confirms that grandfathered Pro 200 subscribers, meaning anyone with an active Pro 200 plan at any point from September 22 to 10 a.m. Pacific on September 29, 2026, keep the old allowance only through October 29, 2026. After that, they move to the lower included allowance and the price stays $200 a month. OpenAI says only affected users get an email with the details. That email, which subscribers have shared publicly, says ChatGPT Work and Codex usage drops from 20x to 10x the Plus allowance, GPT-6 Pro in chat drops from 200 to 100 messages a week, and affected users get a one-time grant of 62,500 usage credits (valued at $2,500) that expires December 31, 2026. Those exact numbers are in the email, not on OpenAI&#039;s public help page.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you lean on Codex or ChatGPT Work every day, your effective limit halves this week for the same $200. The credit grant softens it, but only until December 31, so unused credits simply vanish.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Existing ChatGPT Pro 200 subscribers who qualified for grandfathering, especially heavy Codex and ChatGPT Work users.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The old allowance ends October 29, 2026; the change starts October 30. Price stays $200/month. The 62,500-credit grant is for affected existing subscribers only (per OpenAI&#039;s email), expires December 31, 2026, and counts toward eligible use in Codex, ChatGPT Work and ChatGPT for Word, Excel and PowerPoint, not every model. New Pro 200 subscriptions get the lower allowance from the start.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9793128-about-chatgpt-pro-tiers" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on help.openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/pro-200-allowance-halves-oct-30/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=ChatGPT%20Pro%20200%20usage%20gets%20cut%20on%20Oct%2030.%20Check%20Settings%20for%20the%2062%2C500%20credits%20OpenAI%20is%20handing%20out&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fpro-200-allowance-halves-oct-30%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I have a ChatGPT Pro 200 plan whose Codex allowance is being halved. Here is my usual weekly workload: [paste]. Estimate which tasks eat the most usage and suggest how to batch or trim them so I stay inside the new limit." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="launches-singapore-shopee-grab" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/launches-singapore-shopee-grab/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Meta&#039;s Muse lands in Singapore, plugged into Shopee, Grab, Lazada and Singapore Airlines, and it&#039;s free to start</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta&#039;s personal AI agent Muse is now available in Singapore on iOS, Android and muse.ai. Beyond Gmail, Google Calendar and Instagram, its early local connector partners are Shopee, Grab, Singapore Airlines, Agoda, ShopBack, Klook, Trip.com and Lazada. You can ask it to compare products and prices on Shopee or Lazada, plan groceries and meals through GrabMart and Grab Dine Out, explore flights, hotels and tickets through Singapore Airlines, Agoda, Klook and Trip.com, and claim cashback and dining deals through ShopBack. Meta says connector features roll out progressively, so some arrive after launch. Muse runs on a dedicated cloud computer that keeps passwords and payment methods out of the agent&#039;s view, and it checks with you before sending email or buying anything.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> This is one of the first times a mainstream personal agent launches in a new country with a full set of local shopping, food and travel apps, rather than only US services.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People in Singapore who shop on Shopee or Lazada, order through Grab, or plan trips, and want an agent to do the comparing and booking legwork.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Live in Singapore from October 28, 2026 on iOS, Android and muse.ai (AI glasses coming). Meta says it&#039;s free for most of what people need; local reports say the free tier has a weekly usage limit and paid plans run about S$22 to S$139. Some connectors roll out after launch.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://about.fb.com/news/2026/10/muse-is-now-available-in-singapore-the-worlds-first-personal-ai-agent-built-for-everyone/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Meta on about.fb.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/launches-singapore-shopee-grab/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Meta%27s%20Muse%20lands%20in%20Singapore%2C%20plugged%20into%20Shopee%2C%20Grab%2C%20Lazada%20and%20Singapore%20Airlines%2C%20and%20it%27s%20free%20to%20start&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Flaunches-singapore-shopee-grab%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Compare the price of [product] on Shopee and Lazada, including shipping and any vouchers I can use. Show me the three best options in a table, and don&#039;t buy anything until I say yes." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-deal-watcher-order-concierge" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-deal-watcher-order-concierge/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Grok Bot can now watch prices and coupons for you and chase your refunds, without buying a thing unless you say yes</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Grok Bot 0.77.0 adds two ready-made Bot templates. Order Concierge tracks your orders, refunds and returns, so a late package or a missing refund doesn&#039;t slip through. Deal Watcher keeps an eye on prices and coupons for things you want. Per the changelog, both never buy without your OK. The same release lets Bots try your saved Vault cards first and gives the Vault a Payments tab to set which method is used first, still with your approval on every purchase. Version 0.77.0 also adds Import Memory to Grok Bot in Settings (needs 0.75.2 or later), which brings the preferences and context you built up with another AI assistant into your primary Bot, plus a Permissions section that lists your Auto-review rules.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Watching prices and chasing refunds is tedious work most people skip and lose money on. It&#039;s exactly the kind of background job an always-on agent is good at.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Online shoppers, anyone waiting on refunds or returns, and people who wait for a price drop before buying.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">In Grok Bot 0.77.0 (changelog dated October 26, 2026; stable rollout announced on X on October 28, Dubai time). Grok Bot requires a paid plan; templates are free to add. Tracking orders works best with your email connected. Import Memory needs 0.75.2 or later.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.ai/changelog/bot#v0.77.0" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @SpaceXSI on x.ai ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-deal-watcher-order-concierge/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Grok%20Bot%20can%20now%20watch%20prices%20and%20coupons%20for%20you%20and%20chase%20your%20refunds%2C%20without%20buying%20a%20thing%20unless%20you%20say%20yes&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-deal-watcher-order-concierge%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Every morning, check my email for open orders, returns and refunds. Give me one short list of anything late, stuck or missing a refund, with the next step for each. Never buy or cancel anything without asking me." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-tibot-x-mentions-digest" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-tibot-x-mentions-digest/" class="hover:text-brand-600">This free Grok Bot reads every X post about you, untagged ones too, and sends one tidy digest a day</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">X user lauren (@poteto) shared tibot, the Grok Bot she uses to manage her X account, as a template anyone can add. According to her post, it finds every post about you or keywords you choose, whether you&#039;re tagged or not, and sends one short, sorted digest a day (or hourly if you prefer). It skips spam and noise, translates non-English posts, can automatically block trolls and abuse, and never posts for you. She says she still writes all her own posts and uses tibot only to stay in the loop. The post passed 4,700 likes and Elon Musk reposted it.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Notifications only catch posts that tag you. For a founder, creator or brand, the untagged conversation is often the important part, and this bot surfaces it without the doomscrolling.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Founders, creators, marketers and anyone with a growing X presence who wants to track mentions and keywords.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The template link in the post is free to add, but running it needs a paid Grok Bot plan and uses your Bot usage. Shared October 28, 2026 (Dubai time).</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/poteto/status/2115205951649423585" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @poteto on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-tibot-x-mentions-digest/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=This%20free%20Grok%20Bot%20reads%20every%20X%20post%20about%20you%2C%20untagged%20ones%20too%2C%20and%20sends%20one%20tidy%20digest%20a%20day&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-tibot-x-mentions-digest%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Watch X for posts about me (@yourhandle) and these keywords: [list], tagged or not. Each evening, send me one short digest sorted by importance, translate non-English posts, skip spam, and never post or reply for me." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="github-copilot-generates-images-gpt-image-2-5-flare" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="images">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Images &amp; media</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-copilot-generates-images-gpt-image-2-5-flare/" class="hover:text-brand-600">GitHub Copilot can now draw your app icons and mockups right in your editor and save them straight into the project</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">GitHub Copilot can now generate and edit images inside your coding workflow, powered by OpenAI&#039;s GPT Image 2.5 Flare. Ask for an icon, an illustration, a placeholder graphic or a UI mockup, and Copilot shows a preview inline and saves the file into your project, so you don&#039;t have to switch to a separate image tool and drag files around. It works in VS Code, the GitHub Copilot app and Copilot CLI. Images are billed as image tokens against your AI credits. There&#039;s an optional &#039;Made with AI&#039; watermark, off by default, and admins can turn image generation off through model policies.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Placeholder art and icons are a small but constant drag on side projects and prototypes. Generating them where the code lives, and having them land in the right folder, removes a whole context switch.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and designers on GitHub Copilot Pro, Pro+, Business or Enterprise who build front ends, apps or docs and need quick visual assets.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Public preview for Copilot Pro, Pro+, Business and Enterprise in VS Code, the GitHub Copilot app and Copilot CLI. Usage is billed as image tokens against your AI credits. Business and Enterprise admins can disable it in model policies.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-generate-and-edit-images-directly-in-copilot" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GitHub on github.blog ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-copilot-generates-images-gpt-image-2-5-flare/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=GitHub%20Copilot%20can%20now%20draw%20your%20app%20icons%20and%20mockups%20right%20in%20your%20editor%20and%20save%20them%20straight%20into%20the%20project&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fgithub-copilot-generates-images-gpt-image-2-5-flare%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Create a flat, minimal 512x512 app icon for a habit-tracking app: a rounded check mark inside a circle, teal on white, no text. Save it to assets/icon.png, then make a dark-mode version at assets/icon-dark.png." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="for-legal-artifacts-gallery" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/for-legal-artifacts-gallery/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude for Legal now ships ready-made tools for contract review and cite checks. Some were built by Harvey, PwC and Foley &amp; Lardner</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic added a gallery of ready-made artifacts to Claude for Legal, covering jobs like contract review, regulatory horizon scans and cite checks. Artifacts are interactive tools that sit next to the chat and that you can keep using and share with anyone across the business. Anthropic&#039;s own set includes cite check, tabular review, a playbook deviation board, a regulatory horizon scan, a jurisdiction survey matrix and a matter board. Partner-built artifacts include Harvey Intake, PwC&#039;s Subpoena Response Tool, Foley &amp; Lardner&#039;s Obligations Checker and Goodwin&#039;s AI Governance Benchmark, with more on the way from firms including Legora and Orrick. Each one starts from a built-in example; you then add your own documents and connectors, and outputs link back to their sources. Legal press also reports a program giving law schools and legal aid groups access to Claude to build access-to-justice artifacts.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Legal teams have asked for less setup and easier sharing. Starting from a working example, and having every answer link back to its source, makes the first pass faster while the lawyer still makes the call.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">In-house legal teams, law firm lawyers and paralegals, and legal operations staff. Law schools and legal aid groups can look at the new access-to-justice program.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Live now in Claude. Anthropic&#039;s announcement doesn&#039;t spell out which plans include each artifact, so check claude.com/solutions/legal for your plan. Always have a lawyer check outputs before relying on them.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/claudeai/status/2115467192276025500" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Anthropic (@claudeai) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/for-legal-artifacts-gallery/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20for%20Legal%20now%20ships%20ready-made%20tools%20for%20contract%20review%20and%20cite%20checks.%20Some%20were%20built%20by%20Harvey%2C%20PwC%20and%20Foley%20%26%20Lardner&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Ffor-legal-artifacts-gallery%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Check every citation in the attached brief against the attached sources. Build a table with: the quote as written, the source quote, whether they match exactly, the page cited versus the actual page, and whether the source supports the proposition. Flag anything that needs a lawyer&#039;s attention." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="github-copilot-fusion-half-the-cost" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-copilot-fusion-half-the-cost/" class="hover:text-brand-600">GitHub&#039;s Copilot Fusion scored within 2 points of Claude Code on Opus 5.5 Max at about half the cost. It&#039;s live on every plan</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Copilot Fusion is now generally available. Instead of picking a model for each task, you pick Fusion and an effort level (Standard, High or Max), and Copilot decides which models to use and how they work together, using workflows GitHub calls Single, Cascade and Critique. GitHub says Fusion Max scored 60 on the Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index, within two points of Claude Code with Opus 5.5 Max, at about half the average API cost per task, about half the tokens and about 40% less time. You&#039;re billed for each model Fusion uses at its standard rate, and admins control which models it can pick from.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most developers either overpay by leaving the strongest model on for everything or lose time switching models by hand. Fusion makes that choice per prompt, and GitHub&#039;s numbers suggest near-top results for much less spend.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers on any GitHub Copilot plan, and enterprise admins who want to control model spend without micromanaging the model picker.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Generally available on all Copilot plans in VS Code, the GitHub Copilot app, Copilot CLI and JetBrains IDEs. Billed per model used, with a limited-time 30% discount for paid plans (no end date given).</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-route-and-orchestrate-models-with-github-copilot-fusion" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GitHub on github.blog ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-copilot-fusion-half-the-cost/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=GitHub%27s%20Copilot%20Fusion%20scored%20within%202%20points%20of%20Claude%20Code%20on%20Opus%205.5%20Max%20at%20about%20half%20the%20cost.%20It%27s%20live%20on%20every%20plan&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fgithub-copilot-fusion-half-the-cost%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Using Copilot Fusion at High effort: read this repository, find the three slowest database queries in the request path, explain why each is slow, and propose an index or query change for each with a before-and-after test." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-planchet-team-member-musk-hire" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-planchet-team-member-musk-hire/" class="hover:text-brand-600">An analyst &#039;promoted&#039; his Grok Bot Planchet to full team member. Elon Musk replied &#039;Hire Grok Bot&#039; and it passed 19 million views</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Tech analyst Pierre Ferragu posted that his Grok Bot, named Planchet, has been &#039;promoted to fully-fledged team member&#039;. He says it has access to all of his team&#039;s thinking (research, emails, models, Slack and industry data), calls it incredibly resourceful, ultra-fast and receptive to feedback, and sums it up as &#039;mind-blowing&#039;. Elon Musk quoted the post with &#039;Hire Grok Bot, you won&#039;t regret it&#039;, and Ferragu&#039;s post showed more than 19 million views when we checked. Ferragu didn&#039;t publish his exact configuration, so the steps below are a general way to set up a similar research teammate with Grok Bot&#039;s connectors.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a high-profile example of a small research team treating an agent as a colleague rather than a chatbot: one name, shared context, and real access to the team&#039;s work.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Analysts, investors and small research teams who live in email, Slack and spreadsheets and want one agent that knows the whole context.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot is available on paid plans of The X Subscription; connectors like Gmail and Slack depend on your plan and what you connect. Ferragu&#039;s results are his own account.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/p_ferragu/status/2115239300874850481" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Pierre Ferragu (@p_ferragu) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-planchet-team-member-musk-hire/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=An%20analyst%20%27promoted%27%20his%20Grok%20Bot%20Planchet%20to%20full%20team%20member.%20Elon%20Musk%20replied%20%27Hire%20Grok%20Bot%27%20and%20it%20passed%2019%20million%20views&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-planchet-team-member-musk-hire%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="You are Planchet, a research teammate for a small investment team. Every weekday at 7am, read new emails and Slack threads tagged #research, plus news on the companies in coverage.md, and send me one brief: what changed, why it matters for each company, and any number in our models that may need updating. Never send anything outside the team." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="free-year-google-ai-plus-canadian-students" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/free-year-google-ai-plus-canadian-students/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Students in Canada can get a year of Google AI Plus free (worth $6.99 a month). Claim it before Dec 31</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google is giving eligible university and college students in Canada the Gemini student plan free for one year. That&#039;s 12 months of Google AI Plus, which normally costs $6.99 a month, with 2x higher usage limits in Gemini, Gemini inside Google apps like Gmail, and 400 GB of storage. Google also points students to its student hub at gemini.google.com/students, with study notebooks, interactive 3D visualizations and Deep Research inside Gemini Live. You need to claim the offer by December 31, 2026, and it renews at the regular price after the free year unless you cancel.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a full year of a paid Gemini plan at no cost, right before exam season. Just set a reminder: it renews at $6.99 a month after the free year unless you cancel.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Eligible students at universities and colleges in Canada.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free for 12 months for eligible Canadian university and college students; claim by December 31, 2026. A valid payment method is required, and it auto-renews at $6.99/month after the free year unless cancelled. Offer terms apply.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://blog.google/intl/en-ca/products/explore-get-answers/eligible-canadian-post-secondary-students-can-get-one-year-of-gemini-on-us/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google Canada on blog.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/free-year-google-ai-plus-canadian-students/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Students%20in%20Canada%20can%20get%20a%20year%20of%20Google%20AI%20Plus%20free%20%28worth%20%246.99%20a%20month%29.%20Claim%20it%20before%20Dec%2031&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Ffree-year-google-ai-plus-canadian-students%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Here is my syllabus and lecture notes for [course]. Build a study notebook: list the topics in exam priority, give me a 10-question diagnostic quiz, then make a two-week plan with daily 45-minute sessions focused on my weakest topics. Add the exam dates to my Google Calendar." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="text-your-dot-imessage-rcs" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/text-your-dot-imessage-rcs/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Your ChatGPT dot can now text you first, over iMessage or RCS, like a friend who never forgets</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI is rolling out texting for dots, the always-on ChatGPT agents, as a preview for Pro users in the U.S. Once you switch it on, your dot can message you in your normal phone messages app over iMessage on iPhone or RCS on Android, and it can reach out first, for example with a reminder or an update on something it was tracking. You can text it new tasks or things to keep an eye on, using text, photos or even voice notes. OpenAI&#039;s release notes say the texting thread shares the same memory and plugins as your dot in the app, your dot can only text you, only you can text it, and it gets no access to your other messages. Delivery runs through Linq, a third-party messaging provider.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> An agent that has to wait for you to open an app is easy to forget. Putting it in your texts, with the power to ping you first, makes a dot feel more like an assistant than a tab.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">ChatGPT Pro subscribers in the U.S. who already use a dot for reminders, tracking or errands and want it where they actually look.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Preview (beta), starting to roll out to ChatGPT Pro users in the U.S. (dots require Pro or Business Premium). Works over iMessage (iPhone) and RCS (Android). No extra charge was announced. Announced October 28, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/ChatGPT/status/2115496387613786374" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @ChatGPT on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/text-your-dot-imessage-rcs/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Your%20ChatGPT%20dot%20can%20now%20text%20you%20first%2C%20over%20iMessage%20or%20RCS%2C%20like%20a%20friend%20who%20never%20forgets&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Ftext-your-dot-imessage-rcs%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Text me every weekday at 8 a.m. with my top three tasks for the day, and ping me if any deadline I&#039;ve told you about is less than 24 hours away." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="4-carbon-tops-intelligence-index" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/4-carbon-tops-intelligence-index/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google&#039;s new Gemini 4 Carbon just took #1 on the AI leaderboard, and almost nobody can use it yet</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google announced Gemini 4 Carbon, which it calls its strongest model yet, with a focus on cybersecurity and long, multi-step coding work. Google says Carbon ranks first on version 5.0 of the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index with a score of 59, and leads security benchmarks for finding vulnerabilities (SEC-bench Pro, 88.2%) and patching them (CWE-bench, 71.0%). It arrives only two weeks after Gemini 4 Argon. Because of its cyber abilities, Google is giving it first to a small group of vetted cyber defenders through its Fairwind Program, then widening access after more guardrail testing.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It is a new top score on a widely watched leaderboard and a signal of where Gemini coding is headed. It also shows the new pattern for frontier releases: defenders first, everyone else later.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers comparing frontier coding models, security teams, and anyone tracking the Gemini vs Claude vs GPT race.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Not publicly available yet. Starting this week it goes to a subset of cyber defenders in Google&#039;s Fairwind Program; developers, businesses and consumers get it &#039;as soon as possible&#039;, with no date. Planned introductory API price: $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens, rising to $4 and $20 after the intro period.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/introducing-gemini-4-carbon/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on blog.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/4-carbon-tops-intelligence-index/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Google%27s%20new%20Gemini%204%20Carbon%20just%20took%20%231%20on%20the%20AI%20leaderboard%2C%20and%20almost%20nobody%20can%20use%20it%20yet&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2F4-carbon-tops-intelligence-index%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
