                                <article id="immersive-explorations-free" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="research">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Research</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/immersive-explorations-free/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Gemini can now take you inside a jet engine or along the Silk Road, layer by layer, and it&#039;s free</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">The Gemini app now has a library of immersive explorations: interactive, visual scenes you can dig into one layer at a time. Google&#039;s examples include tracing trade routes on the Silk Road, looking inside a jet engine and the physics of lightning. Tap a label in the scene to zoom deeper, from planet-scale views down to molecules and atoms, with guided explanations at each step. You open the library from the Gemini student hub with Try immersive explorations. Google says you&#039;ll soon be able to open them inside a normal Gemini chat, and audio narration is on the way.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It turns &#039;explain this to me&#039; into something you can poke at and explore, which is a far better way to learn how complex systems fit together than a wall of text.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Students, teachers, parents and curious learners who want a visual way to understand science, history and engineering topics.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and available to all Gemini users, per Google. Localized in English, Indonesian, Hindi, Brazilian Portuguese, French and simplified Chinese; other languages get English for now. In-chat access and narration are coming soon. Announced October 28, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/immersive-explorations-student-hub/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on blog.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/immersive-explorations-free/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Gemini%20can%20now%20take%20you%20inside%20a%20jet%20engine%20or%20along%20the%20Silk%20Road%2C%20layer%20by%20layer%2C%20and%20it%27s%20free&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fimmersive-explorations-free%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
