                                <article id="utah-claude-code-pilot-20-hours" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/utah-claude-code-pilot-20-hours/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Utah gave Claude Code to 34 state developers for 4 weeks. Most say it saved them 20+ hours</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic shared results from a four-week pilot in which the State of Utah gave Claude Code to 34 developers across 10 state agencies. According to Anthropic&#039;s government partnership post, 80% had a working setup within 30 minutes and 71% reported saving at least 20 hours by the end of the pilot. In an interview, Utah&#039;s technology team added that 77% had a first real win within an hour and about 29% reported saving more than 40 hours. Utah&#039;s leaders are now recommending wider use for state developers. Claude Code creator Boris Cherny highlighted the numbers on X alongside Anthropic&#039;s new 40% government discount.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Government IT is famously slow to adopt tools. Self-reported savings from a real state pilot are a useful benchmark for any team trying to justify an AI coding rollout.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Engineering managers, public-sector IT leaders and anyone building a business case for Claude Code.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code comes with Claude Pro, Max, Team and Enterprise plans or API billing. Government buyers can get Anthropic&#039;s 40% discount through the GSA OneGov deal. Results are self-reported by pilot participants.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/bcherny/status/2115491259381072269" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @bcherny on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/utah-claude-code-pilot-20-hours/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Utah%20gave%20Claude%20Code%20to%2034%20state%20developers%20for%204%20weeks.%20Most%20say%20it%20saved%20them%2020%2B%20hours&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Futah-claude-code-pilot-20-hours%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Help me plan a four-week Claude Code pilot like Utah&#039;s for [number] developers on my team. Write a week-one survey on setup time and first real win, and an end-of-pilot survey on hours saved, with the questions and how to score them." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="anthropic-manager-drops-coding-interview" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-manager-drops-coding-interview/" class="hover:text-brand-600">An Anthropic hiring manager just scrapped the coding interview, and his reason is good news for juniors</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Felix Rieseberg, a hiring manager at Anthropic, says he removed the traditional coding interview from his team&#039;s hiring loops this month because Claude is now better than candidates at small coding challenges, so the test no longer tells him much. In his essay &#039;Hunger beats tenure&#039;, he argues this opens doors for newer engineers: pick work tied to real business goals, choose one bold idea, build a working prototype over a weekend, and use your fresh eyes. He points to a graphical interface for Claude Code that two relatively new Anthropic engineers prototyped over one weekend; the first public version shipped about eight days later. His post passed 1.7 million views and 12,000 likes.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If AI makes coding puzzles meaningless, hiring shifts toward taste, judgment and shipped prototypes. That changes how engineers should prepare and how teams should interview.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Junior and early-career engineers, job seekers, hiring managers and anyone rethinking technical interviews.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free to read on Felix Rieseberg&#039;s blog. This is one manager&#039;s policy for his own team, not an Anthropic-wide hiring rule.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/felixrieseberg/status/2115200995546566910" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @felixrieseberg on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-manager-drops-coding-interview/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=An%20Anthropic%20hiring%20manager%20just%20scrapped%20the%20coding%20interview%2C%20and%20his%20reason%20is%20good%20news%20for%20juniors&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fanthropic-manager-drops-coding-interview%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Here is what my company sells and its goals for this year: [paste]. Suggest three small prototypes I could build in a weekend with an AI coding agent that would clearly help one of those goals." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="copilot-agent-merge-fixes-prs" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/copilot-agent-merge-fixes-prs/" class="hover:text-brand-600">GitHub Copilot will now babysit your pull request and fix failing checks and merge conflicts for you</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">GitHub&#039;s Agent Merge, already in the Copilot app and VS Code, is now built into pull requests on github.com. Click Watch and fix in a pull request&#039;s merge box and choose whether Copilot should fix failing GitHub Actions workflows, resolve merge conflicts, or both. When one of those blockers shows up, Copilot starts working on it in a cloud development environment. You can turn it on by default for every pull request you open, and pair it with auto-merge so GitHub merges the moment all requirements pass.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> The last mile of a pull request, red CI and rebase conflicts, eats hours of attention. Handing it to an agent that works in the cloud means fewer context switches back to old branches.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and teams on GitHub who open lots of pull requests and lose time to flaky checks and conflicts.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Agent Merge in the cloud needs a paid Copilot plan (Copilot Pro starts at $10/month), subject to your organization&#039;s and enterprise&#039;s policies. Announced at GitHub Universe on October 28, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-agent-merge-watches-and-fixes-pull-requests-in-the-cloud/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GitHub on github.blog ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/copilot-agent-merge-fixes-prs/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=GitHub%20Copilot%20will%20now%20babysit%20your%20pull%20request%20and%20fix%20failing%20checks%20and%20merge%20conflicts%20for%20you&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fcopilot-agent-merge-fixes-prs%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Before I turn on Watch and fix for this pull request, list the GitHub Actions checks that are failing and any merge conflicts, and tell me which ones are safe to let Copilot fix on its own." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="github-replica-open-source-prototyping" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-replica-open-source-prototyping/" class="hover:text-brand-600">GitHub just open-sourced Replica, a free tool that turns a sentence into a prototype built from your own design system</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">GitHub Design open-sourced Replica, an AI prototyping tool that turns ideas into clickable prototypes using your team&#039;s real components, patterns and docs instead of generic UI. Designers set up the guidance, and anyone on the team can describe what they want in plain language in the GitHub Copilot app, then test and refine the result next to the conversation. Teams can publish prototypes to an optional, self-hosted Replica Hub where teammates explore them and leave comments. The code is on GitHub under the MIT license, so you can adapt it to your own workflow.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most AI prototyping tools spit out generic screens that look nothing like your product. Grounding prototypes in your design system means PMs and designers can test ideas that actually look shippable.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Product designers, product managers and front-end engineers who want faster, on-brand prototypes.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source under the MIT license, available now. Prototyping happens through the GitHub Copilot app, so your Copilot plan and usage apply. Replica Hub is optional and self-hosted.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-introducing-replica-an-open-source-ai-prototyping-tool/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GitHub on github.blog ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-replica-open-source-prototyping/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
