                                <article id="codex-runway-dev-plugin" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="video">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Video</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-runway-dev-plugin/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One plugin lets Codex wire AI video generation into your app while you just describe what you want</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Runway released a Runway Dev plugin for Codex that gives the agent what it needs to build Runway&#039;s generative media API into your app. After a single plugin install, you describe what your app should generate, such as product videos, images or characters, and Codex writes the integration. The plugin bundles account access through MCP plus skills covering Runway&#039;s API, models, routers, characters, recipes and workflows, so Codex isn&#039;t guessing at endpoints. Runway also published a step-by-step guide to building a generative media integration with Codex.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Adding AI video to a product used to mean days of reading API docs. Giving the coding agent official skills for the API means fewer broken calls and a working feature much sooner.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">App developers and indie hackers who want AI video or image generation in their product and already use Codex.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The plugin is free to install. You need Codex (ChatGPT Plus and up, or an API key) and a Runway developer account; Runway API usage is billed by Runway. Announced October 28, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://docs.dev.runwayml.com/guides/plugin/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Runway on docs.dev.runwayml.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-runway-dev-plugin/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=One%20plugin%20lets%20Codex%20wire%20AI%20video%20generation%20into%20your%20app%20while%20you%20just%20describe%20what%20you%20want&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fcodex-runway-dev-plugin%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Add a feature to this app that turns a product photo into a 5-second showcase video using the Runway API. Store the API key in an environment variable and show progress while it renders." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
