        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/instagram-saved-posts-training-plan/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Someone had Muse turn her saved Instagram posts into a real ski training plan</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">X user Brie (@briechong) shared that Meta&#039;s Muse, which connects to Instagram, built her a ski training plan from the posts she had saved on Instagram, and organised her saved collection along the way. She called the Instagram integration Muse&#039;s biggest win for her. Meta&#039;s Chief AI Officer Alexandr Wang quoted her post, called the Muse and Instagram integration awesome and said there are &#039;more fun things planned&#039; there. It&#039;s a neat example of turning a messy pile of saved posts, which most people never look at again, into something you can actually use.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most people&#039;s saved folders are graveyards of good intentions. An assistant that can read them and turn them into plans or tidy collections makes all that saving worth something.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Instagram users who save lots of workout, recipe, travel or how-to posts and never get back to them.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse is Meta&#039;s assistant. What it can read from your Instagram may depend on your account, region and rollout; the post doesn&#039;t spell out the exact setup or plan. Shared October 28, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/briechong/status/2115303444118643034" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @briechong on X ↗</a>
