                                <article id="pro-business-api-credits-up-to-500-month" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/pro-business-api-credits-up-to-500-month/" class="hover:text-brand-600">ChatGPT Pro and Business now come with up to $500 a month in free OpenAI API credits</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Eligible ChatGPT Pro and Business subscribers can now claim monthly OpenAI API credits at no extra cost. Pro gets credits that match its tier: $100 on the $100 plan, $200 on the $200 plan and $500 on the $500 plan. Business workspaces get $20 per paid Standard seat and $100 per paid Premium seat, pooled and capped at $500 per workspace per month. The credits work across the API, including the Responses and Agents APIs (with hosted sandboxes), Realtime voice, image generation and built-in tools, and you don&#039;t need a payment method on the API account to use them.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you already pay for Pro or Business, this is real API budget for building your own apps and agents, and it costs nothing extra.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">ChatGPT Pro subscribers and Business workspace owners who want to build or test apps and agents on the OpenAI API.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Active, paid Pro or Business subscriptions that have been paid for at least 7 days. Plus, free trials, complimentary plans, Enterprise, Edu and legacy Codex seats don&#039;t qualify. The person claiming must own both the subscription and the API organization, with the same email. The first month is prorated, credits expire at the end of each billing cycle with no rollover, and they can&#039;t be used for Codex through API keys or to raise ChatGPT limits. No end date is given. Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001626-api-credits-benefit-for-eligible-chatgpt-subscriptions" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on help.openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/pro-business-api-credits-up-to-500-month/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=ChatGPT%20Pro%20and%20Business%20now%20come%20with%20up%20to%20%24500%20a%20month%20in%20free%20OpenAI%20API%20credits&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fpro-business-api-credits-up-to-500-month%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I have $200 of OpenAI API credits this month. Suggest three small agents I could build with the Responses API in a weekend, with a rough token budget for each, so I don&#039;t waste the credits." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
