                                <article id="strava-connector-training-coach" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/strava-connector-training-coach/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Gemini can now read your Strava runs and tell you if you&#039;re actually getting faster</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Strava is now a connector in the Gemini app. Once connected, Gemini can read your Strava activities and answer questions about your own training, like whether you&#039;re getting faster at the same heart rate, how a race went, how strength sessions line up with your running, your fastest 10K this year versus all time, how heat affected your pace, or how long your streak is. Access is read-only, so Gemini can&#039;t post or change anything in Strava, and you can disconnect at any time.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Your Strava history holds answers that usually take a coach or a spreadsheet. Now you can just ask in plain words.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Runners, cyclists and other Strava users in the US who want quick, personal training insights.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">US only for now. You need a paid Strava subscription (including Strava + Runna, Family, Student and the Military, Educator and Medical plans); it works on all Gemini plans. Read-only: Gemini can&#039;t upload, edit or delete activities. Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://press.strava.com/articles/strava-now-integrated-as-a-connected-app-in-google-gemini-enabling-users-to-get-more-personalized-training-insights" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Strava on press.strava.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/strava-connector-training-coach/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Gemini%20can%20now%20read%20your%20Strava%20runs%20and%20tell%20you%20if%20you%27re%20actually%20getting%20faster&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fstrava-connector-training-coach%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Look at my Strava runs from the last 12 weeks. Am I getting faster at the same heart rate? Show the trend, my best 10K this year versus all time, and one change to try next week." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="connected-apps-platform-mcp-preview" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/connected-apps-platform-mcp-preview/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Build one MCP server and your app can show up in both Google Search and Gemini</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google opened a preview of the Connected Apps Platform, which lets developers build one integration that works in both Google Search and the Gemini app. You connect either a cloud MCP server or an Android app through MCP with AppFunctions (now in beta), then register, test and submit it in the new Google Connected Console, choosing Search, Gemini or both. You can test in Gemini&#039;s Developer Mode before submitting. Adobe, Calm and Peloton are among the new partners. Google also announced A2UI for Jetpack Compose (alpha) and a Gemini Nano 4 agentic API in ML Kit (alpha).</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Instead of building separate integrations for each Google surface, one MCP server can put your app in front of Search and Gemini users.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">App and web developers who already have, or plan to build, an MCP server or an Android app.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developer preview with phased access: you sign up and Google opens access over time. AppFunctions is in beta; A2UI for Compose and the ML Kit agentic API are alpha. Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/connected-apps-one-place/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on blog.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/connected-apps-platform-mcp-preview/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Build%20one%20MCP%20server%20and%20your%20app%20can%20show%20up%20in%20both%20Google%20Search%20and%20Gemini&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fconnected-apps-platform-mcp-preview%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Design the MCP tool list for my booking app so it can work in Google Search and Gemini: name each tool, its inputs and outputs, and which actions should need user confirmation." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="opus-5-5-vibe-game-development-make-it-more-fun" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/opus-5-5-vibe-game-development-make-it-more-fun/" class="hover:text-brand-600">&quot;Make it a LOT more fun&quot;: Simon Willison built 4 real games with Claude Opus 5.5 in under 4 hours each</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Simon Willison calls October an inflection point for vibe game development: Claude Opus 5.5 can now build games that are genuinely fun, not just tech demos. He made four, each with no more than four hours of his own time: Tree Appreciator, one-shotted in a Claude chat; Emberwick, an RPG with about a 15-minute story; Battle Drones, a multiplayer real-time strategy game released as open source; and Quarter Sun Cove, a pumpkin farm game built over about two days with Opus 5.5 Ultracode. His prompts are simple, starting with &quot;Build a mobile-friendly three.js game where...&quot; and then pushing with &quot;Make it a LOT more fun&quot;.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Making a small game used to take weeks of coding. Now a clear idea plus a couple of pushy follow-ups gets you something people actually want to play.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Hobbyists, parents, teachers and developers who want to make small browser games without being game developers.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Works in claude.ai with Claude Opus 5.5; he says it also works on chatgpt.com, though he found GPT-6 Astra isn&#039;t quite there yet for this. Usage limits depend on your plan. Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/28/vibe-game-development/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Simon Willison on simonwillison.net ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/opus-5-5-vibe-game-development-make-it-more-fun/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=%22Make%20it%20a%20LOT%20more%20fun%22%3A%20Simon%20Willison%20built%204%20real%20games%20with%20Claude%20Opus%205.5%20in%20under%204%20hours%20each&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fopus-5-5-vibe-game-development-make-it-more-fun%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Build a mobile-friendly three.js game where I tend a small pumpkin farm that changes with the seasons. Use touch controls, add a score, and keep it all in one HTML file." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="api-guidelines-content-controls" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/api-guidelines-content-controls/" class="hover:text-brand-600">The Grok API now lets you tell the model which content to decline, per request</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">xAI added a guidelines parameter to the Grok API. You pass a list of policies, each with a category (adult content, violence or profanity) and the behavior decline, and the model will refuse that kind of content for that request. It works with Chat Completions, the Responses API and the xAI Python SDK; with the OpenAI SDK you send it through extra_body. Because it&#039;s set per request, one app can use stricter rules for kids or customer support and looser ones elsewhere. It isn&#039;t supported on multi-agent models or deferred completions, and invalid settings return a 400 or 422 error.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Apps for kids, schools or brands need tighter content rules than a general chatbot. Now you can set them in the API call instead of building your own filter.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers building on the Grok API for customer support, education, kids&#039; apps or brand-safe products.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Available to all Grok API customers. Not supported on multi-agent models such as grok-4.20-multi-agent, or with deferred completions. Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://docs.x.ai/developers/advanced-api-usage/custom-moderation-controls" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @xAI on docs.x.ai ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/api-guidelines-content-controls/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=The%20Grok%20API%20now%20lets%20you%20tell%20the%20model%20which%20content%20to%20decline%2C%20per%20request&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fapi-guidelines-content-controls%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Write a Python call to the Grok API with the xAI SDK that sets guidelines to decline profanity and adult content, and handles 400 and 422 errors." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="github-agentic-workflows-ga-markdown" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-agentic-workflows-ga-markdown/" class="hover:text-brand-600">GitHub Agentic Workflows are out of preview: write automations in plain Markdown and Copilot runs them</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">GitHub Agentic Workflows, an open source project from GitHub Next, is now generally available. You describe an automation, like issue triage, CI failure analysis, docs updates or test writing, in a natural-language Markdown file, and it compiles into standard GitHub Actions YAML that runs on your existing runners and policies. GitHub Copilot or another coding agent does the work. Agents run read-only by default inside a sandbox behind a firewall, their outputs are validated, and a threat detection job checks proposed changes before they&#039;re applied. GA adds self-hosted ARC runner support, budget forecasting with gh aw forecast, per-workflow model choice and model routing.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Repetitive repo chores like triaging issues or explaining failed CI runs can now be written as plain instructions instead of scripts.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Maintainers and teams on GitHub who want AI to handle routine repository work inside Actions.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Generally available on github.com for GitHub Free, Team and Enterprise. Using the default Copilot CLI engine requires a Copilot license, and runs use Actions minutes and AI credits (gh aw forecast estimates the cost). Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-github-agentic-workflows-generally-available/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GitHub on github.blog ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-agentic-workflows-ga-markdown/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
