    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/meta-university-research-caltech/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Meta is giving Caltech and 4 other universities access to Muse Wonder and Muse Spark for research</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta announced research support for five universities: Caltech, Ohio State&#039;s medical center, LSU, Indiana University and UTHealth Houston. Researchers get access to Meta&#039;s latest Muse models, including Muse Wonder and Muse Spark, open-weight models like Muse Glimmer and Muse Spark Open, computer vision models such as SAM, V-JEPA and DINO, and the multilingual SeamlessM4T model, to speed up work across science and medicine.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It puts Meta&#039;s newest models into real science and medical labs, which is where we&#039;ll find out what they&#039;re actually good for.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Researchers, students and anyone following how AI labs are working with universities.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">For researchers at the five named universities. Everyone else can still use the open-weight models like Muse Glimmer and Muse Spark Open, and Muse in the Meta AI app. Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/AIatMeta/status/2115490919923548307" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @AIatMeta on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/meta-university-research-caltech/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
