                                <article id="github-enterprise-includes-copilot-10-standalone" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-enterprise-includes-copilot-10-standalone/" class="hover:text-brand-600">GitHub Enterprise now comes with Copilot for every licensed user, plus $10 Standalone seats for everyone else</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Enterprises working with a GitHub or Microsoft account team can now get GitHub Copilot included with GitHub Enterprise for every licensed user, so the thing to manage becomes AI usage against one enterprise budget, not a count of Copilot seats. People in the enterprise without a GitHub Enterprise license can get the same access through Copilot Standalone at $10 per user per month. Both have the same features and models as Copilot Enterprise but no monthly AI credits per seat. Usage is metered from the first request. Code completion and next edit suggestions keep working with no budget left, while Copilot Chat, code review and cloud agents need budget.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Big teams no longer have to ration Copilot seats. Everyone gets access, and spending is controlled by one AI budget instead.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Engineering managers, GitHub Enterprise admins and finance teams that pay for Copilot.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Available now for GitHub Enterprise Cloud customers who work with a GitHub or Microsoft account team. Self-serve customers can&#039;t get it yet; GitHub says it is opening up in stages with dates in the coming weeks. Copilot Business and Copilot Enterprise are still sold. Copilot Standalone costs $10 per user per month. Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-github-enterprise-now-includes-access-to-github-copilot/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GitHub on github.blog ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/github-enterprise-includes-copilot-10-standalone/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=GitHub%20Enterprise%20now%20comes%20with%20Copilot%20for%20every%20licensed%20user%2C%20plus%20%2410%20Standalone%20seats%20for%20everyone%20else&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fgithub-enterprise-includes-copilot-10-standalone%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Estimate our monthly Copilot cost under usage-based billing: 120 licensed users, 15 Standalone users at $10, and our last 30 days of chat, code review and cloud agent usage. Suggest a budget and alert thresholds." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="copilot-shared-automations-team-workflows" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/copilot-shared-automations-team-workflows/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Copilot Automations go team-wide: shared AI workflows that keep running after their creator leaves</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">GitHub is rolling out shared Copilot Automations. An automation combines a prompt, triggers and the tools you allow, and Copilot runs it on its own in the cloud. Until now they were personal and used your identity and AI credits. A shared automation belongs to the repository: anyone with read access can see it, anyone with write access can edit it, its actions on GitHub are credited to Copilot, AI credits are billed to the repo owner, and it keeps running if its creator leaves. Change history shows how its prompt, tools and triggers have changed. GitHub&#039;s examples include reproducing bugs as soon as an issue opens and screenshotting changes when a pull request is ready.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Team chores like bug reproduction or incident triage can become shared, owned workflows instead of one person&#039;s private script.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Engineering teams and maintainers on GitHub who want Copilot to handle routine repo work for everyone.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rolling out to Copilot Pro, Pro+, Max, Business and Enterprise plans; availability may vary during rollout. Runs use AI credits billed to the repository owner. In organization repos, an admin must enable the &#039;Allow use of Copilot cloud agent billed to the organization&#039; policy. Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-build-shared-workflows-for-your-team-with-copilot-automations/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GitHub on github.blog ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/copilot-shared-automations-team-workflows/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
