                                <article id="bot-martin-casado-500-smart-home-order" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-martin-casado-500-smart-home-order/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Martin Casado&#039;s Grok Bot ordered about $500 of smart-home gear and is now guiding him through the install</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Investor Martin Casado posted that his Grok Bot ordered roughly $500 of Home Assistant kit, microphones, smart lights and plugs, and that he&#039;ll report back on whether it can both order and guide the installation of a full smart house. So far, he says, so good. It&#039;s a real test of an agent doing a whole project, not just a single purchase: picking parts that work together, buying them, and then walking a person through setup. Grok Bot asks you to approve each purchase, and its Order Concierge template tracks orders, refunds and returns.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Smart-home setups fail on compatibility. Having an agent plan the whole parts list and then coach the install is a practical, checkable use.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People setting up Home Assistant or smart lights and plugs who&#039;d like an agent to plan, buy and coach.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot comes with The X Subscription from the $30/month Premium tier up; existing SuperGrok and Cursor subscribers keep it. You approve every purchase. Results depend on the gear you pick. Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/martin_casado/status/2115538638092341620" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @martin_casado on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-martin-casado-500-smart-home-order/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Martin%20Casado%27s%20Grok%20Bot%20ordered%20about%20%24500%20of%20smart-home%20gear%20and%20is%20now%20guiding%20him%20through%20the%20install&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-martin-casado-500-smart-home-order%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Plan a Home Assistant smart-home setup for a two-bedroom apartment under $500: lights, plugs and one voice microphone. List each part, why it&#039;s compatible and its price, and don&#039;t buy anything until I approve." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
