                                <article id="bot-theo-t3-code-fleet-mcp-8-machines" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-theo-t3-code-fleet-mcp-8-machines/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Theo started 8 coding threads on different machines from one Grok Bot chat using T3 Code&#039;s new MCP server</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Theo, who makes the T3 Code app for running coding agents, posted that T3 Code can now control your whole fleet of machines through a single MCP server. In a demo video that passed 190,000 views, he asks Grok Bot to spin up 8 threads on different machines at once. A day earlier he showed one T3 Code thread working across several models, coding harnesses, apps, operating systems and networks. With MCP, any agent that supports it can become the dispatcher for coding jobs running on your other computers.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> You can hand out coding jobs to several machines from a single chat, instead of opening a terminal on each one.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers with more than one dev machine, home server or cloud box who run coding agents.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Shown by T3 Code&#039;s maker on X; check T3 Code&#039;s own docs for which version includes the fleet MCP server and how to set it up. Grok Bot comes with The X Subscription from the $30/month Premium tier up; existing SuperGrok and Cursor subscribers keep it. Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/theo/status/2115409288432906341" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @theo on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-theo-t3-code-fleet-mcp-8-machines/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Theo%20started%208%20coding%20threads%20on%20different%20machines%20from%20one%20Grok%20Bot%20chat%20using%20T3%20Code%27s%20new%20MCP%20server&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-theo-t3-code-fleet-mcp-8-machines%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Using the T3 Code fleet connector, start two threads: one on my desktop to run the test suite and fix failures, one on my laptop to update the README. Report back when each finishes." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
