                                <article id="code-le-mans-racing-sim" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-le-mans-racing-sim/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Someone had Claude Code rebuild Le Mans with 12 AI drivers, and you can play it in your browser</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">An X user shared a racing simulation he built with Claude Code: the 13.6 km Le Mans circuit at real scale, 12 cars driven by AI opponents, and tyre physics he says updates 240 times a second. He published it as a playable Claude artifact called Apex Circuit, a top-down 2D racer with overtakes, skid marks and six circuits, including Le Mans with and without the Mulsanne chicanes. It&#039;s a good example of how far one person can now get on a game with a coding agent: track data, AI drivers and a physics loop in one project.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Physics loops and AI opponents used to be weeks of work for a hobby game. Seeing it done as a side project shows what&#039;s realistic to try this weekend.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Hobby game developers, racing fans and anyone learning game physics with an AI coding agent.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Playing the artifact is free in a browser. Building something similar with Claude Code needs a paid Claude plan (Pro or higher) or API credits.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Asserac/status/2115289901147312564" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Asserac on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-le-mans-racing-sim/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Someone%20had%20Claude%20Code%20rebuild%20Le%20Mans%20with%2012%20AI%20drivers%2C%20and%20you%20can%20play%20it%20in%20your%20browser&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-le-mans-racing-sim%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Build a top-down 2D racing game in one HTML file. Use a fixed 240 Hz physics step with simple tyre grip and slip, one oval track, and 3 AI cars that follow a racing line and try to overtake. Add a lap timer and a debug overlay showing speed and grip." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
