                                <article id="spam-texts-tcpa-tracker" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/spam-texts-tcpa-tracker/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One person turned spam texts into a spreadsheet of possible $500 claims with Muse</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Instead of just blocking spam texts, an X user had his Muse agent log them in a Google Sheet as potential violations of the US Telephone Consumer Protection Act (TCPA), noting that statutory damages under the law can be $500 to $1,500 per violation. The post, which Meta&#039;s Alexandr Wang and the Muse account both shared, shows the general idea: point a personal agent at an annoying, repetitive stream of messages and have it build an organised record with dates, senders and content. Whether any message is actually a violation is a legal question, so treat the sheet as evidence to show a lawyer or regulator, not a verdict. Not legal advice.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most people delete spam and move on. A tidy log with dates and senders is what you need if you ever want to report it or talk to a lawyer, and an agent can keep it without effort.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">People in the US who get frequent spam calls or texts and want a record for reporting or legal advice.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse with access to your messages and Google Sheets; which connectors work depends on your plan and region. The TCPA is US law.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/sethrose/status/2115559371492991038" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @sethrose on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/spam-texts-tcpa-tracker/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=One%20person%20turned%20spam%20texts%20into%20a%20spreadsheet%20of%20possible%20%24500%20claims%20with%20Muse&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fspam-texts-tcpa-tracker%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Create a Google Sheet called Spam log. For each spam text I forward you, add a row with the date and time, sender number, the full message, the company it claims to be, and whether I ever gave that company my number. Don&#039;t reply to any of these messages." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="switched-car-insurance-called-geico" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/switched-car-insurance-called-geico/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Muse shopped his car insurance, switched him to a cheaper policy and phoned the old insurer to cancel</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Mike Nichols posted that his GEICO renewal came in at $2,123, so he had Muse compare quotes. He says it found a Progressive policy for $1,536 with better coverage, then called GEICO to cancel the old policy and only merged him into the call for about a minute to verify his identity. He tagged it #MuseMoneyChallenge and says the switch saves him $1,174 a year. The post has been viewed more than 170,000 times.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Insurance renewals quietly creep up because comparing quotes and making the cancellation call is tedious. An agent that does both removes most of the effort.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse users who want to cut recurring bills like car, home or renters insurance without spending an afternoon on the phone.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse is a paid personal agent. Quotes depend on your driver profile and state. Status unverified: the savings and call details are the poster&#039;s own claims, not confirmed by Muse when we checked on October 31, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/MistrDeplorable/status/2115495145437093938" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Mike Nichols (@MistrDeplorable) on X ↗</a>
