                                <article id="spacexai-ambassadors-free-credits-meetup-funding" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="cursor" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-zinc-200 text-zinc-800 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-zinc-200">Cursor</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-28" class="text-slate-400">Oct 28, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/spacexai-ambassadors-free-credits-meetup-funding/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Cursor will pay for your AI meetup: Cursor x SpaceXAI ambassador applications are open</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Cursor and SpaceXAI reopened their joint ambassador program, announced by Cursor&#039;s Ben Lang on October 28. Accepted ambassadors get free Cursor credits for personal use, early access to nightly builds, funding to cover community meetup costs, stickers and merch, forum moderation powers and a private Slack with the Cursor team. In return you host meetups, hackathons or workshops, help new users and moderate community spaces around Cursor, Grok and Grok Bot. Cursor&#039;s community page already lists 300+ ambassadors running events in 250+ cities.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you already run a study group, meetup or campus club about AI coding, this turns your venue, snacks and your own Cursor bill into something the company covers.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Community organizers, student club leads, teachers and developers who like hosting workshops or hackathons about Cursor, Grok and Grok Bot.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free to apply; you must be 18+, fill in the form and accept the Code of Conduct. Space is limited, applications are reviewed weekly and answers usually come in 2 to 3 weeks. The commitment is open-ended, renewable after a year, and Cursor prefers that you don&#039;t join other advocacy programs at the same time. No closing date is listed. Without the program, Cursor Pro is a paid plan. Checked November 2, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://cursor.com/ambassadors" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Cursor on cursor.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/cursor/spacexai-ambassadors-free-credits-meetup-funding/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Cursor%20will%20pay%20for%20your%20AI%20meetup%3A%20Cursor%20x%20SpaceXAI%20ambassador%20applications%20are%20open&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fcursor%2Fspacexai-ambassadors-free-credits-meetup-funding%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Help me draft my Cursor ambassador application: a short intro, a concrete first event like a monthly build night in my city, and how I&#039;d help new Cursor users." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="argon-antigravity-ide-rollout" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/argon-antigravity-ide-rollout/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Gemini 4 Argon is landing in Google&#039;s Antigravity IDE: watch for the update within 24 hours</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Rody Davis from Google posted that Google is starting to slowly roll out Gemini 4 Argon to users of the Antigravity IDE, Google&#039;s agent-first coding editor, and told people to look out for the update in the next 24 hours. Google for Developers also shared a demo of Gemini 4 Argon in Antigravity automating a Unity asset pipeline. Once the update arrives, you can pick Argon as the model behind Antigravity&#039;s coding agents.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Argon is Google&#039;s newest flagship model, and having it inside Google&#039;s own agent IDE lets you try it on real multi-file coding work without wiring up an API key yourself.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers using or trying Google Antigravity, especially for game, web and asset-pipeline work.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Gradual rollout announced October 27, 2026 (Dubai time); the post says to expect the update within about 24 hours, so timing varies by account. Plan limits weren&#039;t stated in the post.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Announced on X by a Google team member. When we checked on October 27, 2026, the rollout was still in progress, so it may not have reached every account yet.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/rodydavis/status/2114878923360342066" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @rodydavis on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/argon-antigravity-ide-rollout/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Gemini%204%20Argon%20is%20landing%20in%20Google%27s%20Antigravity%20IDE%3A%20watch%20for%20the%20update%20within%2024%20hours&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fargon-antigravity-ide-rollout%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Switch to Gemini 4 Argon in this Antigravity workspace. Automate one step of my build pipeline: show me the plan first, make the change, then walk me through the diff before I accept it." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-team-code-review-playbook" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-team-code-review-playbook/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude writes 90% of Claude Code. The team&#039;s review setup doubled merged PRs and cut reverts by 40%+</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic&#039;s Claude Code team published how it reviews code now that Claude writes about 90 percent of it. From June to September, merged pull requests more than doubled while the share that had to be reverted fell by more than 40 percent. The trick is layers, not line-by-line reading: Claude runs the tests, build and linter before a PR exists, a fresh-context review checks the diff, a separate security pass runs, and open findings from either review block the merge. A classifier then sets how many people must approve (none, one or two) based on risk, and paths like auth, billing, CI and release workflows always need a person. A bot&#039;s approval never replaces a required human&#039;s. Review is also capped: one PR went through more than fifty rounds of agent review and fixes overnight, so after three rounds the reviewer now tells the author to step back and rethink the approach.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Agents now write code faster than people can read it. This is a working, measured process from a team shipping at that pace, and most of the pieces are things you can switch on today.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Engineering leads and developers whose teams merge a lot of agent-written pull requests.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The playbook is free to read and copy. Code Review for Claude Code is available on Claude Team and Enterprise plans; the /code-review and /security-review commands run locally in Claude Code.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://claude.dev/blog/solving-code-review-at-anthropic/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on claude.dev ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-team-code-review-playbook/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20writes%2090%25%20of%20Claude%20Code.%20The%20team%27s%20review%20setup%20doubled%20merged%20PRs%20and%20cut%20reverts%20by%2040%25%2B&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-team-code-review-playbook%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Before you tell me this is done, run the tests and the build and show me the output. Then review your own diff with fresh eyes: list any bug, risky change or missing test, with file and line." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="antigravity-free-claude-models-end-nov-2" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-free-claude-models-end-nov-2/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Free Claude Opus 4.6 in Google Antigravity ends November 2. Here&#039;s what the free tier keeps</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google&#039;s Antigravity models page currently lists Claude Sonnet 4.6 (thinking), Claude Opus 4.6 (thinking) and GPT-OSS-120b as available on the Free and Google AI Plus tiers, and marks all three &quot;Will be removed on November 2, 2026.&quot; After that, the free tier&#039;s agent model is Gemini 3.8 Flash. The newer Claude Sonnet 5.5 and Opus 5.5 are listed for paid (non-trial) Google AI Pro, Ultra and Enterprise, and Gemini 4 Argon for Pro, Ultra and Enterprise. Free users get a quota that refreshes weekly, per the plans page.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you&#039;ve been getting Claude Opus for free inside Antigravity, you have until November 2 to finish that work or pick a new setup. After that, Claude in Antigravity means a paid Google AI plan.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers on Antigravity&#039;s free or Google AI Plus tier who pick Claude in the model menu.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and Google AI Plus: Claude Sonnet 4.6 and Opus 4.6 (thinking) and GPT-OSS-120b until November 2, 2026, then Gemini 3.8 Flash with a weekly quota. Claude Sonnet and Opus 5.5: paid Google AI Pro (not trials), Ultra and Enterprise.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://antigravity.google/docs/models" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google Antigravity on antigravity.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-free-claude-models-end-nov-2/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Free%20Claude%20Opus%204.6%20in%20Google%20Antigravity%20ends%20November%202.%20Here%27s%20what%20the%20free%20tier%20keeps&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fantigravity-free-claude-models-end-nov-2%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
