</article>
                                <article id="bot-shared-sales-bots-quote-deal" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-shared-sales-bots-quote-deal/" class="hover:text-brand-600">SpaceXSI&#039;s sales team handed quotes and deal reviews to three shared Grok Bots. Here&#039;s how they fenced them in</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">In an October 27 post, SpaceXSI&#039;s sales team described three Shared Bots that every rep uses. Account Intel Bot preps meeting briefings, reads the call transcript afterward, updates Salesforce and drafts the follow-up email for the rep to review. Quote Bot builds several pricing proposals side by side, submits them for approval and generates the order form. Deal Bot checks non-standard terms against approved policy and asks a Deal Desk specialist before approving. The guardrails are the interesting part: bots act with each user&#039;s own permissions, a rep can&#039;t use Quote Bot to approve their own discount, Salesforce changes are previewed and confirmed first, and anything customer-facing gets human review.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a rare, detailed look at agents doing real revenue work inside a company, including the limits that keep them from approving their own deals.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Sales and revenue operations leads thinking about giving agents CRM access.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">This describes SpaceXSI&#039;s internal setup, not a new product. Grok Bot is included from The X Subscription Premium tier ($30/month); shared Team Bots are a Grok Business (Teams) feature.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.ai/news/grok-bot-sales" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @xAI on x.ai ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-shared-sales-bots-quote-deal/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
