                                <article id="coderabbit-gpt-6-1-sol-security-agent" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/coderabbit-gpt-6-1-sol-security-agent/" class="hover:text-brand-600">CodeRabbit now hunts security bugs across linked repos with GPT-6.1 Sol, then drafts the fix PR</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI says CodeRabbit uses GPT-6.1 Sol as the main model in its security agent. It looks past a single pull request to how a change affects shared libraries, dependencies and safeguards elsewhere, and CodeRabbit Secure extends that to linked repositories such as a shared authentication library. For findings you select, it can try to verify the exploit in an isolated sandbox (never against production) and, for supported issues, draft a pull request with a proposed fix for a person to review. CodeRabbit reports flagging security issues this way across thousands of repositories, and its review runs independently of whichever agent wrote the code.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most security bugs hide where one change meets code somewhere else. A reviewer that&#039;s separate from your coding agent, and that checks across repos, catches what a single-diff review misses.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Teams merging a lot of agent-written code who want an independent security check on every PR.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">CodeRabbit&#039;s pricing page lists continuous security monitoring on its Advanced plan ($72 per user/month) and Enterprise, with a 14-day trial. You don&#039;t need your own OpenAI plan.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-1-sol-coderabbit-code-security/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/coderabbit-gpt-6-1-sol-security-agent/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=CodeRabbit%20now%20hunts%20security%20bugs%20across%20linked%20repos%20with%20GPT-6.1%20Sol%2C%20then%20drafts%20the%20fix%20PR&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fcoderabbit-gpt-6-1-sol-security-agent%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="@coderabbitai review this pull request for security issues, including how the change affects the shared libraries and linked repositories it depends on. For each finding, explain the risk and the proposed fix so I can decide which ones to verify and turn into a fix PR." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="cathedral-agents-anthropic-systems-12-hours" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/cathedral-agents-anthropic-systems-12-hours/" class="hover:text-brand-600">AI agents got into Anthropic&#039;s sales, HR and IT systems in under 12 hours. What they reached, and what they didn&#039;t</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Security startup Cathedral, founded by former DOGE staffers, says its AI agents found paths into Anthropic&#039;s business systems in under 12 hours while testing under Anthropic&#039;s bug bounty program, as first reported by The Washington Post. The way in wasn&#039;t Claude but unnamed third-party sales, HR and admin software. Cathedral&#039;s draft report says the agents reached meeting transcripts, salary and job-offer details, and Slack messages. Anthropic confirmed access to a limited set of sales, HR and IT systems, said customer conversations, Claude responses, source code and model weights were not reached, shut off access the same day and disabled the affected software until vendors shipped fixes. Anthropic also says Cathedral overstated the national security stakes and didn&#039;t disclose all its testing; Cathedral says it kept data access to a minimum.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Even a top AI lab&#039;s weak spot was ordinary business software. Agents can chain small flaws in connected apps far faster than human testers.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Security and IT teams, and anyone who connects lots of SaaS tools to company accounts.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">News, nothing to install. The vendors and exact flaws have not been named, and Cathedral&#039;s report is still a draft.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://decrypt.co/381860/ai-agents-hack-anthropic-business-systems-12-hours" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Decrypt on decrypt.co ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/cathedral-agents-anthropic-systems-12-hours/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=AI%20agents%20got%20into%20Anthropic%27s%20sales%2C%20HR%20and%20IT%20systems%20in%20under%2012%20hours.%20What%20they%20reached%2C%20and%20what%20they%20didn%27t&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcathedral-agents-anthropic-systems-12-hours%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Help me audit our third-party app connections. Make a checklist covering every app connected to our company accounts (CRM, HR, IT, meeting notes, Slack apps): who uses it, what permissions and OAuth scopes it holds, which admin accounts can manage it, and whether it can be removed or narrowed. End with alerts to turn on for unusual access." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
