                                <article id="bot-follow-list-cleanup-prompt" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-follow-list-cleanup-prompt/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Grok Bot is cleaning up people&#039;s X follow lists: one user flagged about 140 dead accounts out of 1,600</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A wave of X users are asking Grok Bot to audit who they follow. Dylan Grabowski had it go through all 1,600 accounts he follows and flag about 140 dead or quiet ones, then build a page listing each account&#039;s handle, profile link, last activity, days inactive and follower count, with a click-through list of accounts to unfollow. His prompt keeps people who went quiet but still follow you on a separate review list, since they might be friends or customers. Others report similar runs flagging hundreds of accounts, and several say they unfollow in small daily batches to stay inside X&#039;s limits.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Who you follow shapes what you see. Clearing out dead accounts makes room for people you actually learn from, and the bot does an hour of clicking for you.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">X users following hundreds or thousands of accounts.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot with the X connector, included from The X Subscription Premium tier ($30/month).</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version. Grok Bot&#039;s October 23 changelog says X doesn&#039;t offer your followers list to the bot, so the &quot;follows me back&quot; check may not work for everyone. X limits bulk unfollowing, so go slowly.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/GrabowskiDylan/status/2114779341276271098" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GrabowskiDylan on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-follow-list-cleanup-prompt/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
