                                <article id="icloud-mail-calendar-plugins" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/icloud-mail-calendar-plugins/" class="hover:text-brand-600">ChatGPT can now dig through your iCloud inbox and move your calendar events, on every plan including Free</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI added iCloud Mail and iCloud Calendar plugins to ChatGPT. Once you connect them, you can ask ChatGPT to find a specific email, catch you up on what landed in your inbox, tell you what is next on your schedule, or update a calendar event. OpenAI&#039;s release notes say it works on all ChatGPT plans, on the web, the desktop app and iOS. Until now the built-in mail and calendar connections centred on Gmail, Google Calendar and Outlook, so Apple users were the ones left out. The launch post passed 260,000 views within a day.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If your mail and calendar live in iCloud, you no longer have to copy and paste emails or event details into ChatGPT to get help with them.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">iPhone and Mac users who keep their email and calendar in iCloud.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free on all ChatGPT plans, including Free, on the web, the desktop app and iOS (per OpenAI&#039;s release notes, Oct 27, 2026).</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/ChatGPT/status/2115139248458191070" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @ChatGPT on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/icloud-mail-calendar-plugins/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
