                                <article id="google-genie-4-world-model-waitlist" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="video">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Video</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/google-genie-4-world-model-waitlist/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google&#039;s Genie 4 builds a world you can walk through, with sound, and rewrite with one sentence. The waitlist is open</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google DeepMind announced Genie 4, a world model that generates an interactive scene in real time while you move through it with keyboard controls. New this time, it generates audio with the world: music, ambient sound and characters who talk. You can also type mid-simulation to change the weather, move the camera or add a person or object, and Gemini adapts your edit to fit the scene. Press reports say scenes stay consistent for about two minutes, double Genie 3, and Google says details can still drift in longer runs. Generated audio and video carry SynthID watermarks. The launch video passed one million views on X within a day.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It is a big step toward prompt-made, playable scenes, useful for game prototypes, film pre-visualisation and simulated training worlds for robots and agents.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Game designers, filmmakers, AI researchers and anyone curious about world models.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Research preview for trusted testers now. Google says it is coming soon to Google AI Ultra subscribers in Project Genie and to early-access partners in the Gemini API and Google AI Studio. Joining the waitlist is free.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://deepmind.google/blog/genie-4-a-new-generation-of-world-simulation/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google DeepMind on deepmind.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/google-genie-4-world-model-waitlist/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Google%27s%20Genie%204%20builds%20a%20world%20you%20can%20walk%20through%2C%20with%20sound%2C%20and%20rewrite%20with%20one%20sentence.%20The%20waitlist%20is%20open&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fgoogle-genie-4-world-model-waitlist%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="A rainy night market in a coastal town, lanterns swaying, vendors calling out. After 20 seconds, make the rain stop and a street musician start playing." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="synthid-check-is-this-ai-generated" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="research">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Research</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/synthid-check-is-this-ai-generated/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Got a suspicious clip? Ask Gemini &#039;Is this AI generated?&#039; and it scans for Google&#039;s hidden watermark in images, video and audio</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google is pushing SynthID detection in the Gemini app: upload an image, a video or an audio file and ask &quot;Is this AI generated?&quot;, and Gemini checks for the invisible SynthID watermark that Google&#039;s AI tools add. Google&#039;s help page says it checks one file at a time up to 100 MB, videos must be under 90 seconds and audio under an hour, and for video it tells you which parts carry the watermark. The big caveat is that Gemini only recognises content made or edited by Google AI, so &#039;no watermark found&#039; does not prove a file is real. Google says over 180 billion images and videos have been watermarked so far.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Fake clips spread faster than corrections. This gives anyone a free, quick first check before sharing something that looks too good to be true.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Journalists, moderators, teachers and anyone who wants to check a viral image or clip before sharing it.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free in the Gemini app for signed-in users. Files up to 100 MB; videos under 90 seconds, audio under 1 hour. It only detects Google AI watermarks.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/GeminiApp/status/2115171788812669225" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GeminiApp on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/synthid-check-is-this-ai-generated/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Got%20a%20suspicious%20clip%3F%20Ask%20Gemini%20%27Is%20this%20AI%20generated%3F%27%20and%20it%20scans%20for%20Google%27s%20hidden%20watermark%20in%20images%2C%20video%20and%20audio&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fsynthid-check-is-this-ai-generated%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Is this AI generated? If you find a SynthID watermark, tell me which parts of the file it appears in, and explain what a &#039;not detected&#039; result would and wouldn&#039;t mean." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="design-mode-annotate" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="cursor" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-zinc-200 text-zinc-800 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-zinc-200">Cursor</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/design-mode-annotate/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Cursor now lets you draw on your app to tell the agent what to fix: meet Annotate in design mode</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Cursor added Annotate to its design mode, a way to give agents visual prompts instead of long text descriptions. You can edit elements directly, draw on the page to point at what should change, and review your design at different screen sizes before handing it to the agent. Instead of typing &quot;move the second button on the pricing card a bit left on mobile&quot;, you circle it and say what you want. The announcement video passed 60,000 views and 1,400 likes within hours.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Describing a layout problem in words is slow and often misread. Pointing at it is faster and leaves less room for the agent to fix the wrong thing.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Front-end developers and designers who build UI with Cursor&#039;s agent.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Part of design mode in the Cursor app; Cursor&#039;s post didn&#039;t list plan limits, and the feature wasn&#039;t in the public changelog yet when we checked.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/cursor_ai/status/2115159585548021814" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @cursor_ai on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/cursor/design-mode-annotate/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Cursor%20now%20lets%20you%20draw%20on%20your%20app%20to%20tell%20the%20agent%20what%20to%20fix%3A%20meet%20Annotate%20in%20design%20mode&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fcursor%2Fdesign-mode-annotate%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I&#039;ve circled the pricing card on mobile. Make the three buttons stack vertically below 640px, keep equal spacing, and don&#039;t change the desktop layout." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="drug-discovery-89-percent-review-time" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/drug-discovery-89-percent-review-time/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude cut drug-paperwork review time 89% and drafted a 3-month regulatory doc in 4 hours: Anthropic&#039;s six pharma tests</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic shared early results from research partnerships with six drug developers: BigHat Biosciences, Bristol Myers Squibb, Divergence Labs, Enveda, Generate Biomedicines and The Column Group. At Enveda, Claude reviewed 1,061 pages of manufacturing records, caught all 11 issues human reviewers had found plus seven they missed, and cut review time by 89%, from over 25 hours to under three. It also drafted one regulatory document in four hours that normally takes about three months. At BigHat, Claude-proposed antibody-fragment variants bound more than 10x more tightly. Anthropic has also started its own drug programs, including for rare childhood muscular dystrophy. Most of the work is still preclinical.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It is one of the most detailed public accounts of an AI model working across real drug development, from molecule design to the paperwork that slows trials down.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Life-science teams, biotech founders and anyone tracking AI in medicine.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">These are research partnerships, not a product launch. Claude itself is available on Free, Pro, Max, Team and Enterprise plans, and the partners&#039; technical reports are linked from the post.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/early-progress-drug-development" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/drug-discovery-89-percent-review-time/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
