                                <article id="codex-designs-3d-printed-camera-mount" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-designs-3d-printed-camera-mount/" class="hover:text-brand-600">He asked Codex for a camera mount, not code: it designed the CAD, exported the STL, and the print snapped on first try</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Maker ThinkerZhang asked OpenAI&#039;s Codex for a mount that holds an M5Stack StickS3 on the hot shoe of a RICOH GR camera, with the screen facing him for selfies. Codex produced a parametric CAD model and exported an STL, and he printed a snap-fit mount and clipped it on. It is part of a wave of hardware builds people are sharing in OpenAI&#039;s &#039;You can just build things&#039; hardware space, from badges to stands. Parametric means the dimensions live in code, so you can ask for a tweak, like 0.3 mm more clearance, and regenerate.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Custom brackets and mounts used to need CAD skills. Describing the part and its measurements to a coding agent now gets you a printable first version.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Makers, photographers and anyone with a 3D printer and a gadget that needs a holder.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Codex is included with ChatGPT Plus, Pro, Business, Enterprise and Edu plans. You&#039;ll need your own 3D printer or a print service.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: shared by a maker on X; we haven&#039;t printed this ourselves, and fit depends on your measurements and printer.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Tinker_Zhang/status/2115066197008134388" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Tinker_Zhang on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-designs-3d-printed-camera-mount/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=He%20asked%20Codex%20for%20a%20camera%20mount%2C%20not%20code%3A%20it%20designed%20the%20CAD%2C%20exported%20the%20STL%2C%20and%20the%20print%20snapped%20on%20first%20try&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fcodex-designs-3d-printed-camera-mount%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Write a parametric OpenSCAD model for a snap-fit mount that slides into a standard camera hot shoe and holds a device 48 x 24 x 15 mm with the screen facing backwards. Put every dimension and the fit clearance in variables at the top, then export an STL." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
