                                <article id="vs-codex-blind-paper-trading-test" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/vs-codex-blind-paper-trading-test/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude 1, Codex 0: one investor&#039;s blind paper-trading test, where one bot made zero trades and the other was 60x faster</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A self-described long-term investor building an AI trading lab gives Claude and Codex the same job from the same rulebook, without letting either see the other&#039;s code, and treats byte-identical output as the best result. After Day 2 the score was Claude 1, Codex 0, ties 3. On one task Claude finished in 11 minutes 39 seconds while Codex first took 11 hours 29 minutes before finding the slowdown. On the practice trading day, Codex&#039;s bot made zero trades and then stopped when his laptop slept, and a test showed it could have failed to sell its holdings at the close. Everything runs on paper money only; it is not investment advice.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Giving two agents the same spec and comparing their output is a cheap way to catch bugs, and this shows the failure modes that matter before any real money is involved.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers building trading or backtesting tools with coding agents, and anyone comparing Claude Code and Codex.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Uses Claude Code (Claude Pro and up) and Codex (ChatGPT Plus and up). Paper trading only: this is not investment advice.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/DrivenByNikiG/status/2115136435242365339" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @DrivenByNikiG on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/vs-codex-blind-paper-trading-test/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%201%2C%20Codex%200%3A%20one%20investor%27s%20blind%20paper-trading%20test%2C%20where%20one%20bot%20made%20zero%20trades%20and%20the%20other%20was%2060x%20faster&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fvs-codex-blind-paper-trading-test%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Implement this paper-trading strategy exactly as the attached rulebook says. Write tests for every rule, including what happens at the market close and when a run is interrupted. Paper trading only; no live orders." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="onegov-40-percent-off-us-governments" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/onegov-40-percent-off-us-governments/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Anthropic cuts Claude prices 40% for every level of US government, with no minimum spend</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic signed a bigger OneGov agreement with the US General Services Administration. Government buyers now get 40% off Claude Enterprise, Claude for Government and the Claude API, and for the first time the discount covers every product surface: buying directly from Anthropic today, and through cloud providers in the coming months. It also extends past federal agencies to state, local, tribal and territorial governments. There is no minimum spend commitment, so agencies pay for the usage they consume. Anthropic estimates the discounts will save government $1 billion, says about 500 US government organizations already use Claude, and is adding a dedicated program to help agencies roll it out.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Public-sector teams usually face long procurement cycles and big upfront commitments. A 40% cut with pay-as-you-go terms makes it far easier for a city IT shop or a state agency to run a real Claude pilot.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">IT leaders, CIOs, developers and procurement staff at US federal, state, local, tribal and territorial government bodies. Not available to private companies or individuals.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Announced October 27, 2026. Eligible US government buyers can purchase Claude at the OneGov discount through GSA&#039;s Multiple Award Schedule now; the discount through cloud providers arrives in the coming months. No end date was given. Claude for Government runs at FedRAMP High.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/expanding-partnership-gsa" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/onegov-40-percent-off-us-governments/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Anthropic%20cuts%20Claude%20prices%2040%25%20for%20every%20level%20of%20US%20government%2C%20with%20no%20minimum%20spend&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fonegov-40-percent-off-us-governments%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="You&#039;re helping a state IT team. Read this legacy repository and write plain-English documentation: what each module does, the database tables it touches, and a list of risks or outdated dependencies, each with a file and line." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-referral-free-usage-reset" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="deals">
