                                <article id="3-sat-eth-paper-14m-tokens" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="research">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Research</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/3-sat-eth-paper-14m-tokens/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude found a faster-than-exponential 3-SAT algorithm on its own in 14M tokens, and the paper names Claude as author</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic posted a paper, A 2^o(n) Time Algorithm for 3-SAT, credited to Claude (Anthropic), in its formal-math GitHub repository. It describes a deterministic algorithm that counts the satisfying assignments of a 3-SAT formula in subexponential time, which refutes the Exponential Time Hypothesis, a widely believed conjecture in complexity theory. The provenance note says an internal Claude research model found the core algorithm on October 16 using 14 million output tokens with no human input, and Anthropic researchers then worked with Claude on the write-up. The proof is formalized in Lean 4, written by AI models. The paper is clear that this doesn&#039;t settle P vs NP and gives no practical speedup for real formulas, and it notes that an internal OpenAI model independently claims a similar result.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s one of the first major math results where the AI is listed as the author and a machine-checked proof comes with it. That&#039;s a strong signal of how far autonomous AI research has come, even though it won&#039;t make your solver faster.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Researchers, computer science students and anyone following AI&#039;s progress on real math problems.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free to read: the paper and Lean 4 formalization are in Anthropic&#039;s formal-math repository on GitHub (marked as a research artifact, not maintained). The internal research model that found it is not publicly available.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/anthropics/formal-math/main/eth/README.md" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on raw.githubusercontent.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/3-sat-eth-paper-14m-tokens/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20found%20a%20faster-than-exponential%203-SAT%20algorithm%20on%20its%20own%20in%2014M%20tokens%2C%20and%20the%20paper%20names%20Claude%20as%20author&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2F3-sat-eth-paper-14m-tokens%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Explain the Exponential Time Hypothesis and what it means that a 2^o(n) algorithm for #3-SAT refutes it. Assume I know basic algorithms but not complexity theory, and spell out why this doesn&#039;t resolve P vs NP." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-director-video-bot-marketplace" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="video">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Video</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-director-video-bot-marketplace/" class="hover:text-brand-600">A Grok Bot called Director takes a one-line brief and plans, shoots and cuts a short film or ad</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Director, a bot by Xi Yan, is now listed in the Grok Bot Marketplace. Its listing describes it as a video director that turns briefs into short films, ads, explainers, music videos and micro-dramas, handling planning, shooting, cutting and delivery. When you import it, it comes with a pack of video skills covering formats, planning, frames, takes, look and a project folder. It builds on Grok Bot&#039;s ability to create videos, adding a structured director&#039;s workflow on top. The X post sharing it passed 2,800 likes and was reposted by Elon Musk.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most AI video tools give you one clip. A director bot that plans shots and edits them into a finished piece is much closer to how real short videos get made.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Marketers, small businesses, creators and anyone who needs short promo videos, explainers or social clips without a video team.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free to import from the Grok Bot Marketplace (listing at x.ai/bot/marketplace/bots/video-director); running it needs a paid Grok Bot plan, and video generation uses your usage. It&#039;s a community bot, not made by the Grok Bot team.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/tetsuoai/status/2115148923337842788" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @tetsuoai on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-director-video-bot-marketplace/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=A%20Grok%20Bot%20called%20Director%20takes%20a%20one-line%20brief%20and%20plans%2C%20shoots%20and%20cuts%20a%20short%20film%20or%20ad&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-director-video-bot-marketplace%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Make a 30-second vertical ad for [product]. Audience: [who]. Tone: upbeat and honest. Show me the plan and shot list first, wait for my OK, then produce the cut with captions." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
