                                <article id="found-62-chrome-cves-update-chrome-156" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/found-62-chrome-cves-update-chrome-156/" class="hover:text-brand-600">An Anthropic model chained four Chrome bugs into a one-click takeover. 62 CVEs later, here&#039;s why you should update to Chrome 156</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic&#039;s Frontier Red Team says an unreleased internal Claude model found and chained four separate Chrome bugs, from V8 heap corruption through a V8 sandbox escape, a CacheStorage race and a FedCM use-after-free, into a one-click remote code execution chain. Its harmless proof of concept simply opens the Calculator app on macOS. Anthropic reported the work to Google, and says 62 CVEs from this research have been assigned and patched as of Chrome 156, all rated critical or high, including 13 sandbox escapes and 21 renderer bugs. The same post describes a Safari same-origin chain Apple has fixed, a Pixel 9 lock-screen data issue Google has fixed, a Windows HTTP/3 denial-of-service bug (CVE-2026-33096) and a Linux MPTCP root bug (CVE-2026-98432) patched upstream. Anthropic is also releasing a Claude Code security plugin and recommends scanning code at pull-request time.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> AI is now finding serious browser bugs faster than most teams ship patches. The fixes are already out, so the practical takeaway is simple: anyone still on an older Chrome is exposed to bugs that are now publicly described.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Everyone who uses Chrome, IT admins who manage browser fleets, and security teams who want to add AI scanning to code review. Qualifying security professionals can apply to Anthropic&#039;s Cyber Verification Program.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Patches are free: 62 CVEs are fixed as of Chrome 156 (Stable 156.0.8078.73/.74 shipped on October 27). The Claude Code security plugin is available to Claude Code users. The Cyber Verification Program is by application for qualifying security professionals. The model that found the bugs is internal and unreleased.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/discovering-vulnerabilities-with-claude" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Anthropic Frontier Red Team on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/found-62-chrome-cves-update-chrome-156/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=An%20Anthropic%20model%20chained%20four%20Chrome%20bugs%20into%20a%20one-click%20takeover.%2062%20CVEs%20later%2C%20here%27s%20why%20you%20should%20update%20to%20Chrome%20156&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Ffound-62-chrome-cves-update-chrome-156%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Review the changes in this pull request for security problems only. For each finding give the file and line, the bug class (for example use-after-free, injection or auth check), how an attacker could reach it, the severity, and a minimal fix. Skip style issues." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="oracle-ai-smb-bundle-12k-oci-credits" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/oracle-ai-smb-bundle-12k-oci-credits/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Oracle and OpenAI are handing US small businesses up to $12,000 a year in free cloud credits, plus ChatGPT credit. Who qualifies</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Oracle&#039;s new AI SMB Bundle, built with OpenAI, packages ChatGPT and Codex with Oracle&#039;s cloud and business apps for small and midsize companies. Approved businesses get US$12,000 in Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI) credits each year, renewable for up to three years in total, a free tier of NetSuite QuickStart for invoices, bills and cash flow, and a free tier of Oracle App Composer with up to 100 app deployments a month. There&#039;s also a one-time US$50 ChatGPT credit per user for up to five users ($250 per workspace), which Oracle&#039;s terms tie to installing the NetSuite QuickStart plugin in ChatGPT Business and using it within 7 days. The idea: plan in ChatGPT, write and test code with Codex, deploy on OCI.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Cloud hosting is one of the first real bills a new software company pays. Up to $36,000 in credits over three years, plus free finance and app tools, can cover a small team&#039;s infrastructure while it finds customers.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">US small and midsize businesses that are privately held, for-profit and independent, building a product with ChatGPT and Codex. Not for government bodies, nonprofits, crypto companies, service-only consultancies, or Oracle customers with more than $250K in Universal Credits.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free to apply; availability is limited and every application is reviewed. One enrollment per company. You&#039;ll need business details, a credit card and OCI tenancy details, and usage beyond the credits is billed. Credits: US$12,000 per year for up to 3 years total. ChatGPT credit: one-time $50 per user, up to 5 users. Oracle hasn&#039;t published an end date.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.oracle.com/artificial-intelligence/smb-bundle/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Oracle on www.oracle.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/oracle-ai-smb-bundle-12k-oci-credits/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Oracle%20and%20OpenAI%20are%20handing%20US%20small%20businesses%20up%20to%20%2412%2C000%20a%20year%20in%20free%20cloud%20credits%2C%20plus%20ChatGPT%20credit.%20Who%20qualifies&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Foracle-ai-smb-bundle-12k-oci-credits%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
