                                <article id="phone-tree-utility-call-dials-you-in" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/phone-tree-utility-call-dials-you-in/" class="hover:text-brand-600">He asked Muse to call his utility company. It got through the phone bots to a human in about 4 minutes, then dialed him in</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Gagan Bansal posted that he asked Meta&#039;s Muse agent to contact his utilities to make changes to his account. He says Muse worked through the automated phone menus to a human representative in about four minutes, and when the rep needed to speak to him directly, Muse dialed him into the call. Muse&#039;s official account quoted the post with &#039;hang it in the louvre&#039;. It&#039;s one user&#039;s experience, and Meta hasn&#039;t published details of how Muse&#039;s calling works or where it&#039;s available.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Sitting on hold and pressing buttons through phone trees is exactly the kind of chore people want an agent to take over, and a hand-off when a human is needed is the right way to do it.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse users who dread customer-service calls: utilities, internet providers, insurers and the like.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse is on iOS, Android and muse.ai in the countries where Meta has launched it. Meta hasn&#039;t said where phone calling is available; this report is from one user.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/bansalg_/status/2114877645053890947" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Gagan Bansal (@bansalg_) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/phone-tree-utility-call-dials-you-in/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=He%20asked%20Muse%20to%20call%20his%20utility%20company.%20It%20got%20through%20the%20phone%20bots%20to%20a%20human%20in%20about%204%20minutes%2C%20then%20dialed%20him%20in&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fphone-tree-utility-call-dials-you-in%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Call my electricity provider and ask them to move my billing date to the 15th. My account number is [number] and the service address is [address]. Get through the phone menu to a person, don&#039;t agree to any new plan or fees, and dial me in if they need to verify my identity. Send me a summary with the reference number afterward." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-7-bots-one-clock-launch-team" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-7-bots-one-clock-launch-team/" class="hover:text-brand-600">7 Grok Bots, 1 clock: the setup that takes an idea from X on Monday to a live launch or a written &#039;kill&#039; by Friday</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A widely shared X guide by Gipp lays out a seven-bot Grok Bot team that turns ideas spotted on X into launches. Each bot has one job: Chief keeps a live Launch Board and tells you what needs you; Scout is the only bot on a schedule and searches X; Pain Miner collects complaints; Judge scores each idea and says GO or KILL; Builder writes a spec, builds on one pull request and never merges; Pitch makes the deck, video and launch posts; and Buyer can pay only with your approval for each purchase (the guide&#039;s example has a $40 cap). An Inbox bot replaces hourly checks with email aliases that trigger narrow routines. The bots hand off work by appending lines to a shared LEDGER.md file instead of emailing each other. The author says this runs about 60 times a week, compared with his estimate of 1,176 for a team of hourly bots.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most people burn their Grok Bot allowance on bots that wake up every hour to find nothing. One clock plus event triggers keeps usage low, and narrow jobs stop one bot from mixing research, opinions and code.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Indie hackers, solo founders and small teams who use Grok Bot and want to test product ideas quickly without losing control of money or posts.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Needs Grok Bot on a paid plan of The X Subscription, plus whichever connectors you use (GitHub, email, payments). The usage figures are the author&#039;s own estimates.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/gippp69/status/2115018135396905000" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Gipp (@gippp69) on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-7-bots-one-clock-launch-team/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=7%20Grok%20Bots%2C%201%20clock%3A%20the%20setup%20that%20takes%20an%20idea%20from%20X%20on%20Monday%20to%20a%20live%20launch%20or%20a%20written%20%27kill%27%20by%20Friday&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-7-bots-one-clock-launch-team%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Set up my launch team in Grok Bot: Chief, Scout, Pain Miner, Judge, Builder, Pitch and Buyer, each with one job. Scout is the only bot on a schedule (Mondays, 9am). Every bot appends one line to LEDGER.md when it finishes. Builder never merges. Buyer never pays without my yes for each purchase. Show me each bot&#039;s instructions before creating anything." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="codex-import-other-agent-memories" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-import-other-agent-memories/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Switching to Codex? It can now pull in the memories you built up in other coding agents</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Codex CLI 0.165.0, released October 27, turns on Memory v2 by default for fresh profiles and adds support for importing memories from other coding agents into it. Write-ups from users describe importing Claude Code memory files, with project scope and file paths kept intact. The same release adds GPT-6.1 Terra to the model list, a built-in Google Cloud Vertex AI provider, a repository filter in the session picker, and lets you change reasoning effort mid-conversation on supported models.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> The biggest cost of switching coding agents is re-teaching them your project quirks. Carrying memories over makes trying Codex alongside another agent much less painful.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers who use Claude Code or another coding agent and want to try or move to Codex without starting from zero.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free CLI update; using Codex needs a ChatGPT plan that includes Codex (Plus and up) or an API key. Memory v2 is the default only for fresh profiles. The import may be behind feature settings, so check the Codex docs for the exact steps.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on learn.chatgpt.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-import-other-agent-memories/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Switching%20to%20Codex%3F%20It%20can%20now%20pull%20in%20the%20memories%20you%20built%20up%20in%20other%20coding%20agents&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fcodex-import-other-agent-memories%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I just imported my Claude Code memories. Tell me what you now remember about this project, including file paths and conventions, and flag anything that looks out of date or wrong." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="anthropic-buys-one-person-biotech-mithril" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-buys-one-person-biotech-mithril/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Anthropic bought a one-person biotech whose founder used Claude to run 11 outside labs</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Cody Tranbarger, known on X as Prof Oak, revealed that Anthropic acquired Mithril Medicine, the one-person biotech he founded to develop bispecific antibodies for LAMA2-CMD, a rare genetic muscle disease in children. Anthropic says he used Claude to coordinate work across 11 external labs and went from an idea to promising results in mice in under 18 months, with steps like turning an idea into a design plan taking two to three days instead of one to two months. The deal closed in July and was disclosed this week alongside Anthropic&#039;s drug development research update.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a concrete example of one person with an AI model doing work that normally takes a full startup team, in one of the hardest fields there is.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Founders, scientists and anyone curious how far a solo builder can get with AI in research-heavy work.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">News, not a product. The work is still preclinical (animal studies), and any human trials are years away. Anthropic&#039;s write-up is at anthropic.com/research/early-progress-drug-development. Checked October 29, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Prof_Oak_/status/2115185849424048564" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Prof_Oak_ on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-buys-one-person-biotech-mithril/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Anthropic%20bought%20a%20one-person%20biotech%20whose%20founder%20used%20Claude%20to%20run%2011%20outside%20labs&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fanthropic-buys-one-person-biotech-mithril%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Here&#039;s a research idea and the outside partners I can work with. Turn it into a design plan: experiments in order, which partner does each, what I need to send them, and what result would make me stop or continue." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
