</article>
                                <article id="sequoia-openai-pokerbot-100k" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-27" class="text-slate-400">Oct 27, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/sequoia-openai-pokerbot-100k/" class="hover:text-brand-600">$100K for a poker bot you build in 60 minutes: Sequoia and OpenAI&#039;s free student tournament</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Sequoia, OpenAI and Citadel Securities are hosting No Limit, an in-person bot-building tournament. Teams of one or two get 60 minutes to build a no-limit hold&#039;em poker bot from scratch, then the bots play 10,000 games against each other. Regionals run 6 to 9 PM local time in the Bay Area (Nov 6), Boston (Nov 9) and Pittsburgh (Nov 12). The top teams from each regional fly to the San Francisco finals on Nov 15, with travel covered, and play for a $100,000 grand prize. Seats are limited and applications are reviewed on a rolling basis.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s free to apply, the build takes an hour, and the final pays $100K. It&#039;s a real test of how fast you can ship a working agent with today&#039;s AI coding tools.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Current students at US and Canadian universities and 2025 or 2026 graduates who can attend a regional in person.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free to apply. Open to current US and Canadian university students (verified by school email) and the classes of 2025 and 2026; 18+, or under 18 with a guardian&#039;s consent for regionals. Apply by 11:59 PM local time: Nov 3 for the Bay Area (PT), Nov 6 for Boston (ET), Nov 9 for Pittsburgh (ET). You must attend the full event in person, and be able to attend the SF final to win.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://pokerbot.sequoiacap.com/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Sequoia Capital on pokerbot.sequoiacap.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/sequoia-openai-pokerbot-100k/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=%24100K%20for%20a%20poker%20bot%20you%20build%20in%2060%20minutes%3A%20Sequoia%20and%20OpenAI%27s%20free%20student%20tournament&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fsequoia-openai-pokerbot-100k%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Help me practise for a 60-minute pokerbot build. Write a minimal no-limit hold&#039;em bot in Python with a hand-strength estimate, a simple betting policy and a local simulator that plays it against a random bot for 10,000 hands. Keep it under 300 lines and explain where I&#039;d improve the strategy first." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="gpt-6-1-terra" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-26" class="text-slate-400">Oct 26, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/gpt-6-1-terra/" class="hover:text-brand-600">GPT-6.1 Terra matches GPT-6 Astra on agent tasks at one-tenth the price, and it&#039;s in ChatGPT now</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI released GPT-6.1 Terra, a fast mid-tier model built for computer use: it reads what&#039;s on screen, clicks and types across apps, and writes more naturally than GPT-5.6 Terra. On Agents&#039; Last Exam, OpenAI&#039;s test of agents doing real office software work, OpenAI says Terra performs on par with GPT-6 Astra at one-tenth Astra&#039;s price per token and finishes tasks over three times faster than both Astra and GPT-6.1 Sol. Standard API prices are 50% lower than GPT-5.6 Terra: $1 per million input tokens and $5 per million output tokens.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Agents that fill in forms, read invoices or click through apps all day get expensive fast. A model that does this work at near-flagship quality for a fraction of the cost makes high-volume automation realistic, and your ChatGPT or Codex allowance covers more tasks.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">ChatGPT Plus, Pro, Enterprise and Edu users, Codex users, and developers running computer-use or high-volume agent jobs on the API.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rolling out from October 26, 2026 to Plus, Pro, Enterprise and Edu users in ChatGPT Work and Codex. In the API it&#039;s gpt-6.1-terra at $1 input / $5 output per million tokens (cached input $0.05; Batch and Flex 50% off). OpenAI still recommends GPT-6.1 Sol or GPT-6 Astra for deep research and the hardest coding.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-6-1-terra/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/gpt-6-1-terra/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=GPT-6.1%20Terra%20matches%20GPT-6%20Astra%20on%20agent%20tasks%20at%20one-tenth%20the%20price%2C%20and%20it%27s%20in%20ChatGPT%20now&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fgpt-6-1-terra%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Open the PDF invoice I attached and copy the invoice number, date, line items and total into a new spreadsheet row. Tell me before you click anything you&#039;re not sure about." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="nonprofits-plugin-8-dollar-seats" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-26" class="text-slate-400">Oct 26, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/nonprofits-plugin-8-dollar-seats/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Nonprofits now get Claude Team for $8 a seat ($3 in lower-income countries), plus a new fundraising plugin</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic released the Claude for Nonprofits plugin, a set of skills and connectors built with about 30 nonprofits. It maps where your organization keeps donor data, grants and policies, answers &#039;can I use Claude for this?&#039; from your own AI policy, researches funders and open grants, breaks down RFPs, drafts proposals and grant reports, and helps with campaign planning, job posts, onboarding plans and board decks. It comes on top of nonprofit pricing: Claude&#039;s nonprofit page lists the Team plan at $8 per user per month, or $3 for nonprofits in low- and middle-income countries, with Claude Code included.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most of the 25,000+ nonprofits using Claude are small teams where everyone wears several hats. Discounted seats plus ready-made grant and donor skills, just as year-end fundraising starts, are a real saving of money and staff hours.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Registered 501(c)(3) organizations and their international equivalents, K-12 schools and some mission-based rural health providers, especially small teams doing their own fundraising.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Checked on October 27, 2026 on Claude&#039;s nonprofit pricing page (claude.com/solutions/nonprofits): Team plan for 2 to 150 seats at $8/user/month nonprofit rate, or $3/user/month for nonprofits based in low- or middle-income countries, after verifying through Goodstack. Larger organizations go through Anthropic&#039;s sales team. The nonprofit skills come pre-installed. No end date was given. Anthropic is also running free webinars for admins (November 10) and staff (November 12).</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://claude.com/resources/articles/expanding-claude-for-nonprofits" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on claude.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/nonprofits-plugin-8-dollar-seats/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Nonprofits%20now%20get%20Claude%20Team%20for%20%248%20a%20seat%20%28%243%20in%20lower-income%20countries%29%2C%20plus%20a%20new%20fundraising%20plugin&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fnonprofits-plugin-8-dollar-seats%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Using our AI policy, tell me whether I can use Claude to draft a grant application. Then research open grants that fit our mission and list each one with its deadline and a link." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="bot-x-connector-no-api-credits" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-26" class="text-slate-400">Oct 26, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-x-connector-no-api-credits/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Grok Bot&#039;s X connector just dropped the developer account and API credits: bookmarks, DMs and drafts at no extra charge</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Santiago, who works on the X API team, posted that last week X removed the need for a developer account and X API credits to use the X connector in Grok Bot. That means you can ask your Bot to sort your bookmarks, go through your DMs or draft an article for you without setting up a developer app or paying for API calls. Before this, using the connector meant creating an X developer account and spending API credits on every read.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> The API credits were the main reason people avoided connecting X to their Bot. Without them, chores like turning hundreds of saved bookmarks into a reading list or summarizing your DMs cost nothing extra beyond your Grok Bot plan.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users who post, read or network on X: creators, founders, researchers and anyone with a pile of unread bookmarks.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Announced on X on October 26, 2026 by Santiago of the X API team, who says the change landed the week before. You still need a plan that includes Grok Bot; &#039;free&#039; here means no extra X API charge. Rate limits weren&#039;t stated.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Announced on X by a member of the X API team. When we checked on October 27, 2026, the change wasn&#039;t listed in Grok Bot&#039;s public changelog.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/santiagomed/status/2114868620933333409" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @santiagomed on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-x-connector-no-api-credits/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Grok%20Bot%27s%20X%20connector%20just%20dropped%20the%20developer%20account%20and%20API%20credits%3A%20bookmarks%2C%20DMs%20and%20drafts%20at%20no%20extra%20charge&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-x-connector-no-api-credits%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Sort my last 100 X bookmarks by topic and list the five most useful ones with a one-line note on each. Don&#039;t post, like or reply to anything." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="agent-sdk-agents-as-code" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="cursor" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-zinc-200 text-zinc-800 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-zinc-200">Cursor</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-26" class="text-slate-400">Oct 26, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/agent-sdk-agents-as-code/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Cursor&#039;s Agent SDK is out: build a PR-fixing or Slack bot as a folder of code and deploy it with one command</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Cursor made its Agent SDK generally available. An agent is a project folder: instructions.md is the prompt, each file in tools/ is a typed TypeScript action, skills/ holds procedures loaded on demand, mcp-connections/ adds MCP tools and channels/ sets where it listens. Agents can wake on GitHub, GitLab and Bitbucket pull request, comment and CI events, Slack mentions and DMs, webhooks or a cron schedule. Built-in evals check which tools ran and what the reply looked like, and agent-sdk deploy runs it on Cursor&#039;s infrastructure, or you can host it yourself.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Most team bots are fragile scripts with no tests. Treating an agent as a versioned project with evals in CI means you can change its prompt or tools and know whether it got better or worse before it touches real pull requests.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Engineering teams that want a security reviewer, PR autofixer, approval bot or Linear/Jira triager running on their repos or in Slack.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Generally available per Cursor&#039;s changelog. Starter templates include a security reviewer, an owners-policy approver, a PR autofixer, and Linear or Jira triagers. Pricing for hosted agents wasn&#039;t listed in the announcement.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/cursor_ai/status/2114793714531102901" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @cursor_ai on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/cursor/agent-sdk-agents-as-code/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Cursor%27s%20Agent%20SDK%20is%20out%3A%20build%20a%20PR-fixing%20or%20Slack%20bot%20as%20a%20folder%20of%20code%20and%20deploy%20it%20with%20one%20command&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fcursor%2Fagent-sdk-agents-as-code%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Scaffold a Cursor Agent SDK project in ./my-bot with npm install --global @grok/agent-sdk and agent-sdk init ./my-bot. Write a short bot/instructions.md for a pull request reviewer, run agent-sdk validate, and show me any errors before I run agent-sdk dev." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="anthropic-files-s1-ipo" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-26" class="text-slate-400">Oct 26, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-files-s1-ipo/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Anthropic just filed to go public: Claude&#039;s maker plans a Nasdaq listing under &#039;ANT&#039;</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic, the company behind Claude, filed a Form S-1 registration statement with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission for a proposed initial public offering of its Class A common stock. It intends to list on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the symbol ANT. The number of shares and the price range haven&#039;t been set, the registration isn&#039;t effective yet, and no shares can be sold until it is. Goldman Sachs and Morgan Stanley are named as contacts for the preliminary prospectus.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s one of the biggest moves yet by a frontier AI lab. For Claude users, nothing changes today, but a public Anthropic will publish far more detail about its finances, risks and plans than it does now.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone following the AI industry, and Claude users curious what an IPO could mean for the product. This is news, not investment advice.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Filed October 26, 2026. Share count, price range and listing date had not been announced when we checked on October 27, 2026. Nothing here is an offer to buy or sell securities.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/s1-sec" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-files-s1-ipo/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
