                                <article id="openai-three-discoveries-kakeya-eth" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="research">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Research</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-26" class="text-slate-400">Oct 26, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-three-discoveries-kakeya-eth/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI says its models cracked 3 open problems in one go, including the Kakeya conjecture in every dimension</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI announced three results produced by its internal models. In math, a proof of Sogge&#039;s local smoothing conjecture in every dimension, which would also settle the Kakeya and Stein restriction conjectures; OpenAI says it was formalized in Lean the day after the model produced it. In computer science, a claimed disproof of the Exponential Time Hypothesis, an assumption that many hardness results rest on. In physics, rigorous existence proofs for certain interacting quantum field theories with gauge fields. Outside experts are leading the work of checking and explaining each result.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If these hold up, AI moves from helping with research to producing major new results. OpenAI treats the outputs as raw research data and says it doesn&#039;t seek academic credit, so independent checking by outside researchers is the real test.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Researchers in math, theoretical computer science and physics, and anyone tracking what AI can now do in science.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Announced October 26, 2026. The math output is public; the computer science output is public with an outside working group explaining it; the physics materials will be released when the outside group decides. These are research results, not a ChatGPT feature.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/building-scientific-understanding-with-academic-communities/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-three-discoveries-kakeya-eth/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%20says%20its%20models%20cracked%203%20open%20problems%20in%20one%20go%2C%20including%20the%20Kakeya%20conjecture%20in%20every%20dimension&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fopenai-three-discoveries-kakeya-eth%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Explain OpenAI&#039;s three announced results in plain English, one paragraph each: what was claimed, what was released publicly, and how outside experts are checking it." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="46-videos-4-days-under-10" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="video">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Video</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-26" class="text-slate-400">Oct 26, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/46-videos-4-days-under-10/" class="hover:text-brand-600">She was quoted $250 for one video, so she had Claude run her content team: 46 videos in 4 days for under $10</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Nadia Zueva, co-founder of the AI stylist app Aesty, says Claude now does everything except the filming. Claude studied 249 viral app promos from the last six months (via Apify and yt-dlp, reading hooks off frames with OCR) and sorted them into 15 hook formats. It rewrites the winners for her app, builds a shoot page with each scene and on-screen line, picks the best 2-3 seconds of every take, cuts videos with Remotion, checks every frame for private info, and schedules posts through Postiz. She reports 46 videos in 4 days for under $10 in scraping costs.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Short-form video is the cheapest way for small apps to get noticed, but creators and editors are expensive. Her workflow keeps the human part, a real face on camera, and hands research, editing and scheduling to an agent.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Founders and small teams promoting an app or product on TikTok, Reels and Shorts without a marketing budget.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Uses Claude together with Apify, yt-dlp, Remotion and Postiz. She says scraping cost under $10. Her article is a paid collaboration with Postiz, and her hook-research skills are open source on GitHub.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Reported by the founder on X in a paid collaboration with Postiz; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed her numbers.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/nestymee/status/2114723318033223994" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @nestymee on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/46-videos-4-days-under-10/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=She%20was%20quoted%20%24250%20for%20one%20video%2C%20so%20she%20had%20Claude%20run%20her%20content%20team%3A%2046%20videos%20in%204%20days%20for%20under%20%2410&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2F46-videos-4-days-under-10%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Find recent viral promo videos in my niche and group their opening hooks into formats. Rewrite the top three hooks for my product and list the exact shots I need to film for each." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
