                                <article id="code-iphone-backup-deleted-photo-audit" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-24" class="text-slate-400">Oct 24, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-iphone-backup-deleted-photo-audit/" class="hover:text-brand-600">The viral Claude Code trick that finds &#039;deleted&#039; iPhone photos in your backup, and what&#039;s overstated</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A widely shared post says that while Claude Code was checking a local iPhone backup on a Mac, it flagged a PhotoData/Thumbnails folder with about 152,000 files, including previews of photos the owner had deleted years ago. You can point Claude Code at your own backup to see what&#039;s in it. Be careful with the bigger claims, though: forensic sources say leftover previews are usually low resolution, and iOS sandboxing means a random app with Files access can&#039;t simply read that folder.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> An unencrypted backup on your laptop holds far more than your camera roll shows, and anyone with access to that laptop can read it. A quick audit tells you what&#039;s there before you sell a Mac or share a computer.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">iPhone and Mac users who care about privacy, and anyone about to sell or hand over a laptop.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Needs Claude Code (paid Claude plans or API) and a Mac. Only run it on your own device and backup.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">File counts and contents are one user&#039;s report. The claim that any app with Files access can read the cache is disputed and we couldn&#039;t confirm it.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Cranefomo/status/2114015154895499302" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Cranefomo on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-iphone-backup-deleted-photo-audit/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=The%20viral%20Claude%20Code%20trick%20that%20finds%20%27deleted%27%20iPhone%20photos%20in%20your%20backup%2C%20and%20what%27s%20overstated&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-iphone-backup-deleted-photo-audit%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
