</article>
                                <article id="opus-blog-post-whiteboard-explainer" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="video">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Video</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-24" class="text-slate-400">Oct 24, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/opus-blog-post-whiteboard-explainer/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Turn a blog post into a TEDx-style whiteboard explainer with Claude Opus 5.5 and your cloned voice</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Mike Taylor shared a 10-minute whiteboard-doodle explainer of one of his blog posts. Claude Opus 5.5 made the animation as code, and his ElevenLabs voice clone did the narration. His point is that with both tools this good, there&#039;s no longer much excuse not to turn written posts into watchable explainers. Creators on X are using Opus 5.5 the same way for launch videos and product demos, built frame by frame with tools like Remotion, Manim or plain HTML.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Writers can now repurpose an archive into video without a motion designer. Because the animation is code, you can fix one scene by asking for a change instead of re-editing a timeline.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Bloggers, newsletter writers, marketers and educators who have more written content than video.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Opus 5.5 is on paid Claude plans and the API, and heavy animation work can use up weekly limits quickly. ElevenLabs voice cloning needs a paid ElevenLabs plan. Only clone your own voice.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/hammer_mt/status/2114104682373435457" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @hammer_mt on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/opus-blog-post-whiteboard-explainer/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Turn%20a%20blog%20post%20into%20a%20TEDx-style%20whiteboard%20explainer%20with%20Claude%20Opus%205.5%20and%20your%20cloned%20voice&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fopus-blog-post-whiteboard-explainer%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
