                                <article id="capcut-plugin-desktop-early-access" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="video">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Video</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-24" class="text-slate-400">Oct 24, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/capcut-plugin-desktop-early-access/" class="hover:text-brand-600">You can already edit videos with CapCut inside ChatGPT&#039;s desktop app, weeks before the official launch</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">CapCut announced at CapCut World LA that its plugin is coming to ChatGPT, and early access already works in the ChatGPT desktop app. You describe a video idea or upload clips in a Codex task, the plugin builds an editable draft with CapCut&#039;s editing and generation tools, and you finish it in CapCut&#039;s web editor. CapCut&#039;s page gives a setup prompt that installs the plugin, then you sign in to your CapCut account to authorize it.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It turns a chat into a first cut of a video you can keep editing by hand, which saves a lot of timeline work for short promos and social clips.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Creators, marketers and small businesses who make short videos and already use ChatGPT.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Early access in the ChatGPT desktop app (Mac or Windows) only, from October 2026; CapCut says the plugin itself is free to try. It runs in Codex, which is limited on ChatGPT Free and Go and included on Plus and up. Support for ChatGPT on the web and mobile is expected around mid-November. You need a CapCut account.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.capcut.com/tools/capcut-x-codex" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @CapCut on www.capcut.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/capcut-plugin-desktop-early-access/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=You%20can%20already%20edit%20videos%20with%20CapCut%20inside%20ChatGPT%27s%20desktop%20app%2C%20weeks%20before%20the%20official%20launch&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fcapcut-plugin-desktop-early-access%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Using the CapCut plugin, make an editable draft of a 30-second video from the clips I&#039;ve uploaded: [describe the idea, tone and length]. Put the strongest clip first, add captions, and tell me what to finish in CapCut&#039;s web editor." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
