                                <article id="bot-auto-review-rule-cards" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-24" class="text-slate-400">Oct 24, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-auto-review-rule-cards/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Tired of tapping &#039;approve&#039;? Grok Bot can now write its own Auto-review rules, but only after you confirm the card</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Grok Bot 0.75.8 lets a Bot offer to add, change or remove one of your Auto-review rules on a card you confirm, so if you keep approving the same safe action you can turn it into a rule in one tap. Auto-review also takes a second look before showing an approval card, so fewer safe actions need one. Other changes in the same release: when background work finishes the Bot completes the steps you asked for and then says what it would do next instead of acting on its own, and new connector tools such as X&#039;s work without reconnecting. The 0.75.5 release raised routines to 300 runs an hour in total.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Approval cards are a safety net, but too many of them train you to tap yes without reading. Rules for routine actions keep your attention for the ones that matter.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users who run routines or several bots and get a lot of approval cards.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rule cards need Grok Bot 0.75.2 or later. Grok Bot is included from The X Subscription Premium tier ($30/month).</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.ai/changelog/bot#v0.75.8" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @xAI on x.ai ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-auto-review-rule-cards/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Tired%20of%20tapping%20%27approve%27%3F%20Grok%20Bot%20can%20now%20write%20its%20own%20Auto-review%20rules%2C%20but%20only%20after%20you%20confirm%20the%20card&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgrok%2Fbot-auto-review-rule-cards%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="I keep approving the same kind of action from you. Propose one narrow Auto-review rule that would cover it, explain exactly what it would allow and what it wouldn&#039;t, and wait for me to confirm." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
