    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-zinc-200 text-zinc-800 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-zinc-200">Cursor</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-23" class="text-slate-400">Oct 23, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/cursor/computer-use-desktop-apps/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Cursor&#039;s agents can now click through your desktop apps to test what they build</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Cursor added Computer Use for agents running on your own computer: they can look at the screen, click and type in desktop apps, not just a browser. Cursor&#039;s demo shows an agent adding a &#039;favorite trails&#039; feature to an iPhone app, then opening the iOS Simulator and tapping through it to check the feature works. Cursor says the agent turns it on by itself when a task needs it, or you can @-mention Computer Use in your prompt.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> An agent that proves its change works in the real app saves you the manual click-through after every edit.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers building mobile or desktop apps with a real interface.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Cursor says to update the desktop app. Supported operating systems and plans weren&#039;t published at launch; self-hosted workers already support computer use on macOS and Linux.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/cursor_ai/status/2113661506634305834" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @cursor_ai on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/cursor/computer-use-desktop-apps/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
