        <time datetime="2026-10-23" class="text-slate-400">Oct 23, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-api-demos-open-in-codex/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI posted 7 free demo apps you can download and remix in Codex</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI&#039;s API demos page has seven new working apps, each with a live demo, an Open in Codex button and downloadable source. Tempo coaches chess puzzles, Facet answers questions about a CSV with charts, Folio turns images and a brief into a slide deck, Lumen finds and fixes accessibility issues, Loupe compares a build against a reference design, and Signal and Ticker show the Decisions API steering traffic and a fictional market.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Starting from a working project is much faster than starting from docs. You can see how the Agents and Decisions APIs fit together, then change one thing at a time.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers learning the newer OpenAI APIs and anyone who wants a head start on a data, slides or accessibility tool.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The demos and source code are free to try and download. Running your own copy uses your OpenAI API key and normal API pricing.</dd></div>        </dl>
