    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-connects-x-money/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Grok Bot now connects X Money when you connect X: what that means for your balance</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Grok Bot 0.75.5 links X Money through the same account when you connect X, and asking a Bot about your X Money balance, activity or card installs the X Money plugin. That means your Bot can look up your balance and recent activity when you ask. The same release lets your routines run up to 300 times an hour in total (up from 100) and lets Bots forward emails with the original formatting and attachments.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> An agent that can see your money is useful for budgeting and spotting odd charges, but it&#039;s also a connection worth knowing about. Some people noticed it only after it appeared in their plugin list.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users who also use X Money and want to check what their Bots can see.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot 0.75.5, released Oct 23, 2026. X Money is only offered where X supports it, currently US states. Grok Bot needs an eligible X or Grok plan.</dd></div>        </dl>
