    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-just-text-it-like-a-person/" class="hover:text-brand-600">&#039;I just texted it&#039;: printed worksheets, family trips and a return label from one Grok Bot</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A widely shared post lists what one person got Grok Bot to do in a week just by texting it: new math and reading worksheets printed for the kids by morning, family trips planned and booked, an order placed from one message, a return label printed with a reminder before the deadline, and a page that breaks down their net worth. They also point to other users booking flights end to end and building Etsy stores.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> These are boring household chores, which is exactly the point. The value of a personal agent shows up in errands you&#039;d never write code for.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Parents and busy people who want to hand off small errands to an agent.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot is included with eligible X Premium and SuperGrok plans. Printing needs a printer the Bot can reach, and bookings or orders should wait for your approval.</dd></div>        </dl>
