                                <article id="notebook-connected-app" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-23" class="text-slate-400">Oct 23, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/notebook-connected-app/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Type @Gemini Notebook in any Gemini chat to create, fill and question your notebooks without switching apps</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Gemini Notebook is now a Connected App inside the Gemini app. Type @Gemini Notebook in a chat to create, edit or delete a notebook, add sources to one (including a copy of the current chat), list a notebook&#039;s sources, or ask questions answered from what your notebooks hold.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Research you collect in notebooks and the chats where you think things through no longer live in separate apps, so you can save a useful answer to a notebook in one line.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Students, researchers and anyone who keeps notes and sources in Gemini Notebook.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Available now to all Google Workspace customers, Workspace Individual subscribers and personal Google accounts, at no extra charge. It&#039;s on by default everywhere except the European Economic Area; you can turn it on or off in Settings &gt; Connected Apps.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2026/10/take-actions-on-your-notebooks-from-Gemini-Notebook-directly-in-the-Gemini-app.html" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google Workspace Updates on workspaceupdates.googleblog.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/notebook-connected-app/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Type%20%40Gemini%20Notebook%20in%20any%20Gemini%20chat%20to%20create%2C%20fill%20and%20question%20your%20notebooks%20without%20switching%20apps&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fnotebook-connected-app%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="@Gemini Notebook create a notebook called [topic], add a copy of this chat to it, then list its sources. After that, tell me what my notebooks say about [question], and cite which source each point comes from." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="code-tradingagents-paper-trading" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-22" class="text-slate-400">Oct 22, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-tradingagents-paper-trading/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Set up TradingAgents, the free open-source &#039;AI trading firm&#039;, with Claude Code (paper trading only)</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">TradingAgents is a free, open-source research framework from Tauric Research (Apache 2.0, with a paper on arXiv) that copies how a trading firm works: four analyst agents cover fundamentals, news, sentiment and technicals, a bull agent and a bear agent argue the case, a trader agent turns that into a decision, a risk team challenges it, and a portfolio manager approves or rejects it. A viral post on X shows how to have Claude Code clone and install it, then run it from the terminal on a ticker and read every report and debate. The project itself says it&#039;s built for research and is not financial, investment or trading advice. Use it to study the reasoning, backtest and paper trade only; this is not investment advice.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Reading a bull-vs-bear debate and a risk team&#039;s objections is a useful way to learn how AI agents reason about markets, with no money at stake.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and finance learners curious about multi-agent systems, as a research and paper-trading setup only.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open source on GitHub (TauricResearch/TradingAgents). You pay for the model you plug in, such as your Anthropic API key or, in recent releases, a ChatGPT Plus or Pro plan. Paper trading and research only, not investment advice.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/carm1nee/status/2113070670590480455" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @carm1nee on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-tradingagents-paper-trading/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Set%20up%20TradingAgents%2C%20the%20free%20open-source%20%27AI%20trading%20firm%27%2C%20with%20Claude%20Code%20%28paper%20trading%20only%29&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-tradingagents-paper-trading%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="auto-mode-default-apps" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-22" class="text-slate-400">Oct 22, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/auto-mode-default-apps/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude switches to auto mode by default next week: safe steps run, risky ones get blocked</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Starting next week, new sessions in most Claude apps (web, desktop and mobile) on Pro, Max and Team plans start in auto mode. Instead of asking you to approve every single action, an automated check lets safe actions go ahead and blocks risky ones, and Claude looks for another way to finish the task. You can switch back to manual approvals whenever you want. Anthropic&#039;s write-up adds that Enterprise admins get an email before auto mode becomes their default.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Agents that stop for a click on every step are slow to use. Auto mode cuts the approvals down to the moments that need you, but it&#039;s worth knowing what&#039;s on before your next long task.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Pro, Max and Team users who hand Claude multi-step tasks, and admins who set team defaults.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Pro, Max and Team plans, rolling out as the default for new sessions from next week. Manual mode stays available. Enterprise admins are emailed before the change. Details: claude.com/resources/articles/auto-mode-default-in-claude-code.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/claudeai/status/2113360845409583307" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @claudeai on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/auto-mode-default-apps/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20switches%20to%20auto%20mode%20by%20default%20next%20week%3A%20safe%20steps%20run%2C%20risky%20ones%20get%20blocked&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fauto-mode-default-apps%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="anthropic-agent-skills-donated-aaif" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-22" class="text-slate-400">Oct 22, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-agent-skills-donated-aaif/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Anthropic hands Agent Skills to the Agentic AI Foundation, already used on 70+ platforms</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic is donating the Agent Skills standard to the Agentic AI Foundation (AAIF), the neutral group under the Linux Foundation. A skill is just a folder with a SKILL.md file that teaches an agent how to do a job. Anthropic says more than 70 platforms already support the format, including ChatGPT, Cursor, GitHub Copilot and VS Code, with about 1 million skills published and nearly 280 million installs. The name, logo, GitHub org and the agentskills.io domain move to the foundation.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> A skill you write once should keep working across Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor and Copilot without one company owning the format. That makes skills a safer thing to invest time in.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone writing reusable instructions for AI agents, and teams standardising how their agents work.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free and open. You can use the standard or contribute without joining AAIF. Spec at agentskills.io.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/donating-agent-skills-to-the-agentic-ai-foundation" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-agent-skills-donated-aaif/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Anthropic%20hands%20Agent%20Skills%20to%20the%20Agentic%20AI%20Foundation%2C%20already%20used%20on%2070%2B%20platforms&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fanthropic-agent-skills-donated-aaif%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
