    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/formal-verification-123-libraries/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude proved 239 open-source entry points can&#039;t crash, and found bugs fuzzers missed</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic&#039;s Frontier Red Team, working with Theorem, had Claude write machine-checked proofs that 239 entry points across 123 OSS-Fuzz libraries never crash on any input under 64 MB. The proofs target the compiled RISC-V binary, not the source, and came to about 180 million lines of Rocq. Along the way Claude turned up bugs that trillions of fuzzing runs had not found. Anthropic also reports Opus 5.5 proves half of its 36 test tasks with roughly 40% fewer tokens than Opus 5.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Tests show bugs exist; proofs show they don&#039;t. Formal verification used to be too slow and costly for most code, and this suggests AI can make it practical.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Security engineers, open-source maintainers and anyone who builds parsers, codecs or other code on a security boundary.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Research results. Open-source maintainers can ask for the same pipeline through Theorem&#039;s free OSS Verify program.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/formal-verification" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/formal-verification-123-libraries/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Claude%20proved%20239%20open-source%20entry%20points%20can%27t%20crash%2C%20and%20found%20bugs%20fuzzers%20missed&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fformal-verification-123-libraries%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
