                                <article id="theorem-oss-verify-free-proofs" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-22" class="text-slate-400">Oct 22, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/theorem-oss-verify-free-proofs/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Free: Theorem will formally verify your open-source project&#039;s fuzz targets</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Theorem, the company that ran the Claude proof pipeline with Anthropic, now offers OSS Verify: it proves that your project&#039;s compiled fuzz targets can&#039;t crash, hang or trip a sanitizer on any input up to 64 MiB, and checks the proof with the Rocq kernel. Any bug that blocks a proof is reported to you privately, with a patch when it has one. Qualifying open-source projects pay nothing. Enrollment is a pull request to theorem-labs/oss-verify, and the repo ships an AGENTS.md so Claude Code, Codex or Cursor can do the setup for you.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> A machine-checked proof that no input crashes your parser is a far stronger guarantee than a fuzzer that hasn&#039;t found anything yet, and it&#039;s normally out of reach for volunteer projects.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Core maintainers of established open-source projects with an OSI-approved licence, a public repo, at least one fuzz target and a security contact.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free for qualifying open-source projects, checked on theorem.dev/oss-verify on 2026-10-23. No deadline stated. Each project is reviewed individually, widely used infrastructure goes first, and smaller binaries are likely to be verified sooner. Builds must be static riscv64. Closed-source code is a paid conversation with Theorem.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://theorem.dev/oss-verify/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Theorem on theorem.dev ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/theorem-oss-verify-free-proofs/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Free%3A%20Theorem%20will%20formally%20verify%20your%20open-source%20project%27s%20fuzz%20targets&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Ftheorem-oss-verify-free-proofs%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
