    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-22" class="text-slate-400">Oct 22, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-decisions-api/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI&#039;s Decisions API answers up to 400 yes/no, pick-one or score questions per call, output free</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI made the Decisions API generally available. You send a POST to /v1/decisions with up to 400 questions, and each comes back as a probability for a yes/no predicate, a choice from your list, or a score. It runs on gpt-6-luna only and OpenAI says it&#039;s up to 10 times faster than asking Luna the same thing through the Responses API. Input costs $0.10 per million uncached tokens and $0.01 cached, and output is free. It also takes JSON inputs, works with GPT-Live and supports US and EU data residency.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Labelling, routing and moderation jobs usually mean parsing free-text answers. Typed answers with probabilities are cheaper, faster and easier to trust in code.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers building classifiers, ticket routers, content filters or lead scoring.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Generally available on the OpenAI API. gpt-6-luna only. $0.10 per 1M uncached input tokens, $0.01 per 1M cached, output free. See OpenAI&#039;s Decisions API guide.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://openai.com/index/decisions-api" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on openai.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-decisions-api/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
