        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-phone-apps-calendar-reminders/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Grok Bot can now use your phone&#039;s Calendar, Reminders, Contacts and more</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Grok Bot can now work with apps on your phone, including Calendar, Reminders and Contacts, rolling out on iOS and Android. Screens shared from the update show a permission page where you allow each area on its own, such as Messages, Location, Calendar, Home, Reminders and Contacts. That means a Bot running on its cloud computer can add a reminder, check your real calendar or find a contact without you copying anything across.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Your phone holds the schedule and people a personal assistant actually needs. Now a Bot can act on them, one permission at a time.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users who want reminders, scheduling and contact lookups handled from chat.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rolling out now in the Grok Bot app on iOS and Android, on eligible Grok Bot plans. Docs: docs.x.ai/grok-bot/mobile.</dd></div>        </dl>
