        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-22" class="text-slate-400">Oct 22, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-muse-1password-sign-ins/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Grok Bot and Muse can now sign in through 1Password without seeing your password</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">1Password launched 1Password for Agents. When Grok Bot or Muse hits a login page, it asks for one specific login from your vault; you approve it on your device and 1Password fills in the password or one-time code directly, so the agent never sees it. Access is per approved login, not your whole vault, and you can disconnect the agent anytime. 1Password says Claude Duet, ChatGPT Work and dots, and Town are coming soon.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Agents stall at every login, and pasting a password into a chat is a bad habit. This removes both problems while you stay in charge of each sign-in.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot and Muse users with 1Password who want their agents to finish tasks behind a login.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Included at no extra cost for 1Password Individual and Family accounts on 1Password.com (not .eu or .ca). Grok Bot and Muse integrations are rolling out over the coming days on all platforms.</dd></div>        </dl>
