        <time datetime="2026-10-22" class="text-slate-400">Oct 22, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/argon-video-soundtrack-canvas/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Gemini 4 Argon built a tool that turns motion in live video into music</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google showed Gemini 4 Argon building a small app inside Canvas in the Gemini app: it draws musical scale lines across live camera video and plays a note whenever something moves across a line. Wave a hand and you get a melody. It&#039;s a good example of the kind of playful, interactive tool you can now make by just describing it, with no setup beyond the Gemini app.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It shows how far one-prompt apps have come: camera input, real-time motion and audio in a browser tool you didn&#039;t code.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Creators, teachers and curious people who want to make interactive toys and demos without coding.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Canvas in the Gemini app. Gemini 4 Argon availability depends on your Google AI plan.</dd></div>        </dl>
