                                <article id="security-continuous-scans-25k-credits" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-21" class="text-slate-400">Oct 21, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/security-continuous-scans-25k-credits/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Claude Security now re-scans your repos on every change, with $25,000 a month in free credits for 2 months</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Claude Security, Anthropic&#039;s code vulnerability scanner, no longer waits for someone to start a scan. You connect up to eight repositories per project (GitHub, GitHub Enterprise Server, GitLab and other Git providers), Claude runs a deep baseline scan, then keeps scanning new changes and marks findings fixed when the fix lands, reopening them if the issue comes back. Each finding gets a severity rating and an explanation of how an attacker could reach the code, and there&#039;s a new API, webhooks and an MCP connector for Claude and Claude Code. Anthropic is giving organizations $25,000 in free usage credits each month for two months, for usage through December 31, 2026. We checked the official page on October 22.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Point-in-time scans miss whatever ships between runs. Continuous scanning plus two months of free credits is a cheap way to test it on your real code.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Security and engineering teams at companies on Claude Enterprise.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Public beta for Claude Enterprise customers only; an admin turns it on in the admin console. Free credits: $25,000 a month for two months, applying to usage through December 31, 2026; full terms are in Anthropic&#039;s Help Center. After that, normal Enterprise usage pricing applies.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://claude.com/resources/articles/claude-security-now-scans-continuously-and-tracks-fixes" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on claude.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/security-continuous-scans-25k-credits/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
