    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-oss-grants-pro-200/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Open-source maintainers: OpenAI&#039;s free Codex grants now come with ChatGPT Pro 200 (10,000 places)</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI&#039;s Codex for Open Source program gives selected maintainers six months of ChatGPT Pro (which includes Codex), API credits for maintainer work, and, for qualifying repositories, conditional access to Codex Security. On October 21 Charlie Marsh of OpenAI said every grant in the current round is being upgraded to the Pro 200 tier, with 10,000 grants still on offer, and that people who already got a grant are upgraded automatically. Applications are open and reviewed on a rolling basis. We checked the official application page on October 22.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Six months of a top ChatGPT tier is a lot of free Codex time for reviewing pull requests, triaging issues and preparing releases.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Maintainers of public open-source projects that other people depend on. You can also nominate another maintainer.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free if selected. Apply on openai.com/form/codex-for-oss with your ChatGPT account email, a public GitHub profile and a public repository. 10,000 grants in this round, reviewed on a rolling basis; no deadline is listed. Existing grants are upgraded automatically.</dd></div>        </dl>
