                                <article id="php2shell-codex-checker" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-21" class="text-slate-400">Oct 21, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/php2shell-codex-checker/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Run a PHP site? Use OpenAI&#039;s free Codex skill to check for the critical &#039;PHP2Shell&#039; bugs</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI says its models, working through its Patch the Planet program, helped find two critical flaws in PHP (CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619, nicknamed PHP2Shell) that allow remote code execution without logging in on PHP installs that serve web requests. Fixes are out now, and the US cyber agency CISA tells everyone to update to PHP 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36 or 8.2.35 right away. To help, OpenAI published a free Codex skill on GitHub (openai/php2shell-checker) that walks you through finding which PHP versions you run and which update applies. Versions 8.1 and older are end-of-life and need a vendor backport or a move to a supported release.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> PHP runs a huge share of the web, WordPress included. A guided check plus a version bump today is far cheaper than cleaning up a hacked server.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone who runs or hosts a PHP site or app: WordPress owners, agencies, freelancers and ops teams.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The checker is a free, public GitHub repo you point Codex at; Codex itself needs a ChatGPT plan that includes it. The PHP updates are free. Fixed versions per CISA: 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36 and 8.2.35.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2112945805686604033" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/php2shell-codex-checker/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Run%20a%20PHP%20site%3F%20Use%20OpenAI%27s%20free%20Codex%20skill%20to%20check%20for%20the%20critical%20%27PHP2Shell%27%20bugs&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fphp2shell-codex-checker%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
