    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-pages-reports-dashboards/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Grok Bot can now build reports, memos and dashboards, and keep them up to date</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Grok Bot can now turn a request into a page: a report, memo, dashboard, tracker or explainer with text, tables, charts and controls like filters. You ask for it in chat, it posts the page as a card you can open, and you change it by asking the Bot, so everyone with access sees the same updated version. You can also have the Bot keep the page current. Pages live in the Bot&#039;s Library, start private, and can be shared with invited people, your team, or anyone with the link.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Plenty of work is a document someone rebuilds every week. A page the Bot keeps current means you share a link instead of copying chat replies around.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Founders, managers and anyone who sends the same status report, tracker or brief every week.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot, rolling out gradually; not on Enterprise teams yet. Needs Grok Bot 0.60.0 or later on desktop and 1.14.0 or later on mobile.</dd></div>        </dl>
