    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-21" class="text-slate-400">Oct 21, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-models-google-cloud/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI models and Codex are coming to Google Cloud</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI and Google Cloud announced a partnership that puts OpenAI&#039;s frontier models and Codex agent workflows into Google Cloud&#039;s Model Garden. Customers will buy them through the Google Cloud Marketplace, and companies with Google Cloud spend commitments can count those purchases against them. OpenAI also says its models will soon be available in Google Antigravity and the Gemini Agent. General availability is planned in the coming weeks, and Microsoft remains OpenAI&#039;s primary cloud partner.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Teams already on Google Cloud could use GPT models without a separate OpenAI contract, and Antigravity users may soon get to pick OpenAI models too.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Companies that build on Google Cloud, and developers who use Google Antigravity.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to Google Cloud customers. Not generally available yet: OpenAI says general availability is planned in the coming weeks, with an access request form on its announcement page.</dd></div>        </dl>
