                                <article id="bot-204-support-tickets-10-minutes" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-20" class="text-slate-400">Oct 20, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-204-support-tickets-10-minutes/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Grok Bot cleared 204 support tickets in about 10 minutes, with one engineer approving</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">The official Grok Bot account says the team uses Grok Bot to spot incidents in its own support queue and reply to every ticket tied to one. During one incident it cleared 204 tickets in about 10 minutes, and a single engineer approved the batch before it went out. The pattern is simple to copy: the Bot groups tickets by cause, drafts one consistent answer, and a human signs off once instead of 204 times.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Outages bury support teams in near-identical tickets. An agent that drafts the whole batch while a person approves it turns hours of copy-paste into minutes.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Support leads and small teams who get ticket floods when something breaks.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot is included in The X Subscription from the $30/month Premium tier up. Your help desk needs to be connected; keep a human approval step.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/bot/status/2112645531076096330" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @bot on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-204-support-tickets-10-minutes/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
