                                <article id="bot-morning-terminal-free-data" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="grok" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/grok/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-slate-200 text-slate-900 dark:bg-white/10 dark:text-white">Grok Bot</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-20" class="text-slate-400">Oct 20, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-morning-terminal-free-data/" class="hover:text-brand-600">One Grok Bot user built a Bloomberg-style morning terminal from free public data feeds (research only)</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A user on X says Grok Bot, working with another agent tool, built him two dashboards overnight. One is a markets screen wired only to free public sources such as SEC filings, FRED macro data, exchange price feeds and RSS news; a panel without a working free source simply isn&#039;t built. The other is a &#039;my day&#039; screen with yesterday&#039;s revenue against the 7-day average, stuck deals, the emails that need him with replies drafted, and last night&#039;s builds. Both rebuild at 6am on weekdays, start with read-only access, and every email or task waits for his approval. This is a research and planning screen, not a trading system, and it is not investment advice.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> You don&#039;t need an expensive pro terminal to see the public data that matters to you on one screen each morning.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Founders and people who follow markets as research and want one morning briefing instead of twenty tabs.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot on The X Subscription Premium tier or higher. Uses free public feeds; check each source&#039;s terms. Paper trading only if you add any trading view, and not investment advice. We haven&#039;t tested his build.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/vmrmax/status/2112462080754278527" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @vmrmax on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-morning-terminal-free-data/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
