                                <article id="locked-chats-pin" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-20" class="text-slate-400">Oct 20, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/locked-chats-pin/" class="hover:text-brand-600">ChatGPT can now lock private chats behind a PIN or Face ID</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Locked chats move chosen conversations out of your regular history, pinned chats and search into a protected section. You open them with a 4-digit account PIN on web and desktop, or a PIN, Face ID, Touch ID or device unlock on supported phones. New messages in a locked chat don&#039;t update the memory used in your other chats. OpenAI&#039;s release notes say your retention and model-improvement settings don&#039;t change, so this hides chats from people using your device; it isn&#039;t end-to-end encryption.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you share a laptop, present your screen or hand your phone to someone, sensitive chats about health, money or a surprise stay out of sight.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone who uses ChatGPT for personal topics on a shared or work device.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rolling out gradually from Oct 20, 2026. The release notes list Free, Go, Plus and Pro on web, iOS, Android and the new ChatGPT desktop app; OpenAI&#039;s post also lists Business, Enterprise and Edu.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/ChatGPT/status/2112597766333673624" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @ChatGPT on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/locked-chats-pin/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=ChatGPT%20can%20now%20lock%20private%20chats%20behind%20a%20PIN%20or%20Face%20ID&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Flocked-chats-pin%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="openai-12-hour-prompt-caching" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-20" class="text-slate-400">Oct 20, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-12-hour-prompt-caching/" class="hover:text-brand-600">OpenAI&#039;s API can now keep your prompt cache for 12 hours</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">In the Responses API you can now ask for a 12-hour minimum cache lifetime instead of the default 30 minutes, so shared instructions, tools and reference context stay cached even when requests are hours apart. OpenAI&#039;s docs say a 12-hour cache write costs 2.5x the normal input rate (30-minute writes cost 1.25x), while cached reads stay at 0.1x input on most GPT-5.6-and-later models and 0.05x on GPT-6.1 Sol. You set it with prompt_cache_options.ttl = &quot;12h&quot;.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Agents that wake up every hour or two, like daily assistants and schedulers, kept losing their cache. Now the cheap cached rate can last a whole working day.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers running long-lived agents or batch jobs on the OpenAI API with a big, stable system prompt.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">OpenAI API, Responses API only, GPT-5.6 and later models. Live since Oct 20, 2026. Older models keep the separate prompt_cache_retention setting.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/OpenAIDevs/status/2112603916076781778" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAIDevs on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-12-hour-prompt-caching/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=OpenAI%27s%20API%20can%20now%20keep%20your%20prompt%20cache%20for%2012%20hours&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fopenai-12-hour-prompt-caching%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="team-tasks-friday-update" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-20" class="text-slate-400">Oct 20, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/team-tasks-friday-update/" class="hover:text-brand-600">ChatGPT team tasks write the Friday &#039;what shipped, what&#039;s blocked&#039; update for your whole team</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Team tasks are recurring ChatGPT jobs owned by a team rather than one person. They run in the cloud on a schedule or a supported event trigger, using the team&#039;s approved app connections, and any authorised teammate can review the results, edit the instructions or pause the task. OpenAI&#039;s example is pulling together what shipped and what&#039;s blocked every Friday; its help docs also suggest daily customer-change digests and meeting briefings posted to an approved Slack channel.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Recurring reports usually die when the one person who set them up goes on holiday. Shared ownership keeps them running.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Engineering, sales and ops teams on ChatGPT Business or Enterprise who repeat the same status report every week.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">ChatGPT Business and Enterprise workspaces, subject to workspace permissions. Enterprise admins control who can create teams and team automations. Tasks don&#039;t inherit the creator&#039;s personal memory or chat history.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/OpenAIDevs/status/2112565702552940794" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAIDevs on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/team-tasks-friday-update/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=ChatGPT%20team%20tasks%20write%20the%20Friday%20%27what%20shipped%2C%20what%27s%20blocked%27%20update%20for%20your%20whole%20team&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fteam-tasks-friday-update%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="android-auto-personal-intelligence" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="productivity">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-20" class="text-slate-400">Oct 20, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/android-auto-personal-intelligence/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Gemini on Android Auto can now read your Gmail and Calendar: &#039;Is my flight on time?&#039; while you drive</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google is rolling out Personal Intelligence for Gemini on Android Auto. If you opt in, Gemini can pull details from Gmail, Google Calendar, Photos, Maps, YouTube and Search while you drive. Google&#039;s examples include asking for your flight gate and delay in one go, &#039;take me to my doctor&#039;s appointment&#039; without knowing the address, finding the car wash from a photo you took last week, and restaurants on your route that match your usual taste. Cars with Google built-in get it in the coming months.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It turns &#039;find the email, then search, then navigate&#039; into one spoken request, so you keep your hands on the wheel.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Android Auto drivers who keep travel, bookings and appointments in Gmail and Google Calendar.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rolling out from Oct 20, 2026 on Android Auto; cars with Google built-in in the coming months. Eligible personal Google accounts, 18+, globally except the EEA, Switzerland, the UK and Nigeria. Not for Workspace business, enterprise or education accounts. Off until you turn it on.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/platforms/android/android-auto-cars-with-google-built-in-gemini-personal-intelligence/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on blog.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/android-auto-personal-intelligence/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
