    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Productivity</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-20" class="text-slate-400">Oct 20, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/receipt-printer-morning-email/" class="hover:text-brand-600">A journalist pointed Claude at a cheap Bluetooth receipt printer, and now his morning email prints itself</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Tech journalist Chris Stokel-Walker bought an inexpensive Bluetooth thermal receipt printer and had Claude work out how to drive it. Now one email he reads to start his day prints out automatically every morning on a strip of receipt paper. He doesn&#039;t share the code, but the idea is easy to copy: Claude writes a small script that fetches the email, formats it for a narrow printer and sends it over Bluetooth on a schedule.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a fun, concrete example of AI making cheap gadgets programmable in an afternoon, even if you&#039;ve never touched a Bluetooth protocol.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Tinkerers who want a screen-free morning briefing, to-do list or daily quote.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Any Claude plan that can write and run code (Claude Code works best), a Bluetooth thermal receipt printer and a computer that stays on. Phenol-free thermal paper is a better choice if you handle receipts daily.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/stokel/status/2112536494623584542" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @stokel on X ↗</a>
