        <time datetime="2026-10-20" class="text-slate-400">Oct 20, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/wonder-in-cursor-openrouter-vercel/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Meta&#039;s Muse Wonder coding model is now in Cursor, OpenRouter, Cline, Vercel and Cloudflare</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta&#039;s Muse Wonder, its model for frontier coding, long-running agents and computer use, is now available through Cline, Cloudflare, Cognition, Cursor, OpenRouter, Oracle and Vercel, with more partners coming. Until now you mostly needed Meta Model API or Muse Code to use it. That means you can pick it in tools you already use and run your own side-by-side test against Claude, GPT or Gemini on real tasks.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> A new frontier option in the tools you already use means more choice on price and speed, and an easy way to compare models on your own code.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers who switch models in Cursor, Cline or OpenRouter, and teams building on Vercel or Cloudflare.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Through each partner&#039;s own plans and pricing. Muse Wonder is also on Meta Model API and in Muse Code. Check each partner&#039;s model list, as rollout may vary.</dd></div>        </dl>
