                                <article id="sharing-paused-chats-found-online" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-20" class="text-slate-400">Oct 20, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/sharing-paused-chats-found-online/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Meta pauses Muse chat sharing after researchers find 6,800+ shared chats online</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta has paused the Muse feature that lets you share a conversation by link, The Verge reports. Security firm Claroc said it found more than 6,800 Muse share links through public DNS records, because each link&#039;s web address was built from the conversation&#039;s title, so the address alone could reveal what a page held. Pages it could open included a company&#039;s revenue review, a loan application and a workplace&#039;s staff calendar. A Muse spokesperson said Meta paused the feature while it reviews the report and considers changes to how these links can be found.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> A share link isn&#039;t the same as private. This has now happened with several AI assistants, so treat any shared chat as possibly public.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone who has shared a Muse chat, and teams that use AI assistants with business data.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to Muse&#039;s share-a-conversation feature, which is paused for now.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1014627/meta-muse-ai-sharing-ai-chats" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: The Verge on www.theverge.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/muse/sharing-paused-chats-found-online/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Meta%20pauses%20Muse%20chat%20sharing%20after%20researchers%20find%206%2C800%2B%20shared%20chats%20online&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fmuse%2Fsharing-paused-chats-found-online%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
    </div>
</div>
