                                <article id="glimmer-30b-free-fine-tuning-fireworks-nov-30" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="muse" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-20" class="text-slate-400">Oct 20, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/glimmer-30b-free-fine-tuning-fireworks-nov-30/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Train your own Meta AI model for $0: Fireworks made Muse Glimmer 30B fine-tuning free until November 30, no card needed</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Fireworks is running supervised fine-tuning (SFT) of Meta&#039;s Muse Glimmer 30B for free through November 30, 2026, in its web app and its Serverless Training API, with no credit card required. You bring example conversations and end up with a version of Glimmer tuned to your task. Fireworks&#039; own recipe trained a LoRA adapter in one pass and says the tuned model beat both base Glimmer and a larger comparison model on its test. Its Agent Skills let Claude Code, Codex, Cursor or OpenCode research, configure and debug the training run for you.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Fine-tuning is usually the step people skip because it costs money to experiment. This lets you test whether a small tuned model beats a big general one on your own task before you spend anything on training.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and small teams with a repeatable task (routing, extraction, classification, a house writing style) who want a cheaper specialised model.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free for Muse Glimmer 30B SFT through November 30, 2026, in the Fireworks UI and Serverless Training API, no credit card required. Inference, including evaluation calls, is billed separately, and other training methods and models use normal rates (from $0.50 per 1M training tokens). Checked on Fireworks&#039; pricing page and blog November 4, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://fireworks.ai/pricing" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Fireworks AI on fireworks.ai ↗</a>
