    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/argon-api-half-price-nov-30/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Gemini 4 Argon&#039;s API is half price until Nov 30: $2 in, $10 out per 1M tokens</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google&#039;s official Gemini API pricing page lists Gemini 4 Argon, its flagship coding and reasoning model, at $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens (thinking included) through November 30, 2026. From December 1 it doubles to $4 and $20. Batch and Flex requests are $1 in and $5 out until the same date. We checked the page on October 19.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you&#039;ve been meaning to test Argon on a big coding or agent job, the next six weeks are the cheapest it will be on the standard paid tier.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers and teams on a paid Gemini API plan who want to benchmark Argon against Claude or GPT on real work.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Paid tier of the Gemini Developer API only; Argon isn&#039;t on the free tier. Intro price runs through Nov 30, 2026, then $4 in / $20 out per 1M tokens (Batch and Flex $2 / $10).</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google AI for Developers on ai.google.dev ↗</a>
