                                <article id="oss-scanner-free-scans" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-19" class="text-slate-400">Oct 19, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/oss-scanner-free-scans/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Maintain a critical open-source project? Anthropic will scan it for bugs for free</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic&#039;s OSS Scanner gives eligible open-source projects free, regular security scans run by its strongest models, including Claude Mythos. Each report comes with a working reproducer and, where possible, a suggested patch. The reports are written by the model and not checked by a human first, so some can be wrong. Anthropic says the first scans have already sent 77 critical and 803 high model-rated findings to maintainers, including a curl bug that has since been patched. Separately, its Claude for Open Source program gives qualifying maintainers 6 months of Claude Max 20x for free.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Security audits cost a lot, and attackers use AI to find bugs too. This gets frontier-model bug hunting on your project at no cost.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Core maintainers of established, widely used open-source projects, especially libraries that handle untrusted input. Brand-new projects and most forks don&#039;t qualify.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">OSS Scanner: free and opt-in. Anthropic accepts projects case by case using OSS-Fuzz-style criteria. You enroll with a pull request to github.com/anthropics/oss-scanner and can pause or leave at any time. Claude for Open Source: 6 months of Claude Max 20x free for qualifying maintainers (for example 500+ dependent repos, 200,000+ monthly downloads, or an OpenSSF criticality score of 0.4+). It&#039;s capped at 10,000 recipients with no fixed deadline. Afterwards you go back to your previous paid plan or to the free plan, and overages can be charged during the free period. Checked October 20, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/ClaudeDevs/status/2112299602510749992" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @ClaudeDevs on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/oss-scanner-free-scans/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
