                                <article id="openai-cobol-fortran-migration" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="chatgpt" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-19" class="text-slate-400">Oct 19, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-cobol-fortran-migration/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Got old COBOL or Fortran? OpenAI&#039;s latest models just got much better at migrating it</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI says its newest models are much stronger at building and migrating software in less common languages like COBOL, Fortran, OCaml and Visual Basic. Its COBOL migration test ports programs to C++, Java, Kotlin, Python or Rust and requires byte-for-byte identical output. On that test, GPT-6.1 Sol scored 86.6% at low reasoning effort, up from 5.4% for GPT-5.6 Sol, and 97.9% at higher effort. On MultiLangBench, where a model builds a SQLite-compatible database engine in 20 languages, GPT-6 Astra averaged 87.4%. OpenAI released the benchmark on GitHub and says production migrations still need expert review.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> A lot of banking, government and weather software still runs on these languages, and the people who wrote it are retiring. A model that keeps the old behaviour makes modernising much less risky.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Teams maintaining mainframe, scientific or legacy business code, and consultants who do migrations.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">GPT-6.1 Sol and GPT-6 Astra through the OpenAI API, and in Codex where your plan includes them. The scores come from OpenAI&#039;s own evaluations, not independent tests.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2112310345863930168" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAI on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-cobol-fortran-migration/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Got%20old%20COBOL%20or%20Fortran%3F%20OpenAI%27s%20latest%20models%20just%20got%20much%20better%20at%20migrating%20it&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fchatgpt%2Fopenai-cobol-fortran-migration%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
