        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-19" class="text-slate-400">Oct 19, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/glimmer-30b-one-gpu/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Run a Meta agent model on one gaming GPU: Muse Glimmer 30B, explained</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Meta published a technical report on Muse Glimmer, its 30-billion-parameter open-weight model built for agent work on your own hardware: tool use, multi-step planning and recovering from failures. Quantized to about 4 bits, it runs on a Mac or PC with a single consumer GPU. The smaller build is about 17 GB and fits under 24 GB of VRAM. It reads text and images, and Meta says it beats similar-sized open models like Gemma4-31B and Qwen3.6-27B on agent benchmarks. The weights have been on Hugging Face under Apache 2.0 since August, with no API key or gated access. The new report explains how Meta built and compressed it.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> You can run private, always-on agents with no per-token bill and no data leaving your machine.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers building local or private agents, and anyone with a 24 GB GPU or a Mac with plenty of memory.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free under Apache 2.0 on Hugging Face (meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B, plus a GGUF version). It runs with llama.cpp, vLLM, SGLang, Ollama, LM Studio and others. The 4-bit builds need roughly 17 to 20 GB of memory. Benchmark claims are Meta&#039;s own.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/AIatMeta/status/2112265822274302066" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @AIatMeta on X ↗</a>
