        <time datetime="2026-10-19" class="text-slate-400">Oct 19, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/grok/bot-iphone-action-button/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Press one button on your iPhone and talk to your Grok Bot</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Grok Bot now works with the iPhone Action Button. Set it up once, and one press opens a voice chat with your Bot, so you don&#039;t have to unlock the phone and find the app. Each Bot runs on its own cloud computer, so a quick spoken request can turn into a task that keeps going after you lock the phone.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> You can brief your agent in five seconds while walking, driving or cooking, instead of waiting until you&#039;re back at a keyboard.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot users with an iPhone 15 Pro or newer who like giving tasks by voice.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Grok Bot iOS app, updated to the latest version, on iPhones with an Action Button (iPhone 15 Pro and later). You need a plan that includes Grok Bot. xAI announced it on October 19, 2026 and hasn&#039;t said whether Android gets something similar.</dd></div>        </dl>
