                                <article id="code-remote-control-phone" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-19" class="text-slate-400">Oct 19, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-remote-control-phone/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Leave Claude Code running on your computer and steer it from your phone</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Claude Code&#039;s Remote Control connects a session running on your own machine to the Claude mobile app or claude.ai/code. Start it with claude --rc (short for --remote-control), or type /rc in a session that&#039;s already open. You can then send messages, attach photos and approve steps from your phone, while the code keeps running on your computer with your files, tools and MCP servers. If your laptop sleeps or the network drops, it reconnects when the machine is back online. A developer on X says he&#039;s used it from the car, a badminton court and a flight.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Long agent runs don&#039;t keep you at your desk anymore. You can answer its questions or change direction from anywhere.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code users who run long tasks and want to check in while they&#039;re away.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Pro, Max, Team and Enterprise plans; API keys aren&#039;t supported. On Team and Enterprise, an Owner has to turn it on first. It doesn&#039;t work through Bedrock, Google Cloud, Microsoft Foundry or a custom gateway. Your computer has to stay on.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/shri_shobhit/status/2112083357916168629" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @shri_shobhit on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-remote-control-phone/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
