    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Images &amp; media</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-19" class="text-slate-400">Oct 19, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/argon-desk-photo-3d-race-track/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google turned a photo of a desk into a playable 3D race track with Gemini 4 Argon</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google snapped a photo of a real desk and had Gemini 4 Argon coordinate subagents, Blender (through a Blender MCP server) and Nano Banana to turn the everyday objects on it into a playable 3D racing track. Argon planned the work, sent modelling to Blender and image work to Nano Banana, and assembled the game. It&#039;s a good example of one model running a multi-tool creative pipeline from a single photo.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Turning a real room into a game level used to take a 3D artist days. Now you can try it from one photo and a prompt.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Hobby game makers, teachers and parents who want a fun weekend build, and developers trying multi-agent tool use.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Needs access to Gemini 4 Argon in Google Antigravity (usage limits depend on your Google plan), plus Blender with an MCP server set up. Shown by Google as a demo.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/Google/status/2112199261899411579" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on X ↗</a>
