        <time datetime="2026-10-19" class="text-slate-400">Oct 19, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/notebooklm-co-create-slides-video/" class="hover:text-brand-600">NotebookLM now lets you steer Slide Decks and Video Overviews before it generates them</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">NotebookLM&#039;s Slide Decks and Video Overviews now have a co-create step. You pick a focus topic suggested from your sources (or type your own), choose the format, length, language and visual style, then review and edit the slide outline or the video&#039;s producer notes before anything is generated. You no longer get one fixed result you have to regenerate until it&#039;s right.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Editing the outline first is much faster than regenerating a whole deck or video because one slide or one scene is off.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Students, teachers and analysts who turn research notes into decks or explainer videos.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Google AI Pro and Ultra subscribers, per the official NotebookLM account (Oct 19, 2026). Still rolling out, so it may not appear for everyone yet.</dd></div>        </dl>
