                                <article id="api-cli-for-claude-code-codex-cursor" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-19" class="text-slate-400">Oct 19, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/api-cli-for-claude-code-codex-cursor/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Google&#039;s new gemini-api CLI lets Claude Code, Codex and Cursor make images, video and Deep Research reports</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google released the Gemini API CLI, a stateless, zero-dependency command-line client called gemini-api that any agent with shell access can use, including Antigravity, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, OpenClaw and Hermes. Your coding agent can call Gemini to generate text, images, speech, music and video, analyze PDFs, audio and YouTube links, and launch Gemini managed agents such as Deep Research in the background. Every command describes itself offline with --help, --usage and --schema, and --dry-run lets an agent check a call without touching the network. Google calls it an experimental, open-source beta and says breaking changes can happen between minor versions.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> You can keep the coding agent you already like and hand it Gemini&#039;s media and research tools with one shell command, without writing SDK code.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers using Claude Code, Codex, Cursor or Antigravity who want image, video, transcription or research help inside their agent workflow.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Experimental open-source beta (Apache 2.0) for macOS, Linux and Windows. It needs a Gemini API key from Google AI Studio, and calls follow normal Gemini API pricing and limits. Checked October 30, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/cli" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google AI for Developers on ai.google.dev ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/api-cli-for-claude-code-codex-cursor/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Google%27s%20new%20gemini-api%20CLI%20lets%20Claude%20Code%2C%20Codex%20and%20Cursor%20make%20images%2C%20video%20and%20Deep%20Research%20reports&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fapi-cli-for-claude-code-codex-cursor%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Use the gemini-api CLI to generate a hero image for this project&#039;s README. Run it with --dry-run -o json first and show me the call before you run it for real." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="anthropic-public-benefit-fund" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="claude" data-cat="news">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/claude/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 dark:bg-orange-500/15 dark:text-orange-300">Claude</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-18" class="text-slate-400">Oct 18, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-public-benefit-fund/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Anthropic puts 5% of its shares into a new Public Benefit Fund</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic announced the Anthropic Public Benefit Fund, a wholly owned LLC that will hold 5% of the company&#039;s shares, subject to stockholder approval. The board can add up to 2% more for every 50% rise in the company&#039;s value above a set baseline. Anthropic says the fund could make large donations or direct payments to groups such as workers hit by AI, and that none of its equity will be used for lobbying or political giving.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> With its co-founders&#039; 80% equity pledge and an employee donation match, Anthropic says about 20% of its shares are now committed to the public good. That&#039;s a rare concrete commitment from an AI lab.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone following how AI companies handle the money and job disruption their products create.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to Anthropic as a company. Governance details and the valuation milestones come in the next few months, Anthropic says.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/public-benefit-fund" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Anthropic on www.anthropic.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/anthropic-public-benefit-fund/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">Read more →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Anthropic%20puts%205%25%20of%20its%20shares%20into%20a%20new%20Public%20Benefit%20Fund&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fanthropic-public-benefit-fund%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
