    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-crypto-research-agent-paper/" class="hover:text-brand-600">The viral prompt that turns Claude Code into a crypto research desk (no real money)</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A widely shared post gives a paste-in prompt for Claude Code that builds a 24/7 crypto research agent. It watches the market, makes paper trades and logs its reasoning. It uses two read-only MCP servers (DexPaprika for on-chain DEX data and CCXT for exchange prices) and the prompt says no exchange keys, wallets or private keys anywhere. Paper trading only in the original post. This is a look at what people are building, not investment advice: automated trading can lose money fast.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a well-scoped example of an always-on agent: read-only data, no money at risk, and a log you can audit.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers curious about agents with MCP data feeds.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code on a paid Claude plan. The MCP servers in the post are free and need no API keys. Paper trading only.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/RoundtableSpace/status/2111249583321858541" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @RoundtableSpace on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-crypto-research-agent-paper/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=The%20viral%20prompt%20that%20turns%20Claude%20Code%20into%20a%20crypto%20research%20desk%20%28no%20real%20money%29&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fclaude%2Fcode-crypto-research-agent-paper%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="Build a crypto research + paper-trading agent in this repo.

Data: use only the dexpaprika and ccxt MCP tools (read-only). No exchange API keys, no wallets, no private keys anywhere in the code.

Loop every 15 minutes:
1. Pull price, volume and 1h/4h candles for a watchlist in watchlist.json
2. Compute trend, momentum and volatility; note liquidity and volume spikes
3. Decide BUY / SELL / HOLD per asset with a written reason
4. Execute PAPER trades only, recorded in a local SQLite ledger

Risk rules (hard):
- Start with $10,000 paper balance
- Max 5% of balance per position, max 3 open positions
- Stop-loss 3%, take-profit 6%, no leverage
- Skip any token with &lt; $500k liquidity

Output:
- A daily markdown report: trades, P&amp;L, win rate, max drawdown, and what the agent got wrong
- Never claim results are predictive. Never place real orders." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
