    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/openai-codex-hardware-weekend-projects/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Need a weekend project? OpenAI&#039;s new gallery shows hardware people built with Codex</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI Developers launched &quot;You can just build things [with hardware]&quot;, a site that collects projects the community has built with Codex and explains how to make them yourself. You can browse projects, read the Learn section, and sign in with your ChatGPT account to vote or share your own build.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a ready-made list of tested ideas with build notes, so you skip the blank-page part and get straight to making something.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Makers, students and developers who want a hands-on Codex project for the weekend.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">The gallery is free to browse. Voting and submitting need a ChatGPT account; building along uses Codex on your ChatGPT plan.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/OpenAIDevs/status/2111585491237650691" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @OpenAIDevs on X ↗</a>
