    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/code-review/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Let Claude Code Review check every pull request</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Boris Cherny says Claude Code Review runs on all of his pull requests and catches almost every bug before it ships, and that it is part of how his team moves fast without lowering the quality bar. It is worth switching on if you merge a lot of agent-written code and want a second reviewer that never gets tired.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Agent-written code ships faster than humans can review it. An automated reviewer on every PR catches bugs before they merge.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Engineering teams that merge a lot of AI-written pull requests.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code; setup and plan requirements are in Anthropic&#039;s Claude Code docs.</dd></div>        </dl>
