    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/parallel-agents-pro/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Split one task across several agents in GPT-6 Astra Pro</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">OpenAI upgraded GPT-6 Astra Pro in ChatGPT on October 16 with faster responses and better use of plugins and tools. Multiple agents can now work on different parts of one task in parallel, and you can follow each agent&#039;s progress and open finished parts to review them. It is aimed at Pro users with big, splittable jobs like research across many sources.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Big research or comparison jobs finish faster when separate agents take separate parts, and you can check each part as it lands.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Pro users doing multi-source research, vendor comparisons or long reports.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rolling out to eligible ChatGPT Pro users; managed workspaces depend on admin settings.</dd></div>        </dl>
