    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/argon-minecraft/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Watch four Argon agents beat Minecraft with code alone</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google DeepMind ran four Gemini 4 Argon agents in a sandbox, using only code and text. They wrote 2,783 programs, split up jobs over chat, shared notes and debugged together to beat Minecraft in 27 hours with no human help. A good read on how multi-agent teams coordinate.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It is a concrete look at how several AI agents can split work, share notes and fix each other&#039;s bugs without a human in the loop.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Anyone designing multi-agent workflows or curious where agents are heading.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Research demo from Google DeepMind; not a product feature.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/GoogleDeepMind/status/2111127991401247033" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GoogleDeepMind on X ↗</a>
