    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/slides/" class="hover:text-brand-600">ChatGPT Slides: build and co-edit decks inside ChatGPT</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">ChatGPT Slides lets you make a presentation from a conversation, your files or an outline, or from an example deck that sets the style. You can edit text, images, shapes and charts yourself or ask ChatGPT to change them, invite teammates to edit at the same time and leave comments, then present from ChatGPT or export to PowerPoint, PDF or Google Slides.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Decks are where a lot of AI drafting used to end in copy-paste. Now the draft, the edits and the team review happen in one place.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Pro, Business and Enterprise users who make decks with their team.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Rolling out to eligible Pro, Business and Enterprise users with Space access, on web and desktop.</dd></div>        </dl>
