        <a href="/trending/claude/wildfire-spread-map/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Map a wildfire&#039;s spread over time with Claude</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Claude&#039;s official account picked six projects from recent weeks that caught its attention. The first is a wildfire analysis prototype built with Opus 5.5 that maps a fire&#039;s spread over time and tracks hot spots. The post had more than 26,000 likes.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Turning public fire and satellite data into a live, readable map is the kind of project that used to need a GIS team.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Data journalists, emergency-planning teams, students and civic hackers.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude with Opus 5.5 on paid Claude plans; public fire data is free from sources like NASA FIRMS.</dd></div>        </dl>
