    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Hugging Face&#039;s launch post shows how to run Muse Spark Open on Apple silicon through llama.cpp or MLX. It is a very large model, so even the 3-bit MLX quant needs more than 256 GB of RAM. Hugging Face reports about 21 tokens a second on an M3 Ultra with 512 GB. Reasoning can&#039;t be switched off, so set it to low for easy tasks to save tokens.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It tells you up front what hardware you really need, before you spend a day downloading weights.</p>
