        <a href="/trending/gemini/synthid-time-best-inventions/" class="hover:text-brand-600">SynthID named one of TIME&#039;s Best Inventions of 2026</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google DeepMind&#039;s SynthID watermarking was named one of TIME&#039;s Best Inventions of 2026. Google says more than 180 billion images and videos have already been watermarked with it, which helps people tell AI-generated media from other content.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> As AI images get harder to spot by eye, invisible watermarks are one of the few ways to check where an image came from.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Journalists, educators, brand teams and anyone checking images.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">SynthID is built into Google&#039;s image and video models.</dd></div>        </dl>
