    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google asked Gemini 4 Argon for a realistic 3D scene in pure Python with zero external libraries. Google says it wrote more than 5,000 lines of code, built its own ray-tracing engine, video tool and audio mixer, and rendered and documented a sunlit library from scratch.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> It&#039;s a vivid stress test of long, unaided coding: no libraries to lean on, just the model building every piece itself.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers, graphics hobbyists and anyone testing how far a model can code on its own.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Gemini 4 Argon in the Gemini app, AI Studio or the API (paid API, Ultra, or AI Pro in AI Studio Build).</dd></div>        </dl>
