    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">One of the most-saved trading posts this week (800+ likes) links a free tutorial in which, as the post puts it, an &quot;ex-Meta engineer&quot; connects Claude Code to the Alpaca brokerage through an MCP server and gives it a simple 20/50-day moving-average crossover. The bot checks the market and buys or sells when the signal fires. The post says everything is tested with paper trading first. Its claims that the bot &quot;trades for you 24/7&quot; and that you don&#039;t need to code are the poster&#039;s framing, not ours. Paper trading only in the original post. This is a look at what people are building, not investment advice: automated trading can lose money fast.</p>
