    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/opus-5-5-fast-mode-ga/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Opus 5.5 fast mode is open to everyone: no waitlist, 2.5x faster output</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Fast mode for Claude Opus 5.5 on the Claude Platform is out of research preview and Anthropic has removed the waitlist. It&#039;s the same Opus 5.5 model, but it writes its output up to 2.5x faster, at $8 per million input tokens and $40 per million output tokens. It&#039;s also live in Microsoft Foundry on Azure, with Google Cloud coming soon.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> When you&#039;re waiting on long generations, like big refactors or long reports, fast mode trades money for time. Developers testing it point out that tool calls and tests don&#039;t get faster, so it helps most when writing the output is the slow part.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">API developers and teams building on Opus 5.5 who care more about speed than cost for certain jobs.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Generally available on the Claude Platform API and Microsoft Foundry (Azure); Google Cloud coming soon. Priced at $8 / $40 per million input/output tokens. Fast mode inside Claude Code is billed separately, as before.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/ClaudeDevs/status/2110825294655562048" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @ClaudeDevs on X ↗</a>
