                                <article id="argon-verification-loop" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="coding">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-13" class="text-slate-400">Oct 13, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/argon-verification-loop/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Get better long runs from Gemini 4 Argon: give it a pass/fail check</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google&#039;s own developer guide for Gemini 4 Argon has one main tip for long autonomous tasks: give the model a way to check its own work. Point it at your test suite, logs or browser screenshots, or ask it to write a verification script, record a baseline and loop until every check passes. The guide also suggests agreeing on goals and success criteria before a long run starts, and using Argon as the orchestrator with faster Flash subagents doing the parallel work.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Long autonomous runs go wrong silently. A check the model can run itself is the simplest way to keep it honest.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers running long Gemini agent tasks.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Any Gemini 4 Argon surface: API, AI Studio or Antigravity.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://aistudio.google.com/learn/gemini-4-argon-developer-guide" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @GoogleAIStudio on aistudio.google.com ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/argon-verification-loop/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Get%20better%20long%20runs%20from%20Gemini%204%20Argon%3A%20give%20it%20a%20pass%2Ffail%20check&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fargon-verification-loop%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
            <button type="button" data-copy-text="We want to fix accessibility and layout issues across our web app, but we don&#039;t have automated checks yet. First, write a headless Chrome script that crawls every route in src/routes/, inspects the live DOM and accessibility tree, and logs all violations to record our baseline score. Group the failing checks into shared root causes across our shared components, then fix them one cluster at a time. Re-run your script after each change to verify that each single fix resolves the entire cluster with zero regressions. Keep going until all routes pass with zero violations." class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200">Copy prompt</button>
    </div>
</div>
</article>
                                <article id="app-tasks-toggle" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="agents">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Agents</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-13" class="text-slate-400">Oct 13, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/app-tasks-toggle/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Switch the Gemini app from chat to tasks so it keeps working while you&#039;re away</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">With Gemini 4 Argon, the Gemini app gained a chat-to-tasks toggle in the main window. In tasks mode Gemini can keep working on a job across your Google apps even when you are not at your computer. Google also says Gemini now connects to more than 40 apps, including Instacart, OpenTable, Adobe and Shopify. Tasks are available to Google AI Pro and Ultra subscribers.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Gemini can keep a job going across your Google apps while you&#039;re away, instead of stopping when you close the chat.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Google AI Pro and Ultra users with repetitive multi-app chores.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Google AI Pro and Ultra subscribers in the Gemini app.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/gemini-4-argon-availability/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @Google on blog.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/app-tasks-toggle/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Switch%20the%20Gemini%20app%20from%20chat%20to%20tasks%20so%20it%20keeps%20working%20while%20you%27re%20away&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fapp-tasks-toggle%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
