        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-500/15 dark:text-emerald-300">ChatGPT</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Coding</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-13" class="text-slate-400">Oct 13, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/sol-vs-opus-same-prompt-cost/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Same one-prompt 3D scene: $12.43 on Opus 5.5 vs $1.42 on GPT-6.1 Sol</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">A developer gave Claude Code (Opus 5.5) and Codex (GPT-6.1 Sol) the same one-prompt job: a rainy Tokyo street with a vending machine in Three.js, both at extra-high effort. He reports Opus took 49 minutes and $12.43, and Sol took 28 minutes and $1.42. He preferred Opus&#039;s lighting and wet-street look but notes Sol&#039;s was about 8.7x cheaper.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Real cost per result, not just benchmark scores, is what decides which agent you leave running all day.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Developers choosing between Claude Code and Codex for creative or front-end work.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Claude Code and Codex on their paid plans; costs depend on effort setting and plan.</dd></div>        </dl>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm italic text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">Note: reported by users on X; we haven&#039;t independently confirmed it works in the current version.</p>    <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://x.com/sprinntt/status/2110107260751884639" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @sprinntt on X ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/sol-vs-opus-same-prompt-cost/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
