                                <article id="antigravity-free-for-scientists" class="card flex flex-col p-6 scroll-mt-28" data-trend data-ai="gemini" data-cat="deals">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-sky-100 text-sky-800 dark:bg-sky-500/15 dark:text-sky-300">Gemini</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Free offers &amp; deals</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-13" class="text-slate-400">Oct 13, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-free-for-scientists/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Scientists can get Google Antigravity&#039;s top usage tier free for 6 months</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Google is giving up to 10,000 selected researchers six months of the highest usage tier in Google Antigravity, its agent-first coding platform, plus its Gemini 4 Argon model, free of charge. The offer is for non-commercial research by people affiliated with a university, a degree-granting institution, a non-profit research institute or a national lab. Google reviews applications weekly on a rolling basis and only contacts the people it selects. A Science plugin in the app connects agents to more than 30 life-science databases, including UniProt, PubChem and ChEMBL.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Researchers get months of heavy agent use for analysis code, data wrangling and figures without paying for a top plan.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Faculty, lab heads, postdocs and PhD or master&#039;s students doing non-commercial research.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Plan &amp; availability:</dt> <dd class="inline">Free for 6 months for up to 10,000 selected applicants. There&#039;s no fixed deadline; Google selects people while it has capacity. The upgrade goes to the individual Antigravity service on the Google account you apply with, personal or institutional. Google doesn&#039;t say what happens after six months or which paid plan the tier matches, so plan for it to end. Checked October 20, 2026.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://antigravity.google/use-cases/science/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: Google Antigravity on antigravity.google ↗</a>
        <a href="/trending/gemini/antigravity-free-for-scientists/" class="font-semibold text-brand-600">How to try it →</a>    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-zinc-100 pt-4 dark:border-white/5"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" data-share>
    <a href="https://x.com/intent/post?text=Scientists%20can%20get%20Google%20Antigravity%27s%20top%20usage%20tier%20free%20for%206%20months&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fagentstacklist.com%2Ftrending%2Fgemini%2Fantigravity-free-for-scientists%2F%3Futm_source%3Dx%26utm_medium%3Dsocial%26utm_campaign%3Dshare" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-share-x class="inline-flex min-h-10 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-zinc-200 px-3.5 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-brand-400 hover:text-brand-600 dark:border-white/15 dark:text-zinc-200"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-3.5 fill-current"><path d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/></svg>Share on X</a>
