    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/chatgpt/codex-composer-predictions/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Codex can now suggest your next message</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Composer predictions in Codex suggest your next message based on the thread and how you usually talk to Codex. After Codex replies, a suggestion can appear in the message box: press Tab to accept it, then edit before sending. Nothing is sent automatically. OpenAI Developers called it one of the most loved features it has tested internally.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> Much of agent work is short follow-ups like &quot;run the tests&quot; or &quot;now fix the lint&quot;. Accepting them with Tab keeps you moving.</p>
