    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/claude/usage-policy-update/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Anthropic updates its Usage Policy, including a rule on abusing Claude</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Anthropic published its first big Usage Policy update in over a year on October 8. It takes effect on November 12. Most changes clarify existing rules for longer, more independent agent work, high-risk uses in health and finance, and Claude taking physical actions. One new rule bans &quot;sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior&quot; toward its models. Anthropic says this is aimed only at extreme, repeated cases, not ordinary frustration, pushback, dark creative themes or model testing.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you build on Claude or use it for agent work in regulated areas, the clarified rules and examples are worth reading before the effective date.</p>
