    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Astrophysicist Brice Ménard worked with Claude Science to make the first complete ultraviolet map of the sky. He guided Claude to find existing datasets, combine them and fill the gaps with statistical inference. Anthropic says the work would have taken weeks by hand but took a few days while he worked on other projects.</p>
