        <a href="/trending/muse/" class="rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 dark:bg-violet-500/15 dark:text-violet-300">Muse</a>        <span class="rounded-full bg-zinc-100 px-2.5 py-1 font-medium text-slate-600 dark:bg-white/5 dark:text-zinc-300">Industry News</span>
        <time datetime="2026-10-03" class="text-slate-400">Oct 3, 2026</time>
    </div>
    <h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-ink dark:text-white">
        <a href="/trending/muse/relationship-profiles-privacy/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Report: Muse builds profiles of people in your life</a>    </h3>
    <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400">WIRED reported that Muse&#039;s operating instructions, which researchers got the agent to export, describe an hourly process that builds a page for each person in a user&#039;s life, such as family, friends and colleagues, with sections like shared history and important dates. Meta told WIRED that an agent needs context about you and the people you deal with to help you, that it uses public information and what you choose to share, and that you can edit or wipe memories and disconnect services.</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-zinc-400"><strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800 dark:text-zinc-200">Why it matters:</strong> If you connect messages, photos or accounts to Muse, it&#039;s worth knowing how it may organise information about other people.</p>
                    <dl class="mt-3 grid gap-1 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Good for:</dt> <dd class="inline">Muse users, especially those who have connected messaging or social accounts.</dd></div>            <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-700 dark:text-zinc-300">Applies to:</dt> <dd class="inline">Applies to the Muse app; settings and behaviour may change.</dd></div>        </dl>
            <div class="mt-auto flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 pt-5 text-sm">
        <a href="https://www.wired.com/story/muse-creates-detailed-profiles-of-all-your-friends-and-family/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-brand-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Source: @WIRED on www.wired.com ↗</a>
